window.AKK_THE_LITTLE_DARLING_WIFE_WHO_IS_A_DIVINE_DOCTOR_SAVED_THE_ENTIRE_FAMILY_OF_THE_DUKES_MANSION_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_THE_LITTLE_DARLING_WIFE_WHO_IS_A_DIVINE_DOCTOR_SAVED_THE_ENTIRE_FAMILY_OF_THE_DUKES_MANSION_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":1,"title":"Chapter 1: Worship with Heroes and Idols","paragraphs":["\"Everyone, please look. This is the famous Mausoleum of Mo Jiuye, the renowned general in history,\" the tour guide said, waving a small flag and leading the tourists towards the entrance of the underground palace.","For some reason, He Zhiran felt a sense of solemnity when she arrived here.","As a special forces medic, she didn't worship celebrities, only heroes.","The owner of this mausoleum, Mo Jiuye, was one of the heroes she admired.","Mo Jiuye was the top general of the Da Shun Dynasty. He led the army to defeat foreign enemies thoroughly.","However, even a hero like him was suspected and dismissed from his official position by the emperor at that time, just because of his great reputation and power.","Listening to the guide's verbose introduction, He Zhiran sighed constantly in her heart.","It could only be said that this hero was born at the wrong time. If Mo Jiuye could have lived a few more years until the new emperor took the throne, he would have been redressed. Unfortunately, fate played a trick on him and he died on the way to exile...","Just as He Zhiran was immersed in her own thoughts, she suddenly felt a violent shaking under her feet.","Someone shouted, \"Run quickly, it's an earthquake!\"","With He Zhiran's skills, she could have successfully escaped from this natural disaster. However, in order to save people, she stayed here forever.","Before she lost consciousness, He Zhiran's lips curled up slightly, \"It's also good to be buried here with the hero.\"","...","Da Shun Dynasty.","The Duke of Protector's residence was decorated with colored lights and resounded with drums and music.","\"First bow to heaven and earth!\"","Following the loud and long yell, He Zhiran felt like a puppet being helped to bow.","\"Second bow to the high hall!\"","\"Bride and groom, bow to each other!\"","\"Enter the bridal chamber...\"","He Zhiran still felt a little dizzy, but it did not stop her from receiving the memory of this body.","Ignoring the noisy congratulations and the endless auspicious words of the matchmaker, He Zhiran's mind was completely immersed in her own thoughts.","After sorting out these memories, she had to accept the fact that she had crossed over.","What's more, she crossed over and became the new bride of the famous hero Mo Jiuye she admired...","The original owner had the same name as her, He Zhiran. She was the eldest daughter of He Yuanming, the current Minister of Revenue. She was betrothed to Mo Jiuye since she was a child.","The Mo family had been loyal for generations. All the men sacrificed themselves for the country, and now only Mo Jiuye was left.","Five years ago, after Mo Jiuye's eldest brother died on the battlefield, the 16-year-old Mo Jiuye took charge of the troops. At the same time, he alone supported the Duke of Protector's residence full of widows.","Now Mo Jiuye had returned triumphantly. Following the arrangements of the old Madam Mo, the wedding took place on an auspicious day.","However, the original owner wanted to cancel the marriage. She didn't want to be a widow like those women in the Duke of Protector's residence for the rest of her life.","After all, the Mo men, without exception, died on the battlefield at a young age.","The original owner tried every means to cancel the marriage. But her righteous and honest father, He Yuanming, did not agree to cancel the marriage under any circumstances.","In order to let the original owner marry into the Duke of Protector's residence smoothly, He Yuanming and his wife Ling Xueyan had no choice but to give the original owner some drugs, thinking that after the rice was cooked into cooked rice, their daughter would have to resign herself to fate.","It was unknown whether they misjudged the dosage, which led to the original owner's death in the bridal sedan. This allowed the arrival of He Zhiran.","However, what confused He Zhiran was that in the history she knew, there was no mention of Mo Jiuye having a wife until he was exiled.","Could it be that the original owner really died in the bridal sedan and failed to worship the ancestors with Mo Jiuye, so it was not recorded?","Just as she was lost in thought, the noise outside the bridal chamber grew louder.","Her maid of honor Qiao Yu lightly touched her arm, \"Miss, the young master is here.\"","He Zhiran responded softly, \"Okay.\"","A group of people escorted Mo Jiuye in red wedding clothes into the bridal chamber.","\"Young Master, lift the veil now! Don't miss the auspicious time.\" The matchmaker happily handed Mo Jiuye a balance rod tied with red ribbons.","\"Ninth brother, hurry up. We are all waiting to see the ninth brother's wife!\"","\"That's right, ninth brother. Don't be shy...\"","Holding the balancing rod, Mo Jiuye was escorted by several sisters-in-law to He Zhiran.","He stopped and lightly lifted the red veil covering He Zhiran's sight under everyone's gaze.","He Zhiran instinctively looked at the person in front of her.","She guessed he was about 185cm tall, with a straight posture and strong limbs.","His distinct features were as exquisite as sculpture. His extraordinarily handsome face was somewhat similar to the portrait in the mausoleum.","His expressionless face and sharp, deep eyes unconsciously gave people a sense of oppression!","In He Zhiran's heart, her great hero should look like this.","Just as she was a little distracted, Mo Jiuye said coldly.","\"Have you looked enough?\"","Only then did He Zhiran realize that she had been absent-minded just now.","Looking into those deep eyes, He Zhiran blurted out, \"Yeah, looked enough. Just so-so.\"","It wasn't that she didn't respect the great hero, but with so many people around, this man didn't give her any face at all, so she didn't have to deliberately flatter him.","Seeing the two were off to a bad start just after getting married, Sister-in-law Deng Xue quickly smoothed things over.","\"Ninth brother, ninth sister-in-law, don't spoil the auspicious time. Drink the wedding toast and rest early.\"","Sister-in-law Feng Cuilian also came up and said, \"Yes, you have to work hard and give birth to many children for the Mo family.\"","Listening to these sisters-in-law, even He Zhiran with a modern soul couldn't help blushing a little.","In her previous life as a 24-year-old only child, she only wanted to serve the country and never thought about encountering such an embarrassing situation one day.","In order not to show her embarrassment, she lowered her head quickly.","This action was misunderstood by others again.","Sister-in-law Xiao Qinger held He Zhiran's hand, \"Ninth sister-in-law, don't be shy. You'll get used to these sisters-in-law after a while. They just like joking.\"","He Zhiran tried to explain, \"I'm not shy.\"","Just as a few other sisters-in-law were about to say something, a voice came from outside the door.","\"Young Master, His Majesty has sent an oral message and ordered you to go to the palace immediately.\"","Upon hearing this, He Zhiran's heart thumped.","Seeing that Mo Jiuye had already turned to leave, she grabbed the maid beside her and asked, \"Qiao Yu, what year and month is it now?\"","Qiao Yu was stunned for a moment. With a puzzled look on her face, she answered, \"Miss, have you forgotten your own wedding day? Today is the eighth day of the seventh month in the 19th year of the Shun Yuan era!\"","\"Oh no!\"","Watching Mo Jiuye's departing figure, He Zhiran's first reaction was that since she had come, she had to do her best to let her idol hero live.","He Zhiran suddenly stood up, regardless of her still weak body and the puzzled eyes of the sisters-in-law. She lifted her skirt and rushed out.","If she remembered correctly, on this day Mo Jiuye was summoned to the palace late at night by the emperor, and was falsely charged with trespassing the imperial harem. He was given one hundred heavy strokes.","The next day, Mo Jiuye was charged with the crime of betraying the country to the enemy. The Duke of Protector's residence was confiscated and Mo Jiuye was exiled."]},{"number":2,"title":"Chapter 2: Reminder","paragraphs":["He Zhiran ran while shouting, afraid that she couldn't keep up with Mo Jiuye's pace.","\"Mo Jiuye, wait for me...\"","She chased him for a long time before finally seeing Mo Jiuye's red figure ahead.","Mo Jiuye turned around, still looking at her with no expression: \"What's the matter?\"","He Zhiran ran over to Mo Jiuye, out of breath, and pulled his arm to walk back.","\"What are you doing?\" Mo Jiuye frowned and asked.","He Zhiran didn't know how to explain her purpose, she could only vaguely say, \"I have a hunch that you're afraid of being plotted against when you enter the palace this time.\"","When she said this, He Zhiran was already prepared to be questioned by Mo Jiuye.","However, Mo Jiuye did not do so, but asked in return, \"What have you heard?\"","In fact, since Mo Jiuye returned to the capital from the border, he had a vague feeling of being targeted, especially by the Emperor, who always gave him a hypocritical feeling when talking to him.","He Zhiran certainly couldn't say that she knew this history, so when asked again, she could only bite the bullet and answer.","\"I told you, I just have a bad hunch.\"","In Mo Jiuye's eyes, her explanation was too far-fetched, but at this moment he was in a hurry to enter the palace, and had no intention of asking further.","He allowed He Zhiran to lead him and gave her the initiative.","He Zhiran lingered around the yard of the Bridal Chamber for a while, and finally settled her eyes on the carriage she was riding in.","She let go of Mo Jiuye's arm, ran into the carriage, and took out a thick cushion.","This was something the original owner often brought with her when going out from her parents' home. Whether it was a carriage or carriage, she hated the bumps, so the meticulous Madam He ordered the servants to make her a cushion.","He Zhiran squeezed the thickness of the cushion, it was still acceptable, turned around and handed it to Mo Jiuye.","\"If you believe me, put this pad behind you, it may help you.\"","After a pause, she added, \"Also, if someone claims the Emperor has summoned you to the harem, you must not go.\"","This was all she could do for now. Whether Mo Jiuye could escape physical suffering depended on his own fortune.","Mo Jiuye hesitated for a moment, but still took the cushion.","As he turned to leave, he said, \"It's late, don't wait for me, go to rest early!\"","Watching Mo Jiuye's retreating figure, He Zhiran still couldn't help reminding him, \"Don't forget to put the pad behind you.\"","Getting no more response from Mo Jiuye, He Zhiran could only go back the same way.","Back in the yard, she saw eight sister-in-laws and one little aunt waiting there.","The eight sister-in-laws were all experienced people. Seeing He Zhiran come back, they couldn't help but come up and comfort her.","\"Sister-in-law, don't worry. The Emperor summoned brother-in-law so late, he must have some urgent matter. I'm sure it won't take too long.\"","\"That's right, brother-in-law will definitely come back in time to consummate your marriage.\"","\"...\"","The sister-in-laws were too enthusiastic. He Zhiran also knew they were all showing her goodwill, but she couldn't take in what they were saying at the moment.","Looking at the eight very young sister-in-laws, He Zhiran felt a moment of heartache.","The poor women were doomed to become young widows.","In the end, they would fall to exile.","Thinking it over, He Zhiran still decided to warn them.","\"Sister-in-laws, I've been having a strange dream these days, saying that the Duke of Protector's mansion will be searched and exiled.\"","The usually calm eldest sister-in-law Cui Biting came over and grabbed her arm, speaking gently, \"Sister-in-law, you can't say such things randomly. Our Duke of Protector's family has been loyal for generations, how could we possibly be searched and exiled?\"","\"Nonsense... We can't say such unlucky things. Sister-in-law, let's pretend we didn't hear that today.\" The second sister-in-law Xie Fang immediately spat on the ground twice.","He Zhiran knew this would be the effect after her warning, but she didn't intend to give up just like that.","\"Sisters-in-law, I also hope this is not true, but this dream is so real, and it's the same scene every day, so I feel we might as well believe it and make some preparations ahead of time, it won't hurt.\"","Everyone looked at He Zhiran talking plausibly there, and they were instantly conflicted.","The little aunt Mo Hanyue, who had been raised by so many elders all her life, was the most timid. Hearing He Zhiran's words, she was already scared to tears.","The little girl said tearfully, \"Sister-in-law, I'm scared. This can't be true.\"","Seeing this, the eldest sister-in-law hugged her and gently comforted her, \"Don't be afraid, Hanyue, they say dreams are reversed.\"","Mo Hanyue wiped away the tears from the corners of her eyes and snuggled into the eldest sister-in-law's arms.","The eldest sister-in-law looked around at everyone and said, \"It's late, sister-in-law has had a tiring day, let her rest early!\"","He Zhiran didn't know if anyone believed her words, but she had done what she should, and could only take it one step at a time from now on.","Back in the room, after several maids had finished helping her wash up, He Zhiran sent them all away.","What she needed now was quiet. Only by calming down could she think carefully about the next step.","In the light of the red candles, she could see the dazzling array of the entire bridal chamber. It was a pity that she didn't have the ability to take these things away.","Since this was the case, she could only focus on the most portable silver tickets.","She didn't know how many silver tickets were in the Duke of Protector's mansion right now. Her dowry from her parents contained exactly two thousand taels of silver tickets.","With the silver tickets in hand, He Zhiran's first thought was that when the house was searched, someone would definitely search her. Where could she hide these tickets without being found?","If she also had a space like those transmigrated female leads in novels, that would be great. She could put the tickets in the space and it would be perfectly safe. But unfortunately...","Just as she complained that transmigration gods were unfair, she suddenly felt the scene in front of her change.","The scene in front of her was so familiar, this was her medical office.","Could it be that she didn't die?","Soon, He Zhiran was ruthlessly defeated by the facts.","She tried to push open the door of the medical office, but the door was like a prop, completely unresponsive, not even a gap could be seen.","The windows were the same, as if welded shut..."]},{"number":3,"title":"Chapter 3: Space Emerges","paragraphs":["He Zhiran quickly sorted out her thoughts. She had indeed transmigrated, and this medical office was the so-called transmigration golden finger.","In order to quickly grasp the operation of this space, He Zhiran softly said, \"Go out.\"","Sure enough, her body reappeared in the dowry storage room.","She first grabbed a box, moved it with her thoughts, and her whole person and the box reappeared in the space, which showed that this space allowed external objects to enter.","After putting down the box, He Zhiran did not stay in the dowry room any longer, but went back to the bridal chamber.","Although she had the space, she had to formulate a reasonable plan before the imperial edict of exile was issued, in order to carry more supplies.","He Zhiran sat on the bridal bed and pondered.","If the historical records were correct, Mo Jiuye was called to the imperial palace in the early morning and was carried back unconscious, with only one breath left.","It was said that less than an hour after Mo Jiuye returned to the mansion, the emperor sent troops to surround the Duke of Protector's mansion, and at the same time issued an imperial edict to confiscate the family property and exile them.","He Zhiran looked at the clock in the space, which already showed 10 pm.","That is to say, there are at most 10 hours left before the imperial edict is issued.","He Zhiran plans to make full use of the remaining time.","With the idea in mind, she flashed into the space, rummaged around, and found a camouflage suit that she often wore when going on missions in her previous life.","He Zhiran changed into camouflage, neatly coiled her hair into a simple bun, put on climbing claws and wire, and slipped out of the yard evading the maidservants' sight.","In order to observe the terrain of the Duke of Protector's mansion, He Zhiran nimbly climbed a thick big tree.","Standing on the big tree and looking around, He Zhiran could initially determine that the courtyard she was in was slightly west, and she needed to go east to get to the area with denser courtyards.","However, she did not do so.","From the environment, He Zhiran analyzed that the courtyards in the east should be the residences of the sisters-in-law and mothers-in-law. Even if there were some valuables there, they were the private possessions of individuals.","However, given the current urgent situation, it would be easier to find the warehouse than to ransack the courtyards one by one like a thief.","Determined, He Zhiran groped her way west.","As expected of the Duke of Protector's mansion, the guards were extremely strict.","All the way, He Zhiran encountered several guards patrolling with weapons from time to time.","And she found that the more west she went, the more guards there were.","Using her skills from her previous life, she came to a courtyard using anti-reconnaissance techniques.","It couldn't be called a courtyard, but rather a relatively large house.","Observing from a distance, He Zhiran found that there were actually two guards guarding it.","Without a doubt, He Zhiran guessed that there must be something important here, most likely the warehouse of the Duke of Protector's mansion.","In order to divert the guards, she picked up a small pebble from the ground and threw it towards the nearby pond.","The pebble fell into the pond with a \"plop\" sound, which was particularly abrupt in this quiet night.","\"Who's there?\"","The guard quickly noticed something wrong and ran towards the pond with his weapon.","He Zhiran dared not delay, and immediately came to the front of the house.","Naturally, there would be an iron lock where there were guards.","Without thinking twice, He Zhiran's consciousness quickly entered the space, took out the finest pointed tweezers, turned the tweezers in the keyhole a few times, and the lock opened.","Taking advantage of the guards not having returned yet, He Zhiran opened the door and entered at the fastest speed.","It was pitch black inside, and in the dim moonlight she could see that the surroundings were all shelves.","He Zhiran had no time to check carefully, she just reached out and touched the items on the nearest shelf. It felt slippery, like some kind of fabric.","There was no doubt that this was the warehouse of the Duke of Protector's mansion.","In order to save time, He Zhiran directly used her mind to put all the items in the warehouse into the space, leaving only the shelves that held the items.","Just as she had finished collecting the items here, the guards who had gone to check the situation came back.","\"I think you're just too nervous. There's no one there, making us rush over for nothing.\"","\"I definitely heard movement by the pond.\"","\"There are plenty of frogs this season. Jumping into the pond could make that sound.\"","\"Alright alright, I was overthinking it, let's not argue, let's stand guard properly.\"","The two guards had returned, and now He Zhiran needed to consider how to leave unnoticed.","After thinking for a moment, she suddenly remembered that there was still a new mini drone in the space.","With a strategy in mind, He Zhiran nimbly leapt onto the roof beam, gently pried open a tile, then took out the drone.","Skillfully manipulating the drone, she flew it to a place further away. When she felt the distance was about right, she used the remote control again to turn on the drone's laser light and sound wave.","The guard, who had just found a position to stand, was instantly attracted by the sound, and then saw a beam of white light shooting at a certain courtyard.","\"What's that?\"","\"There's an assassin.\"","\"Let's go check it out quickly.\"","Listening to the guard's footsteps getting farther and farther away, He Zhiran quickly got out of the warehouse, not forgetting to re-lock the lock.","Running to a safe distance, she leapt onto a big tree, used the remote control to turn off the drone's laser light and sound wave, believing that those people would naturally come back after failing to find the target.","Sure enough, after circling around and finding nothing until the light disappeared, the guards reluctantly returned to the front of the warehouse door.","\"It really feels strange tonight, nothing will happen right?\"","\"I feel very weird too, should we report to the Duke?\"","\"How dare you have the gall to disturb the Duke on his wedding night in the bridal chamber?\"","\"You're right, let's talk about it tomorrow morning, as long as the warehouse is safe.\"","Seeing that the two guards had completely lowered their vigilance, He Zhiran nimbly jumped down from the tree, maneuvered the drone back into her hands, then put it away in the space."]},{"number":4,"title":"Chapter 4: Mo Jiuye was carried back.","paragraphs":["He Zhiran continued to dodge the guards' sight to find the harvest target, while her consciousness also entered the space to check.","She thought that the Duke of Protector's mansion was profound, and would have some savings.","Who knew that except for some fabrics that looked a little gorgeous, there were some food, coarse and fine grain, and half a box of silver ingots.","As for antiques, calligraphy and painting, gold, silver and jewellery, there was little.","The prestigious Duke of Protector's mansion turned out to be so poor, which shows the integrity of the Mo Family.","However, it was such a loyal family for generations that was feared by the monarch, which was simply unreasonable.","That half box of silver, estimated to be only 10,000 taels, although less than imagined, He Zhiran firmly believed that it would be better than nothing on the exile journey.","He Zhiran thought about it while acting. Wherever she could easily enter, she collected all the items into the space until the space was full that she reluctantly returned to her own yard.","At this time, more than an hour had passed since she went out.","Qiao Yu was still conscientiously guarding outside the door. He Zhiran jumped directly into the bedroom through the window.","She had just changed out of her camouflage clothes when she heard hurried footsteps outside.","\"What's wrong with the Duke?\"","He Zhiran heard Qiao Yu's anxious questioning and hurried out.","I saw Mo Jiuye being carried in by two guards on a door plate, walking towards the house.","\"Madam, the Duke is injured. Subordinates will send him back first and immediately invite the imperial physician.\"","After speaking, the two guards had moved Mo Jiuye from the door plate to the bed.","The two guards left, Qiao Yu walked to He Zhiran's side with red eyes.","\"Young Miss, the Duke was fine when he went out just now. How could he become unconscious so soon?\"","He Zhiran was also observing Mo Jiuye's situation. She saw him with his eyes closed, seeming to be in a coma.","\"You go to the door first to wait. Bring the imperial physician in as soon as he arrives.\"","Her first priority was to distract Qiao Yu, and then help Mo Jiuye check his injuries.","\"Yes!\" Qiao Yu responded and turned to leave.","He Zhiran adjusted the two large red candles to the brightest state and placed them on the bedside, ready to check Mo Jiuye's condition.","Unexpectedly, as soon as her hand reached out, Mo Jiuye opened his eyes.","\"I'm fine.\"","Hearing his voice, he was energetic and seemed to be unharmed indeed.","\"What exactly happened?\" He Zhiran asked.","Mo Jiuye hesitated for a moment and shifted his body slightly.","His icy eyes stared tightly at He Zhiran.","\"How did you know that I would be in trouble when I entered the palace today?\"","On the way back from the palace, Mo Jiuye lay on the door plate, guessing in his heart how He Zhiran knew this.","The biggest possibility was that his father-in-law He Yuanming knew about this in advance. Otherwise, he could not explain all this at all.","If this was the case, He Yuanming was undoubtedly a person on the emperor's side, and He Zhiran did not rule out the possibility that she was his spy.","With this thought, Mo Jiuye's eyes on He Zhiran were a few minutes deeper.","If it was the young lady of this era, she would probably be scared to cry.","He Zhiran knew that Mo Jiuye suspected her, but she was not nervous at all.","\"I've been having the same dream for several days in a row, dreaming that you would have this disaster. Whether you believe it or not, this is my explanation.\"","Looking at her clear and bright eyes, Mo Jiuye clearly did not believe her words, but surprisingly did not continue to interrogate.","He Zhiran didn't know what he was thinking. She spoke again, \"Are you injured? I know some medical skills and can help you take a look.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, she saw Mo Jiuye take out the pad she had given him from behind in front of her.","The pad was damaged in many places, and blood stains could be vaguely seen on it.","\"Did you really enter the harem? And got a hundred strokes?\"","This was how it was recorded in history. Now Mo Jiuye was carried back, and there was blood on the pad, indicating that this had all come true.","Mo Jiuye shook his head lightly, \"I didn't enter the harem. The emperor charged me with the crime of disobeying orders. He gave me fifty strokes.\"","After speaking, he looked at the blood-stained pad again, and sincerely said, \"Thank you for the reminder and pad, which allowed me to escape this catastrophe.\"","Thinking of this, Mo Jiuye was still terrified.","He was led into the palace, and as He Zhiran reminded him, the emperor called him to meet in the harem.","Recalling He Zhiran's repeated exhortations before leaving, Mo Jiuye refused to enter on the grounds that men were not allowed in the harem.","Seeing that things did not develop according to his plan, the emperor was furious and charged Mo Jiuye with the crime of disobeying orders.","Although disobeying orders was a capital crime, the emperor also knew that punishing Mo Jiuye like this was unreasonable. Once the truth was revealed, he would lose face as the monarch of the country.","However, he didn't want to let Mo Jiuye go just like that. After weighing, he had him beaten 50 strokes.","Not only did Mo Jiuye get 50 less strokes, but He Zhiran's pad also protected him, leaving him with only minor external injuries.","However, to cover up, Mo Jiuye deliberately pretended to be unconscious and was carried back to the Duke of Protector's mansion.","In Mo Jiuye's mind, he felt that He Zhiran might know some other things.","\"Is there anything else happening in your dream?\"","He Zhiran was just waiting for Mo Jiuye to take the initiative to ask. She solemnly said, \"I also dreamed that the Duke of Protector's mansion was searched and exiled.\"","\"Searched and exiled?\" Mo Jiuye widened his eyes, obviously a little shocked.","He Zhiran nodded seriously, \"If the time is not wrong, it will be tomorrow morning.\"","\"Tomorrow morning?\"","\"Yes, tomorrow morning. After the morning court starts, there will be ministers impeaching, and the evidence of your colluding with the enemy and treason that they prepared in advance.\"","For some reason, Mo Jiuye did not doubt He Zhiran's words too much.","After all, there were often some signs before things happened.","Just like being inexplicably summoned to the palace tonight, and then getting 50 strokes.","And there were other things that Mo Jiuye was not completely unaware of.","At this moment, Mo Jiuye had fallen into deep thought.","Whether or not what He Zhiran said would come true, he felt it necessary to make some preparations in advance.","With this thought, Mo Jiuye looked at He Zhiran.","\"Send someone to inform my mother and sisters-in-law now. Just say that I was seriously injured and unconscious when I returned from the imperial palace. They will definitely come back here to see me. I will mention this to them at that time.\"","For some reason, Mo Jiuye strangely believed in this woman he was not very familiar with at this time.","At the same time, he maintained the same attitude towards He Zhiran, preferring to believe it than not, even if it was a waste of effort, it would be better than being caught off guard when things happened."]},{"number":5,"title":"Chapter 5: Born a Mohist, die a Mohist ghost.","paragraphs":["This matter He Zhiran also felt it was necessary to inform them in advance, moreover, Mo Jiuye reminded in person, it would be more convincing than her, a newcomer, speaking.","\"Alright, I'll send someone to invite them over immediately.\"","He Zhiran gave instructions to several servants outside the door to go to the different courtyards to invite people. Then, she returned to the room again.","She asked Mo Jiuye, \"Do you have any good arrangements in mind?\"","\"You and the Sisters-in-law can take the divorce letters and leave.\" At this moment, the only thing Mo Jiuye could think of was that the fewer people involved, the better.","To this, He Zhiran did not refute.","Although she did not have much contact with the eight Sisters-in-law, she could see that they were all kind-hearted people.","It was pitiful enough for them to be widowed at such a young age. Following along to be exiled and suffer, it was indeed unbearable.","As for herself, she did not think too much about it.","She sympathized with the Mo family's fate, and hoped to change Mo Jiuye's fate of early death with her own ability.","Not long after, Old Lady Mo and the Sisters-in-law successively arrived in a hurry.","He Zhiran could see that the concern on everyone's faces for Mo Jiuye did not seem fake.","Old Lady Mo was the first to come to her son's bedside. Although there were tears in her eyes, she still looked tough to others.","\"Jiuye, how are your injuries?\"","\"Mother, your son is fine. They are just some flesh wounds.\"","\"Ninth brother, how did you get injured?\" asked the fourth Sister-in-law in concern.","Mo Jiuye looked around.","\"When all the Sisters-in-law are here, I will tell everyone together.\"","Hearing Mo Jiuye say this, no one asked any more questions. Instead, they sincerely cared about his injuries.","After a while, the few Sisters-in-law who were farther away also arrived.","He Zhiran vigilantly went out and instructed the servants to guard the door well and not allow anyone in.","Mo Jiuye felt very warm at He Zhiran's thoughtfulness. At the same time, he also had a big change in his previous understanding of He Zhiran.","If not for this encounter, perhaps he would have tried to get along well with the other party and spent his whole life with her.","Unfortunately, fate makes fun of people, and the heavens did not give him such a chance.","Mo Jiuye collected his stray thoughts and said in a deep voice, \"Mother, Sisters-in-law, today I was bullied by the Emperor in the palace and was severely beaten 50 times.\"","Hearing this, the Sisters-in-law were completely uneasy.","\"Ninth brother, what exactly did you do wrong that the Emperor would beat you like this?\"","\"That's right, Ninth brother. 50 heavy beatings is no joke. Are your injuries serious?\"","\"Ninth brother...\"","Hearing the string of concerns, even a tough guy like Mo Jiuye felt a warmth in his heart.","Such a harmonious family would probably cease to exist after today.","Although reluctant, he still had to do what he should do.","\"Mother, Sisters-in-law, from today's events, it can be seen that the Emperor can no longer tolerate the existence of my House of Mo. I'm afraid he will soon issue an decree to punish us, either lightly by exile or heavily by beheading.\"","Mo Jiuye deliberately made the matter sound more serious, hoping that those Sisters-in-law would know when to retreat.","Hearing this, the eyes of the eight Sisters-in-law unanimously looked towards He Zhiran.","When they left the bridal chamber earlier, the Ninth brother and sister had reminded them similarly.","At that time, they did not take it seriously, thinking the Ninth siblings were babbling gloom and doom.","However, after hearing such words from Mo Jiuye again, they had to take it seriously.","He Zhiran met those inquisitive eyes and just solemnly nodded slightly to confirm that she was not talking nonsense earlier.","\"Jiuye, are your words true?\" Even the usually calm Old Lady Mo was a little uneasy now.","\"Mother, the chances are eight or nine out of ten.\" Mo Jiuye did not make his words definite, after all, he had only heard it from He Zhiran and combined some of his own analysis.","Hearing this, Old Lady Mo's body shuddered.","\"To think that my Mo family has been loyal and upright for generations, yet in the end the men in the family died for the country, only to get such an outcome?\"","As she spoke, Old Lady Mo even let out a cold laugh.","\"Back then, I advised your father to return to civilian life. What good are fame, fortune and official positions compared to a family living in peace and contentment? But he just refused to listen.","He said the mission of the Mo family is to protect the Great Shun Dynasty. This one sentence of his cost me my husband and eight sons.","So what if we used our lives to guard the Great Shun's lands?","Hah... What a joke...\"","The eight Sisters-in-law were also filled with righteous indignation.","\"This is too much. What wrong did our Mo family do to deserve this?\"","\"I do not accept this. I will go back to my maiden home now and ask my father to help say some good words.\"","\"I will also find my elder brother to see if he can help.\"","Mo Jiuye shook his head.","\"Sisters-in-law, just give up! The Emperor is determined to eradicate the Mo family. How could he possibly listen to advice?\"","\"Then what should we do? Are we just going to wait for someone to arbitrarily pin a crime on us?\" Seventh Sister-in-law Yang Man asked indignantly.","Mo Jiuye did not answer, but looked towards Old Lady Mo instead.","\"Mother, your son thinks it'd be better to take this opportunity to give the Sisters-in-law divorce letters, rather than letting them be implicated along with our Mo family.\"","Old Lady Mo pondered for a moment, then said solemnly, \"Hmm, what Jiuye said makes sense. You Sisters-in-law are already pitiful enough. Our Mo family should not continue to implicate you all. And the same for the Hes. Having just married in, it would be unjust for her to be implicated along with the Mo family.\"","\"Mother, Ninth brother, I do not want a divorce letter. I, Cui Biteng, was born as a Mo, and I will die as the Mo's ghost.\"","\"Me too. Even if the entire Mo family is executed, I, Xie Fang, will keep the Mo company till the end.\"","\"I also do not want a divorce letter. I will stay and live and die with the Mo family.\"","\"I promised my late husband that no matter what, I will be filial to his mother on his behalf.\"","\"I'm not leaving either.\"","\"...\"","The eight Mo widows were filled with righteous indignation, and none were willing to leave with a divorce letter.","Even if it was the only way out, they did not want it. They were determined to live and die with the Mo family.","Seeing that the eight daughters-in-law could be like this, Old Lady Mo was moved. At the same time, her gaze turned to He Zhiran.","\"Young Lady He, what about you?\"","\"I want to stay too.\" He Zhiran answered loudly without even thinking.","Old Lady Mo looked at Mo Jiuye again, \"Jiuye, you see, the women of our family are all strong-willed. Mother also wants to gratify them.\"","Hearing this, Mo Jiuye solemnly looked at everyone. There was a sense of admiration in his eyes.","\"Sisters-in-law, we only have one life. If one can live, who would choose to die? I hope you all do not let your sense of righteousness get the better of you in this matter.\"","\"Ninth brother, my mind is set. Please do not say any more.\"","Led by the Eldest Sister-in-law, the other Sisters-in-law made the same choice again.","Old Lady Mo knew the temperaments of these daughters-in-law very well. Although there might be some minor friction when everyone was together on normal days, none would become deserters at the critical moment.","This was how the Mo women should be."]},{"number":6,"title":"Chapter 6: Is All this about you","paragraphs":["“Given this, Jiuye and I will not talk about this matter anymore. The most important thing now is that we have to make preparations in advance.”","“Mother, if it really is a massacre of the entire household, we can only accept our fate. If it is exile, we must have money on hand if we don't want to starve to death on the road.”","“Mother, I have three hundred taels in my private funds. As long as we are frugal on the road, it should be enough.” Sixth Sister-in-law said first.","When it came to private funds, Eighth Sister-in-law was somewhat lacking in confidence.","“Mother, you also know that I am the kind of person who likes to eat well, so I used all the monthly silver to buy snacks. However, I still have some decent jewelry that should be able to be exchanged for some silver.”","“I also have some valuable items that I will convert entirely into banknotes to take with me.”","Listening to the sisters-in-law saying something in turn, actively reporting their own property.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran couldn't help but glance at each other.","Both of them knew very well that although the sisters-in-law had some private funds, these things were different from banknotes. How could the emperor possibly let them take them away openly?","If so, wouldn't the family be ransacked in vain when they were confiscated?","\"Dear sisters-in-law, I know you are all well-intentioned. It's already reached this point, and there’s no time left to exchange those things for banknotes.\"","Mo Jiuye's words were like a basin of cold water poured over the eight sisters-in-law.","The women were at a loss all of a sudden.","\"Ninth younger brother, then what should we do? The things in our hands may not be worth much money, but we certainly don't want to give them away cheaply to those bastards.\" In her anxiety, Sixth Sister-in-law actually swore.","Regarding this point, Mo Jiuye had also considered it, but he had not been able to come up with a good solution either.","Just when everyone didn't know what to do, He Zhiran spoke up.","\"Mother, dear sisters-in-law, I suggest that everyone sew a pocket close to the body and pad some cotton to wrap up the banknotes and put them in it.","Cotton is relatively soft. Even if someone searches you, they may not be able to feel it. As for other items, everyone can slowly think of ways during the remaining time.\"","Old Lady Mo agreed: \"Well, He’s suggestion makes sense. Let's do as she said. Everyone should go back and prepare now.\"","In principle, after the mother-in-law had spoken, they should immediately go back and do things. However, the imperial physician had not yet come to see Mo Jiuye's injuries, and they were still worried about Mo Jiuye's condition and didn't want to go back.","In normal times, Old Lady Mo felt pity for these daughters-in-law who had no husbands, and would not easily put on the posture of a mother-in-law to them.","Now that the situation was urgent, it was not the time to indulge them.","So Old Lady Mo said coldly, \"Don't just stand there stunned, hurry back and get ready.\"","Seeing this, the eight sisters-in-law could only leave one after another.","After seeing these people leave, Old Lady Mo's gaze fell back to Mo Jiuye again.","\"How long has it been since someone went out to invite the imperial physician? My daughters-in-law and I have been here for almost an hour, yet the imperial physician still hasn't arrived.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, the little servants who had gone out to invite the imperial physician came back one after another to report.","The news they brought back was the excuses those imperial physicians gave for not being able to come and treat Mo Jiuye's injuries.","Counting on her fingers, He Zhiran could figure out the intricacies. It was nothing more than the emperor deliberately instructing the imperial physicians to do so, not wanting Mo Jiuye to recover, or even to let him leave the capital alive.","Facing such things, Mo Jiuye seemed to have predicted it already. He did not show any abnormality.","However, in order to reassure his mother, he still said, \"Mother, my injury is not serious. You don't need to worry.\"","Old Lady Mo was not a person without foresight either. Things had reached this point, even if she was worried about her son's injury, there was nothing she could do.","Moreover, looking at Mo Jiuye's current state, there should be no major issues.","\"Since this is the case, I will go back and prepare as well.\"","In any case, Mo Jiuye had after all suffered fifty heavy blows. It was still somewhat difficult for him to walk on the ground.","He Zhiran took the initiative to send Old Lady Mo out of the courtyard.","After returning to the room, taking advantage of her sleeve to cover her actions, she took out two slave contracts from her space.","One was Qiao Yu's, and the other was another accompanying maid's.","\"The emperor ordered the Marquis’s mansion to be exiled. They certainly won't be allowed to bring their servants with them on the road. I plan to return the slave contracts and set them free.\"","Mo Jiuye did not object to this, because he had thought of doing the same.","\"Well, it's fine if you think it's appropriate.\"","Just as Mo Jiuye wanted to say something more, a guard ran in to report in a fluster.","\"Reporting to Marquis, the mansion's warehouse has been robbed, and it was completely cleaned out, leaving only empty shelves.\"","As soon as the guard finished speaking, Eldest Sister-in-law and Second Sister-in-law also rushed over in a panic.","\"Ninth younger brother, eldest sister-in-law and I went to the kitchen to prepare some dry rations, but unexpectedly, everything in the kitchen was gone.\"","\"Ninth younger brother, our mansion must have been burglarized.\"","Hearing Eldest Sister-in-law say that thieves had broken into the mansion, He Zhiran felt a little guilty. After all, she was the \"thief\" they were talking about.","However, she soon let it go. She didn't really want to steal anything. She did this entirely for everyone's benefit.","Hearing this, Mo Jiuye was also confused.","Although the Marquis’s mansion was about to fall into the plight of being ransacked and exiled, it hadn't happened yet.","The guards were patrolling normally. Not to mention stealing the warehouse clean, even if they casually stole some small items, there would not have been no movement at all.","His intuition told him that this matter must be related to He Zhiran.","After all, this woman's actions were too puzzling.","He waved his hand at the guard: \"You can go down first. I will personally investigate this matter.\"","\"Ninth younger brother, what about the theft in the kitchen?\" Eldest Sister-in-law asked again.","Mo Jiuye helplessly answered, \"Eldest sister-in-law, it's fine whether the things are lost or not. We can't take them anyway, it's better to give them to the little thief than to fill the coffers of our enemy.\"","Eldest Sister-in-law seemed to agree very much with Mo Jiuye's words. She solemnly nodded, \"What ninth younger brother said also makes sense. Since this is the case, second sister-in-law and I will get busy.\"","After seeing the two sisters-in-law off, only Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran remained in the room.","Mo Jiuye's deep gaze remained fixed on He Zhiran.","Facing his sharp eyes, He Zhiran did not show a trace of timidity.","After a long time, Mo Jiuye asked in a deep voice, \"Are you related to all these things?\"","On the surface, this was a question, but it contained an affirmative meaning.","Even with her experience cultivating an unmoved attitude toward favor and disgrace in her previous life, He Zhiran still felt somewhat at a loss being asked this way.","Not for anything else, from Mo Jiuye's tone, she could completely determine that the other party had already concluded it was her doing.","When encountering this kind of thing, how should she break it?","He Zhiran really didn't know how to explain for a moment.","Although historical records described Mo Jiuye as upright, after all, they were not even familiar with each other. How could she tell the other person that she had a space!"]},{"number":7,"title":"Chapter 7: Taking You to a Richer Place","paragraphs":["Just as He Zhiran was hesitating about how to gloss over this matter, Mo Jiuye spoke again.","\"Everyone has secrets, if you don't want to say, I won't force you. The situation of my Mo Family is bad enough already, my mother and sisters-in-law are all pitiful people, I only hope that you don't have any crooked ideas.\"","When faced with such an inscrutable person, Mo Jiuye didn't dare gamble, nor did he want to gamble. He alone was easy to handle, but he couldn't use the lives of his whole family as gambling chips.","He only hoped that his heartfelt words could move He Zhiran. If she really harbored malicious intentions, Mo Jiuye hoped that for the sake of his pitiful sisters-in-law, she would let them off.","Regarding Mo Jiuye's suspicions, He Zhiran could completely understand. After all, her own behavior was too astonishing, if Mo Jiuye didn't doubt her, it would make one even more uneasy.","\"I don't harbor malice towards the Mo Family, please rest assured on this point.\"","After looking at Mo Jiuye, she had already opened up to him after all, so He Zhiran felt that she could also tentatively reveal some of her background.","The exile journey would be long, and there would definitely come a day when she would need to take out the supplies she had stored in her space. She couldn't keep racking her brains for excuses every time.","She wanted to help Mo Jiuye escape this disaster, but didn't want to spend all her energy on figuring out excuses.","Moreover, with Mo Jiuye's astuteness, trying to deceive him would not be an easy task.","After pondering for a while, He Zhiran tentatively said:","\"Everyone has secrets, I have them, and I believe you do too. I just said that I don't harbor malice towards the Mo Family, so I hope you can respect me and not pry into my secrets.","I can also honestly tell you that the theft at the Duke's Mansion is indeed related to me. On one hand, I didn't want those things to fall into the hands of enemies, on the other hand, having some supplies on hand will make the exile journey easier.\"","He Zhiran stopped speaking there, she had already said enough.","If Mo Jiuye still stubbornly kept asking, she could only choose to leave this place.","He Zhiran believed that with her own capabilities, no matter where she went, she could live a carefree life. There was no need to stay here offering goodwill, only to be doubted.","As for the lives of the entire Mo Family, she would be powerless to help anyway...","After a long time, Mo Jiuye finally spoke heavily: \"I promise you I won't pry into your secrets anymore.\"","His intuition told him that this woman wasn't lying.","Moreover, the things she did were all to help the Duke's Mansion, and didn't have any intention of kicking a man when he is down.","As for how she carried away so many supplies, even if Mo Jiuye was very curious, he endured and didn't ask again.","The two temporarily reached a consensus, and the wedding chamber fell into silence for a time.","After a long while, Mo Jiuye tentatively asked: \"Since you have the ability to silently clear out the storeroom, if I take you to an even richer place, can you empty it out?\"","He Zhiran's eyes lit up when she heard an even richer place.","Although her space was already filled with all kinds of items, many were useless accumulated things.","After exile, who knew what kind of emergencies they would encounter, having more silver and money in hand was the most important.","She also believed in Mo Jiuye's integrity. Since he had promised not to pry into her secrets anymore, then he definitely wouldn't ask again.","As long as he didn't ask, even if she used her space in a turn-a-blind-eye manner it would be fine.","At least she wouldn't have to be overly cautious about it.","\"Where do you want to take me?\"","Hearing her tone, Mo Jiuye knew that this woman had agreed.","\"I plan to rob the National Treasury. As long as you can take the things away, I'll handle the entry.\"","\"National Treasury?\"","He Zhiran was somewhat shocked. She never imagined that Mo Jiuye's appetite was even bigger than hers, and had actually set his sights on emptying out the National Treasury.","It was just that her space was too small, it definitely couldn't hold that much wealth.","Seeing He Zhiran's hesitation, Mo Jiuye asked: \"What's wrong? You don't dare?\"","\"What's there for me not to dare? I was just thinking, with so many things in the National Treasury, how to store them.\"","\"Store them?\" Mo Jiuye couldn't help but ask.","He Zhiran quickly reacted: \"You said you wouldn't ask.\"","\"Sorry, I overstepped.\" Mo Jiuye was frank, and immediately apologized to He Zhiran.","He Zhiran's consciousness entered her space, and glanced at the time, it was already two in the morning.","The time of the decree to ransack their home and exile was drawing nearer and nearer.","\"Wait a moment.\"","After speaking, she turned and left the room, heading straight for the ear chamber.","Her consciousness entered her space, and He Zhiran reluctantly took out all the unimportant items, piling them all over the floor of the ear chamber.","Although reluctant, thinking about exchanging these things for the treasures in the National Treasury, she became reconciled.","Returning to the wedding chamber, she looked at Mo Jiuye still sitting on the wedding bed: \"Can you still walk?\"","Mo Jiuye nimbly got up and put on his shoes. His inadvertent frown had already given away his pain at the moment.","He Zhiran said with concern: \"I know some medical skills, why don't I take a look at you first?\"","Mo Jiuye declined: \"It's nothing, we have to hurry.\"","After speaking, he nimbly opened the wardrobe and took out two night raid outfits.","He threw one set to He Zhiran for her to change into, and put on the other set himself.","These clothes belonged to Mo Jiuye. Although a bit big on He Zhiran, they didn't affect her movement.","Mo Jiuye casually grabbed the soft sword hanging on the wall, and pulled He Zhiran to jump out the window together.","He Zhiran's feet had just touched the ground when she felt her body become airborne again.","The great hero praised by later generations was indeed well-deserved, his lightness skill was so incredible.","She saw him leap a few times, and they had already jumped out of the Duke's Mansion's perimeter.","He Zhiran considered her own skills in her previous life to be not bad, but she had only learned some close combat techniques. Compared to the real martial arts before her eyes, she was probably lacking more than just a little.","While He Zhiran was admiring Mo Jiuye's martial arts on her own, Mo Jiuye had already brought her to land in a somewhat dilapidated courtyard.","He Zhiran was full of disbelief, and softly asked: \"You're saying the National Treasury is here?\"","Mo Jiuye didn't answer, but led her into a room in the corner instead.","He adeptly walked to a fire kang that looked like it would collapse at any moment, and moved aside some bricks. A bottomless black hole appeared before the two.","Mo Jiuye softly explained: \"This is the secret passage to the National Treasury.\"","He Zhiran really wanted to ask how he knew about this place, but remembering that she had just asked the other party not to pry into her secrets, she should also be able to do the same.","Therefore, the question that was about to slip out was swallowed back in an instant.","Following closely behind Mo Jiuye's footsteps, they entered the cave entrance.","Mo Jiuye didn't seem unfamiliar with this place at all. Although it was pitch black and nothing could be seen, he could walk without needing to feel his way at all."]},{"number":8,"title":"Chapter 8: Burning the Treasury","paragraphs":["After walking for about ten minutes, Mo Jiuye raised his hand and opened a trapdoor above his head. Suddenly everything became bright and the two of them appeared inside the National Treasury.","The National Treasury was just that, not only large in area but also filled with a dazzling array of objects that all appeared to be of considerable value.","Especially the two Night Pearls that lit up the entire storeroom as bright as daylight, they could nearly blind someone.","\"Time is limited, move faster.\" Seeing He Zhiran's eyes wandering everywhere, Mo Jiuye had to remind her.","He Zhiran now felt like a country bumpkin who had never seen the world, everything here seemed so nice to her.","She also understood clearly that now was not the time for her to be sightseeing.","\"I want you to look away for a bit.\"","Of course Mo Jiuye understood her meaning, she just didn't want him to see her methods.","\"Alright.\" Without any hesitation, Mo Jiuye opened a trapdoor in the floor and went down inside.","Only after seeing the trapdoor close up completely without even a crack did He Zhiran start looking around for good stuff.","After all, the amount of space that could hold objects was limited. With so many things in the National Treasury, it was impossible for her to take everything.","After quickly surveying the area, He Zhiran used her mind to gather all the silver notes, silver ingots, gold and silver jewelry etc. into her space.","Then she used her mind again to check inside the space, and as expected, just these things had nearly filled up all the space.","However, she was not satisfied.","Thus He Zhiran used her mind to arrange the objects more compactly, piling all the smaller items in the kitchen and bathroom, freeing up some more space.","Calculating the area, she took some more paintings and calligraphy that didn't take up much space, as well as several large boxes of copper coins, all into the space.","Checking the space again, He Zhiran was also intoxicated.","Right now the space was packed full, with just enough room for her to enter left.","Even though she was unwilling, He Zhiran knew she could take no more.","However, she absolutely could not let those two bright Night Pearls go.","After taking the Night Pearls into her space, the National Treasury immediately darkened.","He Zhiran knocked on the trapdoor, \"I'm done, we can go now.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, the trapdoor opened from inside.","He Zhiran supported Mo Jiuye's shoulder as they went back down into the secret chamber.","She turned and looked at the somewhat disordered National Treasury that she had left behind, then immediately had a thought.","\"Too many things, I can't take it all. Many silks and satins still remain.\"","\"You mean?\" Mo Jiuye seemed to guess her intentions.","Taking advantage of the night, He Zhiran used her mind to take out a bottle of alcohol from her space and sprinkled it around inside the National Treasury.","Mo Jiuye was also very cooperative. After the alcohol was sprinkled, he immediately took out a match from his clothes and lit it, tossing it inside.","The alcohol met the fire and the National Treasury instantly became a fiery inferno.","Mo Jiuye pulled He Zhiran away quickly, fleeing the scene...","Although neither of them said anything, they both felt extremely gratified at setting the National Treasury on fire.","Especially Mo Jiuye, he now felt as if he had gotten revenge for some huge grievance.","He even wanted to personally see the Emperor's furious reaction when he found out the National Treasury was burned.","After succesfully returning to the Duke of Protector's Estate, the two of them changed out of their night clothes, and Mo Jiuye went back to bed.","The observant He Zhiran immediately noticed the bloodstains on the floor.","\"You're bleeding, I have to help treat your wounds.\"","Never underestimate surface wounds. In her previous life, how many people died from infections because their wounds weren't properly treated?","She had already done her utmost to save the lives of everyone in the Duke of Protector's Estate, how could she let Mo Jiuye be in danger from such a minor injury?","\"No, my wounds are nothing serious.\"","In fact, Mo Jiuye was very clear himself about the severity of his injuries. Although he had some padding as protection, after all he had been given fifty heavy strikes, the wounds couldn't be too light no matter what.","It was just that when he thought about where he was injured, on his buttocks, he felt awkward about letting He Zhiran look.","In He Zhiran's mindset, patients were genderless.","Therefore, she had no hesitation at all about reaching out to lift Mo Jiuye's clothes.","Mo Jiuye instinctively shied away.","\"No, it's not appropriate for a woman to look at where I'm injured.\"","Only then did He Zhiran react that in ancient times, saying this to someone with deep-rooted feudal ideas was like pouring oil on a fire.","Mo Jiuye stared at her speechlessly, temporarily at a loss for words.","After all, what she said made sense, they were already husband and wife.","But could a woman say something like this so casually?","Thinking of this, Mo Jiuye became even more curious about He Zhiran.","What kind of mentality allowed her to say these things so calmly?","While Mo Jiuye was lost in thought, He Zhiran had already efficiently lifted his outer robe.","The two had just married yesterday, so Mo Jiuye was dressed inside and out in bright red.","Even so, after lifting his robe, the sight that met her eyes still shocked He Zhiran.","She could see that Mo Jiuye's bright red underpants were already soaked with blood, the red fabric dyed a dark crimson.","Thinking of how just earlier Mo Jiuye had still carried her to sneak into the National Treasury, just how strong was this man's willpower to persevere for so long?","Considering this, He Zhiran's respect for Mo Jiuye grew even more.","Seeing that he couldn't prevail over He Zhiran, Mo Jiuye could only awkwardly turn his head away to face the wall with eyes closed, taking on a resigned posture.","Seeing that Mo Jiuye's gaze couldn't see her, He Zhiran calmly took out a bottle of alcohol from her space.","But then, she made a startling discovery.","If she remembered correctly, there were originally three bottles of alcohol in her space. She had used one bottle to burn the treasury, so there should have been two bottles left.","However, she had just discovered that the amount of alcohol didn't seem to have decreased at all, there were still three bottles.","She didn't dare to confirm for sure right now if her space had a regenerative function.","However, she carefully checked the alcohol in her space and confirmed there were two bottles. She would check again after helping treat Mo Jiuye's wounds. If it changed to three bottles, it meant she had discovered a new function of her space.","Coming back to herself, He Zhiran also took out forceps, cotton pads and other items from her space. She gently removed Mo Jiuye's pants.","The wounds were shocking to look at, even He Zhiran, who was used to seeing all kinds of injuries, was no exception."]},{"number":9,"title":"Chapter 9: If I were alive, I would be responsible for you.","paragraphs":["It can be imagined how strong-willed this man was. With such injuries, if it were anyone else, not to mention taking her to empty the national treasury, they probably wouldn’t even dare to move an inch.","Mo Jiuye's skin had turned purplish-blue, with several open wounds still oozing bright red blood.","Moreover, the injured area was extremely large, with almost no good spots left on his buttocks and thighs.","It was evident how merciless the person who administered the punishment was.","Mo Jiuye suddenly felt a chill as he instinctively reached down to pull up his pants.","Due to her profession, He Zhiran instantly transformed into a professional doctor with a strong sense of occupational ethics.","Her voice was stern yet uncompromising.","\"Don't move.\"","Hearing this, Mo Jiuye's hand that had just grabbed his waistband instantly froze in place.","He Zhiran peeled his hand away without hesitation.","\"Although you didn't injure any bones, these injuries are still not minor. Don't underestimate external injuries, or they can also be fatal if not treated promptly.\"","Listening to her nagging on like an old lady, Mo Jiuye finally resigned himself and retracted his hand.","He closed his eyes and allowed He Zhiran to treat his wounds.","He Zhiran worked skillfully. First, she poured some alcohol on a cotton ball, then used forceps to hold the cotton ball and gently dab Mo Jiuye's wounds.","\"It will hurt a little, bear with it.\"","\"Mm.\" It did hurt somewhat, but to Mo Jiuye, this was nothing.","After disinfecting the wounds, He Zhiran took out a package of Yunnan Baiyao powder from her spatial ring. This medicine worked best for Mo Jiuye’s injuries.","She gently and evenly sprinkled the medicinal powder on Mo Jiuye's wounds. Her fingers inadvertently brushed against his skin.","This sensation made Mo Jiuye's body involuntarily shudder. At the same time, he was acutely aware that his face felt like it was on fire.","He Zhiran was fully focused on treating Mo Jiuye's wounds and didn't notice his reaction. By now, she had finished bandaging the wounds.","She nimbly gave him a tetanus shot as well.","Mo Jiuye suddenly felt a stinging pain in his arm, like a needle prick, and his body instinctively tried to avoid it.","\"Don't move,\" He Zhiran reminded him.","Mo Jiuye's body instantly froze until the needle prick sensation disappeared, and only then did he breathe a sigh of relief.","After taking care of these things, He Zhiran looked towards Mo Jiuye's bloodstained underwear.","\"Where are your clothes? I'll go get you a clean pair of pants.\"","Mo Jiuye knew his face was flushed, and didn't dare turn his head when asked.","\"My clothes are in the cabinet on the left.\"","He Zhiran randomly grabbed a pair of white underwear from the cabinet and placed them on the bed. She then went to take off the pants she had already pulled down to Mo Jiuye's knee hollows.","Mo Jiuye quickly stopped her, \"I'll do it myself.\"","He was embarrassed enough already. If he let this woman help change his pants, wouldn't he have to find a crack in the ground and burrow into it?","He Zhiran didn't think much about matters like these. After all, she had undressed countless patients in her previous life.","\"Your wounds have just been treated, you shouldn't move around. What if they start bleeding again? My efforts would go to waste.\"","Mo Jiuye still insisted, \"Men and women should not have physical contact. How could I let you help me change pants?\"","Hearing this, He Zhiran couldn't help laughing out loud. She no longer held back when she spoke, disregarding Mo Jiuye's feelings.","\"I've already seen every inch of your butt, so what's the difference in just changing your pants?\"","Mo Jiuye...","He now felt as if there was a huge boulder blocking his chest, nearly suffocating him.","This woman really had no filter, dredging up past events however she pleased.","But thinking about it, she was not wrong either. His butt had been exposed here for half a day already. If he kept refusing in this situation, it would seem somewhat pretentious.","\"Cough cough... If I live through this, I will definitely take responsibility for you.\"","In Mo Jiuye's mind, this was equivalent to him having physical intimacy with He Zhiran. As an upright man, he absolutely could not let the woman suffer any loss because of him.","Hearing his words, He Zhiran couldn't help laughing again.","However, she tried to restrain her laughter to prevent the servants outside from hearing.","\"Hahaha... Don't take it so seriously, okay? I'm treating your injuries purely out of a doctor's basic ethics. Don't think about responsibility or anything like that.\"","To be honest, He Zhiran had never considered her future with Mo Jiuye.","Although she admired this hero, the two had only just met. There was no feeling between them whatsoever.","To He Zhiran, a soul from the modern world, she only wanted Mo Jiuye to survive the exile journey.","As for anything else, she would let nature take its course.","It could be said that He Zhiran was quite rational in her attitude towards her relationship with Mo Jiuye. She would not blindly accept this marriage that did not originally belong to her just because the other party was her idol and hero.","Of course, if the two developed feelings for each other through their interactions, she would also try dating Mo Jiuye until both felt that the other was their destined partner. Only then would being together seem natural.","But now was not the time to consider such things. The long exile road still lay ahead, and she needed to think about how to cope.","After restraining her laughter, He Zhiran carefully helped Mo Jiuye into his pants.","Once the pant legs were pulled up, Mo Jiuye refused any more help from He Zhiran.","\"I can do the rest myself.\"","He Zhiran did not insist. He could even walk on roofs and walls, carefully pulling up his pants should be no problem.","Before Mo Jiuye turned over, she quickly stored the medical supplies in her space ring.","She also took stock of the alcohol quantity. This made He Zhiran instantly delighted to find there were three bottles left.","Even the Yunnan Baiyao powder, gauze, tetanus medication, disposable syringes and forceps she had just used were all restored to their original amounts.","What was even more exciting was that the number of forceps had increased by one.","What did this mean?","It meant that the original items in her space ring did have a replenishing function.","Of course, those things she had tossed in during ancient times did not replenish, since the items she left in her ear space were gone.","Even so, He Zhiran was very satisfied.","With this feature, she felt her backbone straighten quite a bit.","Because her space ring contained much more than just these simple medical supplies.","She knew now was not the time for joy. Time was tight and she still had many things to handle.","Thinking of this, He Zhiran took out the two indenture contracts and walked out again.","Qiao Yu had been waiting at the door. Seeing her emerge, she hurriedly asked respectfully, \"Miss, is there anything your servant can do for you?\"","\"Qiao Yu, go to your room. I have something to discuss with you and Qiao Xin.\"","After speaking, He Zhiran immediately headed towards the maids' room.","Qiao Yu had served the young miss for many years but had never seen her be so formal. She quickly fell in step behind her.","At the same time, her heart thumped anxiously.","Judging by the young miss's demeanor, there must be some important matter at hand."]},{"number":10,"title":"Chapter 10: Someone Poisoned","paragraphs":["He Zhiran's two maidservants who were marrying into the family lived in one room. Today it was Qiao Yu's turn on duty, and Qiao Xin had already gone to sleep early.","The sound of the door opening woke up Qiao Xin. She thought it was Qiao Yu who had come back, and blurrily asked, \"Qiao Yu, why are you back so early?\"","\"It's me,\" He Zhiran spoke to clear up her confusion.","Qiao Xin immediately sat up in surprise and hurriedly put on her shoes and got out of bed. \"Miss, do you have any orders?\"","\"He Zhiran did not want to waste time and directly placed two slave contracts on the table.","\"Take these slave contracts and leave the Duke's Mansion tonight. From today on, you are free. \"","The two of them did not understand why the young miss was staging this play.","\"Miss, where did Qiao Xin do wrong? You can beat or scold me as you wish.\"","\"Yes Miss, Qiao Yu also wants to serve you for a lifetime.\"","He Zhiran knew these two maids were extremely loyal to her.","She said helplessly, \"The Duke has just returned and said he has incurred the wrath of The Emperor. If nothing unexpected happens, The Emperor will punish the Duke's Mansion.","By then, we will all be in danger, how can we still care about whether you live or die?","It would be better for me to free you now than for you to be resold by the officials.\"","As she spoke, He Zhiran used her sleeve to cover up and took out forty taels of silver, giving each of them twenty taels.","The two little maids did not expect that the reason the Miss was letting them go was this. They could not accept this fact for a while.","After all, the thought of serving by the Miss's side for a lifetime had already taken deep root.","\"Miss, Qiao Xin is not leaving.\"","\"Qiao Yu is not leaving either.\"","In the past, He Zhiran would have slowly explained to them bit by bit, but at this moment, she did not have so much energy and time to do so.","\"This matter does not allow for your opposition. Pack up now and I will send someone to take you out of the mansion after a quarter of an hour.\"","\"Miss...\"","Seeing that Qiao Yu still wanted to say something, He Zhiran raised her hand to stop her, \"That's enough, no need to say more.\"","After letting the two maids go, Mo Jiuye was also not idle on his side.","After He Zhiran left, he called over several capable young servants who often served around him and freed them in the same way.","As for the rest of the servants in the Duke's Mansion, it would depend on his mother and sisters-in-law's own decisions.","After sending away all these servants whose slave contracts were returned, the sky was already bright.","He Zhiran glanced at the clock in the room, it was already past five in the morning.","He Zhiran had emptied the kitchen of the Duke's Mansion, and later wanted to move the goods from the treasury, so she piled all the space-occupying kitchen utensils in the ear room.","Fortunately, Old Lady Mo's courtyard had a small kitchen.","Even if they really had to be exiled, they had to be full before leaving. So Old Lady Mo directly ordered people to cook porridge in her own small kitchen.","The porridge was already cooked at this time, and an elderly maid came to the bridal chamber to invite them to come eat breakfast.","As for He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye greeting the mother-in-law on the first day of their wedding, it was completely ignored.","He Zhiran looked at Mo Jiuye who was still lying on the bed, \"Are you going to your mother's to have breakfast?\"","Mo Jiuye shook his head, \"I won't go. I'll keep pretending to be in a coma.\"","He Zhiran knew Mo Jiuye's actions were right.","Since The Emperor had chosen to summon him to the palace for harassment last night, wasn't it to make him suffer severe injuries and die on the way to exile?","If he went out hale and hearty, when The Emperor found out, he might come up with other ways to deal with the Mo family.","It was better to pretend to be in a coma to avoid potential harm.","\"I'll go over first to take a look and bring some food back for you.\"","After speaking, He Zhiran followed the old maid to Old Lady Mo's courtyard.","The Mo family were all very proper people. The sisters-in-law and young aunts had already gone to the old madam's courtyard first.","All the women were neatly seated at the dining table in the living room, and no one would pick up their chopsticks until Old Lady Mo spoke.","Old Lady Mo was thinking that they would start eating after Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran came, so that everyone could eat together.","After all, it was also the first day of her son's wedding, so it had to be somewhat formal.","Seeing that only He Zhiran came over, and not knowing the impending disaster facing the Mo family, Mo Hanyue warmly came out to greet her.","She smiled brightly and linked arms with He Zhiran, \"Sister-in-law, why didn't my ninth brother come with you?\"","Seeing Mo Hanyue's state, she clearly did not know what was going on in the family.","He Zhiran simply continued to conceal it, \"Your ninth brother returned late from the palace last night and has just fallen asleep.\"","This explanation did not make Mo Hanyue suspicious at all.","\"Ninth brother worked hard, let him sleep a little longer. Sister-in-law, come quickly, let's eat breakfast.\"","Old Lady Mo and the other sisters-in-law knew what was going on and did not ask like Mo Hanyue.","However, everyone's faces did not look very good.","When Old Lady Mo saw He Zhiran come to the table, she personally welcomed her to sit down.","\"Young Lady He, you also know the situation in the family. It's the first day of your wedding, and there's not much preparation. Let's make do with plain rice porridge first.\"","\"Mother, this is already very good.\"","As she spoke, He Zhiran sat down next to Mo Hanyue.","Looking at the bowl of rice porridge in front of her, she immediately frowned.","\"Mother, sisters-in-law, who prepared this porridge?\"","Old Lady Mo picked up the bowl, and was about to take a sip of the rice porridge when she heard He Zhiran ask, so she put it down again.","\"It was prepared by the maid in my courtyard. What's wrong?\"","\"Mother, sisters-in-law, there is poison in this porridge.\"","Hearing this, the sisters-in-law and Mo Hanyue also hurriedly put down their porridge bowls, and their gazes fell on He Zhiran together.","\"Young Lady He, you said there is poison in the porridge?\" Old Lady Mo looked incredulous.","He Zhiran affirmed, \"Mother, if I'm not mistaken, this is a lethal poison called Ascend to Heaven. Anyone who takes it will have no chance of survival.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, a maid ran in panic, \"Old Madam, something bad has happened. Chen Granny and Cui Maid suddenly collapsed on the ground foaming at the mouth after drinking a sip of water...\"","\"What did you say?\" Old Lady Mo hurriedly got up and walked out with small steps.","\"Where are they?\"","\"Replying to Old Madam, they are both in the ear room!\"","The sisters-in-law and He Zhiran followed Old Lady Mo to the ear room.","Sure enough, the two people Chen Granny mentioned were lying on the ground with foaming mouths, convulsing all over, with eyeballs rolling back, looking like they were about to die.","Old Lady Mo checked and turned to look at He Zhiran.","\"Indeed someone has poisoned them.\""]},{"number":11,"title":"Chapter 11: Thanks to the nine brothers and sisters, we were able to avoid this.","paragraphs":["He Zhiran had already analyzed the situation when he heard the report from Granny Chen.","The two maidservants were poisoned by drinking water, and there was a high possibility that the porridge on their table was also poisoned. It was very likely that someone had poisoned the well.","\"Mother, where does the water in the small kitchen come from?\"","\"It comes from the well behind our courtyard.\"","Without much thought, He Zhiran quickly walked towards the location of the well.","As soon as she brought up a bucket of water, she lightly touched it with her fingers, then rubbed her fingertips and carefully sniffed the odor.","Everyone watched He Zhiran's almost seamless actions, holding their breaths.","It wasn't until she placed the wooden bucket aside that Old Lady Mo asked, \"Is the water poisoned?\"","He Zhiran looked extremely serious and said, \"The poison comes from this well.\"","Upon hearing this, Old Lady Mo immediately frowned.","Although the Marquis's Mansion was about to face an unjust disaster, she, as the mistress of the household, still maintained her authority.","\"Someone, go investigate immediately. I want to know who is behind this poisoning.\"","The maidservants in the courtyard immediately took action, and not long after, someone came to report.","\"Old Lady, Granny Liu hanged herself in her room.\"","Old Lady Mo, followed by the masters of the household, walked towards the servants' quarters.","They saw Granny Liu's lifeless body hanging from the beam, already dead.","Old Lady Mo ordered them to take down Granny Liu's body.","Upon seeing everything in front of her, He Zhiran's first reaction was that Granny Liu was most likely driven to suicide out of fear.","If that were the case, the person behind it must be an enemy of the Marquis's Mansion.","In the historical records, besides the Emperor's fear of the Mo family, there was no mention of anyone else holding a grudge against them.","However, since the Emperor had already planned to exile the Mo family, there was no need for someone to come and poison them.","So, who could be the person behind this?","Just as she was wondering, Old Lady Mo had already displayed her authority as the mistress of the household and ordered someone to search Granny Liu's body and her residence.","There was nothing on Granny Liu's body except a few copper coins.","However, a small paper packet was found in a corner of her bedding.","The servants brought the small paper packet to Old Lady Mo.","Old Lady Mo took the small paper packet and carefully opened it in front of everyone.","The packet was empty, but the residue of a white powder on the paper indicated that it once contained some kind of medicine.","If it were in the past, Old Lady Mo would definitely have called for a doctor to examine it.","However, tonight was different. Mo Jiuye was beaten so badly last night that they couldn't even bring a doctor. It would be futile to call for one now.","Just as she was contemplating how to handle the situation, He Zhiran stepped forward.","\"Mother, I have learned some medical skills. Why don't you let me take a look?\"","Old Lady Mo looked at He Zhiran, hesitated for a moment, and then handed the small paper packet to her.","\"This is likely poison. Be careful.\"","He Zhiran took the small paper packet, first sniffed it under her nose, then rubbed a bit on her fingertips.","Then, she looked up at Old Lady Mo and said, \"Mother, this is the poison that was thrown into the well.\"","Old Lady Mo clenched her fists upon hearing the words. \"Liu, who served by my side when she was young, I always thought I treated her well. Why would she do such a thing?\"","\"Mother, there must be someone behind Liu, manipulating her,\" He Zhiran interjected, reminding her.","\"Who could hate the Mo family so much as to orchestrate this?\" Old Lady Mo couldn't figure out who was behind it all.","However, she was well aware that the Duke's Manor was currently overwhelmed with its own troubles and had no energy to investigate such matters.","Old Lady Mo sighed. \"Let's put this matter aside for now and discuss it with Jiuye later.\"","Meanwhile, everyone cast grateful glances towards He Zhiran.","\"Younger Sister Jiuye, thanks to you discovering the poison in the porridge in time, we, the entire family, have been saved,\" the eldest sister-in-law expressed her gratitude first.","\"Yes, thanks to Younger Sister Jiuye, we managed to escape this disaster.\"","\"Younger Sister Jiuye, thank you from the bottom of my heart.\"","\"Younger Sister Jiuye, you're truly amazing.\"","\"...\"","He Zhiran did what she did out of sincerity and had no intention of seeking gratitude. Seeing her sisters-in-law genuinely thanking her, she smiled and said, \"We are all family, sisters-in-law. No need to be so polite.\"","Old Lady Mo looked at her daughters-in-law, who were still unaware of the taste of worry, and said sternly, \"Younger Sister Jiuye is right. We are all family. If you feel grateful, show it through your actions in the future.\"","Seeing her mother-in-law speak with seriousness, the sisters-in-law quickly fell silent.","Old Lady Mo surveyed the room. \"First, dispose of Liu's body, then fetch water from the wells in the other courtyards and prepare breakfast again.\"","Her intention was that if they were to be exiled today, it would be difficult to have a good meal in the future, so they must eat well this time.","The servants promptly carried out her orders.","Old Lady Mo led the women back to the reception hall.","\"How did your preparations go from last night?\" Old Lady Mo inquired while the servants were preparing breakfast again.","\"Mother, as Younger Sister Jiuye instructed, I sewed a pocket in my undergarment and wrapped silver bills in cotton before putting them inside,\" one of the sisters-in-law replied.","\"Mother, I have prepared mine as well.\"","\"Mine is ready too.\"","The eight sisters-in-law expressed that they had all made the necessary preparations.","Old Lady Mo nodded. \"That's good. In case anything happens, all of you must be clever.\"","Mo Hanyue, who was inherently naive, couldn't understand what her mother and sisters-in-law were talking about.","\"Mother, sisters-in-law, what are you preparing?\" Mo Hanyue asked.","Old Lady Mo glanced at her innocent daughter but couldn't bring herself to reveal the truth.","\"Hanyue, as a young girl, you don't need to worry about everything,\" she said.","Mo Hanyue felt a bit aggrieved, but she could also tell that her mother wasn't in a good mood today. In order to avoid angering her, she could only remain silent.","Soon, the servants brought the freshly prepared breakfast.","After He Zhiran inspected it and confirmed it was safe, everyone began to eat.","However, there was a peculiar atmosphere during this meal.","Everyone seemed gloomy, as if they were having their last meal in life.","He Zhiran didn't say much either, quickly finished a bowl of porridge, and then got up.","\"Mother, I will bring some food back to my husband.\"","She was a bit anxious to see Mo Jiuye now, after all, she still didn't know who was behind the scenes instructing Liu Pozhi to poison.","Perhaps she could find the answer from Mo Jiuye.","Back in the bridal chamber, Mo Jiuye was still lying there in the same position.","When he saw He Zhiran return, he asked, \"Anything happening outside?\"","He Zhiran placed the food on the table not far from the bed.","\"There isn't much happening outside, but someone poisoned the well in my mother's courtyard. Fortunately, I discovered it in time. Otherwise, everyone's lives in the mansion would have been at stake.\""]},{"number":12,"title":"Chapter 12: It will happen sooner or later.","paragraphs":["Upon hearing this, Mo Jiuye ignored his injuries and immediately sat up in bed. “What on earth happened?”","He Zhiran knew that Mo Jiuye was anxious, so she recounted everything that had happened and her guesses word for word.","“Can you think of who might have ordered Old Mrs. Liu to poison me?”","Mo Jiuye frowned, and a fierce look flashed through his eyes from time to time.","Although he didn't say a word, He Zhiran could tell from his expression that Mo Jiuye definitely had a suspect in mind.","He Zhiran had never been a nosy person, and she also considered that Mo Jiuye didn't completely trust her at this time.","Since this was the case, she didn't intend to ask for trouble unnecessarily.","As long as he had a grasp on the situation, he would certainly take precautions in advance.","The room was silent for a long time before He Zhiran pointed to the breakfast on the table and reminded, \"The food is cold now. Take advantage of the fact that the emperor's men haven't arrived yet and hurry to eat something.\"","When the emperor's men were mentioned, Mo Jiuye looked outside.","\"It's almost noon now.\"","He Zhiran also found it very strange. If history was not mistaken, the emperor would send people to raid the Duke of Protection's mansion early in the morning.","\"Could it be delayed because of the theft from the imperial treasury?\" She directly voiced her guess.","Mo Jiuye did not deny it.","\"With the imperial treasury being robbed and set on fire, this is no trivial matter. His Majesty must be at his wits' end now and has no time to bother with me.\"","His voice had just fallen when a servant came to report that someone was requesting an audience with the duke's wife.","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye looked at each other, both wondering who would come to see her on the second day after their wedding.","Moreover, the original owner rarely interacted with outsiders, so He Zhiran really couldn't think of who the visitor might be for a moment.","Mo Jiuye didn't help her decide whether to meet the guest or not. Instead, he lowered his head and continued eating.","Obviously, he had left the decision to He Zhiran.","He Zhiran stood up, \"I'll go out and take a look.\"","The visitor did not go to the main entrance of the duke's mansion, but to the small back door where the servants came and went.","He Zhiran was led to the backyard by someone. The visitor was dressed like a household attendant and looked very familiar, but she couldn't remember who he was for the moment.","When the attendant saw He Zhiran, he quickly bowed respectfully, \"Young Lady, the Old Master sent me to find you.\"","Looking at the man's appearance, He Zhiran searched her memory carefully and confirmed that this person was a follower of her cheap father.","\"Why did you come?\"","\"Young Lady, I have an important matter to report.\" As he spoke, he glanced at the person who had led He Zhiran over.","He Zhiran immediately dismissed that person.","\"What is it?\" She had already roughly guessed, but still wanted to hear him confirm it personally.","The attendant whispered, \"Young Lady, the Old Master asked me to inform you that His Majesty will soon send people to raid the Duke's mansion. Please get ready in advance.\"","Sure enough!","\"Did my father say when the emperor's men would arrive?\"","\"I don't know about that. The Old Master also asked me to tell the Young Lady that as a daughter of the He family, you must not betray your faith. No matter what happens to the Duke of Protection's mansion, you cannot leave.\"","He Zhiran didn't take such an exhortation to heart at all. She had never intended to leave the Mo family anyway.","Since she couldn't get any more useful information from him, He Zhiran waved her hand to dismiss him.","Hearing this news directly was much more real than reading about it in history books.","He Zhiran didn't dare delay for a moment and hurried back to the bridal chamber.","Without waiting for Mo Jiuye to ask, she recounted the servant's message verbatim.","There was no visible anger or joy on Mo Jiuye's face. After a long silence, he coldly said, \"What's bound to come will come sooner or later.\"","Although Mo Jiuye didn't show any emotion, He Zhiran could still hear the despair in his tone.","\"Look on the bright side. As long as we work hard to survive, I believe the day we make it big will come eventually.\"","\"Humph... As a grown man, I have to make my family of women suffer with me. What day of making it big can I expect?\" Mo Jiuye said sarcastically.","He Zhiran knew that Mo Jiuye was in low spirits at the moment, and no matter how much reason she gave, it would be of no use. She could only slowly counsel him in the future.","Just then, Eighth Sister-in-law's scream came from outside, \"Ah... Why are the water tank and big wok from the kitchen, as well as the things from the storeroom, all in Ninth Brother's ear room?\"","He Zhiran was caught off guard. Due to her carelessness, someone had discovered the abnormalities in the ear room.","She knew best just how bad the situation was in there.","Basically all of the large items she had stored in her space were now in the ear room.","There were even some vases and ornaments from the storeroom...","Now she was afraid she wouldn't be able to clear her name even if she jumped into the Yellow River.","Mo Jiuye only slightly raised his eyes, and saw He Zhiran's panicked expression flash by in an instant.","\"If they ask about it, just push everything onto me.\"","He Zhiran also only lost her composure for a moment before quickly calming down again.","Especially with Mo Jiuye taking the fall for her, she was even more emboldened.","When she arrived at the door of the ear room, she saw all the sisters-in-law and Old Lady Mo standing there.","Their expressions were almost identical, with their mouths wide open and eyes full of shock.","Seeing He Zhiran come over, Third Sister-in-law immediately grabbed her arm.","\"Ninth Sister, how did the things missing from our storeroom and kitchen end up here?\"","He Zhiran put on a shocked expression like them, widening her eyes and shaking her head vigorously.","\"They weren't like this when I came to tidy up my dowry last night. Why did these things appear here?\"","\"This thief is too shameless! Stealing from the storeroom is one thing, but even taking such a big iron pot...\" Sixth Sister-in-law said indignantly.","\"That's right. They probably took everything they could grab, then felt it wasn't valuable enough and secretly dumped it all here.\"","\"I just want to know, is this thief immortal? How could he move so many things here without making a sound?\"","Listening to the sisters-in-law cursing the little thief, He Zhiran didn't know whether to laugh or cry.","But at a time like this, she didn't dare show her real emotions.","Just as she was about to say something more, Mo Jiuye walked over slowly and with difficulty.","\"Don't guess anymore. It was me who did this. I didn't want to let these things fall into strangers' hands, but then I thought we couldn't take so much with us anyway, so I just piled everything in the ear room.\"","Although his explanation was a bit far-fetched, no one wanted to scrutinize it.","After all, with Ninth Brother's abilities, doing these things would not be difficult for him.","Just as the eight sisters-in-law were about to praise Mo Jiuye for being capable, Old Lady Mo spoke up.","\"That's enough. Since you and Ninth Sister did not forget to tidy up her dowry, don't bother with these unimportant things.\"","The sisters-in-law always listened most to the old lady's words. Seeing that she had spoken, they immediately shut their mouths.","Mo Jiuye invited everyone into the room and informed them of the news brought by the He house servant.","The smiles on the sisters-in-laws' faces instantly vanished and became serious."]},{"number":13,"title":"Chapter 13: As long as I am here, no one in the Mohist family will be short.","paragraphs":["They all knew clearly that now that they had gotten accurate news, the only thing left to do was—wait.","Wait for the Emperor to send people to ransack the house.","...","In the palace, in the Golden Hall.","Emperor Shunwu flew into a rage.","“What use do I have raising you useless wine sacks and rice bags? The national treasury was actually robbed and even burned down completely. What use are you?”","The civil and military officials all lowered their heads like quails, not saying a word.","They were also puzzled—who exactly would have such great ability to empty the national treasury and even burn it down?","It was just that all these people clearly knew Emperor Shunwu’s temper. At this time, who dared to speak? They would just become his punching bag.","Finally, it was the Eldest Prince, Prince Heng, who carefully reminded,","“Father Emperor, please protect your dragon body. Also, there is still an important matter to handle today. The national treasury robbery can be investigated slowly.”","With this reminder, Emperor Shunwu finally calmed down from his rage.","Prince Heng was right to remind him. He still had an important matter he had not dealt with today.","Emperor Shunwu suppressed the anger in his heart and had the eunuch attendant directly read the decree accusing Mo Jiuye of treason and betraying the country.","Many of the officials had already known about this matter in advance and did not appear too shocked.","After all, the emperor of a country did not want anyone to live better off. Whoever he did not like would have to wash their neck and wait there.","However, those who knew in advance were still only a small number of the emperor’s trusted officials. He Yuanming had also coincidentally heard other people whispering about this news. Only then did he secretly find someone to send a message to the Duke of Protector’s estate.","He knew clearly that even sending advance notice would not change anything. He only hoped that the Mo family could make some preparations early on, so that they would not be penniless and helpless on the road to exile.","It could be said that Emperor Shunwu had really gone all out against the Duke of Protector.","In order to prevent the officials from being too suspicious, he had specifically captured some unimportant officials and accused them of wrongdoing along with the Duke of Protector.","He had even connected their crimes to Mo Jiuye...","By doing this, it benefited Emperor Shunwu in three ways:","First, it elevated the crimes of the Duke of Protector.","Second, it silenced any officials who wanted to plead for Mo Jiuye.","Third, it could add difficulties for Mo Jiuye on the road to exile.","Sure enough, his plan was flawless. With the decree announced, the entire court fell silent. One could only see some officials with dissatisfied looks on Mo Jiuye’s behalf.","Emperor Shunwu did not care about this at all. As long as he could smoothly deal with Mo Jiuye, nothing else mattered.","Emperor Shunwu specifically sent Cao Ren, a general who had been scolded by Mo Jiuye, to ransack the house and deliver the decree.","His goal was to make the Duke of Protector’s circumstances even more miserable.","...","Old Lady Mo waited with the estate’s female family members in the bridal chamber.","Seeing that it was already past noon, there was still no movement.","She looked at Mo Jiuye still lying collapsed on the bed, worried.","“Jiuye, could your judgment and information be mistaken?”","Before Mo Jiuye could reply, a servant rushed in to report,","“Duke, Old Lady, this is bad. The estate is surrounded. General Cao charged in with a group of men.”","Upon hearing this, Old Lady Mo helplessly closed her eyes and murmured, \"Alas... I shouldn't have been so wishfully thinking.\"","Mo Hanyue, who did not know what was happening, hurriedly grabbed Old Lady Mo’s arm.","“Mother, what on earth has happened?”","The eight sisters-in-law also looked nervously at Old Lady Mo, no longer calm.","“Since they have come, we can only face it calmly. Everyone, come with me to go take a look.”","Seeing everyone follow Old Lady Mo out in a flurry, He Zhiran looked at the still unmoving Mo Jiuye.","“Don’t worry, I will help Mother handle things.”","Since Mo Jiuye was currently pretending to be unconscious, he could not go out with everyone.","In Mo Jiuye’s pitch-black eyes was some loneliness and self-mockery.","Still, he sincerely responded to He Zhiran’s words.","“Tell them not to struggle unnecessarily and protect themselves.”","As for everything else, at this point, Mo Jiuye did not even dare hope there was any chance of reversal. He only hoped everyone could embark on the road to exile safe and sound.","“Alright, I promise you that as long as I'm here, not a single person from the Mo family will be lost.”","After personally witnessing the hero and his family wrongfully accused by the foolish emperor, He Zhiran also felt somewhat heavy-hearted at this moment.","However, she still tried her best to relax and deal seriously with today’s events.","He Zhiran jogged a few steps to catch up with Old Lady Mo’s group.","Not long after they went out, a chaotic patter of footsteps sounded.","At the same time, some pleading voices of servants could be heard.","Around thirty some men dressed in official uniforms escorted the gloating Cao Ren at the very front as they walked towards them.","Before the men even reached them, someone shouted at them, “Don’t move! We are here to ransack by decree!”","Old Lady Mo was the first to stop. She pretended to be calm as she looked at the approaching men.","Mo Hanyue was so frightened she clutched her mother’s hand tightly, not even daring to breathe loudly.","Although the eight sisters-in-law had boldly proclaimed last night that they would live as Mo family ghosts and die as Mo family ghosts, when faced with this scene, they still trembled in fear.","Only He Zhiran stood at the back of the group, staring intently at the officials without moving or making a sound.","At the same time, she secretly took out a sharp dagger from her space bracelet, tightly gripping it in her palm.","She was prepared to protect the Mo family’s safety at any moment.","Cao Ren arrogantly approached holding the decree.","“Mo family, prepare to receive the decree!”","As he spoke, Cao Ren’s eyes continuously scanned the surroundings.","“For the Emperor’s decree to arrive but the Duke of Protector does not personally come receive it, this is greatly disrespectful!”","As he finished speaking, he looked to the officials behind him.","“You, go invite the Duke of Protector to come receive the decree.”","Seeing that pompous official about to run to the inner residence, Old Lady Mo quickly stopped him.","“The Duke was summoned by the Emperor last night and given fifty heavy strikes. He is currently still unconscious and I'm afraid cannot come receive the decree.”","Cao Ren knew Mo Jiuye did not appear because of this reason. He had only wanted to deliberately make things difficult for the Mo family here.","“What? You said the Duke was beaten by the Emperor last night?”","He exaggerated his expression, pretending he did not know about this matter, while gloating inwardly.","Old Lady Mo coldly snorted, “General Cao, you are also an important minister of the court. Just deliver the decree. There is no need to kick someone who is down.”","Eldest sister-in-law also boldly spoke up, “Everyone in the capital knows that aside from Ninth Brother, my Mo family are all women. To flaunt your power before a group of women will surely not look good once it spreads.”","“That’s right. Even if we are beneath others, our maternal families all have officials in the court. I fear they may hear of this matter,” Third sister-in-law added.","Cao Ren also knew this was reasonable.","Bullying a group of women, moreover women who had some background, could easily spread.","“Since this is so, Cao will not make things difficult for you. Mo family, receive the decree.”"]},{"number":14,"title":"Chapter 14: As long as Cao Ren dares to start, she will not be soft","paragraphs":["Although hating Emperor Shunwu, the proper etiquette could not be abandoned.","Old Lady Mo knelt down first.","The eight sister-in-laws and Mo Hanyue followed suit upon seeing this.","He Zhiran did not want to kneel, but could not behave too differently either.","Luckily, the skirts of ancient people's dresses were wide, she pulled at her skirt to cover her legs and squatted behind everyone else.","\"By the mandate of heaven, the Emperor decrees, upon investigation, Duke Mo Jiuye colluded with foreign bandits, embezzled military provisions, and conspired with court officials to commit treason.","His Majesty is benevolent, and considering Mo family's ancestral merits and contributions, spared them from death penalty.","Now all properties of Mo family shall be confiscated, servants sold off, and Mo family exiled to the northwest...\"","Fortunately, Mo family was mentally prepared, so they were not shocked into collapse by such an unjust decree.","They did not even yell grievances.","Because they knew clearly, the Emperor genuinely wanted to punish Mo family, so even pleading would be futile.","Just by the people sent to confiscate their property, it was evident the Emperor did not intend for Mo family to have an easy time, otherwise he would not have sent Cao Ren, that scoundrel.","Old Lady Mo received the decree, and had just stood up with the women.","Cao Ren was already impatient and ordered the search to start, even claiming that not even mouse holes should be spared.","As for these women present, they would naturally need to be searched.","Looking at these flowers and jade-like beauties, a trace of lewdness flashed in Cao Ren's eyes.","\"Hehe, considering I served in court with Mo Jiuye, I shall personally search you women's bodies.","Hearing Cao Ren's words, everyone instinctively retreated back a few steps.","Although they were widows, they were chaste. How could they allow a grown man to grope them?","Old Lady Mo was also furious, and solemnly said:","\"Lord Cao, what you're doing goes against reason. Although my Mo family is convicted, these women can't be casually humiliated.\"","When saying this, she was prepared to die.","A woman's chastity is above all, she would rather die than let anyone humiliate them.","Cao Ren did not take Old Lady Mo's words to heart at all.","In his view, Mo family was now like locusts after autumn, even if they don't die now, they would die en route during exile.","\"Old lady, don't reject a toast only to drink a forfeit, it's an honor that I'm personally searching you all. If you're unwilling, I don't mind letting all the officials search you together.\"","Old Lady Mo had a fiery temperament, how could she stand such vulgar words?","\"Cao Ren, today I will fight you til the end.\"","As Old Lady Mo spoke, she pulled out the hairpin in her hair and lunged at Cao Ren.","After all, Cao Ren was a military officer, how could he be scared by a woman?","Seizing the chance to get rid of her, he might even earn the Emperor's praise.","Seeing Cao Ren had already assumed a defensive stance, He Zhiran swiftly pulled Old Lady Mo to safety.","Her action caused Cao Ren's kick to hit empty air.","Cao Ren glared at the one who ruined his plan.","This woman had her hair in a married woman's style, looking about 16 or 17. Delicate brows and eyes, wearing an aqua blue modest dress that complemented her fair skin.","She was truly a beauty, he didn't know there was such a beauty in the Duke's residence.","Cao Ren sized up He Zhiran for a few seconds, and immediately put on a smiling face.","\"Hehe...I don't know which widow you are, my lady?\"","If possible, Cao Ren planned to pull some tricks to bring this gorgeous woman into his household.","Seeing this kind of attitude, He Zhiran felt a wave of nausea.","Still, she maintained an icy stare at him.","\"Cao Ren, you dare disregard court rules and harass convicted officials' families.\"","\"Oh? The little lady is quite fierce, I'm harassing you now, what can you do about it?\"","He Zhiran's expression did not change.","\"Court rules state officials on duty cannot harm uncondemned families, and absolutely cannot harass convicted officials' families.","Now you're openly harassing me, are you not afraid of the Emperor's punishment?\"","Of course Cao Ren was very clear on this court rule, he just always believed Mo family women wouldn't understand this, and that he could do as he wished without consequence.","He didn't expect a young and beautiful lady to recite court rules to his face with so many people present.","This made him somewhat nervous.","However, Cao Ren still would not give up, thinking the woman before him was just a young lady, intimidation would make her afraid.","\"Silver tongue is useless before me, I'll say this now, as long as you obey me, we can negotiate the search, otherwise, don't blame me for not cherishing you.\"","He Zhiran had lived two lifetimes, and this was her first time seeing someone so shameless.","Now, she had already switched her dagger to a mini pistol.","As long as Cao Ren dared to make a move, she would absolutely not hesitate.","Although she had made preparations, He Zhiran still chose reason first.","After all, there were still so many Mo women present, if she shot and killed Cao Ren, it would certainly implicate them.","\"Cao Ren, let me advise you, when Mo manor is exiled, our families will certainly come to send us off.","I'm sure you understand hidden troubles will come out, if any of my sister-in-laws mention this to their families after seeing them, do you know what consequences there will be?","Also, although Mo family property was confiscated and exiled, our maternal families were unaffected.","My father is at worst a Minister, if he doesn't see me when sending me off, then hears that I died by your hand, what do you think my father will do?\"","Her words were powerful, making the sister-in-laws increasingly confident.","\"Cao Ren, if my eldest brother doesn't see me when sending me off, he will certainly avenge me.\"","\"My father too, if you insist on being stubborn, I will smash my head and die right here.\"","Seeing the Mo women's indignant manner, Cao Ren suddenly felt at a loss.","He never imagined these women were not afraid of him at all.","Especially the most beautiful one, who said her father was a current Minister.","Although she didn't outright say which Minister, he knew clearly in his heart.","Among Mo family's wives, only one was a Minister's daughter.","That was Mo Jiuye's new wife yesterday, Minister He Yuanming's daughter.","He Yuanming was a second rank Minister, how could he contend against him as a fourth rank officer?","Also, those Mo widows, their maternal families also held office, some even higher than him.","After thinking it over, Cao Ren decided to take the loss this time.","However, he didn't want to lose momentum.","\"Humph! I'll let you all go just this once, considering you've been widowed for many years, quite pitiful.\""]},{"number":15,"title":"Chapter 15: So it is because of Poverty","paragraphs":["After saying that, Cao Ren whispered a few words to the officials behind him. The officials immediately ran away.","Soon, those officials came back with several fierce-looking old women.","Each old woman was holding a large parcel in her hands.","Cao Ren ordered, \"Search their bodies carefully. If anyone dares to be lenient, bring me their heads.\"","\"Yes!\" The old women answered in unison and walked towards the women.","Mo Hanyue shrank behind Old Lady Mo in fear.","\"Mother, Hanyue is scared.\"","Old Lady Mo sternly said, \"Stand up straight, don't lose face for the Mo family ancestors.\"","Hearing this, Mo Hanyue stood up straight with trembling courage, tears still streaming down her face.","The old women showed no mercy at all. In order to search more thoroughly, they took those women to a nearby room and asked them to take off their clothes for inspection.","This way, the pockets sewn into the undergarments according to He Zhiran's method could not be hidden either.","Without exception, all the banknotes hidden in the pockets of the undergarments were found, along with the jewelry on their heads, all confiscated.","Seeing this scene, He Zhiran was extremely relieved that her clinic had crossed over with her, allowing her to take away those assets without any pressure.","Finally, those old women did not even spare the silk dresses of the Mo family women, and made them all change into the coarse linen clothes they had brought.","Looking at these clothes, not only were they gray and shabby, but they also had a lot of patches on them. The sisters-in-law were very troubled.","The eighth sister-in-law complained unwillingly, \"Our clothes aren't worth much, you can't take them away!\"","The old woman bared her big yellow teeth and sneered, \"Look at your current situation. Having clothes to cover your body is already good enough, what more do you want?\"","The eighth sister-in-law wanted to say more, but was stopped by Old Lady Mo.","\"Zhao Shi, no need to say more.\"","After saying that, Old Lady Mo casually took a patched dress and put it on herself.","He Zhiran didn't care either, and quickly followed Old Lady Mo's actions, randomly putting one on.","Seeing this, the other sisters-in-law and Mo Hanyue could only forcibly endure the anger in their hearts, each picking up a dress to wear.","Fortunately, the shoes they were wearing were still their original ones.","Only after they had put on the clothes did the old women turn and leave the room with the \"spoils of war\".","They handed over all the banknotes and jewelry to Cao Ren without any less.","Seeing the banknotes of just over a thousand taels handed over by the old woman, Cao Ren disdainfully put them in his arms. As for the jewelry, he placed them in a prepared wooden box.","With the hidden banknotes searched away, the sisters-in-law all felt hopeless.","Without money, it would be very difficult for them to survive the journey to the northwest.","Old Lady Mo had also lost her previous composure. Without money in hand, what could they use to grease the palms of those greedy officials on the road?","Just when the women were extremely disappointed, the people who had searched the other courtyards of the Duke Who Protects the State mansion also returned one after another.","The news they brought back almost made Cao Ren furious.","\"Report to General Cao, the treasury of the Duke Who Protects the State mansion is empty.\"","\"What did you say?\" Cao Ren looked incredulous.","The official timidly repeated, \"General Cao, there really is nothing in the treasury.\"","\"General Cao, not only is there nothing in the treasury, even the kitchen is empty.\" Another official added.","Cao Ren was furious and looked at the women, \"Say, have you transferred the assets of the Duke Who Protects the State mansion in advance?\"","Old Lady Mo replied in a deep voice, \"General Cao, His Majesty issued the confiscation decree today. Does my Mo family have the foresight to transfer assets in advance?\"","Hearing Old Lady Mo say this, Cao Ren also knew it made sense.","But he did not believe that the prestigious Duke Who Protects the State mansion could be so poor.","No wonder Mo Jiuye wore black robes all day and was never seen changing clothes.","It turned out to be because of poverty.","How could he know that ever since Mo Jiuye was sensible, the family had often held funerals for his elder brothers.","Mo Jiuye also wore black robes every day in memory of those elder brothers who died for the country.","It wasn't that he only had one black robe, it was just that the styles were the same!","Thinking of this, Cao Ren suddenly felt superior in front of the Mo family.","\"I didn't expect the prestigious Duke Who Protects the State mansion to be an empty shell. No wonder, how can a group of women earn money?\"","An official immediately echoed, \"General Cao is absolutely right.\"","Cao Ren liked this feeling of being flattered. He swept his eyes around and saw that the search was over. He ordered,","\"You guys watch over the seized assets and servants first and wait for the emperor's decree.\"","\"The rest are responsible for escorting the prisoners to the suburbs.\"","After saying that, Cao Ren did not forget to look at He Zhiran again, reluctantly leaving.","He Zhiran was disgusted by this look again.","Taking advantage of the officials seeing Cao Ren off, she quickly left the crowd.","She went to a place where people could not see her, briskly lifted her skirt, and climbed onto a thick tree.","With her mind entering her storage space, she took out a sniper rifle she had stored there.","Bullets loaded, aim taken.","The sight stayed steadily aimed at the back of Cao Ren's head.","Not until Cao Ren had left the Duke Who Protects the State mansion and got on the tall horse did she finally pull the trigger.","With a deafening bang, Cao Ren, who had just been arrogant in front of the Mo family, tilted to one side and fell off the horse instantly...","At the same time, He Zhiran immediately entered her storage space.","This gunshot was like thunder, and people would definitely follow the sound to find the source.","She planned to temporarily hide in her space and reappear after people's attention moved away from here.","If not for Cao Ren repeatedly touching her bottom line, He Zhiran would not have wanted to cause trouble at this time.","Such a person, every minute more he lived was a waste of air.","But how could she know that all of He Zhiran's actions were seen by Mo Jiuye hiding in the dark.","Who exactly was this woman, and why did she have such a powerful weapon?","Not only that, she could also disappear on the spot...","Could she be a goddess?","Mo Jiuye shook his head hard, feeling that He Zhiran's actions in the past two days had far exceeded his cognition."]},{"number":16,"title":"Chapter 16: The prosperity of the capital has nothing to do with them.","paragraphs":["No matter what, just based on He Zhiran's performance of protecting the Mo Family people, and her merciless attack on Cao Ren, he could determine one thing at least.","That is, He Zhiran does not seem to harbor any malice towards the Mo Family for now.","Seeing that after hearing that muffled sound, all the officials ran towards the big tree, and the Mo Family's women were not in danger at the moment, Mo Jiuye leaped up and flashed away from his original spot.","No matter how chaotic it was outside, after He Zhiran entered the space, she obtained another big surprise.","The dagger, mini pistol and sniper rifle she had just taken out all had one extra copy.","For He Zhiran, these were the best things that could save her life on the road, the more the better.","After waiting in the space for about ten minutes, He Zhiran flashed out, and saw that all the officials had disappeared, and the Mo Family's women had also vanished from their original spot.","She immediately jumped down from the tree and returned to the bridal chamber.","She only saw that under the supervision of the officials, the sisters-in-law had already carried Mo Jiuye onto the door panel.","The four sisters-in-law were carrying the door panel with great difficulty and walking out.","The officials kept urging them.","\"Walk faster, don't dawdle.\"","Mo Jiuye, carried by several sisters-in-law, felt extremely ashamed in his heart.","It was his incompetence that made these sisters-in-law face difficulties while still having to take care of him.","Seeing the sisters-in-law walking with such difficulty, He Zhiran suddenly remembered the wooden cart found by those officials when they were searching just now.","\"Wait a minute.\"","The leading official looked back and asked displeasedly, \"What's the matter?\"","\"Aren't you in a hurry to send us to the outskirts of the city?\" He Zhiran asked neither hastily nor slowly.","\"So what?\" The official's first reaction was that this woman wanted to play tricks. They had witnessed her scene of yelling at General Cao with their own eyes.","He Zhiran pointed to the four sisters-in-law carrying the door panel: \"You can see that except for the husband, the rest of us Mo Family exiles are all women. It is simply impossible to move quickly.\"","\"What do you want?\" The official asked.","\"When you searched just now, there was a wooden cart, not worth much money. Why not use it to push the husband, so that we can travel faster.\"","The official rolled his eyes.","\"Fine, that wooden cart is yours now.\"","After getting the wooden cart and lifting Mo Jiuye onto it, He Zhiran personally pushed it out.","The sisters-in-law looked at He Zhiran with admiration.","With the wooden cart, it saved both time and effort. Soon, the officials escorted the group to the front door of the Duke of Protector's Mansion.","At this moment, the front door of the Duke's Mansion was crowded with people.","Some were passing by and wanted to watch the excitement, while some were family members of the sisters-in-law, who rushed over after hearing that the emperor had ordered a raid on the Mo's residence to see their own family members.","As a result, before they saw anyone come out of the Duke's Mansion, they were shocked by a muffled sound.","Then they witnessed with their own eyes as a big bloody hole appeared on the back of Cao Ren's head, and his whole body fell off the horse onto the ground.","The Prefect of the Capital had already been summoned.","The Prefect of the Capital ordered the coroner to examine the injury without saying anything else.","It was obvious that the wound that caused Cao Ren's death was the bloody hole on the back of his head.","However, the coroner was unable to determine what kind of hidden weapon had caused it.","After all, Cao Ren was an imperial official executing his duties. His death while on duty was no trivial matter.","Although the incident occurred outside the Duke of Protector's mansion, it was no longer a secret that Mo Jiuye had been severely caned with fifty heavy rods by the emperor last night and had to be carried back. It was simply impossible for him to make a move against Cao Ren.","Moreover, the only Mo Family members who could move freely now were a group of powerless women, who were even less likely to be suspected of attacking Cao Ren.","After thinking it over, the Prefect of the Capital felt that he could not crack the case, so he immediately ordered Cao Ren's body to be taken to the Supreme Court.","When the Mo Family members came out, Cao Ren's body had been taken away.","Most of the people who had originally intended to watch the excitement here had run to the Supreme Court to watch the excitement.","The few who remained were basically family members of the sisters-in-law.","The first to rush over was the Feng family, the family of Sister-in-law Feng Cuilian.","The Feng family's official rank and position were not high, and they did not have the qualifications to attend court.","They had found out about this news by sending someone out after seeing Cao Ren lead people towards the Duke of Protector's mansion.","Upon hearing this news, Sister-in-law Feng Cuilian's mother cried and begged her elder brother to accompany her here.","\"Cuilian, my daughter, mother has no ability to help you...wuwuwu...\"","Old Lady Feng held her daughter's hand and wept bitterly.","Seeing her mother, Feng Cuilian immediately threw herself into her arms crying.","This scene brought tears to the eyes of everyone present.","Old Lady Feng took out a purse from her arms with trembling hands and secretly stuffed it into Feng Cuilian's hands.","\"Mother came out in a hurry and was not well prepared. These silvers are all mother's private savings. Keep them for unforeseen needs on the road.\"","If it wasn't for the silver hidden inside her clothes being searched, Feng Cuilian would not have wanted to take her mother's money.","In her heart, the Mo Family members did not bring anything out, and if she did not accept this silver, it would be difficult to survive the journey to the northwest.","She clutched the purse her mother had given her, choking back tears, \"Mother, don't worry about me. With Mother-in-law and sisters-in-law, and Ninth Brother, we will definitely arrive safely in the northwest.\"","At the same time, Xiao Family, the family of Sister-in-law Xiao Qinger, also came and secretly stuffed Xiao Qinger with a purse too.","When they brought luggage to help prepare, they were rejected by the officials.","The reason was that criminals were not qualified to use these things.","The others without family members to see them off looked at the two sisters-in-law enviously.","At this time, He Zhiran was also guessing in her heart whether anyone from the He Family would come to see her off.","The result was that no one from the He Family came.","Seeing that the time was almost up, the officials urged the Mo Family members to leave and forcibly dispersed the Xiao and Feng family members who had come to see them off.","Taking one last look at the majestic gate of the Duke of Protector's Mansion, Old Lady Mo took the first step.","Mo Hanyue, still somewhat frightened, followed closely behind her mother.","Next was He Zhiran pushing Mo Jiuye on the wooden cart, followed by the eight sisters-in-law.","All along the way, looking at the prosperous streets, with vendors' shouts coming from both sides from time to time.","At this moment, the Mo Family members were extremely clear in their hearts that from now on, they would have nothing to do with the prosperity of the capital...","Under the gaze of the common people, the Mo Family members escorted by the officials had already walked out of the gate of the capital.","Except for Sister-in-law Feng and Sister-in-law Xiao who saw their family members, the other seven sisters-in-law including He Zhiran did not see anyone from their maternal families come to bid farewell.","The sisters-in-law who had still held a glimmer of hope originally were completely disheartened after walking out of the city gate.","They couldn't help but lament at the coldness of the world, that even the usually harmonious maternal families did not even dare to show their faces at this time.","He Zhiran was indifferent to this. After all, she still considered herself an outsider at present, and did not have high expectations for the original host's parents.","Everyone was lost in their own thoughts, and unknowingly they had arrived at the outskirts of the capital.","Unexpectedly, in addition to the officials responsible for escorting them, there were also many other exiled criminals waiting there.","And from the positions of those criminals, it could be seen that they were also exiled by whole families."]},{"number":17,"title":"Chapter 17: Give you a incense stick time, hold on tight.","paragraphs":["He Zhiran was always vigilant. No matter where she went, she would first observe her surroundings.","This observation was no big deal.","She realized that most of the prisoners looked at the Mohists with hostility.","To confirm that she was not seeing things, He Zhiran rubbed her eyebrows and observed again. It was still the same.","Some people could no longer restrain themselves and started cursing loudly at the Mohists.","\"Mo Jiuye, you are a broom star who got your whole family executed. Now you've come to get us too.\"","\"Mohists, I curse you all to suffer a terrible death.\"","\"If it weren't for you, how could the He family suffer such an undeserved calamity?\"","\"... \"","Hearing these people cursing with increasing excitement, while the officers made no attempt to stop them at all.","This made He Zhiran first think that having these people exiled with the Mohists must have been prearranged by the despotic emperor, with the intention of causing trouble for the Mohists.","However, no matter how she thought about it, she just could not figure out why these people were calling Mo Jiuye a broom star.","It looked like with these people around, the journey would not be boring...","Mo Jiuye listened to the cursing, trying hard to control his emotions to prevent lashing out at those people in excitement.","However, he still wanted to see who exactly was cursing him.","So he squinted through the fringe of his bangs to look in the direction of the voices.","He recognized some of these people, who were court officials.","No need to think further, those cursing must be the families of those officials.","What was puzzling was why they would curse him?","Mo Jiuye's mind raced as he considered whether he had any conflicts with these people.","Soon, he was certain of the answer.","One of them with the surname He used to be the vice minister of the Ministry of Revenue. He was in charge of distributing rations when Mo Jiuye was fighting wars on the border.","As a result, He Zhiyuan embezzled rations for his own personal gain. Mo Jiuye submitted a memorial to Emperor Shunwu to thoroughly investigate the matter.","There was also Li Liang, who was a compiler in the Hanlin Academy. He had just returned to the capital when Li Liang took the initiative to ask Mo Jiuye to take his illegitimate daughter as a concubine. Mo Jiuye rejected him outright.","Other than that, he had no other dealings with Li Liang.","Looking at the ones cursing most fervently, it was Vice Minister Fang Chuanzhou of the Ministry of War.","Fang Chuanzhou used to be the vice minister of the Ministry of War and had no conflicts with Mo Jiuye.","He and He Zhiran shared the same confusion about why these people were calling him a broom star.","Could it be that when the emperor convicted them of crimes, he implicated Mo Jiuye as well?","Just as Mo Jiuye was utterly bewildered, Sister-in-law Xie Fang ran towards the cursers in tears.","\"Father, Mother, Eldest Brother, Youngest Brother, how did you all get convicted too?\"","No wonder her closest family members did not come to see her off.","Xie's father had a face full of worry. Facing his daughter, he squeezed out a smile uglier than crying.","\"It was Father who did something wrong and was punished by His Majesty.\"","\"Father, don't lie. The Xie family was clearly implicated by the Duke's residence. Why are you hiding this from my sister?\" Xie Ming was full of resentment, glaring at Mo Jiuye who was lying on the wooden cart.","Just as Xie Fang was about to ask for details, Xie Father scolded Xie Ming.","\"Xie Ming, shut your mouth. Is this a place for talking?\"","Xie Ming resentfully glanced at his father, helplessly shutting his mouth.","Sister-in-law also understood these twists and turns. What's more, with so many people watching the Xie family, even if she was anxious to know the truth, she could not be impatient at this moment.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran saw Sister-in-law run to talk to her natal family, and they both pricked up their ears to listen carefully to the story, but Xie Father was prudent and the two listened in vain.","Just like Sister-in-law, they could only find another opportunity to understand what exactly had happened.","Mother Mo was steadfast. Seeing her in-laws, whether they were pleased to see her or not, she politely nodded her head in greeting.","The officers had finished the handover and then perfunctorily went to stop the cursing against the Mo family.","These people had not yet fully entered the role of criminals. Faced with the officers' rebukes, it could be said that they were neither obedient nor convinced.","They talked back to the officers one remark after another.","In the officers' eyes, these people were no different from dead men, so how could they indulge them?","Some immediately took whips from their waists and lashed the ones who were cursing most fervently.","\"Looks like you're tired of living. Just say so if you don't want to make it alive to the northwest.\"","The whip lashes on their bodies instantly pulled back their sanity.","Looking down again at the coarse hemp clothes even worse than commoners' wear, they had no choice but to believe the facts of their family's seizure and their exile.","Looking again at the whips in the officers' hands, they no longer dared to bristle.","However, they still glared at the Mo family.","The Mo ladies, led by Mother Mo, didn't even look at their faces.","This gave those people the feeling of punching cotton.","An officer shouted, \"While the day is still early, let's hit the road immediately.\"","Just as his voice fell, a carriage came from the direction of the capital.","\"Wait a moment......Please stop......\" the coachman shouted.","Including the officers, everyone squinted to look over.","The carriage soon stopped in front of the convoy.","The coachman immediately jumped down and lifted the curtain.","Two people with their heads wrapped up emerged from inside.","Judging by their figures, it was a man and a woman, both seemingly elderly.","As soon as they got off the carriage, their eyes searched among the crowd and finally landed on He Zhiran.","He Yuanming quickly walked over and took out a large silver ingot to hand to the lead officer.","He did not seem to want to reveal his identity, speaking to the officer very politely.","\"Please do me a favor?\"","The officer weighed the silver ingot in his hand.","\"You have the time it takes for an incense stick to burn. Be quick.\"","\"Alright.\" He Yuanming responded and pulled Ling Xueyan to quickly walk towards He Zhiran.","When passing by Mother Mo, He Yuanming deliberately pulled down a bit of the scarf wrapped around his face.","Mother Mo recognized him and sensibly led the others away, leaving only He Zhiran.","Seeing her daughter in coarse hemp clothes, Ling Xueyan's tears fell like broken strands of pearls.","She hugged He Zhiran's slender body tightly and choked with sobs, \"Ranran, it's Mother who wronged you...Woo...Mother shouldn't have worked with your father to force you to marry into the Mo family...Woo...It's Mother's fault...\"","In her previous life, He Zhiran's parents divorced. From the time she could understand things, she was like a burden in her parents' eyes.","She had never felt the slightest bit of affection from them.","Now being held tightly in the original's mother's arms, this feeling was quite strange to her, but she did not reject it at all.","He Zhiran repeatedly raised and lowered her hand, eventually placing it on Ling Xueyan's back and patting lightly a few times."]},{"number":18,"title":"Chapter 18: No Problem Beggars","paragraphs":["She imitated the scenarios from her previous life's TV dramas and softly consoled,","\"Mother, I'm just being exiled, not going to my death. Don't be upset.\"","When He Zhiran didn't say this, it was fine, but when she saw her daughter had become more sensible, Ling Xueyan cried even harder.","Although He Yuanming didn't cry as hard as Ling Xueyan, his eyes also reddened.","He knew time was limited, so he reached out and pulled Ling Xueyan to his side.","Facing He Zhiran, he solemnly said, \"It is indeed Father and Mother who have wronged you, letting you suffer such an unjust calamity the day after your wedding.\"","Saying this, He Yuanming took out a bulging purse from his robe and secretly put it in He Zhiran's hand.","In addition, he also gave He Zhiran a package of medium size.","The officers didn't interfere with this, after all they had already taken bribes from the family.","Moreover, with this money, the prisoners would have to give them favors on the road.","\"This is travel money your Father and Mother prepared for you. Don't hesitate to use it. Aside from bribing those officers on the road, ask them to get you some better food.\"","\"Also, you've loved cleanliness since you were little. Your mother packed some spare underwear for you,\" He Yuanming said, but he couldn't continue.","He turned his head away, not daring to look at He Zhiran anymore, and finally said, \"It's Father's fault for forcing you to marry into the Mo Family.\"","\"Father,\" He Zhiran called this word without any pressure.","No matter if it was the He Yuanming in the original host's memories, or the affectionate father before her eyes, He Zhiran could confirm he was a good father.","For such a person, she was willing to affectionately call him Father.","\"I was ignorant before and often angered Father and Mother.","Now, I have married Mo Jiuye and will be part of the Mo Family going forward.","Rest assured, I will live well. When the day comes I turn my fortunes around, I will properly serve you and Mother.\"","Hearing He Zhiran's words, Ling Xueyan wept uncontrollably again.","Her daughter had become so sensible overnight, but this sensible daughter had to suffer exile in the northwest.","The more she thought about it, the more aggrieved she felt. Ling Xueyan hugged He Zhiran again and wailed loudly.","He Yuanming could no longer hold back and wept constantly at the side.","Maybe it was because she had blended with the original host's emotions, or maybe because He Zhiran cherished this familial love, but her tears also streamed down her face.","He Yuanming was more sensible. Seeing time was almost up, he lightly patted the backs of mother and daughter.","\"Alright, we don't have much time left. I still want to see Brother-in-law.\"","He Zhiran looked over at Mo Jiuye lying unconscious on the wooden cart nearby.","\"Father, he's still unconscious.\"","Although she knew her parents wouldn't betray them, there were still so many eyes watching them, so He Zhiran didn't dare be careless.","He Yuanming heavily nodded his head. The way he looked at He Zhiran was increasingly remorseful.","\"Father knows Brother-in-law is injured.\"","Saying this, he had already strode towards Mo Jiuye's direction.","Seeing unconscious Mo Jiuye with his own eyes, He Yuanming truly regretted marrying his daughter to him.","His daughter had already said she didn't want to be a young widow like those women who married into the Mo Family.","But he didn't want to go back on his word like a scoundrel, so he forced his daughter to marry into the Mo Family by drugging her.","And in just one day, the Mo Family was raided and exiled.","Looking at Mo Jiuye, it was also unknown whether he would live or die.","As a second-rank senior official at court, how could he not know the hardships of exile?","Not to mention Mo Jiuye's current state, even if he were well right now, safely reaching the place of exile would not be easy.","It seemed his daughter was fated to be a widow.","He could only hope she would be blessed with good fortune and safely arrive in the northwest.","When the Emperor was less wary of the Mo Family, he would find a way to bring his daughter back from the northwest.","Seeing Mo Jiuye, Ling Xueyan kept wiping away tears, feeling more and more heartache for He Zhiran.","At the same time, she regretted insisting on marrying her daughter into the Mo Family.","He Yuanming struggled to compose himself. He found an angle the officers couldn't see, took out a letter from his robe and tucked it into Mo Jiuye's clothes.","Then he stood up and looked at Old Lady Mo, \"Mother-in-law, Ranan was spoiled by our family. If she doesn't behave properly, please be magnanimous and make allowances for her more.\"","\"What is Brother-in-law saying? The He girl is clever and lively. I like her very much,\" Old Lady Mo replied.","\"Since this is the case, I shall take my leave.\" He Yuanming didn't say much more. He pulled the still sobbing Ling Xueyan and turned to leave.","Ling Xueyan looked back at He Zhiran every three steps, reluctantly watching her daughter for a long time until she could no longer see her shadow...","This sudden familial affection left He Zhiran with mixed emotions.","She really envied the original host for having such sensible parents who cherished her.","It was just a pity the original host was ill-fated and only had this familial bond for seventeen short years.","So from now on, she would take the original host's place and serve her parents!","Although this oath was somewhat distant, He Zhiran believed that as long as Mo Jiuye survived, the Mo Family would definitely have a day of returning to the capital city.","Seeing He Zhiran standing there in grief, several sisters-in-law quickly came up to comfort her.","\"Young Sis don't be sad. He Yuanming is an upright official and will surely be safe.\"","\"That's right Young Sis. Look how fortunate you are that your parents personally came all this way to see you off. Not like me, there wasn't a shadow of anyone from my family.\"","\"... \"","He Zhiran felt the kindness of her sisters-in-law and smiled back at them.","\"Sisters don't worry. I believe we will have a day to return.\"","Just as the sisters-in-law wanted to say more, the officers urged them to move on.","\"Alright, stop standing around. Hurry and get moving.\"","He Zhiran used her sleeve to wipe the remaining tears at the corner of her eyes and pushed Mo Jiuye's cart to move forward.","Third Sister-in-Law hurried to catch up. \"Young Sis, let me help you.\"","Old Lady Mo also said, \"Pushing the cart while traveling isn't easy. Let's take turns.\"","In ancient times, the roads were dirt and often had bumps and holes, causing the carts to shake nonstop.","Plus, it hadn't rained in over half a month, and the weather was stifling hot, causing everyone to sweat profusely.","Occasionally a gust of wind would blow, sending dust sticking onto their exposed skin.","By the time they stopped to rest at dusk, everyone including the officers were covered in dirt from head to toe.","The Mo Family members looked at each other in their patched coarse hemp clothes and shoes so worn the colors were indistinguishable, looking no different from a group of beggars.","Although He Zhiran had only pushed the cart for less than half an hour, she was exhausted.","After all, this body had always been delicate and pampered without much stamina.","Just half a day of traveling had already tired her out so much she slumped on the ground unable to get up.","The others were the same, their waists sore from exhaustion as they groaned in misery.","Moreover, they had eaten an early breakfast, so it had been a whole day since their last meal. Their energy was completely spent and they were starving with their stomachs grinding against their backs.","As it was only the first day of He Zhiran's exile, she didn't have any expectations for their meals.","Just as she was lost in thought, the lead officer loudly shouted, \"Dinner time! Coarse flour steamed buns are free, one per person. White flour buns are two taels of silver for two buns. No silver, no fancying!\"","Hearing the officer's shouts, He Zhiran nearly burst out laughing. These officers were quite crafty, pricing the food as if robbing them.","Upon hearing this, Mo Hanyue grabbed Old Lady Mo's arm and complained, \"Mother, I don't want to eat coarse steamed buns.\"","Although she had never eaten coarse steamed buns, she had heard from the servants that they could scrape your throat raw. Just thinking about it frightened her.","Old Lady Mo was now penniless. Seeing her daughter exiled yet still fussily picking and choosing, her face immediately hardened.","\"Hanyue, if you want white flour buns, use silver to exchange for them.\""]},{"number":19,"title":"Chapter 19: This is What a Mohist Woman should Look Like","paragraphs":["Mo Hanyue stared at Old Lady Mo with wide eyes, her face full of disbelief.","\"Mother, where would I get any silver?\"","\"If there's no silver, then just eat whatever there is to eat.\" Old Lady Mo was not unsympathetic to her daughter, it was just that when she left the Mo Residence, all the silver bills she had hidden on her were confiscated, and now she was also penniless.","Although the daughters-in-law had some silver, she as the elder could not bring herself to ask money from the younger generation.","\"Mother, I have a little silver here, why don't I go and buy some white flour steamed buns from the yamen runners?\"","Seeing the usually lively and cute little sister shedding tears for lack of food to eat, Third Sister-in-law felt somewhat distressed.","\"Sister-in-law, don't worry, let's see what others are doing first.\"","This was He Zhiran's intention. All the silver in the national treasury was in her space, so of course she would not begrudge buying some white flour steamed buns for her family to eat.","It was just that they had only been exiled for one day so far, and she had not yet figured out the situation with the yamen runners and other exiles, so she did not want to reveal too much of her capabilities.","\"He's right, let's observe first before deciding.\" Old Lady Mo also agreed with He Zhiran's proposal.","All the Mo family listened obediently without taking any action, maintaining a wait-and-see attitude.","Speaking of which, the other four exiled families were really unlucky.","They had received the imperial edict to confiscate property and exile at almost the same time as the Mo family, with practically no warning at all. It could be said to be a passing whim of Emperor Shunwu.","Just because of this, these four families could be said to be penniless.","Escorting exiled convicts was usually a lucrative job.","They had always turned a blind eye to relatives who came to see the prisoners off, and were even happy to do so.","Only this way would the prisoners have some money on them.","If the prisoners had money, the yamen runners would profit.","But who knew, after shouting for a while that a steamed bun cost one or two silver coins, not a single person came forth with money to buy them.","In anger, the yamen runners reduced the quota of one free black flour steamed bun per person to half a bun per person.","The Mo family was fine, apart from Mo Jiuye they were all women, so their appetites were small to begin with.","The sisters-in-law were thinking that even if it was only half a steamed bun, as long as they didn't starve to death it was fine.","But when they got the buns in hand, their eyes popped.","Those black flour steamed buns were as hard as rocks, just biting down would probably chip your teeth...","\"Mother, the buns are so hard I can't bite them,\" Mo Hanyue cried again.","\"Yes Mother, if we have to rely on these kinds of buns for food throughout the journey, I'm afraid we won't die from hunger but from choking.\"","\"Mother, I and Third Sister-in-law have some silver, why don't we just go buy some white flour steamed buns?\"","Hearing the words of her daughters-in-law and daughter, Old Lady Mo very naturally looked towards He Zhiran.","Although she didn't know much about this daughter-in-law who had just married into the family, Old Lady Mo could see that He Zhiran had her own opinions.","He Zhiran slowly shook her head at Old Lady Mo.","\"Mother, don't be impatient, let's watch a while more.\"","Her words had just fallen when from the nearby Xie family group came the sounds of a child wailing.","Second Sister-in-law hurried over to see what was happening.","\"Big brother, what's wrong with Lin'er?\"","Xie Chao's eyes were full of heartache. He held out his palm flat to Xie Fang.","\"The loose milk tooth that Lin'er had, got knocked out by the steamed bun.\"","Looking again, there was still traces of blood at the corners of five-year-old Xie Lin's lips.","Xie Lin was the Xie family's only grandson, and this child had been educated very well, obedient and sensible since young.","Xie Fang had married Mo Erlang for only three months when the grievous news came that Mo Erlang had died on the battlefield.","Unfortunately, she did not manage to conceive a child of her own after marrying.","Knowing that she would have no children in this lifetime, she devoted all her heart and mind to her sensible and obedient nephew, even thinking of having her nephew provide for her in her old age.","Therefore, Xie Fang's feelings for Xie Lin were much deeper than the average aunt-nephew relationship.","Seeing the blood still oozing from the corner of Xie Lin's lips as he cried, Xie Fang's heart ached unbearably.","She snatched the coarse steamed bun from Xie Lin's hand and threw it on the ground, then turned to argue with the yamen runners.","\"Although we've been exiled, we haven't been sentenced to death after all, so we still have the right to live.","Giving us these rock-hard steamed buns that have been sitting who knows how long to eat, how are we supposed to stay alive to reach the northwest?\"","He Zhiran knew things were taking a bad turn, and hurriedly ran towards Second Sister-in-law.","Because her sharp eyes had already noticed the yamen runners taking out their whips when Second Sister-in-law started reprimanding them.","It could be said she came just in time.","Seeing the whip about to land on Xie Fang, He Zhiran dashed forward and steadily caught one end of the whip, saving Xie Fang from a bout of pain and lost skin.","These yamen runners had been escorting prisoners for many years, but this was the first time they had been thwarted by a prisoner, and a young woman at that.","The yamen runner's face immediately darkened as he turned his pent-up frustration towards He Zhiran, cursing at her.","Lying prone on the cart, Mo Jiuye was like burning coals listening to everything happening.","He even had the urge to get up and stop it.","His tense body was noticed by the attentive Old Lady Mo, who gently patted his back to signal him not to act rashly.","After calming Mo Jiuye, Old Lady Mo also went to stand beside her two daughters-in-law.","In Old Lady Mo's understanding, the Mo family men were heroic, and the women could not be cowards either, they had to face things together.","Xie Fang knew that it was her own rashness that had caused trouble, and seeing the yamen runner about to whip her ninth younger sister-in-law, she quickly shielded her.","\"I was the one who said those things, vent your anger on me alone, don't take it out on my ninth younger sister-in-law.\"","He Zhiran was already prepared to resist the yamen runner, but unexpectedly she was blocked by Second Sister-in-law.","In her anxiety, she grabbed Second Sister-in-law's collar and pulled her back, while her other hand caught the whip lashed at her again.","With a clever exertion of force, she wrested the whip from the yamen runner's hand and took it into her own.","The other yamen runners who had been deliberately eating the white flour steamed buns ostentatiously, planning to provoke the prisoners and enjoy the show, now could no longer watch their entertainment since their companion's whip had been seized.","Putting down the steamed buns in hand, they drew the short swords from their waists and closed in on the three women.","He Zhiran's morale surged.","\"You bunch of cowards, my Mo family's men shed their heads and spilled hot blood to win you your peaceful days of today.","Now my Mo family has been framed and reduced to this, yet you people kick someone when they are down, bullying us weak women to flaunt your might.","Looking at your pathetic manner, this is the only skill you have left. If you were sent to the battlefield to contend with the enemy, I'm afraid your heads would have rolled home long ago.\"","He Zhiran's words rang with righteousness. Old Lady Mo instantly felt her hot blood boil.","\"Well said, this is how a Mo family woman should be.\"","As she spoke, Old Lady Mo scanned the yamen runners' expressions.","It could be seen that not all the yamen runners were villainous people, some had already quietly put away their weapons and assumed a wait-and-see posture."]},{"number":20,"title":"Chapter 20: Silver Ringed Snake","paragraphs":["The two sides were in a stalemate, neither making the first move.","He Zhiran did not make a move, not because she was afraid of these officers, but because she did not want to make a big fuss out of this.","After all, the road ahead was still long. Making a big fuss over such a small matter would not benefit the Mo Family.","As for those officers who had not put down their weapons, they were indeed deterred by the aura of Old Lady Mo and He Zhiran.","At the same time, the other Mo women, including the timid Mo Hanyue, also came over.","Although their hearts were still a little apprehensive, they resolutely stood there to support their mother-in-law and ninth sister-in-law.","In the midst of the stalemate, the people of the three families besides the Xie family spoke up.","\"Officer, don't be fooled by the Mo women. They just want to confuse you and avoid the pain.\"","\"He's right. The Mo Family's contribution was the old Duke and his eight sons.","Even if they didn't die on the battlefield, they would have been angered to death by Mo Jiuye, the traitor.","Even we were implicated by Mo Jiuye. How can there be any leeway in dealing with such a person?\"","\"That's right. The Mo women have all been brainwashed by Mo Jiuye. Not a single good one among them.\"","\"Officer, hit them. Don't go soft.\"","The Xie family was in a dilemma. They hated the Mo Family, but they also knew this matter was provoked by Xie Fang, and the Mo Family was indirectly helping them by assisting Xie Fang.","After thinking it over, Xie Tianhai still spoke up with justice.","\"I don't care what Mo Jiuye did. All I know is that most of these women are the widows of heroes.","There is no doubt that their late husbands died on the battlefield for the sake of the Great Shun Dynasty.\"","The He, Li and Fang families originally thought the Xie family would side with them. They did not expect them to be so stupid as to speak up for their sworn enemies who confiscated their property and exiled them.","For a time, the three families directed their spears entirely at the Xie family.","\"Xie Tianhai, don't forget why your whole family was exiled.\"","\"Xie Chao, Xie Ming, your father must be muddled in his old age. Quickly take him back and don't get involved.\"","Seeing the situation in chaos, the officers hurriedly shouted:","\"Shut up, all of you! Do you want to be beaten?\"","Hearing this, the scene instantly became silent.","They had seen with their own eyes the officers wielding whips. No one wanted to suffer that pain.","Just then, the leading officer, Peng Wang, suddenly cried out and quickly crouched down clutching his right calf.","\"Ah...snake...\"","Seeing this, the other officers raised their weapons and became alert.","He Zhiran's original intention was to get along well with these officers. After all, having people to take care of them on the road would increase the Mo Family's chances of survival.","She did not expect what just happened. Helping her sister-in-law was unavoidable.","Now that Peng Wang had been bitten by a snake, she thought, this was her chance.","When those officers were looking around for the snake, wielding their weapons, He Zhiran's whip was already cracking through the air.","Unerringly, it landed right on the snake's weak spot.","This body was frail, so naturally the force could not compare to her previous life.","Although she hit the snake, it was still coiling in place, just much slower now.","Because of her actions, the officers also found the snake. Someone deftly raised a blade and hacked at it.","Although He Zhiran did not kill the snake with her own hands, she made the greatest contribution.","If she had not promptly located the snake, it was hard to say whether the other officers might also have been bitten.","But years of habit prevented them from softening towards a prisoner.","What's more, who knew whether she really helped them, or if it was just a fluke?","He Zhiran did not look at the officers' expressions. Instead, she focused on the snake.","She recognized this species. It was the extremely venomous silver ring snake.","The venom of the silver ring snake is a neurotoxin that affects the function of the nervous system.","Soon after being bitten there is localized pain, but the pain is not very obvious. Usually numbness, loss of motor coordination, ptosis, dilated pupils, paralysis, breathing difficulties, respiratory failure and other symptoms appear within a few hours after the bite.","Without timely treatment, it can be fatal.","As a doctor, He Zhiran kindly reminded them:","\"This snake is highly venomous. It's best if you first find a rope to tighten around his knee to prevent the venom from spreading, then...\"","\"Where are there so many poisonous snakes? If this was really venomous, could I still be jumping around like this?","I was just startled earlier. The wound doesn't even hurt much anymore. There's nothing serious.\"","To prove he was fine, Peng Wang nimbly stood up.","\"You there, keep this snake. It'll make a nice snack tonight.\"","Seeing Peng Wang's indifference, He Zhiran simply closed her mouth.","She had said what needed to be said. If they didn't believe her, there was nothing she could do.","She would just wait for them to come begging her for help.","Don't try to force a sale!","He Zhiran turned around: \"Mother, let's go back!\"","\"Alright, everyone go back.\" At Old Lady Mo's order, all the Mo women returned to their places.","After what had happened, and with He Zhiran taking the lead in locating the snake, the officers decided to turn a blind eye and not pursue the matter further.","The group had just sat down when Second Sister-in-Law sidled over to He Zhiran and guiltily said:","\"Younger Sister-in-Law, thank you for helping me escape a beating.\"","\"Second Sister-in-Law, we are one family. Helping you is only right.\"","\"Oh...it's all because I was impulsive. I knew those officers would beat people, yet I couldn't help but go demand justice for my nephew.\"","He Zhiran also noticed this sister-in-law had an impulsive personality.","Although she did not blame Xie Fang, she still needed to give a reminder.","\"Second Sister-in-Law, our circumstances now are different than before. It's best to discuss things with everyone first before making decisions.\"","\"Younger Sister-in-Law, don't worry. From now on, I'll tell Mother and you about anything beforehand.\"","He Zhiran felt that was enough admonishing for now.","She got up and brushed the dust off herself.","\"There are bushes all around us. More snakes could appear. I'll go take a look.\"","Listening to He Zhiran's words, Mo Jiuye became even more curious about her.","He could not possibly know nothing about a woman he had been betrothed to for many years.","In Mo Jiuye's mind, He Zhiran was just a brainless young miss who was also very spoiled.","However, after just one day of interaction, this woman did not exhibit any of the traits he knew she should have.","Not only that, she also had the ability to silently empty the national treasury, as well as the weapon she used to kill Cao Ren. It was simply unprecedented. No matter how much Mo Jiuye racked his brains, he could not figure out the reason behind it.","Moreover, every word that came from her mouth was sonorous and forceful, no less so than the eloquent officials in the court."]},{"number":21,"title":"Chapter 21: Collecting Herbs","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye had once doubted whether she was the real He Zhiran. But just now when he saw her parents coming to see her off, he could ascertain that this was the genuine daughter of the He family.","While Mo Jiuye was lost in thought, He Zhiran had already carefully begun searching in the bushes.","Although the banded krait was quite toxic, its body was full of treasures. It would be great if more banded kraits could be found.","She could then find an opportunity to extract the snake's venom and make it into a self-defense poison.","The people of the other families also saw He Zhiran and the officers fighting the snake.","Suspecting there might be more snakes around, some of the women and children were already screaming in terror.","The bolder men had no choice but to follow He Zhiran's example, find some sturdy branches nearby, and search the bushes to prevent being bitten by snakes while sleeping at night.","The officers did not object to the actions of the criminals. After all, they would also spend the night here and it was better to be safer.","However, the criminals could search but not leave their sight.","In fact, He Zhiran went to search the surroundings for more than one purpose.","Just now at the place where she argued with the officers, she discovered herbs in the bushes nearby.","On the road to exile, it was hard to guarantee her family would not suffer from some aches and pains. She could not keep taking modern medicines from her space for them.","If asked about it, she would have to rack her brains to explain.","But wild herbs she gathered would arouse no suspicion as they were from this time period.","Even if these herbs could not specifically treat their conditions, she would have a reasonable explanation for taking medicine from her space.","As He Zhiran looked for herbs, her progress was naturally slower than the others.","Seeing He Zhiran falling behind, several sisters-in-law and Mo Hanyue worried she might encounter danger alone.","The eldest sister-in-law could no longer sit still.","\"I'll go see the Ninth younger sister.\"","\"I'll go too.\"","\"I'll go too.\"","The other sisters-in-law also stood up.","Mo Hanyue looked at Old Lady Mo and saw she did not object, so she joined them.","The group ran up to He Zhiran and saw her using her clothes to hold a large pile of grass.","\"Ninth sister-in-law, weren't you looking for snakes? Why did you pull up so much grass?\" Mo Hanyue asked.","\"These are all commonly used medicinal herbs. I thought we might need them on the road, so I gathered some.\"","When Mo Hanyue heard these were actually medicinal herbs, her eyes lit up at once.","\"Ninth sister-in-law, you said these are medicinal herbs?\"","He Zhiran nodded and randomly picked up a medicinal plant to patiently explain, \"This is called ku di zi. It has the effect of clearing heat and detoxifying. This is che qian cao. It can not only treat illnesses but can also be used for cooking...\"","As Mo Hanyue listened to her ninth sister-in-law, she became more and more interested.","\"Ninth sister-in-law, I've remembered all the medicinal herbs you mentioned. I'll help you gather them too.\"","Although the eight sisters-in-law did not ask as many questions as Mo Hanyue, they also listened carefully to He Zhiran's explanations.","\"Ninth younger sister, we'll help too.\"","By the time the officers called for everyone to come back, no banded kraits were found, but the ten Mo women had gathered a lot of herbs to take back.","At this moment, Mo Hanyue had already cast off the gloom of not having mantou earlier. She went to Old Lady Mo to show off her spoils.","\"Mother, look at all the medicinal herbs I gathered.\"","Old Lady Mo lovingly stroked her head.","\"Your ninth sister-in-law is a wise one. You should learn from her in the future.\"","\"I understand, Mother.\"","While there was still light out, the sisters-in-law and Mo Hanyue worked together to clean and categorize the medicinal herbs as He Zhiran had instructed.","The people of the other families looked disdainfully at the actions of the Mo women.","\"It looks like the Mo family has really gone crazy from hunger, bringing back so much wild grass. Don't tell me they're planning to eat it?\"","\"Tsk tsk, they really are bold. Aren't they afraid those plants are poisonous?\"","\"It would be even better if they were poisonous. If the Mo people were poisoned to death, it would avenge us.\"","Because of the distance, the Mo family did not hear the muted voices.","He Zhiran had just finished laying out all the processed medicinal herbs on the open ground when shouts were heard from the officers' side.","\"Boss, what's wrong with you?\"","\"Someone come quick, the boss can't breathe...\"","Everyone looked in the direction of the officers.","They saw several officers surrounding Peng Wang.","\"Don't tell me the snake that bit the boss just now really was venomous?\"","Hearing this suspicion, the officers instantly recalled He Zhiran's warning.","Someone decisively made a decision.","\"Quick, carry the boss to find that articulate Mo woman.\"","Life was at stake, so none of the officers dared to delay. They hurriedly carried Peng Wang toward the Mo family.","The officers' words were heard by the Mo family.","Their gazes uniformly fell on He Zhiran.","\"He, act within your capabilities,\" Old Lady Mo reminded.","From He Zhiran leading the Mo women to gather herbs just now, it seemed she understood some medicine.","However, Peng Wang being bitten by a venomous snake was not something that could be handled with just some medicinal knowledge.","If Peng Wang really died, these officers might push responsibility onto He Zhiran in order to find someone to blame.","Of course He Zhiran understood the meaning behind her mother-in-law's reminder.","\"Mother, don't worry, I won't casually intervene.\"","As she spoke, the officers had already carried Peng Wang to the Mo family's location.","\"Lady He, say your snakebite treatment method again.\"","He Zhiran expressionlessly looked at the people, speaking slowly and deliberately.","\"The method I described is only useful right after being bitten by the snake.\"","\"Then what should be done now?\" The officer was anxious.","He Zhiran knew that after being bitten by a banded krait, a person would not die so quickly.","Therefore, she deliberately slowed her movements, ambling toward Peng Wang at a snail's pace. Her goal was to make the officers anxious.","Sure enough, seeing her slow movements made the officer angry.","\"Hurry up, what should be done?\"","Even when urged, He Zhiran was not annoyed. She simply stood in place and did not move.","\"Now you are asking me for help. Is this how you ask people for favors?\"","These officers were used to domineering and showing off before prisoners. He Zhiran did not want to continue indulging them.","The road ahead was still long. She did not want to live watching their faces every day.","She had to take this opportunity to let these officers recognize that she, He Zhiran, was not someone who could be casually intimidated into compromising.","Seeing this, Zhang Qing wanted to continue scolding, and had habitually reached for the whip coiled at his waist.","The Eighth Old Zhou promptly stopped him.","\"The boss's life comes first.\"","Zhang Qing immediately halted his actions, glaring fiercely at He Zhiran but not speaking again.","The Eighth Old Zhou stood up, \"Name any conditions you want.\"","He Zhiran was in no hurry to propose conditions. As a professional doctor, the first thing she had to do was understand the patient's condition."]},{"number":22,"title":"Chapter 22: Li Roer","paragraphs":["Although she knew that Peng Wang was poisoned by a silver ring snake, she would not be so reckless without fully confirming there was a cure.","Squatting down in front of Peng Wang, He Zhiran first pried open his eyelids to check, then took his pulse, and finally examined the wound on his leg.","Judging by Peng Wang's current state, he would probably be beyond saving if he had come to find her half an hour later.","Fortunately, her clinic had a few vials of the right antiserum.","One could also say that meeting her was Peng Wang's fate to not die prematurely.","After examining him, He Zhiran slowly stood up under everyone's gaze and returned to the pile of sorted herbs.","She found a bitter-tasting dragon gall herb and broke it off.","He Zhiran handed the dragon gall herb to Zhang Qing, who had just shouted at her.","Dragon gall did not actually treat snake venom, but she happened to be the resentful type.","\"Chew this up and use it to dress the wound later,\" she said.","Zhang Qing was unwilling.","\"Why don't I just pound it with two rocks instead of chewing it?\"","\"If you pound it with rocks, the herbal essence will be lost,\" He Zhiran was clearly somewhat impatient.","Zhang Qing knew he had to chew up this herb for his boss's life.","However, he did not completely trust He Zhiran.","\"You wouldn't be getting back at me for scolding you earlier by giving me poisonous herbs, would you?\"","He Zhiran rolled her eyes. She had not expected this official to be so wary.","\"If you're afraid, then don't do it. Your boss's life and death have nothing to do with me anyway.\"","Seeing this, The Eighth Old Zhou urged, \"Zhang Qing, just listen to the Hes for the boss's sake!\"","Zhang Qing's face was already wrinkled up, ready to bravely sacrifice himself.","Just as he was about to put the dragon gall herb to his mouth, a young woman came running swiftly from the Li family's direction.","\"Sir, don't listen to He Zhiran. She doesn't know medicine at all. Don't let her trick you.\"","He Zhiran squinted at the newcomer, searching the original owner's memories - it was an acquaintance.","Li family maid - Li Rou'er.","The only one the original owner had considered a good friend. He Zhiran recognized her at a glance.","Moreover, the original owner had absolutely refused to marry into the Mo family, which was closely related to this Li Rou'er.","Li Rou'er had always nagged her, saying that any woman who married into the Mo family quickly became a widow.","Why should she have to live as a widow in the prime of her youth?","In short, everything Li Rou'er discussed with the original owner revolved around the word \"widow\".","As a result, the original owner developed a fear of marrying into the Mo family, which led to the later incident of He Yuanming and his wife drugging her.","It could be said that the original owner's death was directly related to Li Rou'er.","Thinking of all this, He Zhiran's gaze at Li Rou'er became sharper. Moreover, she had just tried to undermine her, hardly behavior befitting a good friend.","\"Li Rou'er, since you say I don't know medicine, why don't you cure the officer's poison yourself?\"","He Zhiran said and turned away.","Li Rou'er was stunned for a moment in response to He Zhiran's attitude.","The He Zhiran she knew had always been obedient to her, never this firm before.","Could it be she had made up her mind to marry into the Mo family after all?","While Li Rou'er was lost in thought, The Eighth Old Zhou looked at her unpleasantly.","\"Who are you to come cause trouble?\"","Li Rou'er was scolded back to her senses.","\"Sir, I'm telling the truth. I'm always with He Zhiran but I've never heard she knows any medicine. Don't let her trick you.\"","Hearing Li Rou'er's earnest words, the officials hesitated.","However, after seeing the already dying Peng Wang, they were truly helpless.","Especially out here in the wilderness, it was impossible to call for a doctor.","The officials huddled together to discuss, and finally decided to grasp at straws and keep letting He Zhiran help cure their boss.","Zhang Qing called towards He Zhiran's back, \"Miss He, come back and keep curing the poison.\"","He Zhiran stopped and turned around, but her gaze fell on Li Rou'er.","She said with a mocking smile, \"Li Rou'er said I don't know medicine. Aren't you afraid I'll kill him instead of curing him?\"","Hearing this, Zhang Qing's face immediately darkened.","This time his anger was directed at Li Rou'er.","\"Who do you think you are, interfering in official business? Looks like you're tired of living.\"","To vent his anger, Zhang Qing directly took out his whip from his waist and lashed out fiercely at Li Rou'er.","\"Ah...\" Li Rou'er let out a scream as she was whipped.","At the same time, another woman who looked to be in her thirties came running again from the Li family's side.","The woman fearfully shielded Li Rou'er, pleading in a low voice,","\"Sir, my young miss doesn't know any better. Please be the bigger person and don't take it to heart.\"","After being whipped, the stinging pain constantly reminded Li Rou'er that this was all He Zhiran's doing.","If not for He Zhiran's sarcasm, how could the official have whipped her?","From the corner of her eye, He Zhiran could see Li Rou'er glaring at her hatefully.","She glanced around, then said to Zhang Qing, \"Sir, weren't you worried the herb was poisonous earlier?\"","Zhang Qing was a little confused by her meaning and nodded woodenly.","He Zhiran glanced at the still furious Li Rou'er.","\"Actually, it doesn't matter who chews the herb.\"","Zhang Qing immediately understood and felt a trace of appreciation for He Zhiran's cleverness.","Why hadn't he thought of doing that?","Without hesitation, Zhang Qing handed the dragon gall herb to Li Rou'er.","\"If you don't want to keep getting beaten, chew this up.\"","Li Rou'er was unwilling internally but did not dare to object.","She could only pitifully chew up the dragon gall herb in front of everyone.","Her already unattractive features were immediately twisted up.","This medicine was so bitter...","Zhang Qing also reflexively swallowed mouthfuls of the sour liquid that had risen due to nausea.","After chewing it up, Li Rou'er spat the contents into her palm with a distorted expression.","\"Sir, is this enough?\"","Zhang Qing also did not know and gestured for He Zhiran to check.","He Zhiran made a show of looking at the green, disgusting mess in Li Rou'er's hand.","She reluctantly nodded.","\"That's good enough!\"","Having said that, she did not look at anyone else's reaction and returned to Peng Wang's side.","He Zhiran had the officials help roll up his pant leg higher to fully expose the wound.","Ignoring everyone's stares, she directly tore off a corner of Peng Wang's clothes and said to Zhang Qing, \"I need clean water.\"","Zhang Qing hurriedly took out his water flask and handed it to her.","He Zhiran used the water to soak that piece of cloth, then gently wiped Peng Wang's wound.","Although unsanitary, with so many people watching she could not take out alcohol swabs from her storage space and could only make do for now."]},{"number":23,"title":"Chapter 23: The Last Step in Detoxification","paragraphs":["He Zhiran kept squeezing out the poisoned blood while moving outward, waiting until most of the toxic blood had come out before cleaning the wound thoroughly.","After taking care of all this, He Zhiran only then turned to look at Li Rou'er.","\"Apply the medicine you just chewed up on the wound.\"","Li Rou'er was still standing there in a daze, as if she had not heard He Zhiran's words.","This angered Zhang Qing again.","\"What are you still standing there for? I told you to apply the medicine!\"","Li Rou'er was pulled back to her senses by this shout, she looked at He Zhiran, then looked at Peng Wang's injury.","\"Official... Sir, I dare not.\"","Zhang Qing was impatient, if it wasn't for seeing the disgusting stuff in Li Rou'er's palm, he would have wanted to do it himself.","Helplessly, he could only continue to urge.","\"Don't forget your own status, do whatever you are told to do.\"","The woman who had just rushed over to protect Li Rou'er trembled and stepped forward.","\"Sir, my young miss is timid, it's better if I do it!\"","With that, Zhu took the chewed up medicine from Li Rou'er's hand and applied it little by little to Peng Wang's wound.","\"Auntie.\"","Li Rou'er's original intention was that when she said she was afraid, the officials would let He Zhiran take action.","She didn't expect that her auntie would take the initiative so readily. Thinking of how she was unable to make He Zhiran lose face, she got angry.","But with so many officials present, she didn't dare make trouble, she could only suppress the anger in her heart and wait for a chance to continue making things difficult for He Zhiran.","At this moment, Zhou the Eighth was already somewhat anxious because he was worried about Peng Wang's condition. When he turned his head, he happened to meet Li Rou'er's cold eyes.","Such an expression made people feel disgusted as soon as they saw it.","\"You two, don't just stand there, go back to your places.\"","Zhu was timid, and when she saw the officials' fierce looks, her legs instantly went soft.","She didn't dare delay for a moment, and hurriedly pulled Li Rou'er to run back.","He Zhiran was just going through the motions of helping Peng Wang treat his wound.","The key to undoing the snake venom in his body was the antiserum in her space.","It's just that, with these officials coming and going around, she didn't have a suitable chance yet to take out the antiserum from her space.","While He Zhiran was trying to figure out what to do, Zhang Qing became impatient again.","\"Can you really cure snake venom? It's been so long since the medicine was applied, why is the boss still showing no signs of improvement?\"","Without waiting for He Zhiran to finish speaking, Zhang Qing eagerly asked.","\"I still have to use my master's exclusive medical techniques for the final step of curing the venom.\"","\"What are you still waiting for then? Hurry up and treat him.\" Zhang Qing urged again.","\"Sir, I already said, it's an exclusive medical technique.\" In her heart He Zhiran scolded Zhang Qing for being stupid, he didn't understand her hint at all.","Then a young official cleverly pulled Zhang Qing's sleeve.","\"Brother Zhang, what she means is that no outsiders can watch while she treats the boss.\"","Zhang Qing suddenly realized, but he was also conflicted.","He looked at the other officials, and was at a loss for a moment.","Because they were all somewhat uneasy about letting the unconscious boss leave their sight. If He Zhiran had any malicious intentions, their responsibility would be great.","Seeing the group of men being so indecisive, He Zhiran was also somewhat impatient.","\"I'll give you time to discuss it for one stick of incense, if time is up, I'll be helpless too.\"","Having said that, she turned around to leave.","Seeing He Zhiran about to leave, Zhou the Eighth called out to stop her.","\"You come back to treat the boss, I'll take responsibility for any consequences.\"","The other officials looked at Zhou the Eighth in unison, with some relief on their faces.","They knew clearly in their hearts too that Peng Wang's condition was very bad, if they didn't let He Zhiran treat him, he would only have a fate of waiting for death.","It's just that no one wanted to be the one to step up and make the decision.","Since someone was willing to come forward and decide, they all tacitly did not object.","He Zhiran looked at the surroundings, apart from several thick trees, there was almost no cover.","Fortunately, it was already dark now, as long as she was vigilant when taking action, no one would notice.","\"Carry him behind that thickest tree.\"","Eager to save the man, the officials did as told without a word, carrying Peng Wang to the location specified by He Zhiran.","\"Alright, all of you turn around and walk more than thirty steps away.\"","Without even turning her head, He Zhiran spoke in a commanding tone.","Pricking up her ears to listen as the retreating footsteps grew smaller and smaller until they stopped, she then started looking around.","Making sure no one could see her, she swiftly took out the antiserum and syringe from her space.","Looking at the antiserum in her hand, He Zhiran felt quite pained.","This was the latest developed limited edition high concentration antiserum. Due to the extremely precious materials needed to extract it, it had become something that was priceless and unavailable on the market.","Through a stroke of luck, He Zhiran had obtained these few vials of high concentration antiserum, and had kept them stored in the clinic's refrigerator, unwilling to sell them.","It could only be said that Peng Wang was fortunate, if it wasn't for running into her, he would certainly have lost his life.","If it wasn't for her space having a regeneration function, He Zhiran would have been reluctant to use it on Peng Wang.","Intravenous injection of the antiserum would have a better effect, but the current situation did not allow He Zhiran to operate that way. She could only choose intramuscular injection.","Using the tree to hide her actions, He Zhiran diluted the antiserum with saline according to the ratio, then lifted Peng Wang's sleeve, disinfected, injected, and removed the needle, with her movements almost in one go.","After keeping the remaining packaging and syringe in her space, He Zhiran carefully observed Peng Wang's breathing.","After about five minutes, Peng Wang's condition had greatly eased.","His originally somewhat purplish complexion from breathing difficulties gradually calmed, and his breathing became much smoother.","Estimated after one or two more hours, he would wake up.","After He Zhiran injected Peng Wang with the antiserum, she did not leave in a hurry, intending to observe for a while longer until his condition was completely stable before doing anything else.","While she was in no hurry, the waiting officials were anxiously fidgeting.","In the end, Zhang Qing still could not hold back and loudly asked, \"Ms. He, how is our boss's condition now?\"","In her previous life as a doctor, He Zhiran most disliked two types of patients' families.","One was those who doubted her, the other was those who impatiently urged her.","Zhang Qing had scored full marks on both these points.","\"What's with the yelling, if you don't trust me then go find another doctor.\"","He Zhiran had this kind of temperament, even if those people were officials it was no use."]},{"number":24,"title":"Chapter 24: Don't worry, He can't die.","paragraphs":["Zhang Qing was eager by nature, especially when being scolded by a prisoner he himself had exiled. He habitually took out the whip hanging from his waist.","The Eighth Old Zhou hurried to stop him.","\"Calm down.\"","Zhang Qing was unhappy and tried to get around The Eighth Old Zhou to continue teaching He Zhiran a lesson.","Mo Jiuye was lying on the wooden cart, watching it all from afar.","Seeing that Zhang Qing was about to take action, he was already prepared to stand up and save the person.","No matter what, Mo Jiuye would not let anyone bully his wife from the He family.","The He women were likewise. Ever since He Zhiran went to cure Peng Wang's snakebite, they had been worried.","They even ignored their hunger.","Old Lady Mo's sharp eyes noticed Mo Jiuye's chest rising and falling rapidly. She guessed her son's thoughts.","In order not to affect the overall situation, Old Lady Mo whispered beside the wooden cart,","\"Don't be impatient.\"","How could Mo Jiuye not be impatient?","Whether he had feelings for He Zhiran or not, as the only man in the He family, if he couldn't even protect the women at home, he might as well die.","However, in order not to worry his mother, he forcibly suppressed the urge to get up.","Just then, He Zhiran had already stood up from behind the tree and walked towards the officers.","She looked so calm, as if not afraid of Zhang Qing's whip at all.","Before The Eighth Old Zhou could speak, Zhang Qing shook off the hand restraining him and ran towards the tree.","\"He Zhiran, if you dare to lie, I'll beat you to death!\"","He Zhiran didn't even glance at him, just standing there with her arms crossed.","The Eighth Old Zhou was much more sensible than Zhang Qing. Instead of immediately checking on Peng Wang, he asked He Zhiran,","\"Are you sure the poison is cured?\"","\"I'm sure. What's more, I can tell you clearly that he will wake up within an hour.\"","Seeing He Zhiran's composure, The Eighth Old Zhou could confirm she wasn't lying.","\"Alright, as long as the chief wakes up, he certainly won't mistreat you.\"","He Zhiran had been busy for so long just for this sentence. But reason told her that nothing was certain until Peng Wang woke up.","\"Okay, you guys go take care of Officer Peng. I'm thirsty, tired and sleepy. I'm going to rest.\"","Having said that, He Zhiran walked towards the He family.","The Eighth Old Zhou didn't say anything, but he had already taken note in his heart.","He Zhiran had just taken a few steps when the He women all came to welcome her.","\"Sister-in-law, go back and rest.\" Fifth sister-in-law Zhao Jiajia hurried to support her.","Forget He Zhiran who had been busy saving lives, even they who hadn't moved much felt exhausted.","The other sisters-in-law surrounded He Zhiran as she returned to her seat.","\"He Zhiran, did you really cure the snake venom?\"","Old Lady Mo and Mo Jiuye had the same doubts. Before her son got married, she had also inquired about He Zhiran through some channels.","She only heard that He Zhiran was a young miss who rarely went out. She didn't know that she understood any medical skills.","However, since interacting with her last night, Old Lady Mo could confirm one thing - her ninth daughter-in-law was not simple.","Be it wisdom or skill, she was incomparable to the other eight daughters-in-law.","If she hadn't seen He Zhiran's parents treat her that way with her own eyes today, she would have even doubted He Zhiran's true identity.","Now there was no doubt about her identity, but her medical skills...","Were truly puzzling!","Of course He Zhiran could hear the doubt in her mother-in-law's tone.","She had thought it through before doing all this.","Among her many secrets, the only thing she could reveal was these medical skills.","Therefore, she had to find a reasonable excuse.","\"Mother, when I was young, I was fortunate to obtain a medical book left behind by a great master.","You must know that I don't like going out. I usually pass time at home reading medical books.","After a long time, I thoroughly understood the content of the medical books. Treating illnesses is not difficult for me now.\"","In Old Lady Mo's understanding, He Zhiran did rarely go out.","So she didn't doubt the reason she gave at all.","\"Since you really understand medicine, Mother will stop worrying.\"","Old Lady Mo felt there was no need to beat around the bush in front of her own family, and directly expressed her true feelings.","He Zhiran was really tired now.","Looking around, there was nothing but grass and big trees.","When the officers had raided their home, they didn't let them bring a single thread or needle, let alone any luggage.","Although she had goose down quilts from her past life in her space, she couldn't take them out to use.","This reminded her of a saying - I wander alone under the empty sky and earth, using the sky as quilt and the earth as mattress, with mountains and rivers as pillow.","Just as He Zhiran was lamenting to herself, Mo Hanyue spoke aggrievedly,","\"Mother, I'm hungry and sleepy, what should I do?\"","Speaking of this, Old Lady Mo was also distressed.","Forget about Mo Hanyue who had been pampered since childhood. All the other women, including herself, which one hadn't grown up in a rich family home?","Going hungry with only the stars as cover and sleeping on the ground, it would be odd if they didn't fall sick tomorrow.","She stroked Mo Hanyue's messy hair distressfully and said heavily, \"Hanyue, it's only our first day out. We'll have to live like this in the future, you must learn to adapt.\"","Facing a group of juniors, she could only stay strong. If she lost confidence in front of these children, everyone's mentality would completely collapse.","He Zhiran still couldn't be sure what kind of person Peng Wang was.","If he understood gratitude, it would be fine. He would definitely take care of the He family after waking up.","On the other hand, if he didn't acknowledge their life-saving grace at all, everything she did today would be in vain.","If that was the case, they would have to find other ways to improve the He family's situation.","At this moment, He Zhiran hoped that Peng Wang would wake up soon, and even more hoped that he would be someone who understood gratitude.","That way, perhaps they could have a better night.","Just as He Zhiran was lost in thought leaning against Mo Jiuye's wooden cart, excited laughter sounded from the officers' side.","\"Hahaha......so good, the chief is awake......\"","\"Chief, how are you feeling?\"","\"Chief, you nearly scared us to death.\""]},{"number":25,"title":"Chapter 25: What condition can I bring up now","paragraphs":["When everyone looked over, they saw a group of officials gathered around Peng Wang, inquiring after his health.","Peng Wang was still somewhat weak at this moment, but it didn't stop him from speaking.","\"Old Zhou the Eighth, what exactly happened to me?\"","\"Boss, you were bitten by a snake.\"","Hearing this, Peng Wang carefully recalled the situation before he lost consciousness.","The first thing he felt was that the place on his calf where the poisonous snake had bitten him felt a little numb, and the numb feeling gradually spread.","After that, he felt like he couldn't breathe, and then he didn't know anything.","\"I was bitten by a snake but didn't die?\"","In order to confirm that all of this was true, Peng Wang pinched his own cheek.","Only after feeling the pain did he believe it all.","Zhang Qing stepped forward: \"Boss, you really didn't die.\"","\"Who helped me get the poison out?\" Peng Wang looked around and made sure he was still in this desolate wilderness. Where did these people find a doctor?","Old Zhou the Eighth pointed in the direction of the Mo family: \"It was Mo Jiuye's new bride, He Zhiran.\"","Speaking of He Zhiran, the scene of her warning him appeared in Peng Wang's mind.","Thinking of this, Peng Wang felt somewhat ashamed.","At first when the girl was kind enough to warn him, he had snapped at her.","He swept his eyes around and finally rested his gaze on the several large packages brought from the capital.","\"Old Zhou, go give each person from the Mo family two steamed buns made of white flour. Also, ask them if they have any other requests. Try to satisfy them as much as possible, as long as it's not too excessive.\"","Old Zhou the Eighth knew that Peng Wang was someone who knew how to be grateful.","He also knew clearly that Peng Wang was doing this because he didn't want to owe the Mo family anything. After all, they still had a long road ahead, and their duty didn't allow them to be too lenient towards the exiles.","Seeing Old Zhou the Eighth walking over carrying a bag, the Mo family women became a little nervous.","Old Zhou the Eighth put the bag in front of everyone.","\"Our boss said to give each of you two steamed buns made of white flour.\"","Hearing that there were white flour buns, the Mo family couldn't help swallowing.","They were really too hungry.","Despite this, everyone tacitly did not move, their eyes unconsciously looking towards He Zhiran.","He Zhiran was also hungry, but her composure was stronger than the others.","She didn't say anything, just looked at Old Zhou the Eighth, knowing he had more to say.","\"Our boss said that Miss He saved his life, so if there are any conditions you want to propose, you can mention them now.\"","Hearing they could propose conditions, the eyes of the Mo family women lit up.","Did this mean their days ahead could get better?","He Zhiran didn't expect that Peng Wang would take the initiative to let her propose conditions.","At the same time, she also thought of a possibility - that Peng Wang wanted to repay the life-saving favor all at once, so things could continue as they were afterwards.","Since this was the case, she had to seize this opportunity.","Although He Zhiran already had plans in mind, she still looked at Old Lady Mo.","No matter what, it wasn't good to overstep the elder.","He Zhiran's behavior once again won Old Lady Mo's favor, and made her even more convinced of this daughter-in-law.","\"You saved the man, so think of what conditions you want. Just don't be too greedy.\"","Old Lady Mo knew her daughter-in-law was a very wise woman, and that she would certainly be even more thoughtful than herself when handling matters. She just needed to give a little reminder.","Since this was the case, He Zhiran didn't intend to be polite any longer.","At the same time, she fully agreed with Old Lady Mo's words - she couldn't be greedy, and had to leave some room for the future.","\"Sir, our requests are not much. We only hope that when you pass through the next county, you'll allow us to purchase some supplies.\"","For now, He Zhiran felt this one condition was enough.","She had endless silver in her hands. She just needed to buy more daily necessities, and other matters could be discussed.","Old Zhou the Eighth could hardly believe that when he let He Zhiran propose conditions, she had only made such a small request.","He could have agreed to this without reporting back to Peng Wang.","\"No problem, I promise you this. We'll pass through Yunlai County at noon tomorrow. We'll resupply there, and I'll send someone to accompany you shopping.\"","\"Good, thank you sir.\" He Zhiran didn't show much excitement when the other party agreed to her condition. She just calmly responded.","\"Don't you have any other requests?\" Old Zhou the Eighth didn't rush to leave.","He Zhiran hadn't intended to be greedy in the first place. But seeing Old Zhou the Eighth's manner, it seemed he looked down on her for not proposing enough conditions.","\"Since the sir is letting me speak, I also want the snake that was beat to death today.\"","Old Zhou the Eighth knitted his brows: \"What does a woman like you want that thing for?\"","\"Many things from the snake's body can be used in medicine.\" He Zhiran answered evasively. She couldn't tell them she wanted to make poison.","\"I'll agree to this too.\"","Seeing Old Zhou the Eighth's readiness to consent, He Zhiran didn't want to keep delaying him either.","\"I've said all my conditions.\"","\"Good, I'll go back and report to the boss now.\"","In Old Zhou the Eighth's mind, He Zhiran had saved Peng Wang's life, so these few things were far from enough to repay her.","After returning and reporting the matter to Peng Wang, he took the initiative to bring back several waterskins and the silver snake.","\"These waterskins were prepared to sell to the exiled criminals. Seeing that those people don't seem to have much money, they probably can't afford them. So we might as well give them to you.","We still have some white flour buns there. Now that the weather is hot, they'll go bad if we don't finish them, so I'll give you some more tomorrow morning.\"","After throwing the waterskins and the silver snake in front of He Zhiran, Old Zhou the Eighth turned around and left.","He Zhiran efficiently distributed two buns to each person.","Although the white flour buns weren't bad tasting, with no side dishes they were still difficult to swallow when so dry.","He Zhiran suddenly had an idea as her gaze fell upon the package He Yuanming had given her.","She hadn't had a chance to open the package and check the contents yet, so no one else knew what was inside.","He Zhiran stretched one hand into the package, while her consciousness entered her space.","The sliced braised beef she had newly bought was in the fridge there.","The braised beef packaging was a plastic bag, which of course could not be taken out for others to see. And she couldn't find the oil paper commonly used in this era for a moment.","Left with no choice, He Zhiran could only grab a large handful of braised beef with her hand.","In special times, being too particular was just being pretentious. As long as they could eat a little better, what mattered hygiene or lack thereof...","\"Mother, sisters-in-law, little sisters, this is the braised beef my father and mother sent me today. Please eat it together with the buns.\"","When they saw He Zhiran clutching a large handful of braised beef in her hand, everyone's eyes lit up.","But the rules they had followed since childhood told them that women could not eat so crudely like this, especially grabbing food and eating directly with their hands.","Just when everyone was conflicted, Old Lady Mo spoke up.","\"We should relax our rules a bit for now.\"","Old Lady Mo was a clear-minded person. She was the first to recognize the reality of the situation. By saying this, she intended to try accepting everything.","After all, they were no longer the wives and daughters of prominent families."]},{"number":26,"title":"Chapter 26: Sleeping on the Ground","paragraphs":["The eight sisters-in-law and Mo Hanyue had been drooling over the braised beef jerky, and with Old Lady Mo's words, they no longer had any qualms about eating it.","\"Mother is right, we are no longer the wives and daughters of wealthy families. Now being able to fill our stomachs is already very good.\"","\"Forget about all these rules, I Yang Manxin don't want them anymore.\"","It must be known that extremely hungry people will think anything tastes good when they see food.","What's more, the braised beef jerky He Zhiran took out looked very appetizing, and even seemed to smell better than what they had eaten before.","Seeing the once graceful and proper women sitting on the ground and wolfing down the food, He Zhiran spoke up to remind them.","\"Don't hurry everyone, there's more in the package. We can take out more if it's not enough.\"","Anyway, the items in her space had a regenerative function, so there would be as much braised beef jerky as needed.","Old Lady Mo took a bite of the braised beef jerky and felt it was the most delicious meat she had eaten in her life.","However, she did not agree with He Zhiran's words.","\"Keep some of what your parents gave you for yourself, you don't have to take it all out to share.\"","\"Mother, I still have a lot!\"","He Zhiran said, and took out another large handful of braised beef jerky to distribute to everyone.","Seeing this, Old Lady Mo did not try to persuade her further. After all, she herself also really liked eating it.","Looking at the Mo family women sitting there and ravenously eating steamed buns and braised beef jerky, the people from the other four families were already green with envy.","Why did the Mo family get to eat white flour buns?","And the guards had taken the initiative to give them water pouches.","They knew their own stomachs were rumbling with hunger, and if they wanted a drink of water they had to go beg the guards, who might reward them with a mouthful if they were in a good mood.","Because they had learned their lesson from the whipping earlier in the day, those people were furious but did not dare voice their grievances aloud.","Their eyes were like fire, staring fixedly at the Mo family members eating and drinking over there.","With so many unfriendly gazes on them, the Mo family women were not oblivious.","However, following Old Lady Mo's instructions, none of them looked up, only kept their heads lowered as they ate the white flour buns.","After the Mo family women had eaten and drank their fill, Old Lady Mo took the initiative to move next to He Zhiran and whispered:","\"We have to think of a way to let Jiuye eat something too.\"","Even without Old Lady Mo's reminder, this was something He Zhiran had thought of.","\"Mother, wait a little later, after everyone else is asleep, I'll bring food for my husband.\"","Mo Jiuye lying prone on the wooden cart had also smelled the aroma of the braised beef jerky.","This man who usually did not care much for food started unconsciously swallowing mouthfuls of saliva.","Unfortunately, in the eyes of others he had already lost consciousness, so he could not jeopardize the plan for a mouthful of food.","Mo Jiuye endured the torment over there with great difficulty, while the Mo family women finally ate and drank their fill.","Old Lady Mo instructed everyone to find a place to rest on their own.","Speaking of resting, except for He Zhiran, the other women's faces fell.","\"Mother, we're just going to sleep like this?\" Although Mo Hanyue knew this was the case, she still could not help but complain a little.","Old Lady Mo was also very helpless.","\"Hanyue, our Mo family is not what it used to be. It's already a luxury that we are alive, so don't think too much.\"","Hearing this, Mo Hanyue's tears flowed down uncontrollably.","However, she was sensible enough not to say anything more about it.","Old Lady Mo had given birth to ten children, and Mo Hanyue was her only daughter. Mo Hanyue had been doted on since she was little.","Seeing her daughter's appearance, Old Lady Mo's heart ached terribly.","But she had no choice but to bow to fate and make Mo Hanyue accept reality sooner.","\"If you can't even endure this much bitterness, then you are not fit to be a child of our Mo family.\"","Being able to become a child of the Mo family was what Mo Hanyue was most proud of.","Her father and brothers were all great heroes who defended the Great Shun Dynasty. Hearing her mother say she was unworthy of being a Mo family child, she immediately stopped crying and hurriedly wiped away her tears with her sleeve.","\"Mother, the Mo family is not afraid of hardship, and Hanyue is not afraid either.\"","After speaking, she curled up and lay down next to Old Lady Mo.","Old Lady Mo did not dare look at her daughter again, it pained her more the more she looked, so she could only turn her head elsewhere.","He Zhiran lay right against the wooden cart to make it convenient to bring Mo Jiuye food later at night.","In her previous life, she had often slept outdoors during missions in the wilderness, so she did not find any of this too unbearable.","Seeing the mother-in-law and the others lying down to rest, the sisters-in-law did not show any similar thoughts either, huddling closely together as they slept on the ground.","Perhaps because everyone was exhausted from traveling, they fell asleep soon after lying down.","He Zhiran did not sleep, only leaned there pretending to doze.","Just as she was about to open her eyes to observe and see if everyone was in deep sleep, she discovered the second sister-in-law had sat up.","The second sister-in-law groped silently to He Zhiran's side and whispered: \"Youngest sister-in-law, are you asleep?\"","He Zhiran also replied in a volume only the two of them could hear: \"Not yet, second sister-in-law, do you need something?\"","In the moonlight, it was evident the second sister-in-law had a conflicted expression, clearly having something to ask for.","\"That... um... youngest sister-in-law, I want to ask you for a white flour bun.\"","As the second sister-in-law spoke, she was noticeably very nervous, stuttering and continuously tugging at the hem of her clothes with both hands.","He Zhiran immediately guessed the second sister-in-law's intention, it was nothing more than wanting to bring it to her maternal family.","However, she did not want to be the kind of pushover who did foolish good deeds, after all those several families were hostile towards the Mo family.","Even if the second sister-in-law's maternal family had not insulted the Mo family like the other families, the hatred in their eyes towards the Mo family was impossible to conceal.","\"Second sister-in-law, you didn't eat your fill?\" He Zhiran deliberately played dumb.","The second sister-in-law vigorously shook her head.","\"No, it's because I want my nephew to eat.\"","Hearing this, seeing that He Zhiran had not given her a bun, the second sister-in-law knew she was probably unwilling.","\"Youngest sister-in-law, my father and the others must have some misunderstanding with the Mo family. With so many people earlier, we did not get to talk about this.","I figured, while it was late at night and everyone was asleep, I would bring a bun to my nephew, and also ask what exactly happened.\"","Seeing the second sister-in-law had said this much, He Zhiran could not remain indifferent.","Moreover, the other party wanted buns for a little child to eat. The grudges between adults had nothing to do with little children.","It was a good opportunity to find out at the same time why those families harbored such great hostility towards the Mo family.","He Zhiran took out a white flour bun from the bag, and also reached into her package to take out two slices of braised beef jerky.","\"Second sister-in-law, take these.\"","Seeing there was also braised beef jerky, the second sister-in-law thanked her profusely, moved.","\"Thank you youngest sister-in-law, I will definitely ask about the situation clearly before coming back.\"","\"Second sister-in-law, go quickly!\" He Zhiran revealed an innocuous smile.","After the second sister-in-law had gone far away, He Zhiran looked around again.","The guards had dispersed to the vicinity of each family, with one person on night watch duty at each location.","The one in charge of watching the Mo family was The Eighth Old Zhou. He had probably intentionally been lenient, and seeing the second sister-in-law head towards the Xie Family direction, did not try to stop her."]},{"number":27,"title":"Chapter 27: It's hard for her.","paragraphs":["Although He Zhiran guessed that The Eighth Old Zhou had deliberately let Second Sister-in-Law off easily, she didn't dare to openly give food to Mo Jiuye.","After all, Mo Jiuye pretending to be unconscious was something that had to be kept secret from all outsiders.","However, Mo Jiuye had not eaten anything for a whole day, let alone go to the toilet. If this continued, even someone made of iron would not be able to stand it.","Also, his wounds needed to be checked and dressed.","After thinking it over, He Zhiran could not come up with a good solution.","As a last resort, she decided to sacrifice herself a little.","She took out an olive green blanket from her space, using the package as cover.","Pretending to not be able to stand the dampness on the ground, she climbed onto the wooden cart.","To let The Eighth Old Zhou know that the movement here was caused by her, she deliberately muttered softly, \"The ground is really too cold, it's more comfortable on the cart.\"","As she spoke, she lay down next to Mo Jiuye and then covered both of them with the blanket.","Feeling the warmth beside him, Mo Jiuye's body gave a jerk.","If there was a mirror, he could see how red his face was right now.","He did not know what He Zhiran intended to do, so he could only close his eyes and try his best to calm his mind.","The movement He Zhiran made was not only noticed by The Eighth Old Zhou, but also by Old Lady Mo who had not fallen into deep sleep yet.","She took a look at the wooden cart, at the two people tightly wrapped under the blanket.","Old Lady Mo should not have had any other ideas at this time, but seeing the intimate appearance of the two, she could not help but think more of it.","Her ninth daughter-in-law really liked her son, accompanying her husband to sleep even at a time like this.","This was good too. If they could safely reach the northwest, have them consummate the marriage earlier and give birth to many grandchildren to continue the Mo family line.","The Eighth Old Zhou thought differently.","Moreover, he also negated some of the good impression he had of He Zhiran.","Other than knowing some medical skills, this woman was no different from other women in wealthy households competing for favor.","Her husband was unconscious, yet she was still thinking of getting in bed...","Even so, he did not have the habit of watching a married couple sleep together. He just glanced over to make sure they would not do anything improper, before looking away.","After observing the situation around her again, seeing that no one was watching them, He Zhiran carefully took out two white steamed buns and a large handful of braised beef and stuffed them into Mo Jiuye's hands.","In addition, she also gave him several alcohol swabs and a small bottle of Yunnan Baiyao.","She whispered into Mo Jiuye's ear in a volume that only the two of them could hear.","\"Hurry up, find a place where no one can see you, eat some food, then treat your wounds. I'll find something else to put in your original position so that the officials won't notice.\"","Only then did Mo Jiuye understand that this woman intended to use a strategy of disguising to deceive people.","She really went through a lot of trouble for him.","Without any doubt, knowing that this was a rare opportunity, Mo Jiuye rolled under the cart with a flip of his body, landing without a sound.","His lightness skill was clearly superb.","At the first moment Mo Jiuye left the wooden cart, He Zhiran had already taken out a cotton quilt and placed it in his original position.","Indeed, in the dark of night and with the quilt as cover, no one would possibly see that it was not Mo Jiuye lying there.","She also took the chance while Mo Jiuye was away to check the purse He Yuanming had given her.","Inside was a stack of silver notes, which she confirmed to be three thousand taels after counting. Aside from that, there were also some scattered silver ingots, around twenty taels by estimation.","In this era, so much silver placed in an ordinary family's home could provide for generations without worry.","It showed how dearly the two old Hes loved their daughter.","Mo Jiuye moved very quickly. With a flash of his lightness skill he soon disappeared from He Zhiran's sight.","After about two quarters of an hour, Mo Jiuye returned.","Hearing the sound, He Zhiran immediately put away the cotton quilt. Only after Mo Jiuye lay in his original spot did she heave a deep sigh.","\"How are your wounds?\" He Zhiran asked softly.","\"They've stopped bleeding,\" Mo Jiuye replied just as softly.","He thought for a moment, then added, \"Thank you for everything you've done for me and the Mo family.\"","In He Zhiran's heart, this was not the time for pleasantries. Hearing Mo Jiuye's thanks, she did not respond.","Just as she was considering whether to continue lying here, Second Sister-in-Law came back.","Thinking everyone was asleep, Second Sister-in-Law tip-toed to the wooden cart.","But she did not see He Zhiran.","Just as she was about to look around, He Zhiran sat up from the wooden cart.","\"Second Sister-in-Law, I'm here.\"","Following the voice, Second Sister-in-Law saw that her ninth younger sister-in-law and ninth younger brother were sleeping in the same quilt.","She wished she could slap herself.","The newlywed couple was having an intimate moment, yet she had come to disturb them untimely.","\"Ninth younger sister-in-law, you continue resting. We can talk tomorrow.\"","Seeing Second Sister-in-Law's reaction, He Zhiran knew she had misunderstood.","Moreover, she urgently wanted to know the reason why those families were targeting the Mo family. Where would she have the patience to wait until tomorrow?","\"Second Sister-in-Law, I was just giving my husband some food earlier.\"","Since everyone in the Mo family knew Mo Jiuye was pretending to be unconscious, He Zhiran directly told the truth.","Hearing He Zhiran's explanation, Second Sister-in-Law felt somewhat embarrassed.","So she had thought wrongly.","\"Ninth younger sister-in-law, I just asked and found out the reason.\"","Second Sister-in-Law felt it was more suitable to tell He Zhiran now. On the surface, she was informing He Zhiran, but it could also let Mo Jiuye understand the situation.","Sure enough, Mo Jiuye had already pricked up his ears, intending to listen carefully.","He Zhiran urged, \"Second Sister-in-Law, tell me quickly.\"","Second Sister-in-Law sighed.","\"I guess someone must have deliberately caused this.\"","He Zhiran became even more interested.","\"What exactly happened?\"","\"My eldest brother said that before the Xie family was exiled, there was not the slightest sign.","Today the officials came with an imperial edict, saying that Guardian of the Nation Mo Jiuye had already confessed to colluding with the enemy and betraying the country.","It also said that Jiuye had voluntarily exposed that the Xie family was also involved. Aside from that, he had also presented evidence that my father had accepted bribes several years ago.","My maternal family all feel that the amount my father accepted as bribes was not large, and it only happened twice. It was not enough to confiscate the family property and exile them. The main reason was because Jiuye exposed that the Xie family had colluded with him to betray the country.\"","He Zhiran fell into contemplation.","It was impossible for Mo Jiuye to do such a thing.","Moreover, if she had not told him herself, he would not even have known that the Mo manor would be raided and exiled. Let alone make any confessions.","If what Second Sister-in-Law said was true, there was only one possibility.","And that was the Xie family had offended Emperor Shunwu. Emperor Shunwu took the chance to get rid of the Xie family, while creating more trouble for Mo Jiuye on the road to exile.","Other than this, she could not think of any other reasons.","As for the other three families, although she had not personally heard them state their reasons for insulting the Mo family, this was also a possibility that could not be ruled out.","Mo Jiuye was similarly pondering over the ins and outs of this matter.","His thoughts were almost the same as He Zhiran's. Moreover, he was more familiar with the officials from those families in court, and knew a little about their shady dealings.","Especially Fang Chuanzhou, with whom he had no grudges at all.","According to Mo Jiuye's understanding, this person had indeed offended Emperor Shunwu before."]},{"number":28,"title":"Chapter 28: Husband and Wife Night Talk (Part 1)","paragraphs":["Last year's imperial banquet, if he remembered correctly.","Fang Chuanzhou attended with his wife and eldest daughter Fang Mingzhu. Emperor Shunwu took a liking to their daughter at first sight.","Taking advantage of the drinking, Emperor Shunwu unabashedly disregarded propriety and wanted to take Fang Mingzhu into his harem.","Unexpectedly, Fang Mingzhu was unwilling and publicly refused Emperor Shunwu's \"kind intentions\" on the grounds that she already had a marriage agreement.","Fang Chuanzhou was also unwilling for his daughter to enter the palace and compete with so many women for favor. He knelt down to speak up for Fang Mingzhu.","With so many ministers present, Emperor Shunwu could not forcibly keep her in the harem. He could only reluctantly let her leave.","The second day after leaving the imperial banquet, Fang Mingzhu hurriedly married someone.","Based on Mo Jiuye's understanding of this emperor, he must have resented this and would take this opportunity to confiscate the Fang family's property and exile them, while also adding to his own troubles.","As for the Li family and He family, they had never gotten along well with Mo Jiuye to begin with. It was easy to guess the reason why the Emperor sent them along to be exiled with him.","Seeing He Zhiran was still sitting there deep in thought, he gently hooked her finger.","When He Zhiran looked back, he said softly: \"I'll tell you about these families' matters when there is a chance in the future.\"","Hearing Mo Jiuye say this, it meant he had already figured out the situation.","Since someone understood clearly, the Mo family didn't need to play blind. He Zhiran simply didn't want to get further involved.","\"Okay.\" She casually responded, indifferent to whether Mo Jiuye would tell her or not.","She had already made clear her own purpose, which was first to change Mo Jiuye's fate of dying on the road to exile.","The sister-in-law felt that she had explained her matter clearly and didn't want to continue disturbing the young couple's rest.","\"Younger brother and sister-in-law, this sister-in-law will go back to rest now.\"","He Zhiran had gotten on the wagon to help Mo Jiuye escape, and although the purpose was already accomplished, they should have gone their separate ways to avoid awkwardness.","But if she laid down for a bit and then left, it might make the Eighth Old Zhou suspicious.","Helpless, she could only stiffly lie back down in her original position.","To let her sleep more comfortably, Mo Jiuye deliberately shifted over a little.","Although tired from the journey, He Zhiran was wide awake now.","Mo Jiuye seemed to sense she hadn't fallen asleep, and asked softly:","\"Can't sleep?\"","\"Mm.\" He Zhiran responded absently.","\"Is it because of what sister-in-law said?\" Mo Jiuye asked.","\"I guess so!\" He Zhiran didn't even know why she was having insomnia. Perhaps it was suddenly being in a strange environment and not quite used to it yet.","However, she didn't want to mention any of this to Mo Jiuye.","Mo Jiuye didn't read between the lines and only heard her tone, failing to realize He Zhiran was being evasive with him.","\"The He family and Li family have had some friction with me.\"","Since Mo Jiuye took the initiative to speak, He Zhiran had nothing better to do with her insomnia, so she might as well listen carefully.","\"What friction?\" she asked.","\"He Zhiyuan was originally the Minister of the Ministry of War. When I led troops in battle, he deliberately embezzled military provisions to line his own pockets. I had memorialized this matter to the Emperor at the time.","The Emperor sent people to thoroughly investigate the matter, but I don't know why, for such a big deal, the Emperor only demoted He Zhiyuan's position. He went from Minister of the Ministry of War to Vice Minister of the Ministry of War.\"","After listening to Mo Jiuye's account, He Zhiran had another guess in mind.","\"According to what you said, it sounds like the Emperor had long intended to act against the Mo family. He didn't immediately deal with He Zhiyuan, but kept him around to make things difficult for you?\"","Mo Jiuye didn't expect this woman to analyze things so thoroughly.","It had taken him almost a full day to think things through clearly and arrive at this conclusion after careful consideration.","He felt more and more that He Zhiran was extraordinary.","Since they had already talked this far, He Zhiran was also intrigued.","\"What about the Li family then?\"","When it came to grievances with the Li family, Mo Jiuye didn't know how to bring it up for a moment.","After deliberating, he still chose to tell the blunt truth.","\"My grievance with the Li family can be said to stem from Li Rou'er.\"","Hearing the implication in Mo Jiuye's words, it sounded like he and Li Rou'er were somewhat involved.","Thinking this, her interest grew even stronger.","\"What was your relationship?\"","At the same time, He Zhiran also searched the original host's memories, looking for whether Li Rou'er had ever mentioned Mo Jiuye to her.","She searched for a long time until her head hurt, but still came up empty-handed.","This showed that Li Rou'er had never spoken a word about Mo Jiuye in front of the original host.","\"We didn't have any relationship.\" Mo Jiuye answered decisively.","\"Then why did you say your grievance with the Li family started because of her?\"","Hearing He Zhiran's probing question, Mo Jiuye instinctively felt this woman might be jealous.","So he quickly explained.","\"Her carriage went out of control on the street, charging around recklessly. I happened to run into it and helped control the horse out of good intentions.","At the time, I didn't think much of this incident. I thought it was all over, but unexpectedly, Li Liang brought gifts to my residence the next day, saying it was his daughter thanking me for saving her life.","And he mentioned sending Li Rou'er to the Duke's Mansion as a concubine. I rejected it on the spot, saying I already had a marriage agreement with you, and that it is a Mo family rule that Mo men do not take concubines.","Li Liang didn't have any abnormal reaction when I refused him. It wasn't until three days later when I went out again that I ran into Li Rou'er once more.","You could say she deliberately waited outside the Duke's Mansion entrance.","I was going to ignore her and leave directly, but her two maidservants blocked my way.","Li Rou'er claimed we already had intimate physical contact and I had to take responsibility for her.","When I helped control her horse, there was no contact between us at all. This was clearly her being shameless.","Therefore, I didn't give her any face and didn't explain, directly riding away on horseback.","After that, I noticed Li Liang opposing me in everything, no matter what I said, he would rack his brains to refute it.","Aside from the Li Rou'er incident, I can't think of how else I offended Li Liang...\"","After listening to Mo Jiuye explain so much, He Zhiran also figured out one fact. Li Rou'er deliberately got close to her and talked about how bad the Mo family was every day, in order to make her regret the marriage so Li Rou'er could marry Mo Jiuye instead.","\"Did what you said happen early this year?\"","\"You know about it?\" Mo Jiuye asked back.","Since they had talked this far, He Zhiran didn't intend to hide it either.","She recounted in full detail how Li Rou'er had persuaded her not to marry into the Mo family, and this incident happened right after Mo Jiuye rejected Li Rou'er.","Hearing this, Mo Jiuye's dark eyes sank.","\"I didn't expect a young lady to have such sinister intentions. She really is despicable.\"","\"Very despicable indeed. She pretended to care about me in front of me before, but couldn't wait to reveal her true colors after being exiled for a day.\"","Speaking of Li Rou'er, He Zhiran was very contemptuous.","This was a thoroughly despicable character that He Zhiran looked down on the most.","Seeing He Zhiran unhappy, Mo Jiuye thought it was because of the baseless affair between him and Li Rou'er.","To ease the atmosphere, he added: \"I've already read your father's letter.\""]},{"number":29,"title":"Chapter 29: Husband and Wife Night Talk (Part 2)","paragraphs":["He Zhiran only then remembered that her father had also slipped a letter into Mo Jiuye's hands today.","Since the letter was for Mo Jiuye, she did not have the habit of prying into other people's privacy. Although curious about what was written inside, she did not take the initiative to ask.","Mo Jiuye was able to mention this letter, so he did not intend to conceal the contents.","\"The contents of the letter are very simple. My father-in-law said he would privately collect evidence of my innocence to help me reverse the verdict, and he also hopes that I can treat you well.\"","\"That's all?\" He Zhiran was clearly a little unbelievable.","Mo Jiuye affirmed: \"Well, just that.\"","He Zhiran fell into thought again.","After her parents came to see her off today, the first thing she thought of was her father's situation at court.","He Yuanming was Mo Jiuye's father-in-law. Would Emperor Shunwu vent his anger on him as a result?","If this is really the case, wouldn't He Yuanming's days to come be like an ant on a chopping block, with the possibility of being crushed by Emperor Shunwu at any time?","Seeing He Zhiran lost in thought, Mo Jiuye spoke again.","\"My father-in-law is clean and honest in office, and handles things in an orderly manner. The emperor is reluctant to lose such a capable minister, so don't worry too much.\"","After listening to Mo Jiuye's words, He Zhiran felt a little more at ease.","\"It's getting late, go to bed earlier, we still have to travel tomorrow.\" Mo Jiuye was worried that He Zhiran's body could not stand it.","After talking so much, and wasting a lot of brain cells thinking, He Zhiran was also feeling sleepy now.","\"Okay, you rest early too.\"","She thought she could fall asleep as soon as she closed her eyes, but He Zhiran still tossed and turned, and even though she was sleepy, she still couldn't fall asleep.","The space in the wooden cart was not very large, and she and Mo Jiuye were almost pressed tightly together.","Feeling each other's body heat, not only He Zhiran, but Mo Jiuye was also having trouble sleeping.","Hearing her breathing was not so steady, Mo Jiuye spoke again softly.","\"Pretending to be in a coma is not a lasting solution. I plan to wake up after we are out of the capital.\"","\"You can decide the timing yourself.\" He Zhiran replied vaguely.","In fact, Mo Jiuye had ulterior motives when he said this.","The purpose of what he said was to draw out He Zhiran.","Who knew, she just told him to make up his own mind, and didn't say anything he didn't already know.","\"Aren't you curious why I plan to wake up after we're out of the capital?\"","\"I guess you're worried there are the emperor's spies watching us.\"","This is what He Zhiran thought, and Mo Jiuye's ideas matched hers completely.","\"If it was just me it would be okay, escaping from here would be easy, and I could disappear forever without being found.","But there are too many Mohist women and children, I can't be sure I can take care of everyone.","Moreover, your maternal relatives are in the capital city. Once I take you away, those relatives of yours in the capital will also likely get implicated.","I feel even more sorry for you, having just married into the Mo family, but having to be exiled along with us.","My mother and sisters-in-law are pitiful enough already, having to suffer this misfortune. \"","His heartfelt words unconsciously showed that Mo Jiuye had begun to believe in He Zhiran.","He Zhiran could understand Mo Jiuye's helplessness.","After all, she had witnessed his martial arts skill with her own eyes. Trying to escape under the noses of these yamen runners was simply a walk in the park for him.","This showed that Mo Jiuye was not a selfish person.","\"It's happened already, what we need to do now is protect our family and ourselves, with the first goal being to arrive safely in the northwest.\"","As for her knowledge of subsequent historical events, He Zhiran did not mention it.","Because her arrival had already changed the number of times Mo Jiuye was recorded in history as being beaten with a plank.","She believed that this history was very likely to continue to change because of her arrival.","Mo Jiuye was actually already disheartened, he did not dare to guarantee that the whole family could arrive intact in the northwest.","But after listening to He Zhiran's words, he felt a surge of confidence.","He was a towering man, the only hope for the Mohist family.","If even he was thinking of going with the flow, how would his mother, wife, sisters and sisters-in-law manage?","He had to pull himself together and face all future difficulties positively.","\"I will definitely do my best to keep everyone alive.\"","Perhaps it was the too depressing content of their conversation that successfully distracted He Zhiran.","At this moment, she had forgotten the fact that she was sleeping next to a man.","The two chatted briefly about future plans again, and He Zhiran unknowingly fell asleep.","Hearing the steady breathing beside him, Mo Jiuye thoughtfully pulled the quilt up to cover her before slowly closing his eyes.","Although He Zhiran had fallen asleep, her habit of getting up early from her previous life had not been lost.","She woke up before dawn.","Taking advantage of the fact that the others were still sleeping, she took the quilt covering her and Mo Jiuye and put it away.","Mo Jiuye had been in a light sleep state all night. Feeling the disappearance of the quilt on him, he knew He Zhiran was getting up.","He Zhiran looked around, everyone was still sleeping, and the yamen runner on duty was not as alert as in the first half of the night.","She took out two more white steamed buns and a little preserved meat, and handed them to Mo Jiuye along with the water flask.","\"Take this opportunity while everyone is still asleep to go eat something first.\"","\"Okay.\" Mo Jiuye replied, quickly taking the food and getting off the cart.","Not long after Mo Jiuye came back from eating and drinking, people began waking up one after another.","The yamen runners began distributing the black steamed buns again.","Everyone looked at the black steamed buns that were comparable to rocks, and it could be said that it was extremely unbearable.","But in order to survive, they could only force themselves to swallow it.","The treatment of the Mohist family was different.","The Eighth Old Zhou had said that there would still be some white steamed buns for them in the morning.","He was as good as his word, leaving enough white steamed buns for the yamen runners to last until Yunlai County, and giving the rest to the Mohist family members.","What the others didn't know was that the reason why the Eighth Old Zhou gave white steamed buns to the Mohists was not because he and Peng Wang were so grateful for He Zhiran's life-saving grace.","The real reason was that they had miscalculated on this errand.","Usually before departure, they would prepare two kinds of steamed buns, black ones were free, and they could earn some silver taels from the white ones."]},{"number":30,"title":"Chapter 30: There's still Poison in Your Body.","paragraphs":["Who knew, the exiled criminals this time were different from the past, and they didn't even have a penny on them.","At this hot weather, steamed buns couldn't be kept for a few days before going bad.","With so many government clerks present, they couldn't possibly finish eating all these steamed buns.","The Eighth Old Zhou thought, it'd be better to give these steamed buns to Peng Wang to repay him for saving their lives, rather than letting them go moldy and throwing them away.","Peng Wang didn't object to this idea either, and that was how these white flour steamed buns ended up in the hands of the Mo Family so easily.","This time, He Zhiran didn't take out any food from her interspatial ring, after all the package Old Master He Yuanming gave her was only so big, and she had taken out so much marinated beef and a quilt yesterday.","If she kept taking things out without restraint, it would definitely arouse suspicions.","Although the Mo Family people were only nibbling on white flour steamed buns, for these exiled criminals it was already very satisfying.","Perhaps because the second sister-in-law went to deliver white flour steamed buns to her nephew at the Xie family last night, today the Xie family's hostility towards Mo Jiuye lessened somewhat. Seeing the Mo Family eating white flour steamed buns, they didn't stare at them with hostile eyes like the people from the other three families.","The people from those three families stared at the Mo Family like knives.","If not for fearing the government clerks, they would have hurled insults long ago.","While eating the steamed buns, He Zhiran glanced at those people from the corner of her eyes.","She happened to meet the sinister gaze of Li Rou'er.","He Zhiran deliberately annoyed her by raising the steamed bun in her hand and showing Li Rou'er a big smile.","The provocative meaning was extremely obvious.","Li Rou'er was not to be outdone either. She raised her hand and clenched her fist, posing as if she was about to hit someone.","He Zhiran still maintained her smile, except that smile no longer reached her eyes. She continued eating the steamed bun with big bites.","The little interaction between the two did not escape Old Lady Mo's eyes. It could be said that He Zhiran did this without trying to hide it from anyone.","From the trouble Li Rou'er deliberately caused for He Zhiran yesterday, Old Lady Mo could see that these two knew each other and held grudges.","However, she also saw that her daughter-in-law was formidable, and did not worry too much.","Later she just needed to remind the others to be careful of Li Rou'er.","After all, she understood clearly that it was hard to deal with little demons when the King of Hell wants to see you.","Just as the Mo Family finished eating their fill and were tidying up themselves, the Eighth Old Zhou and Peng Wang came over.","Seeing this, the Mo Family reflexively became nervous.","The Eighth Old Zhou said in a commanding tone, \"Our boss was bitten by a snake yesterday and his body is still a little weak, so he needs to sit in Mo Jiuye's wooden cart for now.\"","Old Lady Mo asked somewhat uncertainly, \"Does the official mean for Jiuye to get off the cart?\"","\"If he doesn't get off, can he expect the boss to squeeze onto a cart with convicts?\" The Eighth Old Zhou was a little unhappy right away.","Old Lady Mo was in a difficult spot.","\"Official, as you know, we of the Mo Family are all women. If Jiuye can't stay on the cart, how are we going to travel together with him?\"","\"That's right, official. Aren't you deliberately making things difficult for us?\" The outspoken second sister-in-law chimed in.","At this point, without waiting for the Eighth Old Zhou to say anything, Peng Wang flared up.","\"It looks like you don't want to live! You actually dare to disobey the government clerks!\"","Seeing that the Mo Family was about to suffer a loss, the people from the other families watched this side with schadenfreude.","In fact, many people were cheering Peng Wang and the Eighth Old Zhou on in their hearts, hoping they would teach the Mo Family a good lesson.","Seeing that her daughter-in-law was about to stir up trouble, Old Lady Mo hurriedly pulled her aside.","However, facing this situation, she was also at a loss for what to do.","Lying on the wooden cart, Mo Jiuye listened to the conversation between the two sides and already had a plan.","Once his wooden cart was taken for Peng Wang's use, he certainly couldn't let the women carry him while traveling. If that really happened, he could only choose to regain consciousness ahead of time.","Just as Mo Jiuye was thinking about how to wake up, he heard He Zhiran speak up.","She walked up to Peng Wang unhurriedly, and her tone could be considered rather respectful too.","\"Peng Official, are you feeling a little short of breath and chest tightness right now?\"","Peng Wang did have these feelings, and quite severely too. Otherwise, he wouldn't have come to wrestle the wooden cart from Mo Jiuye either.","\"That's right, I feel a little out of breath after walking just a few steps.\"","In Peng Wang's view, He Zhiran was a young lady from a prestigious family. She probably read about emergency treatment for snake bites in some book and happened to save his life by coincidence.","He was clear about his own physical condition. Although he felt discomfort, it wouldn't be as severe as yesterday.","After arriving at Yunlai County, he could find an imperial physician to take a good look and prescribe some medicine to recuperate.","But to his surprise, He Zhiran was actually able to point out his current symptoms accurately.","This made it very likely that He Zhiran did know medical techniques. Therefore, when he answered, he was not vague at all.","\"He Zhiran, you do have a way to deal with the remaining venom in me yesterday. Although I saved your life, there is still residual venom in your body. If it's not treated promptly, it will still be life-threatening.\"","In fact, Peng Wang's snake venom had been completely cleared out. The reason he had symptoms was because the venom had damaged some nerve systems in his body.","Basically it could heal by itself within a week.","However, in order to avoid the situation of the Mo Family's women carrying Mo Jiuye while traveling, she could only try to intimidate Peng Wang with words.","Peng Wang completely believed He Zhiran's words, after all, his own physical condition was right there.","\"Miss He, do you have a way?\"","This was exactly what He Zhiran was waiting for.","\"There is a way, but...\"","As she spoke, she looked towards Mo Jiuye lying on the wooden cart.","A sly person like Peng Wang immediately understood He Zhiran's implication.","He suddenly turned black-faced.","In all his years working as a government clerk, this was the first time he was asked for conditions by a convict.","Peng Wang wanted to say, he didn't need her treatment. He could find an imperial physician after arriving at Yunlai County. Mo Jiuye had to give up the wooden cart today no matter what.","But before he could get the words out, the Eighth Old Zhou pulled him aside and whispered a few sentences to him. Only then did Peng Wang reluctantly come back with a disgruntled expression.","\"Miss He, as long as you can completely eliminate the remaining venom in me, I'll permit Mo Jiuye to be on the cart with me.\"","\"Official, as you can see, we of the Mo Family are all womenfolk. Pushing the cart for our husband alone is already very strenuous...\"","He Zhiran would eat anything, she just didn't like taking losses.","Although two or three Mo Family women working together could still push the cart, she didn't want her own people to toil.","Peng Wang was so angry inside. He had already lowered his stance to agree to share a cart with Mo Jiuye, yet He Zhiran still dared propose conditions to him.","Just as he was about to erupt, the Eighth Old Zhou cut in again.","\"That's no problem, I can get some male convicts to push the cart.\"","Peng Wang looked at the Eighth Old Zhou and knew he meant well for him, so he acquiesced to his solution.","\"I've agreed to your conditions already. If you can't completely eliminate the remaining venom in me, beware of the government clerks' whips.\""]},{"number":31,"title":"Chapter 31: Wake Up","paragraphs":["With her goal achieved, He Zhiran was straightforward.","\"Alright, I'll help the official detoxify now.\"","After speaking, she walked towards the herbs they had collected yesterday and casually picked a few to take back.","She handed the herbs to The Eighth Old Zhou: \"Official, these are the herbs we collected yesterday. Boil some water for Mr. Peng to drink and within seven days, the remaining toxins in his body will be completely cleansed.\"","The Eighth Old Zhou was somewhat skeptical: \"Are your words true?\"","\"True,\" He Zhiran answered very definitively.","The herbs she had chosen together only had the effects of clearing heat, promoting urination, cooling blood and detoxifying.","Although they didn't provide much help to Peng Wang's body, they were not completely useless either.","At the very least they could alleviate the current symptoms.","Anyway, there were no real remaining toxins in Peng Wang's body, his recovery just required time.","Seeing He Zhiran's sincere gaze, much of the doubt in The Eighth Old Zhou's heart lessened.","\"Boss, you go rest first on the wagon, I'll go brew the medicine now.\"","Looking at the limited space next to the wagon, Peng Wang could only reluctantly squeeze in with Mo Jiuye since he needed their help.","Because of the medicine brewing, the departure was delayed by almost half a hour.","Before departure, The Eighth Old Zhou observed the prisoners and found two brawny men from the He family.","Naturally, these two became the main force to push the wagon.","When they saw Mo Jiuye lying on the wagon, they were extremely upset.","If not for these officials present, they would have torn Mo Jiuye, who caused the downfall of the He family, into ten thousand pieces.","However, after facing Peng Wang's warning gaze, the He brothers immediately lost all their bluster.","They could only reluctantly push the wagon to get going.","He Zhiran's actions once again attracted worshipful gazes from the Mo women.","Especially Mo Hanyue, who had been chattering nonstop around He Zhiran since they set off.","\"Sister-in-law, you're so amazing. Not only does brother not need to get off the wagon, we even have free labor to use, making it much more relaxing for us all.\"","He Zhiran just smiled lightly at the little sister-in-law's praise.","She didn't feel like what she did was anything amazing, it was just some experience cultivated from her past life, as well as her personality.","Mo Hanyue spoke more and more excitedly, already hooking He Zhiran's arm.","\"Sister-in-law, brother is so fortunate to have married such an amazing wife like you.\"","As she spoke, Mo Hanyue saw some of the herbs they had collected yesterday in the grass by the roadside.","She excitedly pointed at the herbs and said: \"Sister-in-law, there are herbs over there, I'll go collect them.\"","After she finished speaking, Mo Hanyue was about to run towards the roadside when she was grabbed by He Zhiran.","\"Little sister, there will be more chances to collect herbs later, delaying everyone on the road will lead to punishment by the officials.\"","Mo Hanyue was just a simple-minded girl who hadn't considered so much.","After being reminded by He Zhiran, she only then realized they were on the road to exile.","Mo Hanyue's little face scrunched unhappily together.","\"I understand now sister-in-law, I'll be careful from now on.\"","The Mo family members were full and could keep up with the officials' pace.","The other families were not so fortunate, eating only black steamed buns for two consecutive meals, which were not only hard to swallow but didn't fill them up either.","In addition, they were all used to being pampered daily. Not even half an hour after the troop set off, stragglers began to appear one after another.","The officials didn't show any mercy at all, anyone who fell behind would suffer whipping from their rods.","This resulted in endless wailing coming from the back of the troop.","The two He brothers responsible for pushing the wagon were also somewhat exhausted, constantly pleading to Peng Wang for some food.","Peng Wang was not completely heartless, knowing these two needed strength, he was just about to order someone to bring two white steamed buns over.","At this time, the wagon happened to bump into a large rock, the car almost tipping over.","Peng Wang was sitting on top and with this force, his body tilted and pressed down on Mo Jiuye.","Coincidentally, the place Peng Wang made contact was exactly where Mo Jiuye's injury was most severe.","Mo Jiuye didn't react at first, instinctively letting out a muffled groan.","Peng Wang didn't have time to scold the two pushing the wagon, his first thought was that Mo Jiuye had woken up.","He hurriedly called He Zhiran over: \"Come quickly and see if your husband has woken up.\"","Although he was used to seeing prisoners die on the road, Peng Wang still held some respect for Mo Jiuye.","Especially during the dispute between the official and Xie Fang, what He Zhiran said really resonated with him.","No matter what mistakes Mo Jiuye made, it could not erase the Mo men's contributions to the country.","Likewise with Mo Jiuye, recently in the capital there was still widespread talk of his triumphant return.","For such a person, Peng Wang sincerely hoped he could survive.","Of course, these were just his subconscious thoughts. If the Mo family dared to cause trouble on the road, he would still ruthlessly teach them a lesson.","He Zhiran did not know Peng Wang's thoughts. Hearing him call her, she hurried over.","\"Official Peng, did you say my husband woke up?\"","She deliberately showed a shocked expression while mentally preparing how to respond.","Peng Wang shifted his body to one side.","\"I might have bumped into his wound just now. I don't know if it was painful or what, but he let out a muffled groan.\"","He Zhiran stopped the He brothers and went through the motions of taking Mo Jiuye's pulse.","She was actually doing this to give Mo Jiuye some time.","Because she was unclear of Mo Jiuye's plans, whether he would wake up now or wait a little longer.","Mo Jiuye was also deliberating in his heart.","On the surface he appeared to be lying unconscious on the wagon, but in reality he had not relaxed his vigilance at all.","From morning till now, he had been sensing the surroundings, even secretly observing when others were unaware.","In his observations, he did not notice any danger.","After thinking it over, Mo Jiuye decided to wake up.","Just as He Zhiran was still carefully taking his pulse, he let out a faint groan.","Peng Wang pointed at Mo Jiuye again and said: \"See, isn't he really awake?\"","He Zhiran retracted her pulse-taking hand, pretending to be delighted as she said: \"Yes, my husband is awake.\"","Hearing this, Old Lady Mo and the other women also crowded around, the concern in their eyes did not seem fake.","It could be said, their acting skills definitely passed.","He Zhiran took the water bag from her waist.","\"Husband, how are you feeling? Have some water first to moisten your throat.\"","Mo Jiuye also cooperated very well, arduously raising his head slightly and drinking two mouthfuls with He Zhiran's assistance.","Peng Wang kindly reminded: \"He's weak now, dry steamed buns are not suitable. Let him drink more water to moisten his throat.\"","Although it was a reminder, his tone was still impatient as always."]},{"number":32,"title":"Chapter 32: Heat Stroke","paragraphs":["None of the Mohists minded Peng Wang's attitude, and they all nodded in agreement and said that Mo Jiuye would not be given any food for the time being.","Although Mo Jiuye was awake, he still had to maintain his original posture lying on the carriage, and when Peng Wang saw that things had been dealt with, he ordered them to continue on their way.","In the August heat, because it had not rained for so long, the huge sun scorched the earth, and the people walking felt a suffocating sensation.","In the convoy, the prisoners were moaning continuously.","Some could not stand it, and knelt down to beg the officers to find a shadier place to rest for a while.","The Mohists’ faces were also flushed red from the heat.","Seeing everyone’s condition, He Zhiran began to worry.","If this continued, it would be hard to prevent people from suffering heat stroke.","Just as she was thinking about how to prevent it, she suddenly heard someone crying out from the back of the convoy.","\"Your Excellency, please help my child find a doctor, the child is innocent...\"","He Zhiran looked in the direction the voice came from and saw it was from the Xie Family's convoy.","Sister-in-law Two also noticed this and immediately ran over.","Considering the Xie Family was Sister-in-law Two's parental home, He Zhiran felt she could not just stand by and watch them die.","So she followed closely behind Sister-in-law Two to go take a look.","At this time, all the Xie family members were gathered around Xie Lin, wiping away tears.","Xie Lin was being held in the arms of a young woman, while the others desperately shouted his name.","\"Big brother, what's wrong with Lin'er?\" Sister-in-law Two pushed through the crowd and asked anxiously.","Xie Chao's eyes were red.","\"Lin'er was fine when he got up early, but after walking for a while he couldn't go on.\"","Sister-in-law Two was panic-stricken for a moment, then hurriedly said, \"My family's Ninth Youngest Sister understands medicine. I’ll go get her right away.\"","\"Sister-in-law Two, I'm here. Let me take a look at the child first.\" He Zhiran said, already arriving in front of Xie Lin.","Although the Xie family had heard Xie Fang’s explanation, they still had not reconciled with the Mohists.","Therefore, when they found Xie Lin was unwell, they did not immediately ask He Zhiran to come and see him.","Now that she had taken the initiative to come over, the Xie family was worried about Xie Lin's life, and they struggled internally for a moment.","However, they instinctively did not try to stop He Zhiran.","Xie Lin was already unconscious, his face flushed, his limbs hot, which were clear symptoms of heat stroke.","Moreover, judging by Xie Lin's current condition, the child's symptoms were not minor. If he could not be treated in time, his life would likely be endangered.","Seeing He Zhiran finish her examination, Sister-in-law Two pulled her aside and asked, \"Ninth Youngest Sister, how is Lin'er's condition?\"","\"Sister-in-law Two, the child has suffered from heat stroke,\" He Zhiran said, already walking towards the crowd.","Seeing He Zhiran leave, the Xie family became anxious again. She was the only hope left to save Lin'er.","The old patriarch Xie Tianhai was the first to swallow his pride and took the initiative to chase after her.","\"Madam, please wait, I beg you to save my grandson's life.\"","He Zhiran did not stop walking.","\"Your grandson's situation is very dangerous. He must be treated immediately. Do you want to delay the time I need to fetch medicine?\"","Hearing this, Xie Tianhai realized he had misunderstood her intentions.","\"Alright, alright, I’ll leave it to you then.\"","Although he now understood He Zhiran's purpose, Xie Tianhai still followed behind her, as if wanting to express something but not knowing where to start.","He Zhiran knew he was following her.","\"We're all exiled prisoners. According to my relationship with Sister-in-law Two, you're also my elder. In the future, just calling me Lady He or He Zhiran is fine.\"","All that \"Madam\" business made her uncomfortable. A simple form of address sounded more pleasant.","\"Alright, from now on I’ll call you Lady He,\" Xie Tianhai said.","As the two spoke, He Zhiran had already walked to the vicinity of the Mohists’ convoy.","Among the medicinal herbs they had picked yesterday, there were several that could treat heat stroke, and they were each being managed by the sisters-in-law.","Without wasting any time, He Zhiran took the necessary herbs from the sisters-in-law, then looked at Xie Tianhai.","\"Uncle Xie, to decoct the medicine, we'll have to talk to the officers.\"","They had no containers at all, and they would have to negotiate nicely with the officers to get them to stop so they could decoct the medicine.","\"Alright, I’ll go talk to the officers right away.\"","Peng Wang was not far away, and he could hear their conversation clearly.","He was also unbearably hot, and because of the snake venom, his body's heat tolerance was extremely poor.","Seeing Xie Tianhai about to turn around to ask his subordinates, Peng Wang hurriedly called out,","\"There's a small river up ahead, and the trees on the bank can provide shade. Let's rest there for a while.\"","Hearing Peng Wang's words, Xie Tianhai thanked him profusely.","After walking out for about the time it takes to burn a stick of incense, they finally saw a small river up ahead.","The officers arranged for the exiled prisoners to rest separately, and they themselves also sought out shady places to take shelter from the heat.","He Zhiran borrowed a pot from Old Eighth Zhou and Sister-in-law Two volunteered to decoct the medicine for her nephew.","To prevent her family from suffering heat stroke, He Zhiran specifically had Sister-in-law Two decoct a large pot of herbal medicine, not just for Xie Lin to drink, but also to have the family members all drink some as a preventive measure.","When He Zhiran was examining Xie Lin earlier, she could already confirm the child was in the acute stage of heat stroke, and he was already unconscious. With just these herbs alone, the effect likely wouldn’t be very good.","So, when Sister-in-law Two wasn't paying attention, she secretly took some mint cooling water from her storage space and added it in.","After getting the decoction arranged, He Zhiran finally felt some relief.","Looking at the clear river beside her, with fish swimming to and fro,","He Zhiran casually found a thick tree branch on the ground, then went to stand in front of The Eighth Old Zhou.","\"Officer Zhou, may I borrow your saber for a moment?\" There were cleavers and daggers and such in her storage space, but with so many people around she could not openly take them out, so she could only ask the officer for help.","When The Eighth Old Zhou heard she wanted to borrow his saber, he immediately became vigilant.","\"What are you going to use the knife for?\"","He Zhiran shrugged, holding up the tree branch.","\"I want to sharpen this branch. If all goes well, we can add some meat to our lunch.\"","The Eighth Old Zhou did not bother guessing what the so-called meat was. He thought to himself that she was just a young woman, she wouldn't dare lie to him.","So, somewhat reluctantly, he removed his saber and gave it to He Zhiran.","Right in front of The Eighth Old Zhou, He Zhiran sharpened the branch.","After returning the knife, she turned and went back towards the riverbank.","Under everyone's gaze, she took off her embroidered shoes and rolled up her pants, then waded into the river.","Seeing He Zhiran's series of actions, the Mohist women all crowded around.","\"Lady He, what are you doing?\" Lady Mo anxiously asked, and was about to wade into the river to pull her back.","\"Yes, Ninth Youngest Sister, what are you doing?\"","He Zhiran turned back and gestured for them to be quiet, then continued walking towards the middle of the river.","The water was not deep. He Zhiran had to walk several meters out before it barely reached her knees.","He Zhiran stood still, targeted, then fiercely stabbed the sharpened end of the branch into the water surface."]},{"number":33,"title":"Chapter 33: Catch a Fish","paragraphs":["Right after that, she quickly flipped the stick and swung it towards the shore, sending a live big carp flopping in front of the Mo women.","\"Sisters-in-law, put the fish away.\"","He Zhiran didn't think much of it herself. For her, this kind of fishing method was just child's play.","In her previous life when she went on missions, she often had to camp outdoors, so it was only natural for her to grasp some wilderness survival skills.","However, others didn't think the same way.","Everyone was stunned by her effortless actions, even the guards were sighing that they were no match for her.","Every year when they escorted prisoners, they would pass by here and knew there were fish in this river.","They had tried to catch fish before without any success.","They just thought about bringing a fishing net next time but ended up forgetting about it.","Seeing He Zhiran had already caught the second fish, the guards were even secretly admiring her in their hearts.","The Mo women originally wanted to dissuade He Zhiran from revealing her feet, but now seeing the two live big carps in front of them, they had already forgotten their original intention.","Especially Old Lady Mo reassured herself even more.","Women adhering to such proprieties was just to avoid criticism and dislike from their husband's family.","Anyway, He Zhiran was their daughter-in-law, as long as the Mo family didn't look down on her, revealing her feet was fine...","Since Mo Jiuye had already chosen to wake up early, he didn't continue pretending to sleep.","He also benefited from Peng Wang's favor, as their plank cart was parked in the shadiest spot, and that spot didn't obstruct He Zhiran from catching fish at all.","Peng Wang was also stunned by He Zhiran's ability, and couldn't help but say to Mo Jiuye:","\"You really have good fortune. You married such a capable wife just a day before your exile.\"","At this moment, Mo Jiuye also had mixed feelings.","He didn't know why the He house's young miss, who never stepped out of her inner chamber, would have such abilities exceeding most men.","At the same time, he also had the same thought as Peng Wang.","Although this method of catching fish seemed easy to ordinary people, he could also do it perfectly.","However, this seemingly simple action would be impossible without a certain level of martial arts foundation.","He wondered what good deed he had done to be able to marry such an extraordinary wife before his exile.","At the same time, he became even more curious about everything regarding He Zhiran...","Li Rou'er stood not far away, staring fiercely at the scene.","She never knew that fool He Zhiran had such great skills.","Previously in front of her, she had really concealed her abilities.","The more Li Rou'er thought about it, the more upset she felt. Unconsciously, she came to the riverside.","\"He Zhiran, you really have no shame, actually catching fish barefoot in front of everyone without fear of ridicule.\"","At this moment, He Zhiran had just targeted her prey and didn't immediately refute.","However, upon hearing Li Rou'er's sarcastic words, the Mo women couldn't stand it.","Mo Hanyue stepped forward first: \"Li Rou'er, who do you think you are? A young lady from a prestigious family? Relying on food delivered to your mouth, please recognize your own status. You're just an exiled convict.","At this time, being able to fill your stomach is already good enough, yet you still care about such proprieties, really ill-omened.\"","If she had sister-in-law's skills, she would have taken off her shoes and socks to help catch fish already.","Especially after sister-in-law had become her big idol, Mo Hanyue would definitely not allow anyone to slander her amazing sister-in-law.","The other sisters-in-law also chimed in, attacking Li Rou'er one after another.","Just as Li Rou'er was about to argue with them, she suddenly felt a slimy and cold thing slap her face.","The one who struck was precisely He Zhiran.","When she caught the third fish, she directly swung it towards Li Rou'er's face.","It accurately hit the right side of her face.","Seeing this, the Mo family members quickly went forward to collect the fish, while bursting into laughter at Li Rou'er.","Even the few watching guards couldn't help laughing out loud.","Li Rou'er immediately felt she had lost all face.","She grievously turned to look at the few guards.","\"Sir, He Zhiran attacked and hurt someone, won't you do something about it?\"","The guard glanced at Li Rou'er's dirty face and said in disgust:","\"You deserved to be hit for running your mouth.\"","Li Rou'er...","These guards must have been bewitched by He Zhiran's charming face.","Seeing she wouldn't get any benefits here, Li Rou'er fiercely stomped towards the Mo family's direction before turning back to the Li family's spot.","As a result, she suffered the ridicule of her two younger sisters.","\"I thought after you went out, you could also catch some fish like He Zhiran!\"","\"You really made our Li family lose face. Not only didn't you catch any fish, but you were also mocked.\"","When Li Rou'er was still at home, she often suffered bullying from these two younger sisters.","At that time, she chose to endure it since she was a concubine's daughter.","But it was different now. With the whole family exiled, she felt there was no need to continue enduring.","Thus, she raised her hand and slapped one of the sisters in the face.","\"Don't forget, I'm your elder sister. If I lose face, it also reflects badly on you.\"","Li Yuer and Li Ruer had never suffered such grievance before, especially being hit by Li Rou'er.","The two almost simultaneously rushed at Li Rou'er.","At the same time, seeing her two daughters being bullied, Li Yuer and Li Ruer's mother also joined the fight.","For a time, the Li family's resting spot became a scene of chaos.","The guards enjoyed watching the fun and no one bothered to stop it.","Only when Li Liang shouted loudly did the group of Li women reluctantly stop.","Looking at them now, all were disheveled with several scratch marks on their faces...","While the Li family quarreled noisily, it didn't affect He Zhiran's fishing at all.","In less than half a hour after entering the river, she had already caught more than twenty carp.","Seeing the amount was about right, she came ashore.","The medicine on the other side had finished brewing. Second sister-in-law brought a bowl to Xie Lin.","Each person in the Mo family also had a bowl, and so did the guards.","Looking at the remaining medicinal broth, He Zhiran called for her second sister-in-law and asked her to bring some to the Xie family as well.","As for the others, no matter what, she wouldn't bother with them before their hostility towards the Mo family receded.","Not long after drinking the medicine, Xie Lin woke up. Although still a little weak, he was no longer in mortal danger.","Xie Tianhai personally came to He Zhiran to express his gratitude.","\"Thank you for saving my grandson's life. My Xie family will remember this favor.\"","Whether he was grateful or not, He Zhiran didn't care. For her, this was just a flick of her finger.","Her main goal was to resolve the misunderstanding between the Xie and Mo families as soon as possible.","After all, they still had a long exile journey ahead. Seeing those hostile gazes all day certainly made one feel very unhappy.","Moreover, the Xie family was Second Sister-in-Law's maternal family. The two families who should have been close were not supposed to continue interacting this way.","\"Uncle Xie, my husband has woken up today. If you're free tonight, why not come to our side to chat with him?\""]},{"number":34,"title":"Chapter 34: Food and Clothing for Yourself","paragraphs":["He Zhiran did not say things too directly. She believed Xie Tianhai could understand her meaning.","\"Alright, I'll do as you say and come over tonight,\" Xie Tianhai replied in a low voice.","He Zhiran looked at the carp she was processing and spoke again, \"Uncle Xie, I'm planning to roast and eat these fish later. I'll have sister-in-law send one to Lin'er to nourish her body.\"","Xie Tianhai had just seen He Zhiran catching fish, and already instructed his two sons to follow her example and go down to the river to catch a couple fish to nourish their grandson.","Who knew, the two sons were useless beyond belief. After making a fuss for half a day, they caught nothing.","Now that He Zhiran said she would send a fish to Xie Lin, it was like bringing fuel in snowy weather to Xie Tianhai.","He lowered his status to thank He Zhiran profusely.","At the same time, Xie Tianhai had already decided in his heart that no matter whether the Xie family's exile was related to Mo Jiuye, he would let the matter go.","Anyway, the Xie family had already been exiled. Their family was still in-laws with the Mo family. And now they had received such a great favor from He Zhiran, so continuing to resent and blame would be futile.","It would be better for the two families to get along well. To safely arrive in the northwest, even if they could only live on thin rice gruel in the future, as long as they were alive it was good.","The Mo family women were usually waited on by servants at home, and were unfamiliar with handling fish.","However, they had already recognized the reality. If they wanted to avoid starvation in the future, the best way was to work with their own hands for food and clothing.","So everyone gathered around He Zhiran to learn from her and help process the carp.","Although their movements were not as skilled as He Zhiran's, it was still good to have help.","Soon, everyone worked together to cleanly process the fish.","He Zhiran found some evenly thick tree branches to string all the carp, then gathered some large rocks to build a makeshift barbecue grill.","\"Sisters-in-law, please go gather some firewood.\"","Although she felt bad for the Mo family women, she also didn't want them to continue being useless rice worms who never lifted a finger. After all, the road ahead was still long, and it was necessary for them to gain more survival skills.","The women went to gather firewood while He Zhiran went to borrow matches from the officers.","The officers knew they would get a share of the grilled fish the Mo family was making, so they not only did not make things difficult for her, but also took the initiative to give He Zhiran some salt.","He Zhiran had originally planned to ask for some salt too, and was even prepared to spend some silver to buy it from the officers.","Unexpectedly, the officers were so accommodating and took the initiative to give it to her.","Salt in ancient times was unrefined, with large grains that were somewhat black.","But that was no problem. As long as she had this salt for cover, she could find an opportunity to take out refined salt from her space.","One should know, the small kitchen in her medical room still had quite a complete assortment of seasonings.","It was just a pity she still hadn't found an excuse to take these things out yet.","But adding some inconspicuous seasonings was harmless.","He Zhiran returned to the built barbecue grill and quickly started a fire, then neatly arranged the strung carp over it.","Soon, sizzling sounds emerged, and fragrance spread around.","Smelling this scent, people around continuously swallowed saliva.","The smell of grilled fish was appetizing, but He Zhiran was not very satisfied.","She unconsciously muttered softly,","\"It would be perfect if I could brush on some oil.\"","Unexpectedly, her words happened to fall into Zhang Qing's ears as he passed by.","Smelling the fragrance of grilled fish, Zhang Qing had long been drooling with gluttony.","Moreover, hearing He Zhiran's meaning, if she could brush on some oil over the grilled fish, the flavor would be even better.","\"Miss He, did you say the grilled fish needs to be brushed with oil?\"","He Zhiran looked up and casually replied, \"Yes, the taste would definitely be much better than now if I did that.\"","\"Wait for me.\" Zhang Qing threw down a sentence and hurriedly left.","Soon, he came back carrying a small jar.","\"This contains rapeseed oil, extremely precious. Use it sparingly.\"","He Zhiran had not expected the officers to be so well-equipped. They even had rapeseed oil.","If she had known earlier, she would have definitely asked for some oil.","But it wasn't too late now that it was delivered to her.","\"Don't worry Sir, I guarantee I'll use it sparingly.\"","Opening the jar, He Zhiran broke off a leafy tree branch, washed it clean in the river, and used it as a brush.","Sure enough, after brushing rapeseed oil on the carp, the aroma that spread became even more fragrant.","He Zhiran also secretly took some thirteen-spice powder and refined salt from her space and sprinkled it over them. With this, the first outdoor grilled fish meal in ancient times was complete.","This time, He Zhiran grilled a total of ten fish.","It was assumed she would first give the fish to the officers to curry favor with them.","Unexpectedly, He Zhiran did not do that at all.","Instead, she selected the biggest one and first handed it to Old Lady Mo.","Old Lady Mo hesitated for a moment, and deliberately looked at the officers again.","He Zhiran naturally understood mother-in-law's meaning. She just wanted He Zhiran to share the grilled fish with those officers.","To put Old Lady Mo's heart at ease to eat the fish, she gave the other party a reassuring look.","Then she also distributed one fish each to her eight sisters-in-law.","One was left. She looked at Mo Jiuye still lying limply on the wooden cart, then looked at the salivating Mo Hanyue. In the end, she chose to give it to Mo Hanyue.","Seeing her actions, the officers instantly became unhappy.","Especially Zhang Qing. He had hurriedly brought rapeseed oil to her, but in the end there was no share for him.","\"Miss He, is this how you were taught to conduct yourself since you were young?\"","He Zhiran looked up, answering evenly,","\"What's wrong with how I conduct myself?","My father taught me since I was little that when there are nice things, elders should get them first. I gave to mother-in-law first, and my eight sisters-in-law. They are all older than me, so it's not improper for me to give to them first.","My young sister-in-law is younger, so of course I should take care of her a bit more. Sir, tell me, where did I do wrong?\"","Zhang Qing was left speechless, unable to retort.","Indeed there was no issue...","Zhou Laoba, on the other hand, was patient. Seeing Zhang Qing's impatience, he nudged him, hinting for him to keep calm.","After all, it was reasonable for someone to not want to give you their own things.","If needed, they could just find an opportunity to make things difficult for the Mo family later.","Zhang Qing struggled to suppress the anger in his heart as he sat there glaring at He Zhiran.","Peng Wang, upon seeing all this, actually found it quite amusing.","In all his years working as an escort officer for exiled prisoners, this was still the first time he had met someone unafraid of them.","Moreover, the other party could always reason things out, leaving others unable to refute.","Thinking of this, he looked again at Mo Jiuye lying next to him.","\"Your wife is becoming more and more extraordinary.\"","Now, aside from describing He Zhiran as extraordinary, Peng Wang could hardly find other words.","Mo Jiuye turned his head and feigned weakness, \"She just has a sharp tongue.\"","\"Oh... don't be modest. I say your wife is extraordinary and she is.\"","How could she not be extraordinary?","Not only could she heal illnesses, she could also catch fish from the river, and her tongue was so smooth.","Anyway, Peng Wang was now convinced. It was just a pity that He Zhiran was a woman.","Otherwise, with her capabilities, she could definitely become an amazing figure."]},{"number":35,"title":"Chapter 35: Purpose Achieved","paragraphs":["He Zhiran did not know that Peng Wang's evaluation of him was so high. He concentrated on roasting the fish.","He thought those officials would cause trouble for this reason. He Zhiran was already prepared to deal with it.","There was a reason why she did this.","They had just departed from Beijing and still had a long way to go before reaching the northwest.","If she began to flatter and please these officials from the start, making them feel it was all a matter of course, wouldn’t they make exorbitant demands in the future?","In addition, He Zhiran also wanted to test the bottom line of these officials, which would be convenient for her to handle things appropriately in the future.","Judging from the distribution of roasted fish just now, these officials were quite reasonable.","He Zhiran also had a preliminary understanding of them.","The second batch of carp was roasted, still 10 fish.","He Zhiran took two fish and gave them to Peng Wang and Mo Jiuye first.","Although Mo Jiuye was injured and it was not suitable for him to eat fish, there was no other way during this special period. He could not just watch others eat and salivate.","Moreover, Mo Jiuye's injuries were all under He Zhiran's control. Eating one fish would not hurt him.","Peng Wang took a bite of the roasted fish, and his eyes lit up instantly.","It could be said that this was the most delicious roasted fish he had eaten in his life.","\"Mo Jiuye, didn't I say your wife is capable? Even her roasting fish skills are so good. You are really lucky.\"","\"Well, the taste is indeed not bad.\"","Mo Jiuye casually responded with a word, but his mind was even more intricate.","None of the things He Zhiran had done should be something a young lady from a good family was capable of.","However, it was precisely her uniqueness that allowed the Mo family to suffer little since departing from Beijing.","Mo Jiuye's mind was complicated. He felt useless for causing his family to be exiled. Now he had to rely on a woman to resolve various matters.","He Zhiran did not know Mo Jiuye's thoughts. After distributing the roasted fish, four officials did not get any.","Her attitude this time was good. After giving out the food, she naturally could not offend others again.","\"My lords, I will go roast the next batch. Everyone will get a share.\"","Seeing their brothers eat with great appetite, the remaining four officials felt upset.","However, looking at He Zhiran's busy appearance, not resting for a moment, they still suppressed their anger and waited patiently.","After about ten minutes, the four officials finally got the roasted fish contentedly.","The others had finished their roasted fish long ago. Now, looking at the four of them eat, they still could not help but swallow saliva.","The four suddenly felt a sense of superiority, slowly eating the roasted fish, extremely satisfied in their hearts.","He Zhiran left a roasted fish for herself and gave the other three to her second sister-in-law.","\"Second sister-in-law, please take these three fish to Uncle Xie and the others to try.\"","The second sister-in-law looked incredulous.","\"Sister-in-law, are you serious?\"","He Zhiran smiled and replied, \"I'm serious. Uncle Xie and Auntie are getting older and have not eaten enough these two days. Eating some roasted fish will nourish them. Xie Lin also needs nourishing food during her weakness.\"","The second sister-in-law was so moved that tears almost came out.","\"Okay, okay, I'll take them over right away. Thank you, sister-in-law.\"","Watching the second sister-in-law's quickly disappearing figure, He Zhiran found a shady place to sit down, rest and eat roasted fish.","This move once again attracted countless resentful eyes.","After noticing those eyes, He Zhiran did not choose to ignore them.","Instead, she met them one by one.","She wanted to see how much these people hated the Mo family.","The first were the He family, led by the two strong laborers pushing the carts. They all stared at He Zhiran.","Their mouths kept opening and closing. It was obvious they were scolding her.","Perhaps because they were afraid of those officials, they did not dare to speak loudly.","So He Zhiran could not hear their voices from her position.","The Li family was no less hostile than the He family. All their men, women, young and old were glaring at He Zhiran.","Especially Li Rou'er. If looks could kill, He Zhiran would have died countless times from her gaze.","She raised the roasted fish towards Li Rou'er's direction, took another bite, an action that could drive one mad with anger.","Although the Fang family were also looking at He Zhiran, their eyes did not contain endless hatred like the He and Li families.","After careful observation, He Zhiran found that their eyes seemed to contain pleading and unwillingness.","The Xie family needless to say. He Zhiran had saved Xie Lin’s life before. Now she let the second sister-in-law deliver three roasted fish to them. As a result, their hostility towards the Mo family lessened even more.","It seemed that the Fang family, like the Xie family, also harbored hatred that could be slowly resolved.","Of course, it would be most appropriate for Mo Jiuye himself to be involved in this matter.","After all, only confronting the parties concerned could explain things more clearly.","He Zhiran now had a good grasp of the situation. She would find time later to discuss it with Mo Jiuye.","Just as she finished eating the roasted fish, Peng Wang called her over.","\"Miss He, your fishing skills are good. Take this opportunity while we rest to go catch some more fish.\"","He Zhiran smiled sarcastically, \"Lord Peng, you still haven't eaten enough?\"","Embarrassed for having his thoughts seen through, Peng Wang's old face flushed red.","\"Uh... yes, let's just say so!\"","In fact, even if Peng Wang didn't say it, He Zhiran also planned to do so.","However, she did not want to miss any opportunity to gain favor.","\"Lord Peng, I'm just a young lady. If not for the sake of my family eating something, I wouldn't have waded barefoot into the river to catch fish in front of everyone.","Now that everyone has eaten fish, please don't make things difficult for me.\"","Rejected, Peng Wang suddenly looked upset.","But thinking of the delicious roasted fish, he still endured.","\"This time you don't need to catch too many, just ten, ten fish.\"","He Zhiran pretended to bow her head in thought, acting undecided.","Peng Wang became anxious.","\"How about this - you just need to catch ten more fish, and I promise you a condition within my capabilities.\"","\"Since Lord Peng has said it to this point, if I don't go it would be pretentious. Alright, wait for me.\"","Having achieved her goal, He Zhiran didn't say more. She took off her shoes and socks and entered the river again.","There were plenty of fish in the river. Catching ten was like playing a game for He Zhiran.","Soon, she flung ten fish onto the shore.","The sisters-in-law also did not hesitate. They took the fish, squatted by the river to clean them, then strung them on branches.","He Zhiran thought that since she was already in the river, she might as well catch more fish to keep for supper.","So after catching ten fish, she did not hurry out of the water but continued busying herself there.","At this time, Mrs. Zhao, wife of Fang Chuanzhou, came to Old Lady Mo.","She behaved with utmost humility.","\"Old Lady Mo, we were wrong to insult Lord Mo yesterday. Please do not hold it against us.\"","Old Lady Mo looked at her, not knowing what she was scheming.","\"Mrs. Fang, Mo Jiuye is no longer a lord now. Just call him by name directly to avoid others seizing the handle to make trouble.\""]},{"number":36,"title":"Chapter 36: There must be a misunderstanding between us.","paragraphs":["When being spoken to like this, Mrs. Zhao suddenly felt that her previous words were inappropriate.","\"It was me who didn't consider this carefully enough, Old Lady Mo please don't blame me.\"","Knowing that Mrs. Zhao had not come over just to apologize so simply, but she did not say her true purpose.","So Old Lady Mo was going to order her to leave.","\"Mrs. Fang, I can understand how your family feels, and I appreciate your apology. If there is nothing else, you should go back now, to avoid being scolded by the officials.\"","Seeing that Old Lady Mo was starting to drive her away, Mrs. Zhao was no longer modest.","She carefully took out a gemstone ring from her rolled up hair.","\"Old Lady Mo, may I exchange this ring for some fish?\"","As she spoke, Mrs. Zhao turned and pointed to where her family members were resting.","\"My little son saw you all eating grilled fish and craved it so much that he cried. I really had no other way, so I came to ask if you could spare us some.\"","Old Lady Mo looked at the gemstone ring in Mrs. Zhao's hand, then looked in the direction she was pointing.","Sure enough, a little boy who looked eight or nine years old was there wiping his tears.","\"The fish were caught by my ninth daughter-in-law, if you want to exchange it, go talk to her.\"","For such matters, Old Lady Mo felt it was not appropriate for her to make decisions on behalf of her daughter-in-law.","Mrs. Zhao politely expressed her thanks, then went towards the riverbank.","Just then, He Zhiran had also caught enough fish and was walking towards the shore.","She had already seen Mrs. Zhao talking with her mother-in-law, and could roughly guess her purpose in coming over.","He Zhiran did not take the initiative to speak, but slowly put on her shoes and socks at the shore.","Mrs. Zhao came over, trying hard to maintain a proper smile.","\"He... Mrs. He, may auntie discuss something with you, and exchange this ring for some fish?\"","He Zhiran looked at the ring, the red gem was crystal clear, obviously a valuable item at first glance.","It showed Mrs. Zhao was willing to spend a lot just for some fish.","At the same time, she guessed that the Fang family really had no silver on them, otherwise they wouldn't use such a nice ring to exchange for some worthless fish.","He Zhiran did not stand on ceremony with Mrs. Zhao, and directly took the ring.","Then pointing to the crucian carp she had just caught, she said: \"The fish are all here, take what you need.\"","Seeing the other party agreed, Mrs. Zhao expressed her thanks profusely, then squatted down to grab some fish.","He Zhiran just stood there watching, she wanted to see how many fish Mrs. Zhao would take.","Mrs. Zhao hesitated briefly, then took five fish.","\"Is this okay?\"","Given the value of Mrs. Zhao's ring, let alone five fish, even five hundred would not be excessive.","But the other party was not greedy, only taking five.","This gave He Zhiran a good first impression of Mrs. Zhao.","\"No problem, if it's not enough, you can take some more.\"","Mrs. Zhao shook her head: \"No need, I'm very satisfied with this.\"","After speaking, she reluctantly glanced at the ring in He Zhiran's hand, then turned and left.","Just from that one look, He Zhiran could determine that this ring was very important to Mrs. Zhao.","So she chased after her and softly said,","\"There must be some misunderstanding between us. If you want to resolve it, please ask Uncle Fang to come find my husband after dark, then everything will become clear.\"","Mrs. Zhao solemnly nodded: \"Alright, I will pass this on to my Old Master.\"","He Zhiran turned around and secretly stored the ring in her space.","She thought that if the Mo and Fang families could resolve their conflicts in the future, she could completely return the ring to Mrs. Zhao.","Just not right now.","The sisters-in-law continued to clean the caught crucian carp. He Zhiran grilled ten fish at Peng Wang's request, then gave them all to him. What Peng Wang wanted to do with the fish was his business.","After eating the grilled fish and seeing it was about time, Peng Wang gave the order to continue on their journey.","The two miserable laborers from the He family reluctantly pushed the wheeled plank with pained expressions once again.","The afternoon weather remained sultry. Fortunately, He Zhiran had brewed herbal medicine for some people to drink, sparing them from the danger of heat stroke.","The Mo family members, Xie family members, and officials were all fine.","However, it was different for the other three families.","As they travelled, some people from those families developed varying degrees of heat stroke symptoms.","Initially it was still manageable as their family members carried or supported them, keeping up with the large convoy.","But as time went on, the number of people with heat stroke kept increasing. The remaining few who were still relatively healthy simply could not take care of so many people.","In a short time, the entire exiled convoy was filled with wails.","At the same time, the Xie family members and officials were sincerely grateful to He Zhiran.","If not for the herbal medicine she prepared in advance, they would probably not escape the fate of heat stroke either.","Seeing the situation, Peng Wang knew they could no longer continue travelling, and could only order them to stop.","When encountering such circumstances, the first person Peng Wang thought of was He Zhiran.","\"Mrs. He, this matter still needs you to resolve it.\"","But He Zhiran did not agree.","\"Officer Peng, you've seen it these past two days, they've been cursing us Mo family people. Why should I go save them?\"","He Zhiran believed she was no saint who would save anyone just because she knew medicine.","Especially the He family and Li family people, their hatred for Mo Jiuye was down to the bone.","If Mo Jiuye stuck his head out, they would definitely spare no effort to chop it off with a blade.","She would absolutely not lend a helping hand to save people harboring such malice.","Of course the Fang family was different, she could consider treating them.","Peng Wang also understood this reasoning.","As the head official in charge of escorting them, it was not a big deal if a few people died or were injured along the way.","But if the number was too great, he would be unable to explain it to his superiors after returning.","Therefore, he could only continue persuading He Zhiran.","\"No matter how big their mistakes, they are still living people. You can't just watch them die, right?\"","He Zhiran's mind was set, and she crossed both arms stubbornly, not leaving Peng Wang any leeway.","\"Officer Peng, stop saying anymore. I said I won't save them means I won't save them.\"","\"You...\" Peng Wang was also angered, pointing at He Zhiran's nose, wanting to scold her a few times, but held back in the end.","\"Mrs. He, I advise you to be more tactful. There is still a long way to the Northwest, offending me does you no good.\"","He Zhiran's temper also flared up, unwilling to back down.","\"Officer Peng, what you said is unfair. If you were me, would you be willing to save the lives of your enemies?\"","\"This...\" Peng Wang was left speechless by her retort.","He realized this woman He had a stubborn temper, being hard on her really wouldn't work.","So he made an effort to keep his emotions under control, and spoke again in a negotiating tone:","\"How about this, you choose some more agreeable ones to treat?\"","Although unwilling to compromise on her pride, He Zhiran also understood she couldn't offend Peng Wang too severely.","When someone provided a way out, she should take it at the right time.","She looked at the people with heat stroke. The Fang family was still decent. Perhaps because they ate some fish at noon, their bodies had some immunity and only three were down.","The He family and Li family were in bad shape. The two families had over thirty people total, and less than ten could still stand now.","\"Since Officer Peng puts it this way, I will reluctantly save some as a favor.\""]},{"number":37,"title":"Chapter 37: Enter Yunlai County","paragraphs":["After she finished speaking, He Zhiran quickly brought yesterday's picked herbs, and then lit a fire to decoct the medicine.","In less than half an hour, the herbs were decocted.","The officers took the initiative to come over to take the medicine, but were stopped by He Zhiran.","\"Master Peng said, let me pick some people I like to treat.\"","The two men's conversation just now was also heard by Zhou Lao Ba, knowing that this was indeed the boss's intention.","\"Okay, we'll help you carry it, and give it to whoever you say.\"","He Zhiran walked in front, first coming to the Fang family's position.","Mrs. Zhao saw her coming over, as if she had seen a savior.","\"Ms. He, I thank you on behalf of my whole family.\"","He Zhiran just nodded to her, and then arranged for the officers to distribute the medicine.","This time Fang Chuanzhou did not escape, but the symptoms were not very serious, just feeling a little dizzy and nauseous.","He Zhiran let the officers give him a bowl of medicine, and whispered.","\"Uncle Fang, remember to come to my husband at night.\"","Fang Chuanzhou holding the medicine bowl: \"Okay, I must go.\"","He Zhiran also let the officers give medicine to several other heatstroke patients in the Fang family, before heading towards the Li and He families.","Although the Li and He families were hostile to Mohists, they did not dare to show it at this time.","They were still waiting for the lifesaving herbs.","He Zhiran took a look around, these people's symptoms were not very serious, and some people even deliberately lay there groaning.","It is estimated that they do not want to continue on the road.","She did not expose them on the spot, selected a few elderly and young children, and let the officers give them medicine.","As for the others, she chose to ignore them directly.","Just as she was about to leave with the remaining bit of medicine, she heard Li Rou'er scolding loudly from behind.","\"He Zhiran, you are inhuman for refusing to save lives. Mo Jiuye married a daughter-in-law like you, it's bad luck for eight lifetimes.\"","There was no such thing as not talking back in front of He Zhiran.","Just as she was about to curse back, she suddenly heard a crisp whip crack and Li Rou'er's scream.","Zhang Qing was best at wielding the whip, moving quickly and fiercely.","\"Shut up for me, no wonder Ms. He is unwilling to treat you, if it were me, I wouldn't save you either.\"","This whip just happened to hit Li Rou'er's right arm, and also hit her exposed neck.","Li Rou'er clutched her neck, her eyes full of disbelief.","\"Officer, this is unfair. He Zhiran didn't give us medicine to eat, not only did you not scold her, but you even hit me for speaking fairly?\"","Zhang Qing was even amused by Li Rou'er's words, while fiercely whipping her again.","\"I just don't like you, I'll beat you to death.\"","Seeing that Li Rou'er had offended the officers again, Zhu immediately pulled her aside.","\"Officer, my young lady is ignorant, please spare her this time!\"","As Zhu spoke, she had already kowtowed to Zhang Qing several times.","Seeing this, Zhang Qing's anger subsided a lot.","\"Keep her uncontrollable mouth shut from now on. If I hear her talking nonsense again, it won't be as simple as two whips.\"","Li Rou'er was also extremely angry just now, which led her to speak recklessly in front of the officers.","Now that she had calmed down, she really became afraid.","However, her hatred for He Zhiran was even stronger.","She knelt behind Zhu and sobbed softly, while plotting how to make the exile journey more comfortable.","Seeing his usually most sensible daughter become like this, Li Liang felt a headache.","Fortunately, Zhu was sensible and apologized in time.","Otherwise, with the temperament of these officers, it would be hard to guarantee that they would not make things difficult for their Li family on the road.","Seeing the officers and He Zhiran walking away, Li Liang glared fiercely at Li Rou'er.","\"From now on, be mute in front of outsiders.\"","\"Dad...\" Li Rou'er looked at Li Liang aggrievedly, wanting to explain something, but was stopped by the latter.","\"Shut up now.\"","Li Rou'er immediately fell silent, and continued to wipe away tears in Zhu's arms.","He Zhiran looked at the remaining medicine soup in the iron pot, and distributed it all to those in the Fang family who were not suffering from heat stroke. It could play a preventive role.","She wanted these people to see that offending the Mohists had no benefits.","She would rather give the remaining medicine to those who were not suffering from heatstroke to take, and not give it to these enemies.","After traveling for more than two hours, the convoy finally entered Yunlai County before dark.","The officers seemed to be very familiar with this place. After entering the city, they went straight to an inn in the west of the city.","Seeing the inn, everyone breathed a sigh of relief.","Heaven knows how they survived the night camping in the wilderness last night.","Not to mention the cold and damp, they also had to guard against mosquito bites from time to time.","When they got up in the morning, there was dew on their faces and clothes.","Today was different. With the inn to stay in, they could rest well for a night.","Especially those family members who were suffering from heat stroke, although they had recovered a lot after taking He Zhiran’s medicine, they were still weak.","Being able to rest well would surely speed up their recovery.","Zhou Lao Ba looked at everyone.","\"Those who want to stay in a 10-person dormitory, one tael of silver; a room for two, five taels of silver; those without silver can spend the night in the hut in the inn yard.\"","Hearing this, He Zhiran was immediately filled with contempt. Such prices were clearly intended to fleece them.","However, on second thought, she let it go. These officers all relied on fleecing to get rich. How could they miss such an opportunity?","The other families let out sighs of dismay.","\"Officer, we really don't have any silver!\"","\"Yeah officer, please take pity on us, don't let us stay outside!\"","\"Officer please do us a favor, even if you let us stay in a room for twenty it would be fine...\"","Zhou Lao Ba waved his hand impatiently.","\"Stop chattering. Those with silver hand it over now. Those without silver will sleep in the grass sheds outside.\"","The third daughter-in-law immediately took out some broken silver and approached Old Lady Mo and He Zhiran.","\"Mother, sister-in-law, there are twelve of us in total. I was thinking of getting a ten-person room and a two-person room. What do you think?\"","Old Lady Mo was very satisfied with her daughter-in-law's arrangement.","\"Hmm, that's great. Let Jiuye and Zhiran go to the two-person room. I will stay with you sisters-in-law and Han Yue in the ten-person room.\""]},{"number":38,"title":"Chapter 38: Renting an Inn Kitchen","paragraphs":["Third Sister-in-law discussed with He Zhiran and then gave the silver to the Eighth Old Zhou.","Based on Mo Jiuye's intention, she planned to squeeze everyone into the ten-person room so that they could take care of each other.","In case of any danger, she and Mo Jiuye would also be able to protect them in time.","Who knew, Third Sister-in-law snatched it first.","Since the old lady Mo and Third Sister-in-law had arranged it well, and Mo Jiuye did not object, she did not intend to meddle too much either.","It was just a room with Mo Jiuye, no big deal, at worst she could sleep on the floor.","Peng Wang took the silver handed over by Third Sister-in-law, and looked at the other families.","\"Does anyone else want to book a room?\"","Of course they wanted to book a room, who would be willing to live in the shed outside, it was no different from being outdoors.","Unfortunately, their pockets were cleaner than their faces, and they simply could not take out the silver to pay the room fee.","He Zhiran took the opportunity to come to Second Sister-in-law's side and secretly stuffed her with a or two silver.","\"Second Sister-in-law, please help the Xie family book a room!\"","Second Sister-in-law held the one or two silver, which usually looked inconspicuous, but now felt as heavy as a thousand catties.","\"I thanked Ninth Brother-in-law and Sister-in-law on behalf of my parents.\"","At this time, she was not polite with He Zhiran either, because this was what the Xie family urgently needed at the moment.","Although the Xie family had more than a dozen people, squeezing together was still better than living outside.","It was not that He Zhiran was petty.","After all, the relationship between the Xie family and the Mo family had not been completely resolved, and she also felt that there was no need to support other families.","In the future, if the Xie family could truly reconcile with the Mo family, she would teach them some skills to earn money, at least to ensure that their future days would be better.","The Fang family was so envious of the Xie family for having a ten-person room.","They all knew that the Xie family had a daughter who was the daughter-in-law of the Mo family, and the room was opened with the Mo family's money to help.","Unfortunately, their Fang family was still at odds with the Mo family at the moment, and they couldn't even open their mouths to borrow some silver.","He Zhiran's observation skills were extremely strong, and she instantly saw the tangled expressions on the faces of the Fang family members.","Thinking of the ring Mrs. Zhao exchanged for fish today, it was worth at least a few hundred taels.","She didn't want to take advantage of others' misfortune, after thinking about it for a while, she secretly stuffed Mrs. Zhao with a broken silver or two.","Now, the Mo family, the Xie family and the Fang family all had their own rooms to stay in.","Only the He family and the Li family were left.","The two families now hated not only the Mo family, but also the Xie family and the Fang family...","The Eighth Old Zhou worked very quickly, took the silver from several families, opened the rooms, and the sisters-in-law carried Mo Jiuye in.","It had to be said that these officials were really good at fleecing.","The five-tael-a-room guest room looked gloomy and damp.","If it was rented out normally, it was estimated that one hundred and eighty wen would be enough to stay overnight, and that was without encountering picky guests, otherwise people would complain.","However, He Zhiran still understood the principle of adapting measures to different times and conditions. Although the room conditions were not satisfactory, having it was better than nothing.","She simply helped Mo Jiuye tidy up the bed and let him lie down to rest before turning to leave.","Although everyone had roasted fish for lunch, after rushing on the road all afternoon, they were hungry now.","Finally there was an inn to rest, she must take advantage of the convenience here.","The ten-person room for Old Lady Mo and other women was even more bleak.","Not to mention the musty smell in the room, there was only a long kang, on which were placed pillows that were shiny from dirt and a few cotton quilts whose original colors were indistinguishable.","Old Lady Mo was also capable of adapting, seeing that her daughter-in-law and daughter were frowning, she couldn't help but remind them.","\"Think about spending last night outdoors in the wild, staying here we should all be content.\"","\"Mother, we all know, we won't complain.\"","When He Zhiran came to the ten-person room, the first thing she saw was Old Lady Mo preaching there.","Although she intended to arrange dinner for everyone, she felt it necessary to communicate with the elders, and she also needed the help of the sisters-in-law.","\"Mother, I plan to discuss with the innkeeper to borrow the kitchen here and cook some dinner for everyone.\"","Hearing about cooking dinner, the sisters-in-law's eyes lit up immediately.","The Eldest Sister-in-law was best at cooking, and immediately volunteered.","\"Ninth Sister-in-law, I can help out in the kitchen.\"","The Fifth Sister-In-Law also stepped forward: \"I can do it too.\"","Other sisters-in-law were not good at cooking, but were still scrambling to help.","Seeing such a harmonious big family, He Zhiran was already beginning to appreciate her luck.","Although she inexplicably crossed over to another world, and had to face countless days and nights of arduous exile, being able to gain so many loving family members was also one of her great gains.","\"Sisters-in-law, this is just an idea of mine, I still have to discuss with the boss to see if it can be done.","Besides, our situation is special, we can't eat extravagantly, two people to help is enough.\"","After hearing He Zhiran's words, everyone's eyes fell on the Eldest Sister-in-law and the Fifth Sister-In-Law.","Because these two were good at cooking, they would not go and mess things up.","He Zhiran accomplished her goal, then went out to discuss with the innkeeper.","Of course, before the discussion, she still had to communicate with the officials.","He Zhiran went straight to Peng Wang.","Peng Wang had eaten the fish roasted by He Zhiran and guessed that her cooking must be good.","Moreover, when the Mo family made a meal, they would surely bring it to them officials too.","Therefore, Peng Wang agreed without hesitation. As for how to communicate with the boss, it was none of his concern.","With Peng Wang's permission, He Zhiran went to find the innkeeper.","Money makes things easy, although they were all exiled convicts, the boss could not refuse the temptation of silver either.","After accepting He Zhiran's three taels of bribery, the boss claimed that she could use anything in the kitchen.","With things settled, He Zhiran did not immediately call the two sisters-in-law to help, but went to the kitchen alone first.","After surveying the kitchen, she confirmed that there was some white rice and white flour, as well as some common vegetables like scallions, cabbage, radish and so on.","He Zhiran saw that the seasonings in the kitchen were only lard and salt. She immediately took out some thirteen-spice and star anise from her space.","Based on the original owner's memory, she also took out some vegetables that existed in this era.","Cucumbers, eggs, green beans and a piece of pork belly.","There were many people eating, and the amount of food in her space refrigerator was not much. She took them repeatedly after those foods regenerated.","In addition, she poured some vegetable oil from her space into bowls in the kitchen, as well as appropriate amount of white sugar.","As for things like broccoli, green beans, tomatoes in her refrigerator, even if He Zhiran wanted to eat them, she did not take them out.","After all, she hadn't figured out how to explain the origin of these foods yet.","After getting everything ready, she went to call the sisters-in-law to help.","When the two sisters-in-law came over and saw the ingredients, their eyes were full of joy.","\"Ninth Sister-in-law, this inn is really good, it prepared so many kinds of vegetables.\"","\"Yeah, there's meat too!\"","The sisters-in-law said while briskly picking and chopping vegetables."]},{"number":39,"title":"Chapter 39: Beat Up the Ho Brothers","paragraphs":["He Zhiran took the opportunity to go to the backyard to gather firewood while her sisters-in-law were preparing the ingredients.","She happened to pass by the straw sheds where the He and Li families were staying.","Although called straw sheds, to He Zhiran these were more like animal pens.","She guessed since there were no horses brought by the passing guests today, these pens were left empty.","It was really difficult for those officials to come up with the idea of letting them stay here for a night.","The straw sheds were quite spacious, supported by several large pillars and covered fully by hay.","At first glance, they were much better than spending the night outdoors last night.","However, from a distance, she could already smell a stench of foul odor coming from the sheds. Without blocking their noses, those people probably could not fall asleep.","At the moment, the Li and He families were fighting over the spaces, both wanting to stay more inside, hence the yelling with necks stretched and faces flushed red.","He Zhiran chose to ignore them and went straight to the backyard.","But trouble came looking for her when she was not asking for it.","The He brothers had been pushing the wooden carts for a day. Learning from Li Rou'er that it was He Zhiran's idea, they had long held grievances against her.","Seeing her walking alone now, they immediately had the idea of venting their anger on her.","Seeing He Zhiran had walked far away, the two brothers did not continue arguing with the Li family. They strode towards He Zhiran with frivolous tones.","\"Little slut, it was you who made us brothers work hard pushing those wooden carts the whole day. If we don't get some sweetness from you today, we brothers won't be able to sleep well tonight.\"","He Zhiran had always been vigilant. When she passed by the shed earlier, she had already noticed something wrong with the two brothers and was on guard against them!","Hearing the frivolous and grating voices behind her, she stopped and turned around, looking at them calmly.","In the capital city, He Ming and He Liang were often involved in bullying men and overbearing women. Facing what they intended to do now, they were quite experienced.","Seeing He Zhiran stop, He Ming approached her with an evil smile, while reaching out with his disgusting claws.","\"Let brother have a feel first.\"","He Zhiran nimbly dodged He Ming's roaming hands. At the same time, she quickly squatted down and punched him hard in the stomach.","Taking advantage of He Ming's pain, He Zhiran swiftly stood up and swept his legs with hers.","Losing his balance, He Ming stumbled forward.","He Zhiran seized this opportunity to strike him again.","Her actions were almost seamless, leaving He Ming no chance to retaliate.","When He Liang realized things had gone wrong, he rushed over to help. But He Ming had already been beaten down.","Facing He Liang's attack, He Zhiran did not go easy. With a few simple grappling moves, she took him down as well.","Although she had beaten the two brothers down, He Zhiran still showed restrain.","After all, these two still needed to keep pushing the wooden carts tomorrow. Breaking their arms or legs would hinder their labor.","\"This is a warning for you two. If you dare to provoke me again, it won't be as simple as making you suffer a bit like today.\"","Having said that, He Zhiran directly ignored the resentment from the brothers and casually dusted herself off before leaving arrogantly...","As for whether they would report this to the officials, He Zhiran was not too concerned.","After all, no one else saw her take action. Who would believe that she, a weak woman, could take down two burly men?","After gathering some firewood, He Zhiran returned to the kitchen.","Her sisters-in-law had already prepared the ingredients, now just waiting for her to personally cook.","He Zhiran simply made four dishes with one soup: braised pork with broad beans, cold cucumber salad, vinegar-cooked bok choy, scrambled eggs with scallions, and a milky white fish soup made by simmering carp.","He Zhiran's cooking skills were just average. Fortunately, she knew many recipes and had seasoning blends like Shisanxiang to help.","The dishes she made immediately conquered everyone's taste buds.","The officials would occasionally rush to the kitchen door to peek. Seeing the dishes plated, someone immediately ran to report to Peng Wang.","This time, instead of personally handing out the fish like last time, He Zhiran let her sisters-in-law first serve the officials.","She brought the rest to Lady Mo's room for everyone to enjoy together.","As for the Xie and Fang families, it was inappropriate to give them too much favor, lest they become unappreciative. Even helping should be gradual.","Therefore, relatively less food was given to the Fang and Xie families. Superficially, it was to take care of the elderly and children.","Even so, they were still very grateful to the Mo family.","In such difficult times, for others to share some of the fine food with them was already a tremendous favor.","Their resentment towards Mo Jiuye seemed to be cast aside for now.","Although Mo Jiuye was no longer pretending to be unconscious, he still had to appear weak and immobilized in front of others.","Therefore, his meals were personally delivered by He Zhiran to their room.","Seeing the colorful and aromatic food, Lady Mo and her daughters-in-law were so moved they nearly cried.","Mo Hanyue clung tightly to He Zhiran's arm.","\"Sister-in-law, did you make all these dishes?\"","Not waiting for He Zhiran's reply, the eldest sister-in-law spoke proudly, \"These dishes are all made by your sister-in-law. Doesn't just looking make your mouth water?\"","Mo Hanyue nodded vigorously, her bright eyes full of admiration for He Zhiran.","\"My sister-in-law is the best. Not only does she know medicine, she is also fearless when facing those officials, and has such amazing cooking skills too.\"","As she spoke, Mo Hanyue had already rested her head on He Zhiran's shoulder.","\"Sister-in-law, I'll just follow you from now on. I must learn all these skills from you.\"","Seeing the innocent and pure little sister-in-law, He Zhiran stroked her messy hair.","\"Alright, as long as Hanyue wants to learn, sister-in-law will teach you.\"","Alone in the room, Mo Jiuye took a bite of the dishes.","His first feeling was that these must have been made by He Zhiran.","Those sisters-in-law definitely did not have such skills.","Not knowing if he felt lucky, the corners of Mo Jiuye's lips slightly curled up unconsciously.","At Lady Mo's command, the women immediately started eating.","Maybe because they hadn't eaten anything good these two days, they felt today's dishes were especially appetizing.","The full four dishes and one soup were eaten up almost completely.","Similarly, the officials felt He Zhiran's cooking was even more delicious than those restaurants in the capital city.","Especially that braised pork, fatty but not greasy, leaving one craving more after eating it.","Just as the officials were competing to grab food into their own bowls, He Ming and He Liang were helped over.","They knelt directly in front of the officials.","\"My lords, please serve justice for us brothers!\"","Seeing the arrivals, Peng Wang immediately scowled.","\"What happened?\"","He Ming quickly moved forward, \"My lords, relying on your protection, Miss He beat us brothers into this state.\"","As he spoke, he lifted his shirt, revealing the purple-blue mark on his stomach.","\"My lords, look, this is where He Zhiran hit me. And here too.\" He Ming continued lifting the back of his shirt.","He Liang also came forward to show the officials his bruised areas.","The officials looked at each other, clearly disbelief in their eyes.","There were rules for escorting exiled prisoners. It was expressly forbidden for prisoners to fight amongst themselves.","Of course, whether it was truly prohibited also depended on the officials' moods."]},{"number":40,"title":"Chapter 40: This woman's got a lot on her mind.","paragraphs":["Although most of the officials did not believe that He Zhiran would beat people like this, Peng Wang believed it.","He felt that this woman still had many amazing abilities that had not been discovered. Now seeing the miserable state of the He brothers, Peng Wang added another 'good at fighting' to He Zhiran's amazing abilities...","In Peng Wang's mind, this woman could not be provoked, even if she was currently under his command earning a living. He could not offend her.","Especially now, when he was eating the delicious food brought by her family, there would definitely be more such treatment in the future.","He, Peng Wang, would naturally have to take care of someone who could bring him so many benefits.","Peng Wang looked contemptuously at the He brothers.","\"You said you were beaten by the He family?\"","\"It's absolutely true, Sir. It was the He family who beat us.\" The He brothers felt extremely wronged.","After acting arrogantly in the capital for so many years, it was still the first time they had been beaten by a woman. At this moment, the two brothers wished they could kill He Zhiran.","\"It looks like you don't want to live anymore, daring to mock us like this.\" Zhang Qing became angrier the more he listened, and slammed his chopsticks heavily on the table, yelling at the two brothers.","The He brothers were frightened and their bodies shuddered.","However, what they said was the truth. They had come this time to get justice for themselves, so they could only stubbornly continue speaking.","\"Sir, we really didn't lie.\"","Peng Wang saw that Zhang Qing was still angry, and quickly spoke up to avoid ruining the dining atmosphere:","\"Since you said you were beaten by the He family, is there any witness?\"","The He brothers pointed to the few family members who had helped them over.","\"Sir, my family can testify.\"","Peng Wang glanced at the He family members present.","\"That doesn't count. If the He family members come out and testify that you beat her, will you admit it?\"","\"This...\" The He brothers were suddenly at a loss for words, not knowing what to do.","Peng Wang waved his hand: \"I'm in a good mood today, so I won't pursue your false accusations. Hurry up and get out!\"","Just as the He brothers were dejectedly being helped to leave, a woman's voice came from outside the door.","\"Sir, I can testify that I saw He Zhiran beat people with my own eyes.\"","Peng Wang looked towards the door, and it was Li Rou'er.","He cursed inwardly, really not knowing how He Zhiran had offended Li Rou'er, with her coming out everywhere to make trouble.","Li Rou'er had already pretentiously walked in as she spoke.","\"Sir, I saw He Zhiran beat people with my own eyes, this is absolutely true.\"","With so many people present, even if Peng Wang wanted to protect He Zhiran, he could not do so too obviously.","\"Since this is the case, call He over to confront her.\"","While someone went to call He Zhiran, Peng Wang had the He family taken out and asked Li Rou'er alone.","\"You said you saw the He family beat someone, tell me the whole process now!\"","It had to be said, Peng Wang was really wasting his talent as the little head responsible for escorting prisoners. At this moment, his interrogation methods were no worse than those officials at all.","Li Rou'er had not seen He Zhiran lay a hand on anyone at all. Her goal was simply not to let the latter have an easy time.","Since she could not make the other party lose face, she could only make use of these officials.","In order to make her words more credible, Li Rou'er was almost eloquent.","\"Sir, I saw He Zhiran with a very thick and long stick in her hand. She first beat down He Ming, then used the same method to beat He Liang until the two had no strength to fight back before she stopped.\"","Peng Wang nodded impercebtibly: \"Hmm, you stand aside first!\"","By this time, He Zhiran had also been called over.","She had just been wondering if this meal would have to be interrupted by someone calling her away before she could finish eating. Who would have thought the He brothers would be so slow to accuse her.","It wasn't until she was full that the officials came over to invite her.","The He brothers were also brought back by the officials and stood side by side with He Zhiran in front of Peng Wang.","\"Lady He, the He brothers accused you of assaulting them. Did this happen?\"","He Zhiran looked at them in utter disbelief.","She leaned exaggeratedly towards the He brothers, deliberately displaying her petite figure in front of them.","\"Captain Peng, do you actually believe this?\"","Peng Wang was amused by her words.","This woman really had a lot of tricks up her sleeve...","\"Cough cough... this is not about whether I believe it or not, the He family has a witness.\"","Only then did He Zhiran's gaze fall on Li Rou'er.","\"Captain Peng, don't tell me the witness you're talking about is her?\"","\"So what if it's me? He Zhiran, I saw you attack the He brothers with my own eyes, this is a fact, you shouldn't try to talk your way out of it.\" Li Rou'er looked extremely smug.","She wanted to see just how much ability He Zhiran had to reverse the situation.","He Zhiran sneered: \"Li Rou'er, not to mention that we used to be the best of friends who shared everything, even if there was some misunderstanding between us, you shouldn't target me like this, right?\"","As she spoke, He Zhiran pointed at the He brothers.","\"Look at their size, could I have beaten them?\"","The officials had just heard Li Rou'er's eloquent account and had somewhat believed that He Zhiran had assaulted people.","But now looking at the contrast between them, no matter how they looked at it, they could not believe that He Zhiran could lay a hand on two such burly men.","Thinking of this, the officials' gazes unanimously glared at Li Rou'er.","Only one man was different from the others.","He kept signalling to Li Rou'er with his eyes, seemingly reminding her not to keep talking.","All this did not escape He Zhiran's eyes, of course.","She secretly looked over that official who was signalling to Li Rou'er, and immediately had some guesses...","Seeing things were getting more and more out of hand, Peng Wang still wanted to resolve the matter quickly and continue eating.","\"That's enough, let the He brothers say it themselves, how did you beat them, Lady He?\"","Hearing this, Li Rou'er became nervous at once. She kept signalling to the He brothers with her eyes.","Alas, the He brothers just stared at He Zhiran resentfully, completely oblivious to Li Rou'er's signals.","He Liang stepped forward and said, \"Sir, He Zhiran first punched me in the stomach, then tripped me and hit my back...\"","Now Li Rou'er was dumbfounded.","She had planned it so well. As long as she testified for the He brothers, even if they weren't really beaten by He Zhiran, He Zhiran would still have to leave in frustration.","Who knew Peng Wang would be so crafty and turn the outcome around so quickly.","Peng Wang slammed the table hard, sending the chopsticks on it falling to the ground.","\"Take Li Rou'er out and give her ten lashes.\"","\"Sir, I really saw He Zhiran beat the He brothers, what I said is all true.\"","At this point, Li Rou'er could only continue to stubbornly insist, hoping to turn things around.","Who knew, the officials didn't even give her a chance to continue her sophistry, and directly came forward to take her away.","Because they knew clearly in their hearts that Li Rou'er was giving false testimony, and the He brothers definitely weren't beaten by Lady He either.","The official who had looked at Li Rou'er differently just now hurried to catch up.","\"Zhang Qing, leave this minor matter for me to deal with! You go back and keep the boss company to continue eating.\""]},{"number":41,"title":"Chapter 41: Cell Phone","paragraphs":["Zhang Qing was originally eager to eat delicious food. Seeing his companion taking the initiative, he directly handed Li Rou'er over to him.","\"Li Hu, don't make your old mistakes. People like her need to have a taste of bitterness.\"","Li Hu smiled and waved his hand, \"Don't worry! I promise I won't go easy on her.\"","Zhang Qing came back and kicked each of the He family brothers.","\"Get the hell out of here, all of you! If you dare cause trouble again, be careful or I'll whip you.\"","The He brothers were still a bit confused. It was supposed to be a done deal that Li Rou'er's testimony would make He Zhiran lose face. How did it end up like nothing had happened? Not only was He Zhiran unharmed, but Li Rou'er, who had kindly testified, was beaten instead.","The two brothers were puzzled as they were helped out. Seeing this, He Zhiran also bid farewell and left.","As she came out of Peng Wang's room, she saw Li Hu pull Li Rou'er to a corner.","As for what the two were about to do, it was none of her business.","She had just taken a few steps out when she heard Li Rou'er's exaggerated, pretentious cries of pain.","Clearly, it was all fake...","None of her business, she didn't care to expose it. Besides, there were plenty of ways to make Li Rou'er suffer without causing trouble over such a trivial matter. This time didn't matter.","Returning to the ten person room for Mo Family women, the sisters-in-law had already cleaned up the bowls and plates.","A few sisters-in-law had also gone to the kitchen to boil some hot water, preparing for a simple wash.","Speaking of washing up, He Zhiran was not idle either. She carried a basin of hot water to Mo Jiuye for him to wash first.","When no outsiders were around, Mo Jiuye looked the same as when he was uninjured, moving quite freely.","He took the wash basin He Zhiran brought in and placed it on the ground before asking,","\"What happened just now?\"","Although he couldn't go out, the sounds from outside definitely didn't escape his ears.","He Zhiran didn't hide anything at all, recounting how she beat up the He brothers and how Peng Wang broke the case.","Mo Jiuye clenched his fists tightly.","\"Truly too excessive.\"","He Zhiran had already beaten the He brothers, and Li Rou'er who gave false testimony didn't end up well either, so she was already over it and wouldn't take it to heart.","Seeing Mo Jiuye angry, He Zhiran softly comforted, \"I didn't suffer any losses, no need to get upset with those people.\"","Mo Jiuye didn't say anything more, just washed up with dark eyes.","He Zhiran knew it wasn't convenient for her to stay here right now, so she took the initiative to go outside and close the room door.","The rare leisure time, He Zhiran sat on the small horse mat in the courtyard of the inn to rest.","On the surface she was resting, but her consciousness had already entered the space.","Since obtaining this space, besides taking and storing items, she hadn't thoroughly researched it yet.","He Zhiran planned to take this opportunity to properly investigate.","After looking around, He Zhiran discovered a problem.","Although this space had a regeneration function, it was only for items originally within the space.","The silver she had just given the innkeeper, after over an hour had passed, still hadn't returned.","It could be seen from this that items from the ancient times she brought into the space did not have a regeneration function.","Apart from this, He Zhiran checked some medical equipment and medicines in the space again.","After organizing a bit, she suddenly discovered a cell phone in an inconspicuous corner.","This cell phone was not unfamiliar to He Zhiran at all, it was the one she had just replaced not long ago.","Because she got a new phone, the old one was left aside as an idle item.","He Zhiran hurriedly turned on the phone with her mind.","Unfortunately, the phone was already out of battery.","Luckily, her charger was still there.","Plugging in the phone, to her delight, there was still electricity in the space. This made He Zhiran excited again.","There was electricity in the space, she could do a lot.","Especially those advanced medical devices, without electricity they were just decorations.","But right now, her attention was all on this phone.","If she could contact acquaintances from her past life after turning it on, it would be good to explain some matters.","After a few minutes, He Zhiran finally pressed the power button.","The phone screen lit up.","But it didn't show the interface He Zhiran was familiar with.","The original wallpaper of a photo of herself in military uniform had now become an abstract landscape painting.","And those apps were all gone, leaving only a lonely Taobao shopping app.","This shopping app was very familiar to He Zhiran, she often used it for online shopping in her past life.","He Zhiran was in no hurry to open Taobao, and flipped through the phone pages back and forth. She felt like it was just the phone being slow from age, and those apps should still be there.","But after flipping continuously for a while, she could confirm that there really were no other apps on the phone.","Even the phone's basic calling and messaging functions had vanished without a trace.","This puzzled He Zhiran, and she tried connecting to the WiFi originally in the space.","The WiFi connected successfully very quickly, which gave He Zhiran hope again.","She thought that after connecting to WiFi she could go to the app store and download other apps.","The result was frustrating. The app store itself didn't exist.","He Zhiran resigned herself to fate, it seemed the phone was deliberately like this.","In low spirits, He Zhiran opened the Taobao app.","Opening Taobao, it was still the familiar interface, nothing special at all.","She randomly chose a hair clip for a few yuan to purchase, and the payment interface immediately appeared on the screen.","At the same time, He Zhiran also noticed that the delivery address was actually the Da Shun Dynasty...","It could be seen from this that her transmigration was perhaps premeditated.","She just didn't know which bored deity insisted on sending her here to suffer.","Perhaps it was Heaven sympathizing with Mo Jiuye's merits and unwilling to let him die on the road of exile, wanting to give him a chance to survive.","Apart from this, He Zhiran couldn't think of any other more suitable reason.","No matter, He Zhiran tentatively clicked to continue payment.","The prompt below showed payment method.","Seeing there was still 1,300 yuan balance in Alipay, He Zhiran directly chose Alipay.","Right after successful payment, the hair clip appeared before her.","He Zhiran was extremely delighted. Although the phone couldn't contact the outside world, having such a convenient shopping function was an absolute boon for her.","Seeing the successful purchase of the hair clip, she tried buying a pack of snacks, intending to test if she could pay by debit card.","The result this time disappointed He Zhiran a bit.","The interface displayed that she had no linked bank card.","This was unscientific. In her past life, although she didn't have much savings, a frequent shopper couldn't possibly not have a linked bank card on Taobao.","Moreover, charging Alipay also required a bank card.","This could only mean that after her past life death, the card had been frozen or cancelled.","After confirming she couldn't pay by bank card, He Zhiran immediately recognized the preciousness of that 1,300 yuan in Alipay."]},{"number":42,"title":"Chapter 42: I just went to take it out on you.","paragraphs":["Just as she was somewhat disappointedly flipping through the Taobao app, she suddenly discovered a feature here.","That is, become a seller.","But what should she sell to become a seller?","Hesitating, He Zhiran's eyes unconsciously swept over those items from the Duke of Protector and the National Treasury.","He Zhiran's eyes suddenly lit up. She seemed to be able to open an antique specialty store, specializing in selling these ancient good things.","This happened to solve the issue of the future exposure of those things from the National Treasury, so it was killing two birds with one stone.","Having got an idea, He Zhiran then planned to systematically study the store opening process.","She had just opened the instructions for opening a store when she heard someone calling her.","\"He family, is Jiuye asleep? I want to go chat with him.\"","He Zhiran withdrew her consciousness back to space, and saw Xie Tianhai had come. She quickly got up and led him into the room she shared with Mo Jiuye.","Mo Jiuye had already washed up without being noticed and had already emptied the water.","Hearing the voices outside, he hurriedly lay back down on the bed.","Xie Tianhai had just sat down on the edge of the bed when Fang Chuanzhou also came.","This was perfect. Mo Jiuye only needed to receive them once to explain everything clearly.","He Zhiran brought over a chair and put it next to Xie Tianhai, signaling Fang Chuanzhou to sit down.","Then she turned around and closed the door.","He Zhiran chose to avoid them for two reasons.","First, she considered the ancient etiquette that men didn't like women around when they were talking.","Second, this was her real purpose. She wanted to take the opportunity to continue researching opening a store on Taobao.","Returning to her original sitting position, He Zhiran's consciousness entered the space again.","She read the instructions for opening a store carefully.","It turned out that opening a store on Taobao required a deposit of 1,000 yuan. Fortunately, she still had some petty cash in her Alipay account.","She decisively paid the deposit and waited for the certification to be successful.","What He Zhiran had to do next was to find a storefront production team on Taobao to help her design an appropriate interface style.","After picking and choosing, He Zhiran finally selected an antique style design that was very suitable for her store style.","The only thing was that the price made her heartache a bit, it was actually 288 yuan.","Gritting her teeth to pay, He Zhiran felt like she had instantly become a pauper.","But it didn't matter, she was confident that she could earn more money in the future.","The certification would be completed within twenty-four hours. He Zhiran felt there was no need to keep waiting. As long as she kept thinking about checking it occasionally, it would be fine.","After sensing the time, half an hour had passed.","The conversation between Mo Jiuye and the two men should have ended.","He Zhiran dragged her somewhat tired body back to the room.","Sure enough, Xie Tianhai and Fang Chuanzhou had already left.","In the dim candlelight, she observed Mo Jiuye's expression.","Seeing that he looked much more relaxed than before, He Zhiran knew that he had explained the misunderstanding.","Mo Jiuye slowly spoke.","\"It's been resolved.\"","\"Did they believe you?\" He Zhiran asked.","\"Well, with such an obvious loophole, they have no choice but to believe it.\"","As for how Mo Jiuye spoke to the two men, He Zhiran did not ask in detail. She just needed to make sure of the result.","\"In the future when we eat or do other things, should we bring Xie and Fang families together?\"","He Zhiran was thinking that the National Treasury was emptied by Mo Jiuye taking her there, so the things inside naturally belonged to both of them.","As long as Mo Jiuye didn't mind, she didn't object to using his half to provide for Xie's and Fang's families.","Mo Jiuye pondered for a moment.","\"Let's play it by ear. After all, the misunderstanding has been resolved, but beware not to let them find anything wrong.\"","He Zhiran understood: \"Okay, as you say.\"","After chatting for a few more sentences, He Zhiran went out to wash up.","As a result, as soon as she walked to the kitchen door, she heard a kind of arousing sound coming from the corner.","And He Zhiran was very familiar with this sound.","It was Li Rou'er.","She couldn't help but smile. When being interrogated by Peng Wang earlier, she had noticed the abnormal gaze of that yamen clerk looking at Li Rou'er.","And when they left, she also noticed Li Rou'er's fake cry of pain.","She just didn't expect these two to get together so quickly.","He Zhiran didn't have the habit of interfering with others' happiness. She hurriedly fetched water from the kitchen and went back to the room to simply wash her hands, feet and face, then prepared to rest.","Mo Jiuye was still on the bed. She chose to sleep on the floor.","Seeing this, Mo Jiuye immediately got off the bed.","\"You sleep on the bed, I'll sleep on the floor.\"","\"The floor is cold. You're still injured. I don't mind sleeping on the floor.\"","\"No, you sleep on the bed.\"","Seeing Mo Jiuye insist, and unwilling to let an injured person sleep on the floor, He Zhiran could only suggest:","\"Why don't we both sleep on the bed, keeping some distance in between.\"","\"Okay, you sleep inside, I'll be outside, I promise not to touch you.\" Although Mo Jiuye was a little embarrassed, he couldn't be shy forever in front of his own wife.","He Zhiran moved nimbly and crawled to the very inside of the bed, then pulled the corner of the quilt over herself.","Mo Jiuye also lay down right next to the edge of the bed, leaving a large gap between them.","He Zhiran was really tired today, and soon fell asleep.","However, she was a light sleeper.","In a daze, she felt the bed move.","She opened her eyes slightly to see Mo Jiuye get up and tidy up his clothes, then left the room.","If Mo Jiuye hadn't tidied up his clothes, He Zhiran would have thought he went to the bathroom.","Could he tidy up his clothes to go to the bathroom?","Therefore, He Zhiran could determine that Mo Jiuye must have gone to do something.","Out of curiosity, she also got up and followed him out.","She saw Mo Jiuye leave the room. After observing for a while, he activated his lightness skill and leapt towards the back courtyard.","He Zhiran didn't know any lightness skills. Seeing Mo Jiuye's figure disappear from her sight, she could only helplessly return to the room.","At this moment she had no sleepiness at all, and kept wondering what Mo Jiuye went to do.","After about the time it takes to burn a stick of incense, Mo Jiuye returned and gently lay down at the edge of the bed.","He Zhiran was alert, and so was Mo Jiuye.","From He Zhiran's breathing he could determine that she was not asleep at the moment.","\"I just went to avenge you.\"","\"Don't tell me you went to deal with the He brothers?\" He Zhiran was shocked.","This man really...really was a bit protective.","She had already taught the He brothers a lesson, yet he still had to take revenge...","\"I will never let anyone who dares to bully you get away with it.\"","He Zhiran was a little curious how Mo Jiuye avenged her.","\"What did you do to them?\"","Mo Jiuye deliberately sold her a dilemma: \"You'll know tomorrow morning. Unfortunately I didn't see Li Rou'er at the Li family. She got away today.\"","\"You hit women too?\" Hearing Li Rou'er's name, He Zhiran suddenly became interested.","\"This is the first time I've had the urge to be violent towards a woman.\""]},{"number":43,"title":"Chapter 43: Watch the Fun","paragraphs":["He Zhiran listened to Mo Jiuye speak in such a matter-of-fact tone, and knew that he was also very helpless, so she didn't intend to continue teasing him.","\"When I went to the kitchen just now, I saw Li Rou'er fooling around with an officer.\"","Chatting about this kind of gossip was not Mo Jiuye's forte, so he did not respond.","Seeing that he was no longer speaking, He Zhiran simply closed her eyes and continued to brew her sleepiness.","Perhaps it was because Mo Jiuye was by her side, He Zhiran's vigilance relaxed a lot.","That night she slept exceptionally soundly, and still got up early the next morning.","Just out of the door, she saw Mrs. Zhao waiting there.","Mrs. Zhao looked left and right, then pulled He Zhiran into a corner.","\"Auntie, what's the matter?\" He Zhiran knew that Mrs. Zhao wanted to tell her something in private, so she spoke very softly.","Mrs. Zhao looked around cautiously again, and after making sure no one was around, she said in a low voice:","\"Auntie got up last night and saw the maid from the Li family fooling around with an officer.\"","He Zhiran had also witnessed this with her own eyes, so she was not particularly surprised.","\"Auntie, that's their business. Let's just turn a blind eye.\"","\"I wanted to turn a blind eye, but I heard what they said, and I feel I should give you a reminder.\"","From Mrs. Zhao's words, Li Rou'er must have mentioned her when messing around with Li Hu. Otherwise, Mrs. Zhao would not have come to find her so early in the morning.","\"Auntie, did they talk about me?\"","\"I was a little far away at the time, but I vaguely heard that officer seem to promise Li Rou'er that he would make trouble for you.\"","Upon hearing this, He Zhiran's face darkened a little.","Li Rou'er really was asking for death. She saw her acting like a clown all day long, and was too lazy to pay any attention to her, yet she was still relentless.","\"Thank you for the reminder, Auntie. I'll be careful.\"","Seeing that He Zhiran's response was nonchalant, Mrs. Zhao couldn't help but remind her.","\"An officer wanting to make trouble for you is no trivial matter. You should discuss it with Jiuye and see how to deal with it!\"","\"I understand, Auntie. I'll discuss it with my husband in a moment.\"","He Zhiran verbally agreed, pretending to chat idly with Mrs. Zhao so that no one would notice anything unusual.","After sending Mrs. Zhao away, He Zhiran went to the inn's kitchen, intending to borrow a wooden basin to wash up.","At this time, Peng Wang and several officers also came out of their respective rooms.","The officers were preparing to distribute breakfast of black flour buns to the exiled prisoners. Of course, now the only recipients were the He and Li families.","As for the Fang and Xie families, Peng Wang could see yesterday that Mo Jiuye was deliberately befriending them, so of course he could not continue to watch them nibble on black flour buns, and did not go to call them to receive it.","Needless to say about the Mo family, with such a capable woman there, they certainly would not eat black flour buns.","Moreover, they had money on hand to buy some food at the inn, which was not a big deal.","He Zhiran did intend to buy more ingredients from the inn owner.","However, this time she only gave the owner one or two taels of silver.","Breakfast didn't need to be so extravagant, just some rice porridge and side dishes would suffice.","Seeing He Zhiran enter the kitchen, sister-in-law and fifth sister-in-law knew she was going to prepare breakfast, and they hurried to follow her.","Breakfast was simple, and sister-in-law and fifth sister-in-law did not need He Zhiran to lift a finger.","Seeing this, He Zhiran was also happy to relax.","As she walked out of the kitchen, she was called over by Peng Wang.","\"Today I will send two officers into town to purchase supplies for the road. You can go with them to purchase.\"","Being able to go out and shop, He Zhiran couldn't hide the smile on her face.","She had been here for many days and still had not toured the market!","Now she finally had a chance. Not only did she want to get a feel for the market conditions here, but also to replenish the supplies she would need for the future.","\"Thank you, Officer Peng.\" He Zhiran sincerely thanked him.","\"We still have to continue on the road in the afternoon. Make good use of the morning time.\" Peng Wang kindly reminded her.","\"A morning is enough.\" He Zhiran said and then went to prepare.","She had just walked out a few steps when she heard a shrill scream coming from the thatched hut.","\"Ah... what's wrong with my son...\"","When the officers distributed the black flour buns just now, they cringed at the heavy smell and simply threw a package of black flour buns over from afar, without bothering to check.","Hearing this sound, the officers rushed towards the thatched hut in unison.","He Zhiran thought to herself that this must be Mo Jiuye's doing, she just didn't know how miserably the two brothers had been tormented by him to make their family members scream so painfully.","With a gossipy mindset, He Zhiran followed the officers running to the thatched hut.","Through the gaps in the crowd, two bloody masses could be seen lying inconspicuously on the ground.","To be precise, they were the He brothers, He Ming and He Liang.","At this moment, their faces were completely unrecognizable, smeared with blood, and their long hair was matted against their faces.","There seemed to be no visible wounds on their bodies. On closer inspection, the injuries were actually on their wrists and ankles.","This scene frightened the women and children to hide far away. Some huddled in the corner sobbing but did not dare come closer.","A woman who looked to be around fifty years old knelt next to the two men, crying her heart out.","\"Which heartless bastard did this... Woo... Inflicting such cruelty on my sons... Woo... Our He family is already miserable enough, suffering this unjust calamity of having our home raided and being exiled, yet my son is also injured like this... Woo...\"","Although He Zhiyuan saw his two sons' miserable state, he did not wail loudly. Instead, he stood there with his hands on his hips, pacing back and forth, looking extremely vexed.","Seeing the officers come over, He Zhiyuan was as if he saw a savior.","He grabbed Peng Wang's sleeve.","\"Officer, you must do justice for my sons. They were still hale and hearty pushing carts for you yesterday. This morning they became like this. \"","Peng Wang also felt this was a headache when he saw this scene.","In all his years working as an escort officer, this was still the first time he had encountered such an incident.","If it was said the He brothers held a grudge against someone?","Then it could only be the Mo family.","Other than Mo Jiuye, who was bedridden with serious injuries, the rest of the Mo family were all women.","Even though He Zhiran was quite capable, she was still just a frail woman. Bullying and intimidating people with some fancy fist and foot work was one thing, but Peng Wang did not believe in his heart that He Zhiran could inflict such injuries on someone.","Just as he was frowning in thought, He Zhiyuan's eyes landed on He Zhiran, who was standing at the back of the crowd watching the commotion.","He pointed at He Zhiran and said, \"Officer, it must be her, this venomous woman who injured my sons so badly.","Other than the Mo family, we haven't offended anyone. This venomous woman beat up my sons last night too. Officer, you must do justice for my sons...\"","Peng Wang impatiently pushed He Zhiyuan aside.","\"How could you think she, a weak woman, could injure someone like this?\""]},{"number":44,"title":"Chapter 44: To the Fair","paragraphs":["Peng Wang said, pointing to the crowd and asking, \"Who among you believes this? Who believes these two were injured by the He family?\"","At this moment, the families staying at the inn also came over upon hearing the commotion.","When the crowd heard Peng Wang's question, they shook their heads to indicate disbelief.","Not to mention that they didn't believe it, even He Zhiyuan himself didn't believe it.","On one hand, he couldn't find the real culprit, on the other hand, he also wanted to take this opportunity to make things difficult for the Mo Family.","Little did he expect, Peng Wang didn't buy into his tricks at all.","An arrow released cannot be brought back. He Zhiyuan had already said those words, so he had to stick to it till the end.","\"My lord, you said she couldn't do it, but look at so many people here, only the Mo Family hates us the most, who else could it be if not them?\"","\"Shut up!\" Peng Wang's patience was completely exhausted by him, shouting loudly, and He Zhiyuan instantly fell silent.","The Eighth Old Zhou stepped forward.","\"Boss, let me go take a look first to see if they still have a breath in them.\"","\"Mm.\" Peng Wang was thinking the same thing. They still had to figure out whether these two were dead or alive.","The Eighth Old Zhou checked the breaths of the two men, and turned his head.","\"Boss, they're not dead.\"","Indeed they were not dead. Mo Jiuye felt that letting them die so easily would be too cheap. When making his move, he was extremely careful about proportions.","Last night, he had quietly come out and went directly to the hut. After finding the He brothers, he pressed their acupoints, then brought them to the corner and severed the sinews in their hands and feet.","As for the blood on their faces, it was also deliberately done by Mo Jiuye, taking blood from their wrists and smearing it on.","The purpose was to make them look more terrifying and frighten the Li and He families.","Since the people were not dead, Peng Wang still had to make a show of saving them out of his sense of duty.","The first person he thought of was He Zhiran.","\"Ms. He, you're the only one here who understands medicine, so why don't you go take a look?\"","Through the interactions over the past two days, Peng Wang knew that He Zhiran was smart and didn't have much confidence in ordering her to do things.","Nevertheless, he still had to get He Zhiran to treat them.","The He family simply didn't have the silver to hire an imperial physician. He didn't want to pay out of his own pocket either.","Even if He Zhiran ended up healing them to death, it didn't matter.","He Zhiran had already carefully observed their wounds. She had to say, Mo Jiuye's technique of severing the sinews in people's hands and feet was quite skillful.","The size of the wounds was like that of minimally invasive surgical incisions in her past life. They didn't even need suturing.","Also, the fact that the two were still alive now meant that Mo Jiuye had avoided their arteries.","Treating these two wasn't difficult. All that was needed was to stop the bleeding from the wounds, then slowly nourish them. She could even reconnect their severed sinews.","But she felt that she had no obligation to treat her enemies.","\"Prefect Peng, I'm not skilled at treating external injuries. You should think of another way!\"","In any case, these two wouldn't die. Their hands and feet were just disabled. Even if they lived, they would be cripples for the rest of their lives.","Seeing that Peng Wang was on the verge of losing his temper, He Zhiran quickly added.","\"Prefect Peng, surely you wouldn't force someone to do the impossible?\"","Peng Wang...","Now that she had put it this way, if he continued to insist, it really would be forcing her.","Left with no choice, Peng Wang could only wave his hand to let He Zhiran leave.","Having seen enough of the commotion, He Zhiran took this opportunity to return to the front yard of the inn.","The two sisters-in-law had prepared breakfast, a big iron pot full of white porridge, with a side dish.","He Zhiran took the initiative to call the Fang and Xie families to eat together, once again receiving their gratitude.","She didn't know how Prefect Peng had dealt with the matter of the He brothers being injured. In any case, after the yamen runners came back, the people at the hut had quieted down.","When the yamen runners came back and saw Mo Family eating white rice porridge with the Fang and Xie families, they suddenly felt their steamed buns were no longer fragrant.","However, seeing that the porridge in the big iron pot was almost gone, the yamen runners could only reluctantly keep their distance.","After breakfast, the Eighth Old Zhou came to call He Zhiran to go to the marketplace together.","He Zhiran planned to purchase a lot of supplies, so she pushed along the wooden cart.","Arriving at the entrance of the inn, she saw Li Hu waiting there, and Li Hu's gaze at her carried a sinister feeling.","He Zhiran pretended not to see it.","\"Prefect Zhou, let's go!\"","The Eighth Old Zhou didn't say anything more either, walking side by side with Li Hu in front.","After turning a corner, there were more and more people. He Zhiran knew the marketplace was close.","The Eighth Old Zhou halted his footsteps, pointing ahead, \"This is the marketplace. We need to buy some rations. You follow behind and buy what you need at the same time.\"","He Zhiran certainly didn't want to go shopping together with the two yamen runners.","She still had quite a lot of grain in her space that was moved from the Mo Residence before the confiscation. If she followed them, she wouldn't have a chance to take it out.","So, He Zhiran's eyes spun in thought.","\"Prefect Zhou, I have a lot of things to buy. Following you would likely delay a lot of time. Why don't I go buy them myself, and let's agree on a time and location to meet up later?\"","The Eighth Old Zhou hesitated.","He Zhiran was an exiled convict. Once she left his sight, there was a possibility she would run away.","A convict escaping was no small matter for a yamen runner. They would be punished upon returning to the capital.","Seeing the Eighth Old Zhou's hesitation, He Zhiran decided to meticulously explain her reasoning.","\"Prefect Zhou, if I didn't want to be exiled together with my husband, with my father's capabilities, he would definitely have tried to find a way to keep me in the capital. I wouldn't be so silly as to secretly run away during exile.","Moreover, the Mo Family people are still at the inn. I wouldn't leave them behind and escape alone.\"","The Eighth Old Zhou also felt He Zhiran's words made a lot of sense, but he was timid and still somewhat worried.","Just then, Li Hu spoke up.","\"Brother Ba, I think Ms. He's words make sense. If she dares to run away, when we return I'll break Mo Jiuye's legs.\"","On the surface, Li Hu was speaking for He Zhiran, but He Zhiran discerned other intentions in it.","Li Hu was probably hoping that she would deliberately not come back, helping Li Rou'er eliminate an eyesore, while also taking the chance to torture Mo Jiuye.","This made He Zhiran begin to doubt Li Hu's true identity.","He was highly likely someone planted here to monitor Mo Jiuye, only pretending to work as a yamen runner on the surface.","If that was really the case, Li Hu had to be gotten rid of.","Although she was thinking this in her heart, He Zhiran didn't show any of it on her face.","\"Prefect Zhou, I really won't run away.\"","\"Brother Ba, don't hesitate anymore. Doing our job is most important.\" Li Hu urged again.","The Eighth Old Zhou nodded with difficulty.","\"Alright, I'll trust you this once. Let's regroup here before noon.\"","He Zhiran's goal was achieved, and she let out a sigh of relief.","\"Don't worry, I guarantee I won't be late.\"","Parting ways with the two yamen runners, He Zhiran headed straight to the marketplace pushing the wooden cart.","The marketplace was bustling with people coming and going, and vendors' shouts rang out continuously.","He Zhiran's time was limited, so she only casually looked around at the lively atmosphere.","The shops lining the streets had their doors open for business."]},{"number":45,"title":"Chapter 45: Procurement","paragraphs":["Fortunately, He Zhiran completely inherited the original host's memory, so she could recognize these traditional character signboards.","When she got to a pork shop, He Zhiran asked about the prices. She was happily surprised to find that the pork ribs here were actually cheaper than the pork meat.","Pork was 18 wen per catty, while pork ribs only cost 8 wen.","He Zhiran bought a slab of pork ribs without hesitation. Not only was it cheap, but it was also her favorite thing to eat.","Other people would think she was stingy for not buying the more expensive pork and only getting the cheap ribs.","After buying the pork, she asked the boss to chop it into small pieces and put it in her wheelbarrow.","He Zhiran went into a general store again.","The shopkeeper looked completely listless, sitting with his head down behind the counter, not even glancing at the customer who had entered.","In her previous life, if He Zhiran encountered a shopkeeper like this, she would have just left immediately.","However, it was different here. She didn't want to waste time looking for another general store, so she could only browse around the shop herself.","The goods were arranged somewhat messily here. After looking around, He Zhiran still hadn't found what she wanted to buy.","\"Shopkeeper, do you have oil paper here?\"","The shopkeeper finally listlessly lifted his head upon hearing a customer ask a question.","\"There is oil paper. Young lady, how much do you need?\"","He Zhiran thought that in the future, she would often take things out of her space. She couldn't always grab things with her hands like the pickled pork belly.","Therefore, the more oil paper the better for her.","\"However much oil paper you have here, I want it all.\"","The shopkeeper clearly didn't believe her words.","\"Young lady, you're not joking are you? I have a lot of oil paper here.\"","\"I'm not joking. As long as the price is fair, I guarantee I'll take it all.\"","The shopkeeper hurriedly got up and went behind the curtain. He quickly came back carrying a large stack of oil paper.","He Zhiran estimated that there were at least over a thousand sheets, which was indeed a lot.","The shopkeeper put the oil paper on the counter.","\"Young lady, there are one thousand one hundred sheets of oil paper. It's ten sheets for one wen here, a price you definitely won't find anywhere else.\"","Although He Zhiran wasn't very familiar with the prices in this era, she could tell from instinct that the shopkeeper wasn't deceiving her.","\"Alright, I'll take all of these oil paper sheets.\"","She used her sleeve to cover as she took out two strings of copper coins from her space.","These copper coins were all pilfered from the national treasury. She had cartons of them, so she didn't feel bad about spending them at all.","She counted out one hundred and ten wen and gave it to the shopkeeper. Just as He Zhiran was about to hug the oil paper and leave, she saw a young man rush in looking panicked.","\"Father, I just went to ask around at the inn again. The merchant who we ordered the oilcloth from really ran away.\"","The shopkeeper sat despondently on the chair, covering his face with his hands, not knowing if he was crying or not.","The young man passed by He Zhiran and went behind the counter.","\"Father, what do we do now?\"","The shopkeeper shook his head, his tone full of helplessness.","\"Sigh...We used all our family's savings to order that batch of oilcloth. Now that the merchant has absconded, we can only try to sell off this oilcloth at a low price.\"","When He Zhiran heard this, she immediately turned back.","She was very interested in the oilcloth they mentioned.","\"Shopkeeper, can I take a look at the oilcloth you're talking about?\"","The shopkeeper looked at He Zhiran, still with a helpless expression.","\"Young lady, don't make things more complicated. That oilcloth is for making umbrellas. You won't be able to use it even if you buy it.\"","He Zhiran had guessed that the oilcloth they mentioned might have waterproof properties. Hearing the shopkeeper say this, she could now fully confirm that this was exactly what she wanted.","\"Shopkeeper, in any case you're going to sell the oilcloth. Why don't you let me take a look? If it's suitable, I'll buy some.\"","\"Young lady, please wait a moment. I'll bring some samples for you to see.\" The young man's mind was nimbler than the shopkeeper's. He didn't mind the trouble and immediately got up to fetch the oilcloth.","Soon, he came back holding a piece of green and black oilcloth.","\"Young lady, take a look. Our family's oilcloth is thin and makes umbrellas that are lightweight and durable.\"","He Zhiran reached out to feel the oilcloth. Indeed, as the young man said, the oilcloth was very thin.","However, it was woven very densely and looked to be very good quality at first glance.","\"Young sir, how much does this oilcloth cost?\"","The young man probably couldn't make decisions on his own. He turned to consult with the shopkeeper.","\"Father, I think as long as we can recover some of the capital on this oilcloth, that's good enough. Why don't we just sell it at cost price?\"","The shopkeeper nodded with difficulty.","\"Young lady, if you buy a whole bolt, it will be at our cost price of 500 wen per bolt.\"","He Zhiran didn't understand the prices, but hearing any amount of wen was cheap to her ears.","She asked some more questions about the length and width per bolt of cloth, and calculated that one bolt of oilcloth could make two simple tents if used to create makeshift tents.","\"Shopkeeper, how much oilcloth do you have?\"","The shopkeeper's eyes bulged again. \"How much do you want?\"","After some calculations, He Zhiran wanted to make simple tents that could fit two people each. There were twelve people in the He family, plus another twenty from the Xie and Fang families.","She couldn't leave out those officials who were always trying to fleece the convicts either.","With so many people, they would need at least twenty five tents.","\"Shopkeeper, I want thirteen bolts of oilcloth.\"","Hearing this number, the shopkeeper felt like there must be something wrong with his ears. Disregarding his image, he vigorously picked at his ears.","The young man reacted quickly again. \"Young lady, please wait. I'll fetch the oilcloth for you now.\"","He Zhiran raised her hand to stop him.","\"No rush. I've bought so many things that I'm not sure if your shop can deliver them to my door?\"","\"We can deliver within Yunlai County.\" The young man quickly agreed.","After confirming they could deliver, He Zhiran bought enough bamboo poles and hemp ropes.","When paying the silver, she also remembered to remind them:","\"Young sir, I need eight black and five green bolts, delivered together with the bamboo poles to the inn west of the city.\"","\"Ok, no problem.\" The young man agreed and immediately ran to the back room to prepare the goods.","Seeing that the general store didn't have anything else she needed, He Zhiran pushed her cart and left.","On the road, she deliberately looked for a few deserted alleys and gradually took the foodstuffs out of her space and loaded them onto the wheelbarrow.","She had also purchased various vegetables the farmers were selling, to use as cover when taking things out of her space.","As He Zhiran shopped along the way, she stealthily took out some seasonings and other items from her space.","When she passed the grain shop, she bought a jar of vegetable oil, and also bought two empty jars from the boss. She used the peanut oil from her space to gradually fill up the jars.","Finally, at the blacksmith's shop she bought three large iron pots and three iron spatulas, three water kettles and other commonly used items.","The wheelbarrow kept getting heavier, and He Zhiran was starting to have trouble pushing it.","There was no other way. She had to take all these things out into the open, and didn't dare put them into her space to transport back. She could only painfully push the wheelbarrow forward.","He Zhiran knew that with the physical strength of this body, she probably wouldn't be able to go much farther.","Therefore, she could only reluctantly choose to go back the same way."]},{"number":46,"title":"Chapter 46: Beating Li Hu","paragraphs":["Luckily there was a fabric shop at the entrance to the market.","He Zhiran bought over thirty cotton quilts and large quantities of needle and thread, and still asked the fabric shop owner to deliver them to the inn.","Looking at the clock in the space, there was still half an hour before the time she had agreed with The Eighth Old Zhou.","He Zhiran strenuously pushed the cart and rushed over, intending to find a shady place to rest for a while.","The cart stopped outside a high wall, and He Zhiran casually sat on a large rock.","Taking advantage of her free time, she entered the space with her consciousness to check whether her shop had passed the review.","The result was somewhat disappointing to her, with the words \"Please be patient and wait\" displayed on the phone screen.","He Zhiran boredly withdrew her consciousness and looked around.","She didn't know why, but she inexplicably had a bad premonition.","She always felt something would happen.","It was very likely that Li Hu had done something.","Although she had this sense, He Zhiran really couldn't guess for a while how Li Hu would make things difficult for her.","Time passed bit by bit, and when it was already past noon, He Zhiran increasingly felt something was wrong.","Given The Eighth Old Zhou's personality, he didn't seem like the kind of person who would break an appointment.","What's more, they were just going to buy some rations, which really wouldn't take so much time.","He Zhiran immediately made a decision - that was, not to wait any longer, she would go back to the inn alone.","No matter what medicine Li Hu's gourd sold, it was definitely not wrong for her to go back on time.","So, He Zhiran pushed the cart towards the Western Inn without hesitation.","Yunlai County was not big to begin with. After walking for about two quarters of an hour, she saw the gate of the inn.","Just as He Zhiran was about to push the cart through the gate, a whip came flying at her face.","Luckily she was agile and dodged it in time.","The other party didn't give her any chance to catch her breath at all, and the second whip lashed out at her face again.","\"Ms. He, you actually dared to run away. Watch me beat you to death.\"","Li Hu brandished the whip in his hand, looking extremely fierce,","As if he and He Zhiran had some deep enmity.","He Zhiran was suddenly attacked when she least expected it, and was already angry.","Seeing Li Hu's hideous face made her anger rise sharply.","She raised her hand and mercilessly grabbed the whip that hit her.","With a clever twist, she pulled Li Hu along with the whip outside the gate.","Taking advantage of Li Hu not having stood firm yet, He Zhiran flew up and kicked him in the waist.","Li Hu yelled in pain, and the whip slipped from his hand.","Clutching his kicked waist, he pointed at He Zhiran, cursing viciously.","\"You cheap woman, you actually dare to attack an official. I see you don't want to live to go to the northwest.\"","The commotion at the gate was not small, and other officials and prisoners also came over to see what was going on.","They saw He Zhiran with her hands on her hips, glaring angrily at Li Hu.","While Li Hu was just like a shrew, not daring to fight back but only cursing.","Seeing his companions come over, Li Hu suddenly gained courage.","\"Boss, it's good you guys are here. Quickly catch this cheap woman. She is unruly, not only trying to escape, but also daring to attack me.\"","He Zhiran was now completely infuriated by Li Hu. Seeing him still falsely accusing her, she flew up and kicked him squarely in his dirty mouth without hesitation.","Li Hu gave a muffled grunt, and put his hand over his mouth.","When he took his hand away, there were two bloody teeth in his palm.","This showed how much strength He Zhiran had used.","This still wasn't enough for He Zhiran to vent her anger. She was about to go up and give Li Hu a beating when Peng Wang finally spoke.","\"Ms. He, stop.\"","No matter how angry He Zhiran was, her reason was still there.","She was very clear in her heart that of all these officials, the one she could not offend was Peng Wang.","He was the boss of this group. Once she offended him, there would be endless trouble from the Mo Family people in the future.","\"Lord Peng, I will spare him for now because of the face you have given me, but this matter today must be explained to me.\"","If it was in the past, when his subordinates were beaten, Peng Wang would have chosen to protect them without listening to any explanation.","However, today's protagonist was different.","This Li Hu had been inexplicably arranged in his team half a year ago.","At first Peng Wang thought that having a newcomer was nothing much, but he found that Li Hu was greedy and lecherous, and often played mind games with his brothers.","After a long time, Peng Wang became very displeased with Li Hu.","Thinking that someone might be backing him, Peng Wang didn't kick him out of the team, but would reprimand him from time to time.","The other protagonist He Zhiran, in Peng Wang's eyes, was not only resourceful but also smart. She would not inexplicably fight with Li Hu.","Moreover, looking at He Zhiran's angry appearance, Li Hu must have done something unforgivable.","In fact, Peng Wang had thought too much. He assumed it was Li Hu coveting He Zhiran's beauty and his old problem had recurred.","If it were other matters, with He Zhiran's composure, she would not have been angered to this extent.","In any case, Li Hu was his own subordinate. He could not let He Zhiran expose Li Hu's true face in front of everyone.","That would reflect badly on him as the boss.","\"Don't argue anymore, come with me, all of you.\"","Seeing the officials silently following Peng Wang towards the guest room, He Zhiran quickly scanned around but did not see any sign of The Eighth Old Zhou.","He Zhiran suddenly had an enlightened feeling.","The reason Li Hu was waiting at the door to hit her was probably just to get back at Li Rou'er.","What would really ruin her was The Eighth Old Zhou's disappearance.","Thinking of this, He Zhiran ignored the cart in front of her and hurried to catch up.","\"Lord Peng, Lord Zhou is in danger.\"","Li Hu, who was walking at the back of the officials, hurriedly turned his head and glared angrily at He Zhiran.","He said unclearly with his swollen mouth, \"Isn't this your fault?\"","He Zhiran was too lazy to listen to his nonsense.","\"Lord Peng, I agreed with Lord Zhou at the market entrance that we would each go purchase supplies separately and meet up there by noon.","I went back to the market entrance at the agreed time and waited for a long time without seeing Lord Zhou's shadow. I thought he was anxious and went back first.","I was worried that everyone would be anxious, so I rushed back in a hurry. But when I got to the gate, Li Hu attacked me and kept yelling that I ran away.","I didn't see Lord Zhou come back just now. He went with Li Hu to buy supplies, so why did Li Hu come back alone without seeing Lord Zhou, yet falsely accused me without discernment?","I suspect Lord Zhou must have encountered some danger.\"","After hearing He Zhiran's account, the Mo Family women were immediately outraged.","The fiery second sister-in-law rushed over first.","\"My Lord, although we were sentenced to exile, everyone has seen the things my younger sister has done these past few days. Even if she has no credit, she has worked hard. She absolutely cannot be bullied like this!\"","\"Anyone who bullies my ninth sister-in-law is bad.\" Mo Hanyue also plucked up the courage to chime in.","In their hearts, whether Lord Zhou was in danger or not was not as big a deal as He Zhiran being bullied."]},{"number":47,"title":"Chapter 47: Hypnosis","paragraphs":["Peng Wang's brow furrowed instantly as he yelled at the Mohist women: “All of you get lost! Don't cause more trouble here.”","At this moment, he was thinking the most about whether the Eighth Old Zhou had really encountered danger like He Zhiran had reminded, as she said.","The Eighth Old Zhou had been with him for many years and he knew the man’s character very well.","The Eighth Old Zhou was always punctual, not to mention they had only gone out to purchase some rations, it was impossible for them to be away for so long without returning.","Then looking at Li Hu, there was some evasiveness in his eyes.","Peng Wang instantly felt suspicious.","He looked coldly at Li Hu.","“Li Hu, where's the Eighth Old Zhou?”","“Boss, the He clan escaped, the Eighth Brother went to find people, I came back to report the news.” Li Hu murmured unclearly the excuse he had already prepared.","He knew clearly that escape of prisoners was what people in this line of work hated the most.","Li Hu didn’t believe that if he said He Zhiran had escaped, Peng Wang wouldn’t pursue it.","Peng Wang really hated when prisoners escaped. Although he didn’t completely believe Li Hu’s words, he still looked towards He Zhiran, preparing to investigate.","He Zhiran shrugged, feeling there was no need for her to explain too much about this matter.","She had already returned, which was the best proof that she didn't escape.","\"Master Peng, I've come back, can this be considered escaping?","If you believe me, you'd better go find Master Zhou quickly!","As long as the living Master Zhou can be found, won't the truth come to light?\"","After listening to He Zhiran's words, Peng Wang also felt that finding the Eighth Old Zhou was imminent.","He looked at Li Hu and asked in a deep voice: \"Where did you two separate?\"","He Zhiran saw that time was slipping away second by second, worried that the Eighth Old Zhou would be in danger.","If Peng Wang kept asking like this, not only would he not get any useful information, but he would also lose the most precious rescue time.","Before Li Hu could think of what to say, He Zhiran had already pulled Peng Wang away from the crowd.","Seeing the boss leave with He Zhiran, Li Hu immediately felt a sense of crisis.","It was obvious that the boss didn't believe his excuses, otherwise why would he leave with He Zhiran?","\"Boss, don't believe that cheap woman's words.\"","Peng Wang glared coldly at Li Hu before looking at He Zhiran.","\"Do you know where the Eighth Old Zhou is?\"","\"I don't know, but I have a way to make Li Hu tell the truth.\"","\"What way?\" Peng Wang urged her to speak quickly.","\"I've learned a secret method that can hypnotize a person's will and easily ask about things you want to know.","But I'm not very skilled at it, and I still need Master Peng's cooperation.\"","In her previous life, He Zhiran had a good friend who was extremely skilled in hypnosis. She had learned some basics from the friend, and was seventy percent confident she could ask some simple questions.","To increase the success rate, Peng Wang's cooperation was necessary.","\"What do I need to do, speak quickly.\" Peng Wang was not at all suspicious about He Zhiran's skills.","In the past two days he had already witnessed a lot, and believed this woman must still have many skills she hadn't shown.","\"Master Peng, as I just said, I'm not very skilled. To be more secure, I hope you can get someone to get Li Hu drunk, of course, not the kind of drunkenness where he can't even make a sound, it'd be best to get him half sober and half drunk.\"","Peng Wang looked suspiciously at He Zhiran. He didn't know why this woman wanted to get the man drunk before interrogating him.","However, for some reason he felt strangely trusting of He Zhiran.","\"Alright, wait here, I'll go take care of it.\"","Peng Wang was very efficient in doing things, he immediately had people go to the innkeeper to buy a jar of wine, then ordered the officers to work together to hold Li Hu down and force him to drink.","At first Li Hu resisted.","The boss was called away by He Zhiran and said a few words before coming back, and then everyone started pouring wine down his throat.","If there wasn't something fishy about this, Li Hu wouldn't believe it even if he was beaten to death.","Therefore, when Li Hu was being held down by the group to drink wine, he used all his strength to dodge.","However, the officers outnumbered him. As long as each person used some strength, Li Hu simply couldn't evade.","Peng Wang was still somewhat familiar with Li Hu's alcohol tolerance. Seeing that he had been forced to drink about enough, he ordered everyone to stop.","Then he had people take Li Hu to a private guest room, leaving Zhang Qing and another officer there to keep watch. Only then did Peng Wang call He Zhiran over.","He Zhiran looked at Li Hu's state, he was just starting to feel the effects of the alcohol.","At this time, people's consciousness was usually relatively weak, much easier to overpower compared to normal.","Without a doubt, He Zhiran's consciousness entered her space and found a bejeweled pendant necklace to take out, concealing it in her sleeve.","Then under everyone's gaze, she had Li Hu look at the necklace.","Li Hu was greedy and lustful. Seeing such a high quality necklace, his eyes immediately shone with avarice, the alcohol overwhelming him causing him to already forget he was supposed to conceal the Eighth Old Zhou's disappearance.","He stretched out his hand, about to grab the necklace in He Zhiran's hand.","He Zhiran nimbly dodged, a trace of ridicule in her tone as she asked, \"Want this necklace?\"","Li Hu made no attempt to conceal his desires, nodding repeatedly.","\"Want it.\"","\"Alright, do as I say and I'll give you this necklace.\"","\"No problem, I'll do as you say.\"","He Zhiran fully extended the necklace, swinging the pendant rhythmically before Li Hu's eyes.","Soon, Li Hu's eyes began to glaze over, even losing their proper luster.","Sensing the timing was about right, He Zhiran started questioning.","\"Where is the Eighth Old Zhou?\"","When asked about the Eighth Old Zhou's whereabouts, an abnormal smile appeared on Li Hu's stiff expression.","\"I had him knocked out and taken away by people I arranged, he's probably become fish food by now.\"","Hearing Li Hu's words, the officers present all tensed up.","\"Boss, I'll take people to the riverbank to search for the Eighth Old Zhou right now.\"","Seeing Zhang Qing's loud voice, He Zhiran's heart tightened as she quickly made a silencing gesture and reminded him.","\"Master Zhang, you mustn't speak loudly, it might wake him up, there's still many things that haven't been asked clearly.\"","Peng Wang worried that Zhang Qing wouldn't listen to He Zhiran and glared fiercely at him.","Zhang Qing hurriedly shut his mouth, staring tensely at Li Hu.","Seeing that Li Hu hadn't been woken up by Zhang Qing's shout, He Zhiran instantly let out a breath.","She shook the pendant and continued questioning.","\"Where can we find the Eighth Old Zhou now?\""]},{"number":48,"title":"Chapter 48: A Woman of Skill and Wisdom","paragraphs":["Li Hu still answered with a blank look in his eyes.","\"About one li to the west of the pier, there are some reefs where they often throw people into the river.\"","Having gotten a precise answer, Peng Wang immediately ordered Zhang Qing to take all the officials to look for the person.","At the same time, he also realized clearly that He Zhiran must still have something to ask, so he did not hurry to leave with them.","He Zhiran continued to ask in front of Peng Wang.","\"Why did you harm the Eighth Old Zhou?\"","\"Only with him not coming back could the crime of He's escape be confirmed.\"","\"Why did you do this?\"","\"Because Miss Li Rou did not like the He family, and I also wanted to take this opportunity to deal with the Mohist School.\"","Having asked this far, He Zhiran was already certain of her guess.","Li Hu must absolutely be someone stationed here as an eye from the capital city.","No wonder Mo Jiuye did not discover anyone tailing them...","Peng Wang knew that later He Zhiran would ask who had commanded Li Hu to do these things.","These were all the rotten affairs between the higher-ups, and he, a petty little official, did not want to get involved.","The more one knew, the faster one died.","Therefore, before He Zhiran opened her mouth to ask Li Hu the next question, Peng Wang turned and left the room.","He Zhiran secretly admired Peng Wang for living wisely, and at the same time, impatiently asked the next question.","\"Who ordered you to deal with the Mohist School?\"","\"I don't know.\"","\"You don't know?\" He Zhiran was very clear that at this moment Li Hu would not lie. Since he said he didn't know, then he certainly didn't know.","But having gotten a bit of a lead, she didn't want to give up just like that.","\"Who was the person you were in contact with? You don't know either?\"","\"The person who had me do these things, I've only seen him once. It was dark and I didn't see his appearance clearly, but the sound of his voice was rather shrill, he should be a eunuch.\"","A eunuch?","The only ones who could order eunuchs around were the imperial family.","Other than the Emperor, the princes, princesses, and concubines in the harem were all possibilities...","Thinking this way, the target had become quite large.","But He Zhiran also knew that it was unlikely she could get any more useful information from Li Hu.","He Zhiran put the necklace into her space, then turned and left to find Peng Wang.","\"Master Peng, I've finished asking my questions, Li Hu will be able to regain consciousness soon.\"","At this moment Peng Wang was already somewhat at his wit's end.","Even without hearing He Zhiran's later questions, he could guess that Li Hu was someone's man higher up.","The facts of Li Hu's harming the Eighth Old Zhou were clear, how should he deal with the aftermath?","In principle, Li Hu was extremely evil, and any punishment would not be excessive, but if he offended someone important, could he keep his own head?","He Zhiran had just taken a few steps and did not hear the sound of Peng Wang entering the room.","She turned back and indeed saw Peng Wang still standing there in a daze.","\"Master Peng, Li Hu's crime is a fact. It is most appropriate for the government to try this kind of case.\"","He Zhiran's words could be said to have pointed a bright path for Peng Wang.","Peng Wang nodded gratefully at He Zhiran: \"Good, I understand.\"","This method was too good. It would not only punish Li Hu and avenge the Eighth Old Zhou, but also spare him from having to personally tidy up the aftermath of Li Hu provoking someone higher up. It was simply killing two birds with one stone.","At this time, Peng Wang admired He Zhiran even more. She was absolutely a woman with both ability and wisdom.","He Zhiran knew she would not stay at the inn for long. According to Li Hu's meaning, the Eighth Old Zhou would be thrown into the river.","The Eighth Old Zhou was quite a decent person, and she thought that if she could save him, she would lend a hand.","But before leaving, she had to give the Mohists a reassurance, to let them know clearly that she was not in danger.","Also, the goods from the general store and cloth shop being delivered soon would need someone to receive them.","The Mohist women were anxiously waiting for news from He Zhiran's side. Seeing her return, they all crowded around her to ask after her health, afraid she had suffered, it seemed.","It was easy enough to say a few words to reassure those sisters with simpler thoughts, He Zhiran just told them she was fine to set their hearts at ease.","But with Mo Jiuye it would not be so easy to gloss things over in a few words.","From the moment he heard the quarrel break out between He Zhiran and Li Hu at the door, Mo Jiuye had been standing at the edge of the door. If He Zhiran suffered any disadvantage, he would rush out to save her regardless of anything.","Later, hearing that Peng Wang had come forward and did not make things difficult for He Zhiran, his tense heart finally relaxed a little.","Now seeing He Zhiran return safe and sound, he would ask for a clear account of things before letting her leave, no matter what.","\"Did you get any useful information from Li Hu just now?\"","\"I found out that he had someone tie up the Eighth Old Zhou to drown him in the river.","Li Hu had someone behind him giving orders, but it's a long story. Let me go save the person first, then come back and explain in detail to you.\"","Although Mo Jiuye still had countless more questions in his heart, hearing that she was going to rescue someone, he could only repress asking for the time being.","He now only resented himself - on the surface he was still an injured person unable to move easily. Otherwise, he would never have let He Zhiran face these things alone.","\"Since that's the case, be careful about your own safety.\"","Mo Jiuye guiltily turned away, no longer looking at He Zhiran.","He Zhiran did not dare delay time. She rushed to the location Li Hu had described together with Peng Wang.","At this time Peng Wang was also eager to save the person. Despite his body still feeling a bit uncomfortable, he did not dare delay one bit.","The two ran all the way, and in about fifteen minutes they arrived at the specified place.","In addition to the officials, it was also surrounded by common folk who had come to watch the lively scene.","Peng Wang pushed through the crowd and squeezed in, with He Zhiran following close behind.","The Eighth Old Zhou lay in the center of the crowd, eyes tightly shut, seemingly already dead.","The officials had sorrowful expressions. Seeing Peng Wang come over, Zhang Qing wiped his eyes and came before him.","\"Boss, the Eighth Old Zhou, he... he... has passed away.\"","Peng Wang had already guessed the answer upon first seeing the Eighth Old Zhou's condition.","It seemed they had still come too late.","But He Zhiran did not watch as the officials grieved there. She swiftly came before the Eighth Old Zhou, resting her fingers on the carotid artery at his neck, hoping she could still detect the presence of vital signs.","One official came over with reddened eyes.","\"Miss He, we've already checked, he's dead.\"","But He Zhiran did not respond to the official, and started performing CPR on the Eighth Old Zhou right in front of everyone.","Her bizarre actions provoked a wave of sighs from the people around.","\"What is this woman trying to do?\"","\"That's right, the man's already dead through and through, what's she still fussing over?\"","\"Look at her, her actions are so indecent. She really has no shame.\"","But He Zhiran completely ignored their words. In her heart, even if there was only a shred of hope, she would not give up on treatment.","Seeing that two minutes had already passed with the Eighth Old Zhou still completely unresponsive, Peng Wang did not understand the principles of CPR, but he knew clearly in his heart that He Zhiran was trying to save the person.","However, seeing that the Eighth Old Zhou remained motionless, he couldn't help stepping forward to advise:","\"Miss He, since Old Zhou has already passed away, let him rest in peace!\"","But He Zhiran's actions did not cease because of Peng Wang's words.","Only seeing her next move once again shocked everyone present."]},{"number":49,"title":"Chapter 49: Eight really was kissed by Hirsch woke up.","paragraphs":["She gave up cardiopulmonary resuscitation, pinched the Eighth Old Zhou's nose, and was about to give him artificial respiration.","Just as she leaned over, she saw the disdainful looks from the onlooking crowds out of the corner of her eye.","He Zhiran had just been eager to save lives, and at the same time realized that this was ancient times.","Such behavior was simply unacceptable to the ancients.","Even if it was an emergency, she could not ruin her reputation just to save someone.","\"Lord Peng, I need your help.\"","Peng Wang was completely helpless.","\"Miss He, I know you are eager to save lives, but the Eighth Old Zhou is already gone, so don't make things worse.\"","He Zhiran was anxious immediately. Given the Eighth Old Zhou's current condition, if he could not be rescued in time, he might really die.","\"If you want him to live, do as I say immediately. If you don't listen to me, Lord Zhou will really go to see King of Hell.\"","Seeing He Zhiran’s serious tone, Peng Wang walked over with two yamen runners.","\"What do you want me to do?\"","He Zhiran pulled Peng Wang down to squat in front of the Eighth Old Zhou.","\"Lord Zhou, first pinch his nose, then blow air into his mouth.\"","Peng Wang and the two yamen runners he had brought over were dumbfounded.","Pointing at his own nose, he said, \"You want me to kiss the Eighth Old Zhou?\"","He Zhiran urged, \"Hurry, just do as I said.\"","Hearing He Zhiran’s words, the two yamen runners immediately ran far away, leaving only the puzzled Peng Wang here.","Peng Wang had no choice but to bite the bullet.","The moment Peng Wang's lips touched the Eighth Old Zhou's, he immediately started blowing air.","He Zhiran watched as the air Peng Wang blew out all escaped outside, and became anxious instantly, gesturing in a direction.","\"Lord Peng, it has to be this angle, and all the air you blow needs to enter Lord Zhou's mouth.\"","Her actions didn't seem like anything to Peng Wang, she was still quite a distance from the Eighth Old Zhou's lips.","But from the perspective of the onlooking crowd, it looked like He Zhiran was kissing the Eighth Old Zhou.","It immediately caused another sigh from the crowd.","Even the yamen runners were no longer calm.","\"Miss He, you must be crazy?\"","Peng Wang didn't have time to explain for He Zhiran, and followed her instructions to blow air into the Eighth Old Zhou's mouth again.","He Zhiran stood by and saw the Eighth Old Zhou's fingers move.","If nothing unexpected happened, he would spit out some water soon.","She reminded Peng Wang, \"Lord Peng, that's about enough.\"","No one knew whether it was from fatigue or holding his breath, but in any case, Peng Wang's face turned red after getting up.","Seeing their superior stand up, the yamen runners immediately gathered around.","In order to make the air around the Eighth Old Zhou more circulated, He Zhiran asked those yamen runners to keep their distance.","Initially, those yamen runners were unwilling, but after a shout from Peng Wang, they obediently took a few steps back.","Just then, the Eighth Old Zhou coughed violently, and soon spat out a mouthful of water.","Zhang Qing exclaimed, \"Boss, the Eighth Old Zhou really came to from Miss He’s kiss!\"","Hearing Zhang Qing’s nonsense, Peng Wang scolded him on the spot.","\"Don't talk nonsense and ruin Miss He's reputation.\"","Zhang Qing quickly covered his mouth, \"I misspoke, misspoke.\"","The other yamen runners looked at each other, thinking that their superior was clearly too partial to Miss He.","They had clearly seen that it was Miss He who kissed the Eighth Old Zhou first, and then their superior went on...","However, they didn't dare say such things in front of Peng Wang.","Zhang Qing still didn't know that his casual slip of the tongue had brought great trouble to He Zhiran.","Seeing the Eighth Old Zhou spit out a few more mouthfuls of water, and his eyes slowly opened.","Peng Wang was so excited that he cried with joy. He didn't care to immediately explain the misunderstanding to help He Zhiran.","\"The Eighth Old Zhou is not dead, he is alive. Miss He, it really is all because of you, you are the Eighth Old Zhou’s lifesaver.\"","As soon as he said this, the yamen runners' gazes fell on He Zhiran in unison.","Indeed, if it hadn't been for Miss He, they all thought the Eighth Old Zhou was dead.","Then, led by Peng Wang, the yamen runners surrounded the Eighth Old Zhou.","Everyone shouted his name in unison, and some even reached out to touch his body.","Zhang Qing grabbed Peng Wang's arm excitedly, unable to hide his excitement at all.","\"Eighth Old Zhou, look at me, do you know who I am?\"","Although the Eighth Old Zhou was still weak, he still struggled to say, \"Zhang Qing.\"","Hearing this, Zhang Qing was overjoyed and jumped high.","\"Boss, look, the Eighth Old Zhou still recognizes me, he really is alright!\"","Peng Wang was also extremely excited and couldn’t express it in words, he just kept nodding, his eyes full of gratification.","However, he was much more sensible than the others.","He immediately asked He Zhiran, \"Miss He, it should be no problem to carry Lord Zhou back to the inn now, right?\"","\"No problem at all, Lord Zhou is just weak right now, he is already out of danger.\"","Having obtained He Zhiran’s affirmation, Peng Wang ordered people to carry the Eighth Old Zhou back to the inn.","Peng Wang paid out of his own pocket to book a upper room for the Eighth Old Zhou, then ordered someone to help change his wet clothes.","He Zhiran had accomplished her mission and directly returned to the Mo Family members.","At this time, people from the grocery store and fabric shops had delivered the goods she bought.","There were too many things, especially the thirty-odd quilts, which were piled up like a small mountain.","Seeing He Zhiran come back, the Mo Family members had complex looks in their eyes.","The inn attendant who had gone to the riverside to watch the excitement came back and told the boss about how a female prisoner taught the yamen runners to kiss and resuscitate someone.","They happened to be overheard by Li Rou'er.","If it was said that a female prisoner went with the yamen runners to save someone by the river, it could only be He Zhiran.","Li Rou'er finally got the goods on He Zhiran and immediately spread the news far and wide.","He Zhiran noticed her mother-in-law, sisters-in-law and aunt acting strange at first glance.","\"Mother, what exactly happened?\"","Old Lady Mo's eyes were somewhat evasive, not knowing how to ask He Zhiran about this.","The sisters-in-law also similarly, all dared not look her in the eye.","Mo Hanyue was straightforward.","\"Sister-in-law, everyone is saying that you used the method of mouth-to-mouth to resuscitate Lord Zhou.\"","After hearing Mo Hanyue's words, He Zhiran had to admire the ancients' ability to distort facts.","Not to mention how conservative the ancients' thinking was, if a married woman dared to do such a thing to another man, being drowned was also a possibility.","At the moment, He Zhiran felt the first thing she had to do was explain things clearly to her family. As for who was slandering her behind her back, she could look into it a bit later.","\"I didn't kiss Lord Zhou, I just gestured to show the direction and taught Lord Peng how to do it.\"","After she finished speaking, looking at the Mo Family women's expressions, it seemed they didn't completely believe it at all.","Seeing this, He Zhiran immediately put on a stern face.","\"Since you all don't believe what I say, after we get to the northwest, I will divorce my husband, so as not to ruin the Mo Family's reputation.","But before that, I hope we can still get along like before, so as not to be laughed at by outsiders.\"","He Zhiran was not a person with high EQ. If it was a battle of wits and courage she could handle it, but smoothing things over with in-laws, as someone who had never had a boyfriend in her previous life, she really had no experience at all.","She had explained things as clearly as she could, if they didn't believe her, she didn't need to continue fawning over them.","He Zhiran had said her piece, as for whether those people would continue to cling to this fabricated matter and be difficult with her, she could only ignore it.","As long as she could escort Mo Jiuye safely to the northwest, she would have lived up to the hero in her heart.","As for everything else, she would take it one step at a time and let nature take its course.","Seeing He Zhiran's change of expression, the Mo Family women felt a twinge of pain in their hearts for some reason.","They liked the usually kind and gentle He Zhiran, they liked He Zhiran who was thoughtful of them everywhere.","But it seemed that they had lost this He Zhiran.","He Zhiran turned and walked out of the room. Although she was scorned by everyone, there were still days to come in the future.","Due to the Eighth Old Zhou’s incident, it looked like they probably wouldn't be able to continue traveling today.","He Zhiran planned to take this opportunity to get people to make those tents.","It wasn't possible to stay in inns every day on the road to exile. In case they encountered days of sleeping in the open air again, these tents would come in very handy.","Seeing her sister-in-law turn to leave, Mo Hanyue felt a tightness in her heart. She hurriedly chased after her.","\"Sister-in-law Nine, I don't care what they think. Anyway, I believe in Sister-in-law Nine,\" He Zhiran said. She hadn't expected that the only person in the Mo Family's women's quarters who believed in her was actually a little girl of only thirteen or fourteen.","She tried her best to squeeze out a smile and stroked Mo Hanyue's head.","\"Sister-in-law Nine thanks Hanyue for her trust.\""]},{"number":50,"title":"Chapter 50: It's enough for Me to trust You.","paragraphs":["Looking at the oilcloth He Zhiran was fiddling with, Mo Hanyue curiously asked.","\"Sister-in-law, is this oilcloth you bought?\"","\"Yes, I plan to make some tents with oilcloth.\"","\"Tents?\" Mo Hanyue's eyes were full of curiosity.","He Zhiran patiently explained the use of tents to Mo Hanyue.","Mo Hanyue became more and more happy as she listened.","\"Sister-in-law, I often do needlework when I have nothing to do at home. I can help.\"","\"Good, after sister-in-law cuts it, let's get Hanyue to do it.\"","The sister-in-law and the two women were fiddling with the oilcloth in the courtyard of the inn.","In the room of the Mo family women, everyone was at a loss.","\"Mother, although we haven't had much contact with ninth brother and his wife, she is definitely not the kind of fickle person. I believe she must have been tricked by someone with ulterior motives.\"","These words were said by the sixth sister-in-law Deng Xue.","Deng Xue didn't talk much usually, but everyone knew her mind was the most perceptive.","The eldest sister-in-law also agreed with Deng Xue's words.","\"Mother, I think the same as the sixth sister-in-law. We have all seen the character of the ninth sister-in-law. If she was really that kind of person, she would have found a way to escape long ago instead of taking care of us all this way.\"","\"Yes mother, I also believe the ninth sister-in-law is not that kind of person.\" The eighth sister-in-law also chose to believe in He Zhiran.","Old Lady Mo of course knew He Zhiran's character.","It was just that keeping the rules all her life made her somewhat unable to let go.","Now that the daughters-in-law had all stood on the side of the ninth daughter-in-law, Old Lady Mo felt that she didn't need to keep worrying about it either.","\"You are right about the ninth sister-in-law. She is a good one, we have all seen it.","I will say it today, this matter ends here. From now on, whoever dares to raise doubts again will face family law.\"","\"Mother, we guarantee not to mention a word.\" The second sister-in-law was the first to make a guarantee.","The others also chimed in, saying they would forget about it.","The Mo women reached a consensus and walked out of the house together.","Thanks to the little girl Mo Hanyue being around, after her lobbying back and forth, the women were soon reconciled with He Zhiran.","He Zhiran did not hold grudges against her own family. Besides, she could also understand those deep-rooted rules of these ancient women.","That they could choose to trust her so quickly was also a pleasant thing for He Zhiran.","Under her leadership, the women took up needles and threads and started making tents.","Seeing this, the women of the Xie and Fang families also joined in.","However, the eyes of the two families were a bit wrong.","The way they looked at He Zhiran was not contempt, but somewhat probing.","They wondered how the Mo family could turn a blind eye after such a big incident.","The Xie and Fang families were outsiders to He Zhiran. How they thought in their hearts would not affect her in the slightest.","The busy women here were in full swing, while Mo Jiuye, who was pretending to be sick in the room, paced back and forth.","He had also heard clearly what Li Rou’er had spread.","He didn't believe these words, but somehow he felt a little sour in his heart inexplicably.","With his current situation, following him, He Zhiran would probably never get ahead in life.","Mo Jiuye sincerely didn't want to delay He Zhiran's happiness.","However, when he thought that He Zhiran might leave him, that suffocating feeling became more and more strong.","At this moment, he only hoped that He Zhiran would come here and explain the truth to him.","If it was really as Li Rou'er said, he would rather be mocked for a lifetime, but choose to let go.","......","He Zhiran understood the principles and methods of making tents, and could also tailor the right sizes.","But when it came to sewing, she couldn't do it.","The original owner Lady Hong was useless, so there were no such memories for her to inherit.","Moreover, in her previous life, she didn't need to do these things by hand, they were all ready-made products that could be purchased.","Therefore, the sewing of the tents had to be left to the women of the three families to do.","Seeing that everyone was already skilled at getting started, He Zhiran remembered Mo Jiuye.","With the rumors flying, the Mo women all knew about it, and it must have reached Mo Jiuye's ears as well.","After all, they were still husband and wife, she felt it necessary to explain.","As soon as she opened the door, she saw Mo Jiuye sitting upright at the edge of the bed, staring at her without blinking.","Before Mo Jiuye asked, He Zhiran explained:","\"What's being spread outside is not true. I didn't kiss the Eighth Old Zhou.\"","Immediately after, she told Mo Jiuye the whole story of the rescue.","She had thought that after telling him all this, Mo Jiuye would still ask some questions. He Zhiran was already prepared to be interrogated.","Unexpectedly, Mo Jiuye just tapped the bedside with his fingers and said softly:","\"When I was on the frontier, there was an army doctor who blew air into the patient's mouth through a bamboo tube. It must be the same principle as you saving people.\"","He Zhiran was extremely surprised that she encountered someone who understood this so quickly.","She nodded vigorously at Mo Jiuye.","\"That's exactly what you said.\"","Mo Jiuye believed that He Zhiran did not kiss the Eighth Old Zhou, but somehow there was still a sour feeling in his heart.","However, he could also understand He Zhiran's feelings after being vilified by so many people. To help relieve her stress, Mo Jiuye sincerely said:","\"You don't have to take those rumors outside to heart. It's enough that I alone believe you.\"","He Zhiran felt very surprised that Mo Jiuye could say such things.","After all, Mo Jiuye was a native ancient person. Although she had no contact with the Eighth Old Zhou, those rumors outside were still not easy to face for a man.","\"Do you really think so?\" He Zhiran was still a little uncertain.","\"Yes, you don't need to worry about this matter.\"","Seeing Mo Jiuye like this, He Zhiran felt a little moved in her heart for some reason.","A hero with a broad mind was what a great man should be like.","Seeing He Zhiran suddenly moved, ripples rose in Mo Jiuye's heart instantly.","He even had the urge to hug her in his arms and comfort her well.","However, he didn't dare take such actions rashly.","In the short few days they had been together, he realized that his new wife was different from ordinary women.","She had her own secrets and her own personality.","Mo Jiuye was afraid his actions would annoy her, and then she would disappear in front of him...","In order not to show her too much of his fluctuations, Mo Jiuye tried his best to appear calm.","At the same time, he also decided to change the subject and say something to divert He Zhiran's attention.","\"You just said someone was behind Li Hu's actions. Have you asked who it was?\"","He Zhiran then remembered that she hadn't explained this to Mo Jiuye in detail yet.","\"Li Hu said the person he was in contact with had a shrill voice. I suspect it should be a eunuch.\"","Mo Jiuye frowned and murmured, \"If it's a eunuch, then the suspects are quite broad.\""]},{"number":51,"title":"Chapter 51: The Tent","paragraphs":["\"Yes, if you analyze it from the eunuch's perspective, it is really not easy to find the real mastermind behind the scenes,\" He Zhiran agreed with Mo Jiuye that it was not easy to find the real mastermind behind it all.","Both of them were very clear that just this little clue from Li Hu was not enough to find his real backer.","However, it was hard to say whether it was good or bad that they had found spies around them so soon after leaving the capital.","Thinking of this, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye both fell into contemplation.","After a long time, He Zhiran finally spoke her analysis.","\"In the matter of Li Hu causing the Eighth Old Zhou to fall into the water, there were several accomplices who helped him.","And when the officials rushed to fish the Eighth Old Zhou out of the river, no one was carrying anyone on their back, and many people were watching.","I believe Li Hu's accomplices must have been able to see this.","And I publicly saved the Eighth Old Zhou, so Li Hu's failure was completely exposed.","There must be someone among them who will report this matter to their superiors and seek ways to deal with the aftermath.","I suspect that as soon as Li Hu's superiors know that something has happened to him, they are very likely to send someone to silence him.\"","Upon hearing this, Mo Jiuye took a deep breath.","\"Do you mean we should follow this lead on Li Hu to find out who is behind him?\"","He Zhiran nodded, \"That is what I mean, but with our current status, it may not be very convenient to take action.\"","\"Action is not a big problem, I have my own ways, but I have already offended them. Even if we find the person who really wants to harm the Mo family, what can we do?\"","He Zhiran could hear that there was some self-abandonment in Mo Jiuye's words.","\"With your skills, it shouldn't be difficult to take revenge, right?","Besides, I suspect that Li Hu's backer is very likely to be the same person who sent someone to poison the Mo family.\"","Reminded this way, Mo Jiuye's mind suddenly became clear, and at the same time, endless hatred and injustice surged in his heart.","\"You're right. I'll find a way to follow Li Hu tonight.\"","Seeing that Mo Jiuye had figured it out, He Zhiran went out to continue making tents with the women.","As soon as she came out of the room, she saw several officials dragging Li Hu, all tied up, and shoving him outside the inn.","Li Hu's mouth was blocked by a piece of cloth so he couldn't shout, he could only look at the officials with pleading eyes.","The officials' feelings for the Eighth Old Zhou were in no way comparable to Li Hu's, who had only been here for half a year.","After seeing the Eighth Old Zhou almost killed by him, they hated Li Hu to the extreme. How could they be merciful to him?","Zhang Qing saw Li Hu struggling and kicked him in the butt.","\"Behave yourself. When you see the county magistrate, beg for mercy however you want.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, he looked up and saw He Zhiran.","Unlike before, Zhang Qing did not swagger arrogantly at He Zhiran, but nodded gratefully to her.","He Zhiran also nodded in return.","From her understanding of ancient conditions, she knew that the county magistrate usually heard cases in the morning, and it was already near dusk now.","She guessed that when Li Hu was taken to the county office, he would only be temporarily detained in the prison, and would not be interrogated until tomorrow morning at the earliest.","Therefore, He Zhiran guessed that tonight would be the best time to silence Li Hu.","Thinking of this, she hurried back to the room and told Mo Jiuye again that Li Hu had been taken to the county office by officials, as well as her analysis.","Mo Jiuye said he would grasp the timing.","Although he had never done anything like assassinating and silencing people, after so many years in officialdom, he had heard about some of these nasty things.","Most people who went to prison cells to silence people generally chose between 1-3 AM, because that time was when people were most prone to doze off and the guards would be relatively lax.","But to be on the safe side, Mo Jiuye planned to go before 1 AM.","Now that everything was arranged clearly, He Zhiran was much more at ease while working.","The women were making handicrafts much faster than she had imagined, especially tents which did not require very tight stitches.","When He Zhiran came to the production site, she was pleasantly surprised to find that the women had already made several finished products.","However, they still didn't understand how to use the tents, so they were all neatly placed together.","Seeing He Zhiran come over, Mo Hanyue excitedly said, \"Sister-in-law, look, my tent is almost finished!\"","As she spoke, Mo Hanyue tied a knot in the thread that had just been pulled through the corner of the oilcloth, then cut it, got up and handed the tent she had made to He Zhiran.","He Zhiran happened to want to see if the tent she had designed herself was successful.","In front of everyone, she unfolded the tent.","The tent was a simple pyramid shape, with bamboo poles as the frame.","A few hemp ropes hung down from the top of the tent, and the other ends of the ropes were tied to thicker bamboo segments, which could be buried in the ground to secure the tent.","Although the tent looked a little crude, it was practical.","Seeing He Zhiran put up the tent, the women were shocked and couldn't believe their eyes.","\"Sister-in-law, I was just wondering what this tent you mentioned was for, now I see, isn't this just a little house?\"","Mo Hanyue was so excited that she was silly smiling. She had made such a good \"house\" with her own hands.","Seeing Mo Hanyue smiling foolishly, He Zhiran felt a strong sense of accomplishment bubbling up inside her.","\"It's a bit of an exaggeration to call it a house, but it's pretty good for blocking wind and rain.\"","The women of the Xie and Fang families looked enviously at the Mo family women.","In the future, when sleeping outdoors at night, they would no longer have to lie facing the sky.","Although Miss He behaved indecently, her mind was indeed first-class smart, to even come up with ideas like this.","Zhao held her sister-in-law's hand.","\"Aunt Cui, having such a daughter-in-law is really a blessing that your Mo family has cultivated over three lifetimes.\"","\"That's right, our Ninth younger sister is good at a lot of things, not just something as simple as making tents,\" the second sister-in-law was happy to hear her younger sister being praised.","Faced with praise, He Zhiran humbly said a few words, and at the same time, she also saw the longing for tents in the eyes of the Xie and Fang family women.","\"Aunt Fang, Aunt Xie, our three families made this tent together, two people to one tent, there is absolutely no problem.\"","The Xie and Fang family women were so delighted to hear that their own families also had a share that they did not know how to express themselves.","They thanked He Zhiran profusely.","Zhao looked at He Zhiran gratefully and sincerely said, \"When our family was ransacked, we didn't bring anything out. Fortunately, you and the Mo family helped us.","Now I understand too. Since we can no longer live the kind of carefree life we had before, I might as well accept reality.","From now on, my Fang family will look up to the Mo family. I'm saying this today, and anyone who dares to go against it will face family law.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, the other Fang women also expressed their willingness to do the same."]},{"number":52,"title":"Chapter 52: The Mind of Zhou Ba","paragraphs":["Upon witnessing the situation, the Xie family members turned their attention to Qiu, the mother of the second sister-in-law.","They hoped that she would assert herself with the same dominance as the matriarch of the Fang family and speak such words.","In this way, when they received the benevolence of the Mo family, they would feel more at ease.","Qiu hesitated and looked around but couldn't make up her mind.","The second sister-in-law understood her own mother's temperament the best. She always obeyed her father's words and would never dare to make decisions in such matters.","\"Mother, you don't have to worry about this matter. We can show it through our actions in the future.\"","Qiu nodded repeatedly, \"Fang'er is right, that's exactly what I have in mind.\"","He Zhiran did all this not only because he had Mo Jiuye's consent but also because he considered that having more people together would provide more support.","The road of exile is long, and who can guarantee that they won't need each other?","\"Aunties, you are being too serious. We help each other in difficult times without the need for so much pressure.\"","The several sister-in-laws chimed in, and the atmosphere quickly became lively again.","When He Zhiran finished making thirteen oiled fabrics and twenty-six tents, it was dinnertime.","Coincidentally, the official escort who had taken Li Hu to the yamen also returned at this time.","He Zhiran planned to distribute all the tents while everyone was present.","The female members of the Xie and Fang families took the tents they needed and left.","The six tents of the Mo family were neatly folded by a few sister-in-laws and taken away.","The rest were meant to bribe the official escorts.","He Zhiran intended to find Peng Wang and check on the condition of the Eighth Old Zhou.","After inquiring with the duty officer, she learned that Peng Wang had been staying in the room with the Eighth Old Zhou, so she went straight there.","She knocked on the door, and Peng Wang let her in.","Peng Wang was indeed a person of clear likes and dislikes. Although his attitude towards He Zhiran had been good for the past two days, it wasn't as pronounced as it was now.","When Peng Wang saw He Zhiran enter, he unexpectedly stood up and deeply bowed to her.","\"He Zhiran, I thank you on behalf of the Eighth Old Zhou for saving his life.\"","This was different from when he was poisoned by the snake. At that time, he had no consciousness and hadn't personally witnessed the critical situation.","Therefore, Peng Wang's feelings towards He Zhiran saving his life weren't as deep as when the Eighth Old Zhou was saved.","He had seen with his own eyes a person who had been deemed beyond saving by many others being brought back to life by He Zhiran.","Although the method of saving him was somewhat difficult to describe.","Of course, this was only in his own opinion.","He felt guilty towards his own wife...","Faced with Peng Wang's bow, He Zhiran didn't dodge.","No one knew better than her that if it weren't for her, the Eighth Old Zhou would have long become a water ghost.","After Peng Wang finished bowing, he straightened his body and resumed his lofty appearance.","\"He Zhiran, do you have something to discuss with me?\"","He Zhiran wasn't particularly surprised by the drastic change in his demeanor within less than a minute.","On the contrary, she admired Peng Wang's character.","\"Peng official, I just made several tents with the female members of the family, and the official escorts also received their share. Please send someone to retrieve them later.","Also, I wanted to come and check on the condition of the Eighth Old Zhou.\"","As she spoke, He Zhiran looked towards the Eighth Old Zhou lying on the bed with his eyes tightly shut.","What puzzled her was that the Eighth Old Zhou's face was unusually red.","\"Is Master Zhou running a fever?\"","Peng Wang had been taking care of the Eighth Old Zhou in the room and knew very well that he wasn't running a fever.","However, when Peng Wang's gaze fell upon the face of the Eighth Old Zhou as He Zhiran mentioned it, he was also taken aback.","\"Old Zhou, are you feeling unwell? Why is your face so red all of a sudden? You were perfectly fine just a moment ago.\"","With both of them mentioning it, the Eighth Old Zhou felt his face growing even hotter.","At this moment, he wished he could find a hole to hide in.","Seeing Peng Wang's \"claw\" reaching towards his forehead, the Eighth Old Zhou dodged it and spoke with difficulty.","\"I'm not feeling unwell, and I'm not running a fever.\"","Peng Wang became even more confused.","\"If you're not running a fever, why is your face red? Since He Zhiran is here, if there's anything bothering you, just let her know so she can help you.\"","Upon hearing the name \"He Zhiran,\" the Eighth Old Zhou's face grew even redder, and he could even feel the burning sensation of embarrassment.","Based on a physician's experience, in this kind of situation, there must be something wrong with the Eighth Old Zhou's body.","So, without a second word, He Zhiran approached the bedside and reached out to feel the Eighth Old Zhou's pulse.","Everything seemed normal except for a slightly faster heart rate...","He Zhiran tried her best to think of various reasons that could explain the symptoms the Eighth Old Zhou was experiencing.","Peng Wang stared intently at He Zhiran, waiting for her to speak about Peng Wang's condition.","Just then, the Eighth Old Zhou sat up from the bed.","\"I'm not sick.\"","\"Old Zhou, what's wrong with you? Don't startle us like that. It could give someone a heart attack,\" Peng Wang said, patting his chest cautiously.","The Eighth Old Zhou didn't explain anything to Peng Wang but looked at He Zhiran with difficulty.","His words came out somewhat incoherently.","\"He...He Zhiran, I...I've heard that it was you who...who kissed me and saved me. I know that a woman's chastity is of utmost importance, but you...you are already a married woman. I shouldn't say anything that would make you responsible.","Of...of course, if Mo Jiuye rejects you and divorces you, I...I can...I can marry you.\"","After saying that, the Eighth Old Zhou turned his head away, too afraid to look at He Zhiran.","He Zhiran...","What kind of trouble had she gotten herself into?","She had only saved someone's life, but how did it end up like this?","Furthermore, she didn't even kiss the Eighth Old Zhou.","Peng Wang was also infuriated by the Eighth Old Zhou's words.","He never expected that after explaining for so long, the Eighth Old Zhou still hadn't figured it out.","\"Old Zhou, didn't I make it clear just now? It wasn't He Zhiran who woke you up, it was me, it was me. Why don't you believe me?\"","This matter had ultimately damaged He Zhiran's reputation, and Peng Wang felt it necessary to clarify.","He Zhiran was currently feeling extremely emo.","She vented her frustrations internally, calmed herself down, and then spoke lightly.","\"Master Zhou, I saved you out of the responsibility of being a physician. It was indeed Peng Wang who woke you up, and I merely taught him some proper methods.\"","Seeing this, Peng Wang continued to explain with a brave face, \"Old Zhou, do you even doubt me now? I went all out to save you, and I even kissed you, a grown man.\"","He Zhiran echoed, \"Both Peng Wang and I have gone this far. What else is there for you not to believe?\"","He Zhiran originally wanted to say, \"Don't have those inappropriate thoughts, Eighth Old Zhou,\" but she realized that such words could be hurtful, especially when facing an official who had authority over her. She had to choose her words carefully.","Eighth Old Zhou turned around without giving a definite answer. He glanced at He Zhiran and then at Peng Wang.","\"Boss, everyone says they saw He kissing me. Whose words should I believe?\"","He Zhiran and Peng Wang spoke almost simultaneously.","\"Listen to me.\"","\"Listen to me.\"","Peng Wang sighed, \"I was right by your side at that time. No one knows the situation better than I do.\"","Although Eighth Old Zhou had already started to believe their words, he still held onto his stubborn belief.","\"While I believe what you're saying, so many people saw He kissing me, which damages her reputation.\"","Seeing Eighth Old Zhou's unyielding attitude, He Zhiran couldn't control her temper.","Her anger got the better of her, and she became somewhat reckless.","\"Eighth Old Zhou, I've already made myself clear. Please stop overthinking things, and by the way, my reputation is none of your concern.\""]},{"number":53,"title":"Chapter 53: The outsider knows what he knows.","paragraphs":["The Eighth Old Zhou saw that He Zhiran was furious and suddenly felt guilty.","At this moment, he no longer had the dignity a government official should have when facing a criminal.","\"No, no, no, that's not what I meant.\"","\"Then what do you mean? I've made it so clear, what more do you want?\" He Zhiran was really angry now.","The thinking of these \"ancient fossils\" was really stubborn and ignorant. If she didn't take a stand, she would definitely be angered to death.","He Zhiran's loud shout immediately silenced the Eighth Old Zhou.","The Eighth Old Zhou looked to Peng Wang for help, hoping his boss could help him at this time.","Who knew, Peng Wang didn't help him either.","It was a case of outsiders see more clearly. What He Zhiran had explained so clearly, the Eighth Old Zhou was indeed latching onto a trivial issue.","\"Old Zhou, He is your lifesaver. If you want to repay her kindness, tell those ill-intentioned people clearly that He did not kiss you. I was the one who really woke you up.\"","After saying this, Peng Wang felt that even his dead heart was revived.","However, compared to a woman's reputation, he felt this was nothing.","The Eighth Old Zhou did not object to this, and also felt that this was what he should do.","But as a man, he was worried that Mo Jiuye would dislike He Zhiran because of this. If that was really the case, wouldn't he become a sinner?","Thinking of this, the Eighth Old Zhou said solemnly to He Zhiran:","\"I will find time to explain the misunderstanding to everyone. If Mo Jiuye still dislikes you because of this, I can be responsible for you...\"","Without even thinking, it was clear what the Eighth Old Zhou wanted to say.","He Zhiran did not want to hear anything about being responsible or not. She just saved someone, and she had already explained it clearly that there was no physical contact between them.","Although the Eighth Old Zhou said this out of kindness, He Zhiran just didn't like hearing it.","The Eighth Old Zhou instinctively raised his hands.","\"Ok ok, I won't say any more, I promise I won't say any more from now on...\"","This woman was definitely a tigress reborn. He was really a little afraid of provoking her.","\"It's not enough to not talk about it, don't even think about this matter from now on.\" He Zhiran warned domineeringly.","At this moment, she had completely forgotten that she was still an exiled prisoner.","Seeing that the atmosphere was almost diffused, Peng Wang hurriedly stepped in to mediate.","\"Alright, alright, I'll bear witness to this. Let's pretend it never happened.","Also, He's method of saving people is not bad. If possible, take some time to teach us carefully. In case we encounter any danger on the road, we can also save ourselves.\"","\"No problem. Chief Peng can come to me anytime if you want to learn this life-saving technique.\"","With the matter resolved, He Zhiran didn't want to stay here a moment longer. She bid farewell to Peng Wang and turned to leave.","Unexpectedly, as soon as she opened the door, several guards collapsed into the room.","If He Zhiran hadn't been in such a temper just now, she would not have failed to notice that there were people eavesdropping at the door.","Seeing these sneaky guards, He Zhiran angrily stomped on their bodies as she walked out of the room.","Peng Wang was also very helpless seeing the miserable state of his subordinates. He waved his hand.","\"You guys, hurry up and get some steamed buns with white flour for the Mo family.\"","The guards looked at each other in dismay.","It was obvious that the boss was trying to appease He here.","Could it be just to learn that life-saving technique?","This was really the first time the guards had ever taken the initiative to appease an exiled prisoner...","Seeing that they were still in a daze, Peng Wang said impatiently, \"What are you staring for, go quickly!\"","As the guards were about to leave, the Eighth Old Zhou called out to them, \"Also, He is my lifesaver. Her reputation cannot be ruined like this. You must make it clear to those people that He did not have any intimate contact with me.\"","Hearing this, Peng Wang added, \"I heard this rumor was spread by Li Rou'er. Don't forget to teach her a lesson too.\"","\"Yes, yes, we'll go right away.\" The guards brushed the dust off their bodies and rushed off in a streak.","Only Peng Wang and the Eighth Old Zhou were left in the room.","The Eighth Old Zhou had a bewildered expression.","\"Boss, tell me, was there anything wrong with what I just said?\"","Peng Wang was speechless.","This Eighth Old Zhou was usually so clever and slick, how did he get stuck on such a trivial matter today?","\"Didn't we agree earlier? Don't bring up this matter again in the future.\"","Although the Eighth Old Zhou felt aggrieved in his heart, seeing that even Peng Wang had started reprimanding him, he could only swallow his words resentfully.","He Zhiran walked back furiously and met Li Rou'er leading several women from the Li and He families.","Li Rou'er's contempt was obvious in her eyes.","She crossed her arms to block He Zhiran's path.","\"He Zhiran, after doing such a degrading thing today, you still dare to show your face. If it was another shameless woman, she would have already smashed her head to death.\"","He Zhiran was in a bad mood right now and was too lazy to engage in a war of words with Li Rou'er.","She raised her hand and slapped Li Rou'er hard several times, then looked at her scornfully.","\"Li Rou'er, today I'm teaching you on behalf of your parents how to behave. In the future, if that dirty mouth of yours dares to speak nonsense again, watch out for your tongue.\"","Li Rou'er was caught off guard by several slaps. By the time she reacted, she saw that He Zhiran had already walked away.","She hurled abuse at He Zhiran's back.","\"He Zhiran, you are a cheap whore, a worthless woman. Just for a little benefit, you didn't even let go of a dying official...\" Ah...","She hadn't finished cursing when she let out a scream, then quickly covered her mouth with her hand.","Seeing her daughter at a disadvantage, Zhu hurried over and asked with concern, \"Rou'er, what's wrong?\"","Li Rou'er slowly lowered her hand, revealing a bloody tooth in her palm.","Zhu was timid in front of the guards, but in front of He Zhiran she was like a different person.","\"He, you are simply lawless, actually daring to attack people in front of so many!\"","In fact, He Zhiran was really wronged. She had walked so far away, how could she have hit Li Rou'er?","At this moment, she was truly infuriated by these scum from the Li family.","He Zhiran strode back to stand in front of Li Rou'er.","She didn't even bother using her hands, just lifted her leg and kicked Li Rou'er flying.","\"Who do you think you are?","Don't think I don't know about your disgraceful affairs with Li Hu.","But ah, I really can't understand, Li Hu has already been sent to the government, who gave you the courage to still strut arrogantly here?\"","\"He, shut your mouth!\" Hearing her own daughter being slandered like this, Zhu pounced at He Zhiran, clawing at her.","Of course He Zhiran would not let a powerless woman injure her.","She didn't even dodge, just lifted her foot and kicked Zhu in the lower abdomen.","Zhu yelped in pain, clutching her stomach as she sat on the ground crying.","\"Officials... Hurry and see... He is simply lawless!\"","The women of the Mo, Fang and Xie families were in the backyard preparing dinner with the ingredients He Zhiran had bought back today. Hearing He Zhiran's name being cursed, they put down what they were doing and rushed over quickly.","\"Little sister, who is cursing you? Watch your second sister-in-law deal with them.\"","As she spoke, the second sister-in-law raised the ladle in her hand to stand protectively in front of He Zhiran.","The other sisters-in-law also stared fiercely at the few women across from He Zhiran.","Mo Hanyue quickly ran to He Zhiran's side.","\"Sister-in-law, Hanyue will beat up the bad guys for you.\"","Although Old Lady Mo didn't say anything, the cleaver in her hand already said it all.","The Xie and Fang family members were also glaring fiercely at the group Li Rou'er had brought, just waiting for the Mo family's order to take action...","He Zhiran's angrily beating heart instantly felt warmth.","\"I didn't suffer any losses.\" To keep her family from worrying, He Zhiran told the truth.","At this time, the guards who had been ordered to bring steamed buns to the Mo family arrived.","Without a doubt, no matter who was right or wrong in this matter, it was definitely the Li and He families who were at fault.","Their boss had also told them to fix up Li Rou'er, so they could just take care of it all together.","He Zhiran was someone even the boss had to cover for. How dare they offend her?","Without hesitation, two guards raised their whips and started beating. The screams of the Li and He families' women pleading for mercy filled the air."]},{"number":54,"title":"Chapter 54: This is what Happens when you piss me off.","paragraphs":["Today, the people who angered He Zhiran were Li Rou'er mother and daughter. When she saw the officers go after other people, she took the opportunity to stand in front of Li Rou'er again.","Li Rou'er was still sitting on the ground. Seeing He Zhiran come over aggressively, her body instinctively shrank back.","\"He...He Zhiran, what are you trying to do? You still dare to use force in front of the officers?\"","He Zhiran looked at Li Rou'er coldly, not showing any warmth in her eyes. Li Rou'er moved back a little, and she moved forward a little.","\"I was thinking of not arguing with you, but you repeatedly provoked me.\"","As she spoke, He Zhiran viciously stomped on Li Rou'er's ankle, and then twisted hard a few times.","Li Rou'er screamed in pain.","Seeing Li Rou'er's painful state, He Zhiran had no intention of stopping.","She continued kicking Li Rou'er's sore spots one foot at a time.","\"I know your petty thoughts clearly, and you know mine as well. I'll make it clear today that in the future, if you live an honest life, then fine. But if you dare provoke me again, I will definitely make you suffer a fate worse than death.\"","Li Rou'er was in so much pain that tears and snot streamed down her face. At this moment, she truly realized He Zhiran's fierceness.","\"He Zhiran, please stop beating me in the name of our former friendship as good sisters.\"","\"Good sisters? When did you ever treat me as a good sister?\" He Zhiran couldn't help but sneer coldly.","Li Rou'er had strung along the original host, yet still shamelessly claimed that the two of them were good sisters...","He Zhiran increased her force again, punching and kicking Li Rou'er.","At the same time, the other women of Mo's family were not idle either. Although they still didn't completely understand the situation, they could see that it was Li Rou'er and her mother who had provoked He Zhiran.","So while He Zhiran was beating Li Rou'er, they also went up and attacked Zhu one by one.","In a short time, the courtyard of the inn was thrown into chaos, attracting countless lodgers to come and watch.","The one-sided battle quickly ended with Li's family and He's family begging for mercy.","He Zhiran did not hold back when beating Li Rou'er this time.","Li Rou'er's face was swollen like a bun, completely unrecognizable from its original appearance.","Her right arm was also dislocated and drooped limply.","He Zhiran panted as she stared at her, her eyes full of warning.","\"Li Rou'er, remember this - this is the consequence of provoking me. If you don't want today's events to repeat themselves, you'd better keep your mouth shut and behave.\"","At this moment, Li Rou'er was so afraid of He Zhiran that she didn't dare to speak out even though she was angry.","But she was not convinced in her heart, and her hatred for He Zhiran grew even deeper.","Why is it that even though they were both exiled, He Zhiran could eat fragrant food and dress well every day? Even if she lost her virtue, not only did Mo's family not blame her, but they even protected her more?","What was even more infuriating was that those officers helped her without even bothering to distinguish right from wrong.","The more Li Rou'er thought about it, the more she hated He Zhiran. She wished she could tear He Zhiran into pieces immediately!","It was a pity that she was no match for He Zhiran at all...","Just then, the officers took the opportunity while everyone was present and said in a loud voice,","\"Today, He did not save Old Eight Zhou like Li Rou'er said. She taught us the method to save people and the one who woke up Old Eight Zhou was our boss, not Miss He. Li Rou'er was making up lies and damaging Miss He's reputation.","Even if Miss He does not punish you today, we will not let you off. Hurry up and scram. Be careful of the whip next time we hear you babbling nonsense.\"","Hearing this, everyone's eyes fell on Li Rou'er.","They knew it! How could He Zhiran disregard her own reputation just to save someone? It turned out that all this was Li Rou'er making up rumors.","Thinking of this, even the He family, who were on the same side as the Li family, became unhappy and began verbally accusing Li Rou'er.","The fiery temper of the second sister-in-law flared up again. She rolled up her sleeves, went forward and grabbed Li Rou'er's hair, slapping her viciously twice.","\"Good for you, Li Rou'er, to actually slander my ninth younger sister-in-law's reputation like this. Let me beat you to death today.\"","Li Rou'er screamed miserably as she was beaten, but no one from the Li family came forward to stop it except for Zhu.","Seeing this, the other sisters-in-law of Mo's family also surrounded Li Rou'er, criticizing her while lashing out to avenge He Zhiran.","In order to avoid causing any deaths in public, the officers came forward to discourage them, which allowed Li Rou'er to escape this calamity.","After viciously beating Li Rou'er, He Zhiran's anger also subsided somewhat.","She beckoned to the sisters-in-law and the women from the two families who had helped her to leave.","The sisters-in-law followed He Zhiran, their eyes filled with guilt as they looked at her.","The eldest sister-in-law was the first to speak: \"Ninth younger sister-in-law, it was we sisters-in-law who did not trust you enough, so we listened to Li Rou'er's words and wrongly thought you had lost your virtue.\"","The fifth sister-in-law also said: \"That's right, it was all our fault. We won't listen to the slander of villains so casually ever again.\"","He Zhiran smiled at everyone: \"Sisters-in-law do not need to blame yourselves. All is well now that the misunderstanding is resolved.\"","Seeing that He Zhiran really did not intend to hold it against them, the sisters-in-law heaved a sigh of relief and escorted her back.","Hiding in the dark and watching all this, Mo Jiuye also quietly returned to his room.","Just now, he was the first to hear the argument between He Zhiran and Li Rou'er outside, and saw that Li Rou'er had brought so many people with her.","He was afraid He Zhiran would suffer losses, so he took the opportunity to quietly slip out of the room when no one was paying attention.","It was him who knocked out Li Rou'er's tooth with a stone, hoping that the pain would make her know better and retreat.","But Li Rou'er was still unrepentant.","Mo Jiuye was already prepared to take action again, but unexpectedly, He Zhiran's martial arts skills were so sharp.","Although he could not see her martial arts moves clearly, he could determine that the moves He Zhiran used must have been taught by someone.","After observing and discovering these past few days, all of He Zhiran's circumstances had formed countless mysteries in Mo Jiuye's mind.","He Zhiran did not know that Mo Jiuye was lurking nearby ready to help her. The group of women who had won a big victory all felt a sense of arrogance.","Back in the capital, no one had dared provoke them either, but that was because of their status.","It was different now. They could unite together and rely on their own power to beat their opponents until they screamed.","This was a feeling they had never had before, and they thought it was quite exciting.","The second sister-in-law enthusiastically pulled He Zhiran's arm: \"Ninth younger sister-in-law, if something like this happens again in the future, don't forget to call everyone together.\"","He Zhiran also saw that if these women in the family experienced a few more incidents like this, they would definitely become battle-hardened by her training.","However, she also quite liked this spirit of unity.","\"Alright, if anyone dares to clamor again, I definitely won't forget Second Sister-in-Law.\"","\"Ninth Sister-in-Law, and me too! I can do it too.\" Mo Hanyue was afraid the Ninth Sister-in-Law would forget about her, so she quickly declared her stance.","Then, the other sisters-in-law and the women from Xie's family and Fang's family also said they would stand shoulder to shoulder with He Zhiran and fight together.","Everyone was in good spirits at the moment. Especially since He Zhiran had purchased large quantities of supplies during the day, they busily started making dinner, working more efficiently than ever.","Especially the women from Fang's family and Xie's family - perhaps because they considered that their families would be freeloading off Mo's family's light, they competed to do the work.","While there was harmony in Mo's family, Fang's family, and Xie's family, bursts of noisy quarrels could be heard from the grass shed where Li's family and He's family were staying.","The two families were already unhappy with each other yesterday because of fighting over the location of the grass sheds. Today, the He family's women were provoked by Li Rou'er to go find trouble with He Zhiran, and they ended up being beaten badly.","The He family became increasingly dissatisfied with the Li family.","If it wasn't for He Ming and He Liang's current state, they might have already attacked the Li family.","Thinking of the root cause of all these consequences, Li Rou'er, Li Yuer and Li Ruer seemed to have gone crazy as they violently shook Li Rou'er.","\"Li Rou'er, you broom star, back in the capital Father found so many good families for you, yet you refused to marry any of them.","Instead, your sights were set too high, wholeheartedly wanting to become the wife of a duke or prince.","And now, the man Mo Jiuye married was his childhood sweetheart He Zhiran. You're an old maid still stuck at home, not only unable to make any contribution to the family, but causing trouble everywhere.","Not only are you bringing disaster on yourself, but even implicating the whole family. You're a broom star, deliberately staying here to prevent the Li family from living in peace.\"","Hearing Li Yuer's heart-piercing words, Li Rou'er could no longer control her emotions.","One of her arms was dislocated, and even though she was in excruciating pain, she didn't want to keep listening to such words.","Li Rou'er pounced on Li Yuer as if she had been possessed, opening her mouth wide to take a fierce bite on her face.","Li Yuer cried out in pain while kicking and flailing her limbs to fight off Li Rou'er.","Seeing this, Li Ruer also went to help Li Yuer.","The already injured Li Rou'er was no match for her two younger sisters. She was quickly pinned to the ground and beaten up.","Zhu did not have much standing in the Li household. Seeing her daughter being bullied, she did not dare to intervene. She had completely lost the arrogance she had when dealing with He Zhiran, and could only plead for help from Li Liang."]},{"number":55,"title":"Chapter 55: Thank You for All You have Done for Mohism","paragraphs":["Li Liang was fighting with the He family while seeing his own unfilial daughters fighting each other again, and felt utterly helpless at that moment.","He didn't bother to scold the He family and hurried to pull his daughters away.","The He family also saw this scene and felt extremely delighted.","At this moment, Li Rou'er had completely lost her composure.","Her face, which had already been beaten into a pig's head by He Zhiran, now had countless more claw marks, which gave people a creepy feeling when looking at it.","Seeing this, Li Liang almost passed out from anger.","\"Li Rou'er, I used to think you were decent and always wanted to help you fulfill your wishes. Now I realize you are a good-for-nothing who causes more harm than good.\"","Being scolded like this by the father who had always favored her, Li Rou'er hated He Zhiran even more.","If it wasn't for He Zhiran saving Old Eight Zhou, Li Hu wouldn't have been taken to the yamen.","She thought she could get better treatment by giving herself to Li Hu.","But all this was ruined by that bitch He Zhiran.","Thinking of this, Li Rou'er clenched her fists tightly and gritted her teeth, saying in a voice that only she could hear:","\"He Zhiran, I will definitely not let you die well.\"","...","In the kitchen behind the inn, the aroma of food was already wafting out faintly.","The braised pork ribs made by He Zhiran herself had been served, arousing everyone's praise.","Mo Hanyue's cute big eyes looked at He Zhiran admiringly.","\"Sister-in-law, this is the first time I've seen someone who can make bones so delicious. I admire you so much.\"","He Zhiran realized that her innocent little sister-in-law had become her little fan.","\"It's the same principle as stewing meat. It's just that we used to live well-off lives and didn't think about eating bones before.\"","What He Zhiran said was true. According to historical records and the original owner's memories, wealthy families in this era would not buy bones with little meat to eat.","So it's not surprising that people from wealthy families don't know how delicious pork ribs are.","Seeing her daughter-in-law, Old Lady Mo somehow felt a little heartache.","She used to be the treasure held in the hands of the Hes. The second day after her wedding, she followed her husband's family into exile, and now she had learned to calculate money to get through the days so quickly. It was really not easy for her.","He Zhiran didn't know what her mother-in-law was thinking. She scooped a bowl of long-awaited braised pork ribs and handed it to a sister-in-law, asking her to take it to the dining table first.","As for the rest, it would be distributed by Old Lady Mo, the head of the household.","Old Lady Mo had always been fair, treating the Fang and Xie families equally, dividing the food according to the number of people.","She was not stingy with the officials either. After all, getting along well with them would mean less suffering on the road.","In addition, the sisters all wanted He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye to improve their relationship as soon as possible, and strongly urged He Zhiran to have dinner with Mo Jiuye.","He Zhiran was not coy. Since she came here, she felt she got along well enough with Mo Jiuye, so having dinner alone together was no big deal.","Seeing the fragrant food brought in, Mo Jiuye knew clearly that being able to eat such good food on the road to exile was all thanks to He Zhiran.","Before starting his meal, he sincerely said,","\"Thank you for everything you've done for the Mo family.\"","This sudden expression of thanks left He Zhiran stunned for a moment.","\"Uh...we're all family. I like mother, sisters-in-law and auntie, so I'm happy to do these things.\"","Just like them?","Mo Jiuye didn't know why, but the first thing that came to his mind after hearing He Zhiran's words was this question.","His years of military service allowed him to well conceal his thoughts in front of He Zhiran.","Mo Jiuye was not a talkative person to begin with. After expressing his gratitude, he didn't know what else to say.","So he picked up his bowl and chopsticks and started eating.","After eating a piece of ribs, Mo Jiuye intuitively felt that this dish must have been made by He Zhiran.","Others probably couldn't produce such flavor.","The women also praised that the ribs tasted better than meat.","It was just a pity that with so many people eating, the amount of ribs each person could get was limited.","While eating, the officials kept talking about He Zhiran.","They all agreed that although this trip didn't gain much benefits, being able to eat such delicious food made it worthwhile.","After dinner and freshening up, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye just sat in the room staring at each other until it was time for Mo Jiuye to quietly leave.","When they were alone with nothing to do, they both felt a little awkward.","Finally enduring until Mo Jiuye went out, He Zhiran let out a sigh of relief and lazily lay on the bed, letting her consciousness enter her space.","She wanted to see if the store application she submitted yesterday was approved.","To her delight, the screen showed that the review was passed and she could add product links now.","Adding product links was not difficult. The software had a photo taking function that allowed her to simply take photos of products and upload them.","Mo Jiuye had just gone out and surely wouldn't be back too soon.","For ease of operation, He Zhiran simply entered her space.","She casually picked a vase and used her mind to bring it into the operating room, which had stronger lighting that would make product photos look better.","He Zhiran imagined the product photography she had seen before, planning to take photos of the vase from every angle.","Unexpectedly, when the phone camera was aimed at the vase, she couldn't find the shutter button.","Just as He Zhiran was a little confused, a product valuation message appeared on the phone screen.","【Vase from Shun Dynasty era, no damage, valued between 400,000-500,000 yuan, confirm listing?】","He Zhiran had just been worrying about not being able to determine the value of these antiques. She didn't expect the mall to be so user-friendly as to solve her biggest headache.","She unhesitatingly chose to list the product.","He Zhiran was not greedy either, she just set the lowest price as the selling price.","400,000 was already very satisfying for her, not to mention there were still so many items taken from the palace that could be sold.","If she took the money from selling these antiques to modern times to live on, she would be a complete winner in life.","Unfortunately, she had already crossed over to this time and becoming a winner in modern life could only remain a fantasy.","Bringing her thoughts back to reality, after selecting the price, the product was successfully listed, and the antique vase in front of her disappeared into thin air.","He Zhiran wanted to check it from a customer's perspective by opening the product link.","This made her even more satisfied with the mall.","The price was still 400,000, and somehow the built-in camera of this software managed to take eight pictures that showed the product clearly from every angle, even marking the exact dimensions."]},{"number":56,"title":"Chapter 56: Do you know that man","paragraphs":["In order to make the variety of goods in her newly opened store not so singular, He Zhiran also randomly selected some calligraphy, paintings and jewelry, and hung them in the store.","Similarly, after hanging up these selected items, they instantly disappeared.","He Zhiran was not worried. After all, this Taobao treasure was completely different from what she knew in her previous life. It could automatically estimate prices and upload pictures. It was understandable to put away the goods in advance.","After being busy for about two hours, He Zhiran successfully uploaded 20 items.","The most valuable was a painting by a certain famous person. The system valued it between 100-130 million.","The cheapest was a silver hairpin, priced at 150,000.","For Taobao Treasure, He Zhiran's goods were relatively expensive. She didn't expect the sales volume to be very large either.","As long as it could bring her some money that could be used as a buffer, it would be fine. Anyway, there was plenty of gold, silver and jewels in her space.","As long as she could get along well with those officials, she would have a chance to replenish supplies at any time.","After the goods in the store were put on the shelves, it was also a big deal for He Zhiran.","Since she came here, this was the first time she had stayed in the space for such a long time.","Looking at the clock on the wall, it was already eleven thirty at night.","Thinking that Mo Jiuye would not be back for a while, He Zhiran simply went to the bathroom.","She tentatively turned on the faucet, and water spurted out directly, and it was hot.","After leaving the capital, she had been displaced all the way, and her body was covered in dust.","He Zhiran decided to wash herself clean before going out again.","She quickly took off the clothes with patches and threw them into the fully automatic washing machine for washing. She took a nice hot shower.","The long-lost feeling made her feel inexplicably comfortable. As the white bubbles silently drained from the floor drain, it seemed to take away all the unpleasantness of her day.","He Zhiran was afraid that Mo Jiuye's estimated time would change, so she didn't dare to delay here for too long.","After a quick wash, she wrapped herself in a towel from her previous life and walked out of the bathroom.","She found a hair dryer and dried her hair.","At this time, the washing machine also gave a prompt that the work was finished.","He Zhiran took out the still slightly damp clothes and dried them as much as possible with the hair dryer.","Then she quickly put them on and left the space.","At this time, it was already past midnight, and Mo Jiuye had not yet returned.","He Zhiran thought that she still had to travel tomorrow to rest up, so she lay on the bed to rest.","However, when there are concerns in the heart, it is really difficult to fall asleep. Helplessly, He Zhiran could only close her eyes to nourish her spirit.","As time slowly passed, looking at the clock in the space, it was already more than two o'clock in the middle of the night.","Mo Jiuye still hadn't come back.","He Zhiran was a little uneasy.","She was afraid that Mo Jiuye would have an accident during this special period, then all her efforts would be in vain.","However, at this time, waiting was the only thing she could do.","Looking at the window paper opposite, there were already faint signs of whitening.","There were still occasional chicken calls outside.","This predicted that daylight was not far off.","He Zhiran became more and more uneasy, and there were several times when she wanted to go out and look for him.","However, considering Mo Jiuye's great skills, he should not be in danger, so she held back.","Just when she was extremely anxious, the door was finally pushed open.","The tall figure that had worried her all night appeared in He Zhiran's sight.","Mo Jiuye's expression was very serious. He Zhiran guessed that he must have heard some useful information.","\"Did everything go well?\"","Mo Jiuye nodded and sat on the edge of the bed.","\"Very smooth. I thought the assassins wouldn't come, and I was about to leave when the target finally appeared.","There were two people who came to kill Li Hu. After they killed Li Hu, I followed them all the way to a courtyard and saw with my own eyes the eunuch who Li Hu had contacted.\"","He Zhiran widened her eyes and asked, \"Do you recognize that person?\"","Mo Jiuye's eyes became even deeper, and at the same time, He Zhiran could also see that he was somewhat disappointed.","\"I'm all too familiar with that person. It's the eunuch Li Lu who has been waiting on the Third Prince since he was a child.\"","Hearing Mo Jiuye mention the Third Prince, He Zhiran looked very surprised.","In the history books she knew, the Third Prince Nan Qi was the next emperor of the Great Shun Dynasty.","It was also him who exonerated Mo Jiuye of his crimes and built Yiguang Tomb so that future generations would always cherish his memory.","If the records in the history books were not wrong, Nan Qi should have treated Mo Jiuye well. Why did he do this?","He Zhiran racked her brains but could not figure it out.","And from Li Hu's actions, he could indeed frame himself with the incident of framing Zhou Laoba to give himself the charge of escaping, which could be understood as him taking revenge for Li Rou'er.","However, once his charge of escaping was established, Mo Jia people would also be punished more severely, and the officials might even report it to the court to increase the punishment of the Mo family.","This meant that Li Hu did not have good intentions towards anyone in the Mo family.","If there was no instigation from above, He Zhiran absolutely did not believe Li Hu would do this.","\"Did you and the Third Prince have a falling out before?\"","When asked about his relationship with the Third Prince, Mo Jiuye explained in a deep voice.","\"We were born on the same day and were selected by the Emperor since childhood to be his study companions. Before the age of sixteen, except for sleeping, we were almost inseparable.","Our relationship can be said to be unbreakable. Even Shunwu Emperor believed that I would become the biggest help for the Third Prince in his fight for the throne in the future.\"","Upon hearing this, He Zhiran became even more confused.","\"You were on such good terms, why would he still send someone to trip you up?\"","\"After following those two to the courtyard, I eavesdropped on their conversation.","According to Li Lu, it was because I knew too much about Nan Qi's affairs that he was afraid I would leak it out, so he planted spies in the ranks of officials.","Unexpectedly, Li Hu ruined their original intention because of a Li Rou'er, and turned from monitoring to backstabbing.\"","For what Mo Jiuye said, He Zhiran did not completely believe it.","Since it was an unbreakable relationship, Nan Qi should have trusted Mo Jiuye. There was no need to monitor him at all. Giving some assistance would have been more reasonable.","However, considering the records in the history books, He Zhiran did not intend to make any judgement about Nan Qi, she just wanted to let Mo Jiuye know her true thoughts.","\"Before the Duke of Protection's mansion was searched, it was impossible for Nan Qi to not hear anything. Did he send anyone to give you a heads up?\"","Mo Jiuye resolutely shook his head: \"No, he didn't.\"","\"Not giving you advance notice, it could be that he had some difficulties that were hard to tell. Based on your unbreakable relationship, when your family met such great danger, he should have helped you deal with these officials.","As a result, not only did he not do so, he even planted spies to monitor you among the officials.","Can you think of what Nan Qi's purpose was in doing so?\""]},{"number":57,"title":"Chapter 57: Your Excuses Are OK","paragraphs":["Mo Jiuye was not without thoughts of these things, but he cherished the friendship between Nan Qi very much.","Just because of this, he instinctively wanted to ignore these negative reasons.","Now, as He Zhiran carefully told them out, Mo Jiuye had to face reality again.","\"I have suspected that the one who instructed Old Mrs. Liu to poison the well was Eldest Prince Nanheng. From this matter, the suspicion of Nan Qi cannot be ruled out either.","Although I still can't think of his real reason for doing this for the time being, we still have to be very vigilant in the future.","If you do too many things, sooner or later you will reveal your tricks.\"","Although the two talked so much, they still couldn't figure out Nan Qi's original intention.","However, they were both aware that there was one more person to guard against in the future.","Unknowingly, the sky outside was already bright. Although both of them had not slept all night, they could not sleep at this time.","Mo Jiuye was still better off. In the eyes of outsiders, he had serious injuries and could take a nap lying on the cart.","On the contrary, He Zhiran would probably have to spend the whole day on the road tomorrow.","Thinking of this, Mo Jiuye finally began to look carefully at He Zhiran, intending to show some concern.","As a result, he was surprised to find that He Zhiran's clothes, which were covered in dust, were now very tidy, although they were still patches upon patches.","And her slightly oily hair had also become shiny and faintly exuded a light fragrance.","Seeing Mo Jiuye staring at her, He Zhiran thought there was something wrong with her.","Her hands instinctively touched her face, and then asked.","\"What's wrong? Is there something wrong with me?\"","Because she had been worried about Mo Jiuye, who had not returned for a long time, she ignored the fact that she had taken a bath in the space.","\"Did you wash your clothes?\"","Mo Jiuye still wanted to ask, did you take a bath?","However, with his modest character, he always felt embarrassed to ask a woman if she had bathed.","Asked like this, He Zhiran only noticed her own changes.","She had indeed been careless just now, thinking only that washing herself clean would be more comfortable, but ignoring that people would question this.","\"You went out to do something, I couldn't sleep, so I just washed up simply.\"","Although the reason was a bit far-fetched, this was all He Zhiran could say.","This time Mo Jiuye did not intend to let her off.","\"Your clothes dried out overnight?\"","\"Uh... I always hung my clothes outside the back window, where the ventilation was good. They were almost dry before you came back.\"","Seeing He Zhiran's far-fetched explanation, Mo Jiuye knew that this must be related to her big secret.","Thinking of this, he stopped asking.","Who let him promise not to explore her secret.","Even though his curiosity had reached the extreme, he could only let it go.","\"Your excuse is still possible, it should be okay to fool Mother and Sister-in-law.\"","He Zhiran knew that Mo Jiuye was reminding her, while also telling her that he didn't believe what she said at all.","She could only continue to play dumb.","\"I didn't lie, others will naturally answer the same if they ask.\"","Just then, the shouts of the officials came from outside.","\"Get up early, eat breakfast and continue on the road.\"","The two people in the room glanced at each other tacitly. Mo Jiuye tidied up and lay back on the bed, while He Zhiran walked out.","It was thought that nothing would happen today, and everyone would continue on their way after breakfast.","Unexpectedly, there was a cry to heaven at the He family.","It turned out that He Liang had not survived and was found to have lost his breath when his family was about to feed him some black noodles.","Fortunately, He Ming had escaped the danger of his life, leaving the He family with one son left.","Upon hearing this news, both He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye were somewhat puzzled.","Mo Jiuye said in a deep voice, \"I know my limits, He Liang can't possibly die.\"","\"I also observed their wounds yesterday. It absolutely wouldn't be severe enough to be fatal,\" He Zhiran said, already lost in thought, seeming to have made a bad guess.","Mo Jiuye's thoughts were equally heavy. Both felt that He Liang's death was absolutely suspicious.","In order to verify their guesses, He Zhiran decided to take a look at the He family.","Now, the officials had a good impression of her and would not restrict her movements.","He Zhiran easily came to the grass shed where the He family lived.","At this time, Peng Wang was also there with several officials, preparing to handle the aftermath and continue on their way.","He Zhiran thought that if she rashly went forward to examine He Liang's corpse, she would definitely be rejected by the He family.","After thinking about it, He Zhiran decided to make a little use of Peng Wang.","She went up to Peng Wang and first pretended to gossip and asked, \"Master Peng, how could He Liang suddenly die?\"","Peng Wang didn't seem to have any doubts about He Liang's death. After all, he saw that his injuries were serious yesterday.","\"He must have died from his heavy injuries!\"","He Zhiran shook her head regretfully, \"It's really a pity that he died so young.\"","After a pause, seeing that Peng Wang had no reaction, she continued, \"Master Peng, I'm soft-hearted. Why don't we help check He Ming's injuries before we set off?\"","Peng Wang was not simple-minded either. Hearing He Zhiran's words, he guessed that she must have some purpose in voluntarily going to help He Ming with his injuries.","However, he was still very polite and did not expose it.","\"If you are willing to help He Ming with his injuries, it would be a good thing, saving us from having another burden on the road ahead.\"","With that said, Peng Wang took He Zhiran to He Ming.","The He family became vigilant when they saw He Zhiran come over.","Many people in the He family had seen with their own eyes her ruthless beating of Li Rou'er yesterday.","If it wasn't for the lingering fear in their hearts, they would have scolded her long ago.","Peng Wang ignored the He family's expressions.","\"I finally persuaded the lady He to help He Ming, so we don't have another death in our exiled team.\"","Although his words were unpleasant to hear, this was also what the He family feared most.","Now that He Zhiran was willing to help He Ming with his injuries, they couldn't ask for more.","Everyone tacitly made way to give He Zhiran space to treat He Ming.","In fact, He Zhiran had already seen He Ming's wounds from afar yesterday, and was already aware of his condition.","However, to hide from people's eyes and ears, He Zhiran still pretended to roll up He Ming's sleeves.","The wound was suddenly exposed to air, and He Ming's arm instinctively shrank back.","The He family stared at her closely, waiting for the result.","He Zhiran did not immediately announce the results, but asked the He family,","\"Were He Liang's wounds the same as his?\"","He Zhiyuan thought her question was related to treating He Ming, and answered without thinking.","\"I personally used clear water to treat their wounds yesterday, and they looked exactly the same.\""]},{"number":58,"title":"Chapter 58: He Liang Is a Scapegoat","paragraphs":["As soon as He Zhiyuan finished speaking, he immediately felt that something was wrong.","He didn't care that the people who were helping He Ming with his injury had a grudge against his family, and continued, \"This is not how it should be. He Ming and He Liang's injuries are exactly the same, and their conditions were almost the same yesterday. Could it be that He Liang did not die because of his injury?\"","After examining He Ming's injury, He Zhiran had completely confirmed this point.","According to what Mo Jiuye said, when he made his move, there was no deviation at all, and the two's injuries could be said to be identical.","When she examined He Ming's injury just now, she could completely confirm that apart from He Ming being a little weak physically, he was in no danger of losing his life, and it was impossible for someone to just die after sleeping for a while.","He Zhiran looked at the corpse parked on the other side, and strode over.","In front of everyone, she lifted a tattered piece of clothing covering He Liang's head.","He Liang's eyes were closed tightly, not forced shut after death, which showed he did not suffer when he died.","And she could determine that from the time of He Liang's death until now, it was less than an hour.","To be precise, it should have been after Mo Jiuye returned from his night visit to the county prison.","After carefully examining it, He Zhiran pulled out a long silver needle from He Liang's Baihui acupoint.","During her examination of the corpse, Peng Wang and He Zhiyuan had been standing on the side watching the whole time.","When He Zhiran pulled out that silver needle, they were both shocked.","He Zhiyuan cried again, \"Who was it? Who was it? It's not enough that my son was injured, they actually took his life too... woo woo... \"","After working as an official for many years, he was not completely ignorant about this kind of assassination.","To be able to kill someone in such an imperceptible way, they must be top experts among experts.","And the main purpose was to silence him.","He Zhiyuan couldn't help but ponder who He Liang might have offended back when he was in the capital.","Perhaps this way, he could guess who the murderer was.","It's just that no matter how hard he racked his brains, he couldn't think of when He Liang had offended such a formidable figure.","He Liang's wife came over crying, and once again covered his head with the tattered clothing, sobbing, \"Near dawn, my husband said he was thirsty, and I fed him some water.","And I didn't sleep too heavily either, if someone came to kill my husband, how could I not have noticed? Husband, I have wronged you... woo woo... It's all because I didn't take good care of you... woo woo...\"","Seeing her daughter-in-law grieving, He Ming's wife cried too.","\"Our He family has already been exiled, who would still be so relentless towards the brothers?","Fortunately I took my husband to the other side of the hut last night to take care of him, otherwise if the two brothers were put together, it would probably be two lives lost now ...\"","After listening to He Ming and He Liang's wives' grievances, He Zhiran obtained another piece of information, that the two brothers did not lie together last night.","Relying on this clue, He Zhiran's line of thinking seemed a bit clearer.","With this kind of thing happening among the exiled convoy, Peng Wang could not send He Liang's corpse to the yamen to ask the county magistrate to investigate the real murderer, he could only order people to deal with the aftermath as soon as possible, so as not to delay the journey.","While the He family was still grieving, the officials had already found a local man who specialized in handling corpses, gave him a few copper coins, and the man took He Liang's corpse away.","He Zhiran had made discoveries during the autopsy, and she did not linger here either. After nodding at Peng Wang, she returned to Mo Jiuye's room.","As soon as she stepped into the doorway, Mo Jiuye impatiently asked, \"Did you find anything?\"","He Zhiran told Mo Jiuye the results of the autopsy, and emphasized the fact that the He brothers did not sleep in the same place.","Mo Jiuye's eyes instantly darkened.","Seeing his expression, He Zhiran knew that he must have thought of something.","\"Do you think that He Liang was your scapegoat?\"","Mo Jiuye looked up, and his eyes became even more profound.","\"You think so too?\"","He Zhiran nodded, and stated her inference.","\"He Liang's time of death should have been after you left that courtyard, which means those people took new actions that you did not know about.","If the assassin was coming for you, they would definitely take action against the injured person when they got here.","And He Liang happened to be resting on the edge of the hut, his wife helped him get up to drink some water near dawn.","I guess the assassin noticed their interaction, confirmed He Liang was seriously injured, and his physique was also somewhat similar to yours, so they mistakenly took He Liang for you.\"","He Zhiran's account was very comprehensive, completely consistent with Mo Jiuye's guess.","He felt more and more that this woman was more extraordinary than he had imagined.","At the same time, he was also glad to have encountered such a wife, she was simply a great help sent by the heavens.","Mo Jiuye himself didn't even know why, even at this time, he could still think about such irrelevant things.","But very soon, he brought back his wandering thoughts.","\"He Liang's death is a good thing for us.\"","\"Why?\" He Zhiran asked.","\"If it really is as you just said, the assassin must have reported back that the assassination was successful.","In the short term, Nan Qi will think I'm dead. Even if he finds out it's wrong, he won't be able to act too quickly the next time, so we can live in peace for a while.\"","He Zhiran knew that Mo Jiuye's analysis was reasonable.","But the peace he spoke of could only be temporary. If they wanted permanent peace, it was probably impossible for now.","When He Zhiran followed Mo Jiuye on the road to exile, she was mentally prepared that the journey would not be smooth, and the future would continue to be so.","\"Since this is the case, let's face everything in the future with equanimity, we'll cross the bridges when we come to them.","Evil has never prevailed over righteousness since ancient times, I don't believe those with malicious intents can rampage for too long.\"","Take Nan Qi for example. Historical records state that he did not reign for even five years before his health declined due to indulgence in carnal pleasures, and he died prematurely.","Later, his only 6-year-old son ascended the throne, the court was controlled by powerful ministers, and it wasn't long before the Great Shun dynasty changed hands.","However, He Zhiran had no intention of telling Mo Jiuye any of this. She had already changed Mo Jiuye's destiny once. As for what would happen in the future, who knew?","When Mo Jiuye was stripped of his assets and exiled, he had already lost hope for the future, and even developed a kind of self-destructive mindset.","But after he discovered Nan Qi's true face, his thinking had completely transformed.","He Zhiran, a woman who had just married into the Mo family, was full of hope for the future. If he, the only Mo man, continued to be self-destructive, it would be too disappointing to the Mo ancestors and the family members exiled with him.","No matter what, he had to try his best to survive, even if he could only live out his days in the barren northwest in the future. As long as the family lived in harmony, it would still be a blessing.","With this thought, Mo Jiuye immediately cheered up.","\"Don't worry, I will do my best to protect you and the family.\""]},{"number":59,"title":"Chapter 59: He watched her all the way.","paragraphs":["He Zhiran knew that Mo Jiuye had completely come to understand.","\"Alright, let's work together and not let those people harm our families one bit.\"","Inside the room, the husband and wife were united in their interests and determined like gold being cut. Outside, the officials had already called for people to get ready to set off.","The sisters-in-law had long since packed everything neatly, some carrying tents on their backs, while others carried new quilts bought just yesterday.","Food, vegetables, large iron pots and other items had already been distributed by He Zhiran yesterday, giving the Fang and Xie families a share each, with each family responsible for carrying their own belongings.","Peng Wang had already said after getting up early that his health was fine, so he would not squeeze onto the wooden cart with Mo Jiuye again.","Therefore, the Mo family placed all of the food and kitchen utensils to one side of the wooden cart, leaving the space for Mo Jiuye.","Thinking of He Ming's tragic death, Mo Jiuye, for safety reasons, did not plan to continue riding in the wooden cart.","He had He Zhiran help him as he walked out of the room.","The Mo women all knew that Mo Jiuye's serious injury was fake, but even so, when they saw Mo Jiuye walk out of the room they were still dumbstruck.","Out of deference to the presence of outsiders, everyone tacitly did not ask questions.","On the contrary, it was Peng Wang who walked over in surprise.","\"Mo Jiuye, don't overexert yourself, I didn't see you yesterday for a day, and now you can walk?\"","Mo Jiuye tried his best to make his expression a little gentler.","\"I'm physically tough, and my wife took good care of me, so I should be fine walking.\"","As he spoke, he looked sympathetically in the direction of He Ming's family.","\"I heard He Ming's injuries are more serious. In order not to delay the progress of the journey, my wife and I discussed lending them the cart for a few days.\"","Upon hearing this, He Zhiran gave a bellyful of complaints to Mo Jiuye in her heart.","This man was sinister enough, not only using others as scapegoats to attract the target, but also saving the Mo family's manpower needed to push the cart.","His move really killed two birds with one stone.","Thinking of what He Ming's family did, He Zhiran did not feel sorry for them at all, and even felt a sense of satisfaction.","The feud between the He family and Mo Jiuye ran too deep for them to let go of the past just because Mo Jiuye lent the wooden cart to He Ming.","However, looking at the current situation of the He family, they did indeed need this wooden cart.","Seeing that Peng Wang did not object, He Zhiyuan did not even give his thanks before pushing the wooden cart away.","Mo Hanyue was confused and did not understand, and was a little anxious seeing there were still so many of their family's belongings on the cart.","\"Ninth brother, there are still our things on the cart. What if someone steals them?\"","Mo Jiuye calmly replied, \"It doesn't matter, with so many officials here, who would dare steal someone else's belongings?\"","He wouldn't have said this, but it nearly made He Zhiyuan throw those things off the cart in anger.","However, he still tried his best to restrain the rage in his heart.","If he did that, it would relieve his anger for the moment, but what about He Ming?","Apart from the women in the family and the children, there was only him, a man who could not carry or lift things, how could he carry the sturdy He Ming on his back?","No one paid attention to He Zhiyuan's face as black as the bottom of a pot. Just at Peng Wang's order, the exiled convoy set off again.","Ever since leaving Yunlai County and walking on the official road, Zhou Laoba had been in low spirits, and would glance at He Zhiran from time to time.","He walked at the back of the convoy with Peng Wang, so He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye did not notice anything abnormal about him.","However, Zhou Laoba's actions did not escape Peng Wang's eyes.","Peng Wang strongly disapproved of this, but it was not easy for him to say it outright, he could only try to subtly hint for Zhou Laoba to know the difficulty and give up.","\"Mo Jiuye was once so prestigious, I still remember when he returned triumphantly, His Majesty personally led civil and military officials out of the city to welcome him.","The scene I witnessed with my own eyes at that time was sensational throughout the city.","Even though today he is exiled, that glory at the time cannot be erased.\"","Hearing Peng Wang suddenly mention Mo Jiuye, Zhou Laoba was very sensitive.","\"Boss, why are you talking about these things out of the blue?\"","Peng Wang seriously suspected that Zhou Laoba was deliberately avoiding the issue.","Since it was already brought up, he did not plan to let the other person continue to equivocate.","\"What I want to say is that Mo Jiuye is a dragon and phoenix among men, and his wife is no ordinary woman either. I see they are a well-matched couple in looks and talent.\"","\"Boss, no matter how glorious Mo Jiuye was, that's in the past. Today he is exiled, even if he can survive the journey to the northwest, he can only be an ordinary commoner in the future.","Spending his whole life as a farmer facing the soil with his back to the sky, how can he give He Zhiran happiness?\"","Zhou Laoba pinned down the implied meaning in Peng Wang's words, as if rebutting them from his heart.","\"Moreover, Lady He has already been intimate with me, how could Mo Jiuye not despise her?","Rather than letting her savior be despised by her husband for life, it'd be better if she came with me, at least I can treat her well.\"","Hearing Zhou Laoba's stubborn words, Peng Wang wished he could give him a few slaps to wake him up.","\"Old Zhou, I see you as a brother, that's why I'm telling you this.\"","He paused, then pointed at He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye supporting each other as they walked.","\"Can you stop deceiving yourself?","Look at Mo Jiuye, does he look like he despises Lady He?","The husband and wife clearly have a good relationship, I advise you to rein in those inappropriate thoughts as soon as possible.\"","In fact, the words Zhou Laoba said also came from the heart.","He was a man who valued emotions and integrity, especially after finding out He Zhiran had awakened him, he always wanted to take responsibility.","This was the minimum decency for a man.","However, looking carefully in the direction Peng Wang pointed, he happened to see Mo Jiuye wiping sweat for He Zhiran.","He had to admit that, as the boss said, Mo Jiuye did not despise He Zhiran because of it, on the contrary he took even better care of her, this was indisputable.","Since this was the case, he would just silently protect her on the journey.","\"Boss, as long as Mo Jiuye can always treat Lady He this way, I won't do anything.\"","Seeing Zhou Laoba could say such things, Peng Wang felt somewhat more at ease.","This brother placed too much importance on emotions and integrity, Peng Wang feared he would become mired in it and unable to extricate himself.","However, this kind of reminder was just touching on it, saying too much could make people weary, so Peng Wang simply changed the topic to chat with Zhou Laoba, in order to distract his attention and prevent him from always staring at Lady He.","In case the Mo family noticed, it would put He Zhiran in an awkward situation...","The convoy marched for a day, still the same as before, stopping by a small river at dusk for the group to rest, as ordered by Peng Wang.","The officials went to the riverside first to fill their water bags, then leaned against big trees to rest.","The prisoners also did the same, those with water bags all ran to the riverside to refill them.","Seeing the Mo women were also about to do the same with their water bags, He Zhiran quickly stopped them.","\"Sisters, there are many people by the river, we can go a bit later.\"","The Mo family now followed He Zhiran's words almost without question, obediently sitting in place to continue resting.","Mo Jiuye, learning from He Zhiran's actions last time, found a thicker tree branch and used an official's knife to whittle it into a point, preparing to try catching some fish in the river to enrich everyone's dinner."]},{"number":60,"title":"Chapter 60: Mo Jiuye's Way of Vent","paragraphs":["He Zhiran was very interested in sitting on the shore watching.","Mo Jiuye had martial arts skills. Entering the water to walk did not feel any resistance.","Seeing the river water was about to reach his thighs, Mo Jiuye stopped.","He concentrated and stared at the water surface. He saw him make a quick move, inserting the branch into the river water.","When he raised the branch, there were two large carps jumping around.","It made the people watching on the shore cheer.","He Zhiran had just stood up when Mo Jiuye swung the two large carps onto the grass in front of her.","The sisters-in-law and Mo Hanyue swarmed over to compete for cleaning them.","The officials also felt happy seeing this scene. They would be able to eat delicacies tonight.","No matter it's eyesight or action, Mo Jiuye was much faster than He Zhiran.","One lively large carp after another was swung ashore by him.","Seeing the sisters-in-law competing to process them, He Zhiran simply took their water bags and went farther away to draw water from the river bank.","She pretended to put the water bag into the river water, but a finger remained at the opening of the water bag.","With her consciousness, she slowly led the water from the water purifier in her space into the water bag.","Although the ancient river water was not polluted, there were still many bacteria.","When possible, she tried to choose clean and sanitary pure water for her family.","At Mo Jiuye's side, it seemed he had good luck, in He Zhiran’s view, all the fish in the small river had swum to his vicinity.","She saw him move almost non-stop, constantly swinging fish ashore.","And it was not just large carps he caught, there were other varieties.","Such as sheatfish and crucian carp.","The sisters-in-law kept running back and forth, taking the fish he caught to process.","Everyone from Fang Family and Xie Family also ran over to help.","Even so, everyone was still busy and swamped. It showed how amazing Mo Jiuye’s fishing speed was.","Seeing the pile of fish getting higher, He Zhiran couldn’t help but remind him.","\"Dear, there are enough fish already.\"","In fact, no one else knew that while Mo Jiuye looked like he was fishing in the river, only he himself knew best that this was his way of venting.","The gloom in his heart these days gave him a suffocating feeling.","Only this way could he feel that he still had some use.","Hearing He Zhiran's reminder, Mo Jiuye stopped his actions and waded through the river water towards the shore.","His pants were already wet a lot, and he had no spare clothes to change into.","Fortunately it was summer. The wind would quickly dry it after blowing on it.","Old Lady Mo understood her son best. She knew he was upset because the Mo family was exiled unjustly.","She walked over with eyes full of distress, wiping Mo Jiuye's forehead, wanting to say something but hesitated.","Mo Jiuye had just vented, and felt much more relaxed.","Seeing his mother's struggles, he gently comforted her.","\"Mother, don't worry. I will try my best to survive. If there is a chance, I will definitely exonerate the charges against the Mo family, and let you and the sisters-in-law live a good life.\"","Old Lady Mo nodded, \"As long as you are mentally prepared, remember to look forward. I believe Heaven will not always be unfair to the Mo family.\"","The mother and son spoke softly here, and the river bank had already exploded.","All the women from the three families were gathered there cleaning Mo Jiuye's caught fish.","The joy on everyone's faces could not be concealed.","None of these women were not born in prominent households. They had lived a life of luxury since childhood, and had countless people waiting on them.","Now it was up to them to work for food and clothing, but they felt it was a kind of fun, and temporarily forgot the reality.","What He Zhiran thought was that if the word \"exile\" and their current status were ignored, this kind of life would be like backpacking in her previous life.","Although everything had to be done by themselves and life was harsher, this unlimited contact with nature could make people relaxed in body and mind.","Among the exiled, only some of them had this refreshing feeling.","The He family and Li family were now glaring at those busy women on the riverside, eyes burning with fire.","Looking at the fish in their hands, they wished they could rush forward and grab some.","But with so many officials watching, they could only think about it in their hearts...","The women kept chatting by the riverside.","\"Ninth younger brother, with so many fish, wouldn't they go bad if we can't finish them?\"","\"Ninth younger brother is really amazing. He caught so many fish at once. I guess he didn't even think about whether we could finish them.\"","\"Sister-in-law Mo, can we eat with big appetites tonight?\"","\"Miss He, I've lived half my life and this is the first time I'm cleaning fish. I have to say, it's quite simple.\"","Little Xie Lin was not afraid of the fish being dirty either. He hugged a big fish and ran to He Zhiran.","\"Auntie, look, the fish is looking at me!\"","In her previous life, He Zhiran's living environment made it difficult to get in touch with children. Seeing Xie Lin's lively appearance now, ripples rose in her heart.","She gently touched Xie Lin's head.","\"Lin'er, good boy, auntie will give you candy.\"","Speaking, He Zhiran used her sleeve to conceal as she accessed her space, took out two pieces of rock sugar from the spice cabinet in the kitchen.","\"Lin'er, go eat them secretly. Don't let the bad guys snatch them.\"","After all he was a child, as soon as He Zhiran mentioned bad guys, Xie Lin subconsciously looked towards the He family and Li family.","Seeing the fiery eyes of those people, Xie Lin shrank his little neck.","In order not to let the rock sugar fall into the bad guys' hands, he hurriedly stuffed it into his mouth. He also abandoned the fish he was hugging and quickly ran to his father's side.","He Zhiran watched Xie Lin run away, and picked some fish from the ones the women had finished processing.","Mo Jiuye was very perceptive and followed along. He found several large rocks and built a simple stove, then squatted beside to help make a fire.","Seeing this, the men from Fang Family and Xie Family also followed Mo Jiuye's example and built stoves.","The Mo family's benevolence had bought them large iron pots, and also gave them grains and vegetables.","If they kept eating food prepared by others, it would be somewhat undeserved.","The three large iron pots were all set up. He Zhiran was responsible for making dinner for the Mo family. The Fang family and Xie family also had women returning to start making dinner.","Peng Wang knew that the Mo family's dinner would definitely have a share for them. So he ordered the officials to gather some firewood and deliver it, which was also helping out.","The women from Xie Family and Fang Family did not know how to cook. They all followed He Zhiran's example.","After half an hour, the braised fish from the Mo family came out of the pot with full aroma and taste.","As soon as the pot lid was lifted, the aroma drifted very far away.","Now they didn't need to think about sharing with Fang Family and Xie Family. They simply gave some to the officials. Everyone in the Mo family hugged a bowl of rice and enjoyed the meal surrounding the iron pot.","At this time, the braised fish made by Xie Family and Fang Family was also ready, but compared to the Mo family's, the taste was barely satisfactory.","Even so, it still made the He Family and Li Family people far away green with envy."]},{"number":61,"title":"Chapter 61: Ancient and Modern Express","paragraphs":["Today, the officials uncharacteristically showed mercy and gave each person a dark steamed bun.","Still, after going without oil and water for days, their stomachs growled incessantly.","Li Rou'er's uninjured hand was clenched into a tight fist, her fingertips dug into her flesh without her realizing it.","Zhu noticed something was off with her and recalled how they were mobbed by the Mo Family people. Zhu was still a little scared.","She quietly reminded Li Rou'er, \"Rou'er, we're no match for that wicked woman. Let's not provoke them in the future.\"","Li Rou'er glared fiercely at Zhu.","She really didn't want to say anything to this mother who only knew how to resign herself to her fate.","She turned her head away, closed her eyes, and pretended to rest. Her mind was filled with the scene of Mo Jiuye squatting by the stove to help He Zhiran make a fire.","She watched them from afar. Although they didn't interact, the harmonious couple scene really stung her.","From the moment Li Rou'er first laid eyes on Mo Jiuye when he stopped a startled horse, she was deeply attracted to Mo Jiuye's aura, unlike that of ordinary men.","Of course, she was also drawn to Mo Jiuye's status as the Duke of Protector.","Her desire to marry Mo Jiuye grew stronger over time.","So much so that when she learned He Zhiran had successfully married Mo Jiuye, she wished she could ruin their marriage herself.","Mo Jiuye was no longer the youngest duke in Da Shun, and reason told her that no matter how good-looking that man was, he would not be a good match for her.","A few days of exile had made Li Rou'er afraid of this kind of precarious life.","The only way to change her current predicament was to get away from here...","After the Mo Family people ate their fill, He Zhiran led everyone to salt and preserve the remaining fish before nightfall completely set in. They tied them with grass ropes and hung them around the wooden carts.","After the busy work was done, the sky had darkened, and the Mo, Fang, and Xie families set up tents.","The tents He Zhiran designed could fit two people. The sisters-in-law tacitly looked for companions to share a tent.","Old Lady Mo stayed with Mo Hanyue.","Undoubtedly, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye shared a tent.","The officials, aside from those on sentry duty, also crawled into tents following the Mo Family's example.","The He and Li families looked on bitterly, the unnamed fire in their hearts burning even more vigorously.","Why was there such a huge disparity in treatment when they were exiled under the same decree?","Li Yuer and Li Ruer hugged Li Liang's arms on both sides, ceaselessly wiping away tears.","\"Father, I don't want to sleep outside. My clothes get drenched with dew in the morning.\"","\"Father, could you please go beg those officials to give us a tent like that?\"","Seeing this, Li Liang was already unhappy. Now he was dizzy from his daughters' shaking and scolded irritably, \"If you want to sleep in a tent, go beg for one yourselves. I don't have that ability.\"","If the sisters had that courage, why would they need to plead with their father here?","Rejected, they could only use their tears to express their dissatisfaction, not daring to say another word.","Li Madam's heart ached for her daughters, but she knew clearly that even if she knelt before those officials, they would not give tents to them out of charity.","She hurriedly pulled her daughters aside to comfort them.","The same scene was unfolding in the He family, as they crowded around He Zhiyuan, asking him to find a way to get tents from the officials.","At this moment, He Zhiyuan's mind was very clear. He knew this was impossible, so he poured cold water directly over them.","\"The Mo Family people bought oil cloth and made those tents themselves. If you want them, use silver to buy your own, then learn from them how to make tents.\"","His words silenced the He family, leaving them speechless.","If they had silver, why would they gnaw on dark buns every day?","Not only did they lack silver and tents, but they also lacked the skills to catch fish...","The tents received approval from everyone after the first day of use.","Including the officials, this was their first time feeling that escorting prisoners was not a bad duty.","He Zhiran was not unfamiliar with being alone with Mo Jiuye, so she no longer felt any pressure.","Hearing the steady breathing beside her, He Zhiran's consciousness entered space.","The shops in Taobao had been open for a full day already. She naturally wanted to check the sales figures after listing so many kinds of merchandise.","As soon as she opened the Taobao page, a dialog box popped up.","[Successfully sold item(s) in store. Income automatically deposited into Alipay account.]","He Zhiran hurriedly clicked to check her account balance.","She saw 7,500 yuan had been added to her account.","Seeing this number, He Zhiran was a little confused.","The cheapest item she sold in her store was 15,000 yuan. What was this 7,500 yuan about?","To clear her doubts, He Zhiran went back to the app and checked the store's transaction records.","This casual glance nearly angered her to the point of vomiting blood.","The transaction record showed that the silver hairpin in her store had been successfully sold today for 15,000 yuan.","Understandably, the platform automatically deducted 10% as a fee from the sale price.","But the shipping fee charged was 40% of the sale price, which was 6,000 yuan...","He Zhiran couldn't help but curse in her heart, what blackhearted delivery company was this to charge so much for shipping?","To willingly be a wronged big spender, He Zhiran could only keep looking for answers.","After some searching, she finally found the courier company's name—Ancient and Modern Express!","She had never heard of this one before, but judging from the literal meaning of the name, this courier company was probably specialized in transporting goods across ancient and modern eras.","This meant there were other transmigrators like her using the shopping platform.","However, other users were irrelevant to her. Right now, He Zhiran just wanted to know why the shipping fee was so expensive.","Fortunately, there was a company overview:","Ancient and Modern Express was founded in XXXX.","Business scope: All transmigrators who open stores in the Taobao app.","Fees: 40% of product price.","Contact customer service with any questions.","He Zhiran decisively tapped the Contact Customer Service button.","Soon, a series of formatted text appeared on the screen.","He Zhiran was too lazy to read it carefully. She typed:","Can the shipping fee be discounted?","Customer Service: [Due to the high costs of transporting your goods across time and space to customers, the price cannot be discounted.]","He Zhiran: Why don't the products I bought have such high shipping fees?","Customer Service: Other merchants use different shipping channels.","He Zhiran...","She conceded. Who made her a transmigrator?","The ungreedy He Zhiran quickly accepted this.","In any case, she finally earned income in the Taobao app. This meant she could purchase some necessary items according to her financial ability.","With her first income, the first thing He Zhiran thought of was safety here."]},{"number":62,"title":"Chapter 62: Shailene Is Missing","paragraphs":["Although there were several types of firearms stored in her medical office, He Zhiran knew that these weapons should not be exposed unless it was absolutely necessary. After all, they were unfamiliar to people, and she would have a hard time explaining their origin if she used them.","After browsing through Taobao, He Zhiran decisively spent 1,000 yuan to purchase two mini sleeve arrows.","Although these items didn't have the same killing power as firearms, their advantage lay in their concealability.","Even if she used them openly, it wouldn't raise suspicion from others, at most just curiosity.","With the sleeve arrows purchased, He Zhiran felt tired. Besides, there were still plenty of goods available in the online store, so she wasn't in a rush to restock.","She withdrew her consciousness and started to prepare for sleep.","She thought it would be an uneventful day, but little did she know that when everyone had already fallen into a deep sleep, Mo Jiuye suddenly sat up.","At the same time, He Zhiran also sensed that something was wrong, and she followed his lead, rising from her bed half a beat slower.","\"It seems like I heard the howling of wolves.\"","Speaking softly, as if confirming her own judgment, He Zhiran said.","\"Yes, it's indeed the sound of wolves.\"","Mo Jiuye replied, already lifting the curtain and walking outside, with He Zhiran closely following his footsteps.","Meanwhile, the guards on duty also noticed something unusual and shouted, \"Boss, it's not good, there's a pack of wolves.\"","Based on her past experience in outdoor combat, He Zhiran knew that wolves were afraid of fire.","Therefore, taking advantage of the darkness, she quickly retrieved three bottles of alcohol from her spatial storage.","He Zhiran swiftly ran around the exiled prisoners and guards who were resting.","All the guards came out of their tents, tightly gripping their large knives.","Except for He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye, the other prisoners huddled together in fear.","Mo Jiuye caught a familiar scent and, seeing He Zhiran's actions cease, instinctively ignited a match, setting fire to the alcohol she had just poured around them.","As flames erupted, the pack of wolves had already surrounded them.","However, hindered by the flames in front of them, the wolves didn't approach any further and instead stood not far away, digging their paws into the ground while howling incessantly.","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye's first priority was the safety of their own people.","After creating a ring of fire with the ignited alcohol, they quickly returned to their camp.","Old Lady Mo tightly hugged Mo Hanyue, looking towards the pack of wolves with fear in her eyes.","The sisters-in-law huddled together, their bodies trembling uncontrollably.","\"Mother, sisters-in-law, Hanyue, with me and my husband here, don't be afraid. We won't let any harm come to you.\"","Mo Jiuye knew that the fire would eventually burn out.","He glanced deeply at He Zhiran and said earnestly, \"I will go out and drive away those wolves. You stay here and protect our family.\"","Although He Zhiran was well aware of Mo Jiuye's abilities, judging by the howling of the wolves, she could tell that their numbers were considerable.","Even with his skills, it would be impossible for him to deal with so many wolves without any weapons.","\"No, we'll go together. Trust me, I can handle it.\"","Mo Jiuye could see how resolute He Zhiran's gaze was as she spoke.","After pondering for a moment, he ultimately didn't refuse.","\"You can come with me, but you must never stray more than three steps away from me. That way, if we encounter any danger, I can save you in time.\"","\"Okay,\" He Zhiran replied without hesitation.","The two of them quickly reassured their family members at home and ran towards the outskirts of the fire circle.","Just as they crossed the fire circle, a thought flashed through He Zhiran's mind, and two mini sleeve arrows appeared in his hand.","Seizing the moment when Mo Jiuye glanced at her, she directly tossed one of the mini sleeve arrows to him and quickly explained the operating method.","Although Mo Jiuye had never seen such small and delicate crossbow arrows before, being passionate about various weapons, he quickly learned how to use them.","The two of them ran several tens of meters away and stopped only when they confirmed that the sleeve arrows could reach the wolves.","Mo Jiuye held He Zhiran's slender waist, lightly leaped, and carried her up onto a sturdy tree.","The husband and wife quickly found suitable positions and shot at the wolf pack in perfect harmony.","At the same time, the government officials leaped out of the fire circle, wielding large knives to fend off the wolves that evaded the feather arrows.","Inside the fire circle, the bolder men on the ground found large rocks and held them in their arms. If a wolf happened to come their way, they would not hesitate to throw the rocks.","The mini sleeve arrows came with ten feather arrows. Before long, the two of them had shot all the feathers.","He Zhiran quickly entered the space in his mind, purchased a sufficient number of feather arrows, installed them, and continued to engage in the battle.","The wolf pack finally couldn't withstand the onslaught and, following the lead of the alpha wolf, fled in all directions.","Taking advantage of the dim remaining light from the fire, they checked the wolf corpses and found at least fifty or sixty.","Mo Jiuye carried He Zhiran as they jumped down to the ground.","Peng Wang quickly ran over and looked at the many wolf corpses before him, still feeling lingering fear.","\"I've been an escort official for so long, and this is the first time I've encountered such a massive wolf pack. Tonight, thanks to you two, otherwise, all of us would have perished in the wolves' jaws.\"","Peng Wang's words were not an exaggeration. With their abilities as government officials, they would have been absolutely unable to disperse the wolf pack.","Mo Jiuye remained expressionless, simply nodded slightly at Peng Wang, and then pulled He Zhiran to go back and check on their own family's situation.","Just then, a scream came from Xie Lin's family: \"Lin'er, my Lin'er is gone...\"","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye exchanged a glance and quickly ran over.","Peng Wang also hurried over with the government officials.","\"What happened exactly?\"","Xie Lin's mother, Lv, was already in tears. When asked, she anxiously said, \"Lin'er is missing. Lin'er, where are you? Come out quickly, don't scare your mother...\"","However, her calls received no response whatsoever.","Peng Wang looked deeply at Xie Ming, the man from the Xie family.","\"When we were driving away the wolf pack just now, what were you all doing?\"","Xie Ming quickly explained, \"Sir, we were worried that you wouldn't be able to hold them back, so we held rocks behind you, constantly on guard in case any wolves managed to break through.\"","Lv also chimed in, saying, \"Lin'er has been by my side all along. But later, my husband and younger brother went to help, and I was worried about their safety. My attention was focused on them, causing me to overlook Lin'er.","Lin'er, it was my carelessness that failed to watch over you... Sob... Sob...\"","Impatiently, Peng Wang scolded, \"Enough, stop crying. Finding people is what matters now.\"","He Zhiran couldn't help but remind him, \"Peng Wang, should we ask other families if anyone else is missing?\"","Upon hearing this, Peng Wang shouted loudly, \"Everyone, check your own families and report immediately if anyone is missing.\"","The disappearance of exiles is no small matter, as it raises suspicions of them becoming fugitives."]},{"number":63,"title":"Chapter 63: Lee Ro-er is Gone","paragraphs":["Once a fugitive appears in a family, the entire family will be implicated.","Even the officials like Peng Wang will be punished for their negligence in guarding.","Therefore, no one dares to be careless about this matter.","Old Lady Mo was the first to speak: \"No one from the Mo family is missing.\"","Fang Chuanzhou also reported, \"No one from the Fang family is missing.\"","\"Official, Li Rou'er is missing...\" Li Yuer shouted loudly, her tone even filled with excitement.","Li Yuer only thought about the absence of her annoying stepsister at home, and her mood instantly improved. She didn't realize the consequences her family would face in the future.","Peng Wang's face turned dark, and he ordered the officials, \"Light up the torches. Even if we have to dig three feet into the ground, find that person for me.\"","\"Yes.\" The officials responded in unison and began searching for Li Rou'er's traces with torches in hand.","Mo Jiuye whispered to He Zhiran.","\"I suspect Xie Lin was taken hostage by Li Rou'er.\"","\"Yes, when I heard Li Yuer shouting just now, I had the same suspicion.\"","Their speculations reached a consensus again, and they fell into silence, pondering why Li Rou'er took Xie Lin and where she might be hiding.","Not knowing what Mo Jiuye was thinking, he pulled He Zhiran to the front of Peng Wang.","\"Official, my wife and I want to help find the person.\"","Peng Wang inexplicably trusted Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran as a couple and also believed in their character, that they wouldn't abandon their family members and escape secretly.","Therefore, he agreed without hesitation.","\"Alright, regardless of the outcome, you must return here before dawn.\"","Before they left, He Zhiran reminded, \"Peng Official, please take care of my mother-in-law, sister-in-law, and aunt.\"","\"Don't worry.\" Peng Wang nodded, waved his hand at the two of them, urging them to leave quickly.","Mo Jiuye held He Zhiran's hand, and they first arrived at the spot where Lv had last seen Xie Lin.","Then, starting from that spot, their eyes carefully observed, not missing any trace.","At the same time, they were calculating in their minds the most advantageous escape route and direction if they were to depart from that spot.","If they were not discovered, the best direction would be where the officials rested.","The officials were outside the circle of fire, intercepting the wolf pack. When Li Rou'er escaped with Xie Lin, there was no one there, and there were tents to provide cover, making it easy to avoid the sight of others.","Passing by the officials' tents, a small path appeared ahead.","Following the path, they observed very carefully, not even missing the grass by the roadside.","After walking about a hundred meters, a fork in the road appeared ahead.","The two of them tacitly split up, with He Zhiran going left and Mo Jiuye going right. Just a few steps out, He Zhiran squatted down and picked up a piece of torn cloth.","Mo Jiuye quickly approached and asked, \"Did you find something?\"","He Zhiran held up the palm-sized piece of torn cloth in front of Mo Jiuye.","\"If I'm not mistaken, this is Xie Lin's kerchief.\"","She vividly remembered that she had touched Xie Lin's head earlier today.","Because the silk kerchief was dark green, she couldn't help but find it amusing. She thought to herself that ancient people really paid attention to detail, even boys would wear a green silk kerchief on their heads.","Mo Jiuye clenched the silk kerchief in his hand.","\"Let's go, let's continue the pursuit,\" he said.","The two of them continued along the small path, becoming more meticulous in their search...","The story goes back half an hour.","Li Rou'er watched as the government officials ran outside the circle of fire to drive away the wolves. She knew that this was her opportunity.","To be safe, she decided to observe from a place where there were many people.","As she arrived at the spot where the Xie family rested, she saw Xie Lin standing alone behind the crowd.","So she boldly approached, forcefully covered his mouth, and spirited him away unnoticed.","The escape route she chose was indeed as Mo Jiuye had anticipated—it was behind the government officials' tents.","Li Rou'er had dislocated one of her arms, making it difficult to control Xie Lin with just one hand.","Furthermore, Xie Lin kept resisting.","So she casually entered a tent, picked up a sock that one of the officials hadn't had time to put on, and stuffed it into Xie Lin's mouth.","The pungent smell made Xie Lin momentarily dazed. Taking advantage of this, she found a rope and tied up Xie Lin's hands and feet separately.","Then she carried Xie Lin and quickly ran towards the small path.","As they approached a fork in the road, it was evident that one of the paths had been walked on more frequently, indicating that it was often used by people.","At this moment, Li Rou'er feared encountering other people, so she decisively chose the path with fewer footprints.","It was precisely at that moment that Xie Lin struggled to shake loose his hairpin, causing the silk kerchief to fall to the ground, providing valuable clues to He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye.","Li Rou'er had thought that Xie Lin, being a small child, wouldn't weigh much.","However, she had overestimated her own physical strength. She hadn't run far when she started to feel exhausted.","She looked back and saw no signs of anyone chasing them, so she took Xie Lin and hid in the bushes by the roadside.","She thought that as long as they could evade capture tonight, the government officials would give up their search in their haste to continue their journey. At that point, Xie Lin, this little brat, would be of no use, and she could just send him straight to the afterlife, sparing him the suffering of being with that group of criminals...","Little did she know that as Li Rou'er crouched in the bushes lost in her own thoughts, she heard footsteps not far away.","She immediately became alert and pulled Xie Lin forcefully in front of her.","Li Rou'er found a sharp stone from somewhere and pressed it against Xie Lin's neck.","If she were discovered, she would use Xie Lin's life as leverage, which would surely give her a chance to escape.","Mo Jiuye possessed exceptional martial arts skills and heightened perceptiveness.","As he passed by the patch of bushes, he halted his steps and sharply gazed in the direction where Li Rou'er was hiding.","By now, the eastern sky had begun to show a hint of pale light.","He clearly noticed something unusual in the bushes.","It was precisely a corner of Xie Lin's clothing.","\"Li Rou'er, what's the big deal about using a child as leverage?\" He Zhiran mercilessly exposed Li Rou'er's intentions.","This revelation not only surprised Li Rou'er, but she also knew deep down that she couldn't hide anymore.","In order to successfully escape, she struggled to suppress the anger she felt towards He Zhiran.","\"Zhiran, I know that I've done many wrong things to you these past few days. It's because I couldn't accept the fact that I was exiled. Now I realize my mistakes. Considering our sisterhood, can you forgive me?\"","\"It's impossible.\" Before He Zhiran could respond, Mo Jiuye coldly rejected Li Rou'er's plea.","In his heart, Li Rou'er's actions towards He Zhiran were simply unforgivable. He didn't care about their past sisterly bond.","For someone like her, letting her go would be like releasing a tiger back into the mountains, guaranteeing future troubles.","The reason Mo Jiuye preemptively answered was because he was worried that He Zhiran might soften her heart.","If these words had come from He Zhiran, Li Rou'er might have found them more acceptable.","After all, in these past few days, their conflict had escalated to the point of no return."]},{"number":64,"title":"Chapter 64: How easy it is to die like this.","paragraphs":["However, when those words came out of Mo Jiuye's mouth, Li Rou'er found it difficult to accept for a moment.","This was the man she had once liked. How could he say such things?","\"Mo Jiuye, do you know how much this woman didn't want to marry you?","She was worried that marrying into the Mo Family would turn her into a widow like your eight sisters-in-law. She didn't hesitate to come to me for strategies to annul the marriage.","Also, she has always been selfish and irresponsible. Such a woman doesn't deserve your protection.\"","Although Mo Jiuye hadn't spent much time with He Zhiran, he already had some understanding of her character and how she treated the Mo Family.","\"As Mo Jiuye's woman, it is only natural for me to protect her even at the cost of my life. It has nothing to do with you.\"","Li Rou'er was completely provoked by Mo Jiuye's words.","She slowly stood up, pressing the pointed part of the stone against Xie Lin's neck.","Her still swollen face looked even more ferocious.","\"Since that's the case, I don't intend to waste any more words. I'll give you two choices.","First, let me leave. Once I'm in a safe place, I will spare this kid's life. Second...\"","\"No need to say it. We will never let you leave,\" He Zhiran coldly interrupted Li Rou'er.","At that moment, several government officials arrived at the scene.","Seeing Li Rou'er holding Xie Lin hostage, they reprimanded her.","\"Li Rou'er, do you know what awaits a fugitive?\"","Li Rou'er no longer felt any fear in her heart at this moment. She realized clearly that if she couldn't escape successfully today, she would only face death.","\"Hahaha... I don't care what awaits me. I haven't committed any crimes. Why should I endure all this?\"","As she spoke, she forcefully scraped the pointed part of the stone against Xie Lin's neck.","Blood flowed down Xie Lin's collar.","Xie Lin was still just a child. Feeling the pain, he instinctively struggled.","However, the more he struggled, the harder it was for Li Rou'er to control her strength, causing his wound to grow larger and larger.","At the same time, Li Rou'er, holding Xie Lin, was gradually retreating.","Seeing this, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye disregarded the presence of the government officials. They both raised their arms and shot two hidden arrows toward Li Rou'er's forehead.","In the blink of an eye, Li Rou'er's forehead was pierced by the two feathers, and she fell backward instantly.","With his swift lightness skill, Mo Jiuye swiftly caught the little guy and then turned around to carry him away.","Back at their original positions, Zhang Qing stepped forward to remove whatever was stuffed in Xie Lin's mouth.","But when he saw what he had in his hand, he immediately became repulsed.","\"Where did Li Rou'er find this stinky sock? It's making me sick...\"","The Eighth Old Zhou felt that the smell was somewhat familiar. He then looked down at his own foot, which was not wearing a sock.","\"This seems to be my sock.\"","\"Ugh...\" Zhang Qing couldn't control his urge to vomit anymore.","\"Cough, cough, cough... Zhou Lao Ba, your socks are definitely poisonous...\" Zhang Qing coughed while venting her dissatisfaction.","Having her stinky socks exposed, especially in front of He Zhiran, Zhou Lao Ba felt a deep sense of embarrassment.","Fortunately, everyone's attention was not focused on Zhou Lao Ba at the moment.","Looking at Xie Lin's flushed face, He Zhiran couldn't determine whether it was due to difficulty in breathing or the stench of the socks.","Regardless, the child was definitely not feeling well.","Moreover, there was a wound on his neck caused by a stone scratch. Although it didn't look too serious, it needed to be treated promptly.","So, He Zhiran quickly untied the hemp rope binding Xie Lin's hands and feet, then took out a water pouch from her waist and fed him some water.","\"Officials, we have found the person. Let's hurry back!\" she said.","In front of so many people, she couldn't use spatial items to help Xie Lin with his wound.","Besides, they had already promised Peng Wang that they would return before dawn, regardless of whether they found the person or not.","With this in mind, He Zhiran didn't want to stay for even a moment. She picked up Xie Lin and started walking back.","Mo Jiuye and Zhou Lao Ba almost simultaneously rushed over, intending to take Xie Lin from He Zhiran's arms.","Zhou Lao Ba was a beat slower than Mo Jiuye, and Xie Lin had already been embraced by Mo Jiuye.","Then, without looking back, he continued walking side by side with He Zhiran.","Watching the beautiful couple ahead, singing and accompanying each other, Zhou Lao Ba intentionally slowed down his pace and refrained from disturbing them.","However, the inexplicable sense of loss in his heart was known only to himself.","Leaving two officials to handle Li Rou'er's body, the rest of the people hurried back to the camp.","Throughout the journey, He Zhiran thought about how Li Rou'er, such a malicious woman, had died. It was really letting her off easy.","But it was also good, sparing herself from unnecessary trouble. It could be considered as avenging the original owner of the body.","The group quickly returned to the camp.","Seeing Xie Lin being carried back by Mo Jiuye, the Xie family members crowded around.","When Xie Lin saw his relatives, tears welled up in his eyes again, and he reached out his little hand towards Lv, wanting to be held.","Lv, crying, approached and reached out her hand to take Xie Lin.","Just as she was about to inquire about what had happened, Lv turned her head and happened to see the wound on Xie Lin's neck.","\"Lin'er, how did you get hurt? Quickly tell Mother, who hurt you... sob, sob, sob... my poor child,\" Lv exclaimed in shock.","Upon hearing Lv's exclamation, all the Xie family members ran to check on Xie Lin's condition.","He Zhiran pushed through the crowd and said, \"Everyone, don't worry. I have some medical supplies with me. Give the child to me, and I'll take care of his wound.\"","Upon hearing this, Lv couldn't care about other things. She grabbed He Zhiran's arm and was about to leave.","\"He Zhiran, let me go with you,\" Lv said.","He Zhiran planned to use the spatial items to treat Xie Lin's injuries. How could she let an outsider come along?","She spoke softly, \"The space inside the tent is small, and it will be crowded for the three of us. Besides, treating external wounds won't take much time. I will return Xie Lin to you soon.\"","After hearing He Zhiran's words, Lv also found them reasonable.","She cautiously handed Xie Lin over to He Zhiran.","\"Then I'll trouble you,\" she said.","\"No trouble at all,\" he replied.","He Zhiran took Xie Lin back to his own tent.","Xie Lin had always been a well-behaved and sensible child. Despite being frightened by Li Rou'er, he didn't cry or make a scene in front of his family.","Furthermore, he understood that Aunt He was treating his wounds, so even though it hurt, he didn't cry and endured the pain.","With Xie Lin facing away, He Zhiran quickly tended to his wounds and bandaged them.","When she came out of the tent with Xie Lin, Zhang Qing had already recounted the incident to everyone.","Upon hearing that Li Rou'er had kidnapped Xie Lin and escaped, Li Liang was so angry that he nearly fainted.","He slapped Zhu in the face and angrily reprimanded her, \"It's all because of you! You can't even keep an eye on a person and let her escape.\"","After learning that Li Rou'er had been killed by Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran working together, Zhu had been crying non-stop, even contemplating following her.","Despite being slapped by Li Liang, she remained indifferent, shedding tears without any reaction."]},{"number":65,"title":"Chapter 65: The More Guilty","paragraphs":["Li Liang saw her like this and became even angrier. He kicked at her, \"Don't cry. Having given birth to a daughter like that, what face do you have to cry?\"","Zhu seemed to have been kicked awake. She casually wiped away a tear, got up, and unexpectedly threw herself towards He Zhiran's direction.","\"He family, give me back my Rou'er's life!\"","Mo Jiuye and The Eighth Old Zhou saw He Zhiran was in danger and both moved to stop Zhu at the same time.","Only to see The Eighth Old Zhou fiercely whip Zhu's body while Mo Jiuye kicked her, sending her flying several meters away.","Zhu heavily fell to the ground, stirring up dust. A mouthful of bright blood sprayed from her mouth.","It was clear how heavily she fell from the kick...","None of the Li family members went forward to help Zhu up as they saw her miserable state.","Zhu covered her lower abdomen, loudly gasping for breath.","Only to see her painfully get up again. This time, she did not attack He Zhiran again. Instead, she used all her strength to run towards the riverbank.","Peng Wang yelled, \"The criminal is trying to jump into the river, stop her!\"","Several officers quickly ran over. Just as Zhu had one foot over the river, she was pulled back up.","Zhu failed to jump into the river and instantly went mad.","\"Let me go, let me go find my Rou'er!\"","As she spoke, she bit at the officer who was grabbing her collar.","The officer felt pain and instinctively let go of her. Only to kick her heavily once he came to his senses, kicking her until she fell back down.","Zhu already had internal injuries from Mo Jiuye's kick. Falling down again now, she lost consciousness.","The officers called for the Li family members to carry Zhu back.","For now, the farce came to a temporary end. Peng Wang immediately made a decision.","Prisoners escaping was no small matter. All family members' crimes will be increased by one level.","As for the specifics, he and these officers had no authority.","Especially since the Li family's property confiscation and exile was personally decreed by the Emperor. Li Rou'er's crime was equivalent to deceiving the ruler.","With such a big matter, Peng Wang did not dare to delay. He immediately sent The Eighth Old Zhou along with four officers to escort all of the Li family members back to the capital for retrial.","Upon hearing Peng Wang's decision, the Li family members instantly became spiritless.","Especially Li Liang. Having mingled in court for over a decade, how could he not understand that escapees during exile would have their crimes increased by one level?","By being brought back to the capital this time, even if their entire clan is not beheaded, they would likely face life imprisonment charges.","Thinking of this, Li Liang's legs turned soft.","He stumbled to Peng Wang and kneeled on the ground with a thud.","\"Official, please show mercy and spare my family this once. I beg you...I beg you...\"","With such a big matter, how could Peng Wang possibly let his heart soften just because Li Liang kowtowed to him several times?","\"Come, pull Li Liang away. Pack up and set off immediately.\"","As soon as he finished speaking, several officers came over and roughly pulled Li Liang back to his original spot.","Peng Wang loudly ordered the frightened Li family members, \"Get up, I'm sending all of you back to the capital.\"","Li Liang was forcibly taken back, disheartened.","He clearly knew in his heart that the Li family was thoroughly finished this time...","The Eighth Old Zhou and the other officers were ready. Seeing the Li family members hesitate to move, they took out their whips from their waists and swung them around.","The Li family feared returning to the capital city but feared the officers' whips even more.","In order to avoid physical suffering, they could only obediently follow them back to the capital.","Luckily, with their starts and stops these past few days, they did not make it very far.","As long as they do not delay the journey, The Eighth Old Zhou and the others would be able to turn back in four to five days.","Peng Wang simply ordered everyone to wait here until The Eighth Old Zhou and the others came back before continuing on.","Seeing the outcome of the Li family, everyone sighed.","It seemed that escape plans really could not be made. Not only would it implicate their families but there would not even be a way out.","Li Rou'er was a prime example. She died but that was not enough, she also dragged that entire family down with her...","By the time the Li family members disappeared from everyone's line of vision, the sky had completely brightened.","When He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye returned to their own campsite, their sisters-in-law had already started preparing breakfast.","This body had not been physically trained much by the original owner so it was rather frail. He Zhiran now panted heavily, feeling extremely fatigued. Even if she wanted to help her sisters-in-law, she likely did not have enough strength.","Old Lady Mo saw her state and quickly said, \"He Shi already worked hard searching for Xie Lixin. For breakfast, there is no need for you to do anything to help. Let your sisters-in-law take care of things.","From now on, we will have to depend on ourselves for food and clothing. Let them train more.\"","He Zhiran also did not force herself, \"Then I will listen to mother. I'll rest a bit, I really am quite tired.\"","As she spoke, she had already lifted her fists and rhythmically punched her shoulders.","Mo Jiuye saw this and walked over to ask, \"Do you need help?\"","Right now, He Zhiran truly needed a massage.","\"Do you know how to massage?\"","Mo Jiuye instinctively looked down at his own hands.","\"I can try.\"","Old Lady Mo quickly spoke on her son's behalf.","\"Our Jiuye is best at massaging. His father was often away at war, leaving his body full of problems. Jiuye has learned to massage his father since he was young. Other than using a bit more strength, it is quite good.\"","He Zhiran raised her brow in disbelief towards Mo Jiuye, \"I did not expect that you had this skill.\"","Mo Jiuye was teased by his wife and his face reddened slightly.","To prevent her from noticing anything strange, he had already lowered his head and arrived behind He Zhiran.","His sharp and long hands were placed on her shoulders, very skillfully kneading them.","After only a few kneads, Mo Jiuye could not help but sigh.","\"Eat more in the future, you're too skinny. It's just bones. I don't even dare to use much strength.\"","\"Where am I skinny? I think this is good.\"","For the original owner's figure, He Zhiran was quite satisfied.","Although she looked rather thin overall, the parts that should be full were plentiful.","This kind of figure would have been envied by everyone in her previous world.","\"Still too thin.\" Mo Jiuye continued to think so.","He Zhiran was about to retort when she saw Peng Wang come over with Zhang Qing.","Seeing Mo Jiuye massaging He Zhiran, Peng Wang's heart stirred to tease them.","\"Yo...you little couple are quite harmonious.\"","At his words, Mo Jiuye's face instantly reddened.","He wanted to stop the massage and continue after these people left. However, seeing He Zhiran's enjoyment, he could not bear stopping.","Thus, his hands continued to stay on her shoulders without moving for the moment.","He Zhiran did not feel like there was anything wrong about this. Furthermore, she did not see that Mo Jiuye was embarrassed.","\"It was feeling good, don't stop!\"","Only then did Mo Jiuye react. His face red as he continued to serve his wife.","He Zhiran once again felt her body relax in comfort. Only then did she look at Peng Wang.","\"Official Peng, did you come over for something?\"","\"Mm. I just led people to bring all those wolves back. Right on fifty. I was thinking that most of these wolves were killed by you two. So I came to ask what you plan on doing with them.\""]},{"number":66,"title":"Chapter 66: Handling the Wolf","paragraphs":["He Zhiran had a sudden realization. If Peng Wang hadn't mentioned it, she would have almost forgotten about killing the wolves last night.","Hearing Peng Wang ask her how she handled it, He Zhiran didn't get carried away and forget her current identity.","Peng Wang is a decent official who considered their wishes.","If it was one of those unscrupulous officials, they wouldn't care who killed the wolves. They would just take them into town to exchange them for silver. Wouldn't that be great for them?","Therefore, He Zhiran did not overstep. Instead, she asked back, \"What does Officer Peng plan to do?\"","Peng Wang spread his hands and told the truth.","\"If this was in the past, after killing so many wolves, I wouldn't have considered whose credit it was. I would have directly taken them into town to exchange them for silver.\"","Hearing this, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye felt it was honest enough.","Frankly, they were just exiled criminals under these officials, surviving on their mercy. For Peng Wang to say this to them meant he no longer saw them as criminals.","This kind of person was definitely worth befriending.","In fact, when Peng Wang asked this question, He Zhiran already had a plan in mind.","Now that she understood Peng Wang's thoughts, she no longer held back.","\"Officer Peng, even if you take the wolves into town to exchange for money, you probably wouldn't get much, right?\"","Peng Wang nodded. \"Last year, we killed two wild wolves on the road. We took them into town and got one or two taels of silver each.\"","He Zhiran raised her eyebrows. \"You took the wolves to a fur shop?\"","\"Yeah. The fur shop owner said no one eats wolf meat so he only bought them for the fur price.\"","Actually, Peng Wang felt one or two taels per wolf was pretty good. After all, it was free money and he wouldn't complain about less.","Moreover, they had killed so many wolves last night. At one or two taels each, they could still get fifty taels!","He discussed it partly out of respect for the two of them, and partly thinking that if they agreed to his proposal, he could ask them to split the silver later.","However, judging by He Zhiran's attitude, she didn't seem to approve of taking the wolves to the fur shop to exchange for silver.","\"If I can make these wolves more valuable, would Officer Peng be willing?\"","\"Why would I not be willing?\" Peng Wang answered without thinking.","Getting an affirmative answer, He Zhiran instantly became spirited.","The comfortable massage would have to wait. She stood up abruptly.","\"Let's go process the wolves now.\"","Mo Jiuye was also curious how He Zhiran would make the wolves more profitable.","So he followed along.","He Zhiran called over the Xie Family and Fang Family men.","Then she looked at Peng Wang, \"First Officer Peng, we need to skin these wolves.\"","Hearing this, Peng Wang had already guessed He Zhiran's plan. She would just sell the wolf pelts separately. A pelt could still sell for one tael.","But the wolf meat was worthless. Where would the extra profit she mentioned come from?","Even if he didn't understand, he still chose to support He Zhiran. He wanted to see how this woman would turn the useless wolf meat into treasure.","He ordered the officials to take out their daggers and hand them over to He Zhiran.","He Zhiran casually picked up a dagger and nimbly started skinning a wolf by the hind legs.","Seeing this, Mo Jiuye also picked up a dagger to help.","The Xie and Fang men followed their example and started working.","He Zhiran reminded them to be careful not to damage the pelts, or they would sell for less silver.","The bolder women also came over to help. By breakfast time, they had skinned twenty wolf pelts.","With the Li family sent back to the capital for reassignment, the He family stood out even more among the exiles.","As they ate their black sesame buns, the He family looked with envy at the others busily working together, even regretting opposing the Mo family earlier.","Now they were stuck gnawing on those choking black buns, and completely ostracized...","Indeed, the Mo, Fang and Xie families were used to such stares and simply ignored the He family, not even glancing at them.","The officials had no choice but to look at the He family, especially cautious after what happened with Li Rou'er, making sure to check they were all present whenever they looked over.","In contrast to the He family, the treatment of the other three families was completely different. Although their meals could not compare to their former luxury, they were very content to eat this well on the exile journey.","Seeing the harmonious relations between the other families and officials, and even enjoying fragrant meals, the He family's eyes burned with envy.","But everyone was used to such stares and directly chose to ignore them.","After breakfast, seeing that those people could now independently skin the wolf pelts, He Zhiran left them to it and went to get busy with something else.","She called the women over and they cut the wolf meat into thumb-thick strips, then secretly took out some seasoning from her space and started marinating it.","While marinating the meat, the other women continued cutting it up. He Zhiran took Mo Jiuye to the riverbank.","If she remembered correctly, when she was filling up the waterskins by the river yesterday, she saw a very thin slab of bluestone there.","Dragged by his wife to the riverside, Mo Jiuye was still confused.","He wondered if she still wanted him to massage her, but didn't dare with so many people around, so brought him somewhere more secluded?","Just as Mo Jiuye was figuring this out, thinking that this time he would definitely put in more effort to massage his wife, he saw He Zhiran point to a bluestone slab on the riverbank and say:","\"Let's take this slab into the river to wash it, then use it to dry jerk the meat.\"","Wash the slab?","Jerk meat?","For a moment, Mo Jiuye's thoughts couldn't keep up.","Seeing He Zhiran had already moved to lift up one side of the slab, Mo Jiuye finally understood.","He pulled He Zhiran aside without another thought, then exerted his strength and shifted the slab to the riverbank.","He Zhiran tore off some tough grass and deftly squatted by the river scrubbing the bluestone slab.","No choice, they had to make do in this special period.","Mo Jiuye followed her example, helping to scrub."]},{"number":67,"title":"Chapter 67: Our Majestic Duke is Henpecked.","paragraphs":["Before long, the two had scrubbed the bluestone slabs clean and propped them up on the spot.","By this time, the first batch of cured wolf meat was just about ready. He Zhiran brushed some oil on the bluestone slabs and neatly arranged the wolf meat on top.","Mo Jiuye was squatting to one side, adding firewood under the slabs.","The husband and wife worked together seamlessly. Before long, the tempting aroma began to drift through the air, making everyone's mouths water.","Peng Wang came running over, following his nose.","He Zhiran picked up a piece of roasted dried wolf meat and gave it to him.","\"Master Peng, try this and tell me if dried meat that tastes this good can fetch a good price.\"","Peng Wang couldn't wait to pop the dried meat into his mouth and chewed it carefully.","\"Tender and delicious, rich wolf flavor, this is the first time I've had such chewy meat. It's a rare delicacy.\"","This was Peng Wang's heartfelt evaluation.","He Zhiran was delighted that the first batch of dried meat had been approved. She happily picked up a piece and stuffed it into Mo Jiuye's mouth.","\"Husband, you try it too.\"","In an unintentional move, her fingertips gently brushed Mo Jiuye's lips.","Mo Jiuye shuddered slightly, feeling his heartbeat quicken by half a beat.","Unconsciously, he touched the place He Zhiran had brushed, not knowing why he suddenly felt elated.","To cover up the awkwardness, Mo Jiuye chewed the dried meat seriously.","Soon, He Zhiran’s sweet voice rang in his ears again.","\"Husband, is the dried meat tasty?\"","\"Yes, very tasty.\" At this moment Mo Jiuye's mind wasn't on the dried meat at all, unable to carefully evaluate it like Peng Wang. But it really was very tasty.","He Zhiran didn't look at Mo Jiuye's expression. She thought his simple answer was just his cold personality, and didn't think too much of it.","She looked at Peng Wang again: \"Master Peng, do you still think this is worthless wolf meat?\"","\"No, absolutely not. This dried meat will definitely fetch a good price in the city.\"","Peng Wang seemed to see countless coins raining down on him already.","\"Good. Let's dry all the wolf meat into dried meat this way and take it into the city to sell.","Also, while the sunshine is good, dry those wolf hides too. If handled properly, I guess we can sell them for some extra silver.\"","Hearing He Zhiran speak knowledgeably, Peng Wang admired her even more.","He really didn't know how much this woman had stuffed into her little head to have so many ideas.","\"We'll do as you say.\"","Peng Wang simply lingered here instead of leaving. This tasty dried meat, he had to have his fill first.","After all there was so much wolf meat, he eating a little wouldn’t matter...","As Peng Wang ate, he seemed to remember something. He turned and ran off.","Soon he returned, tenderly cradling a gourd of wine.","He uncorked the wine, but instead of drinking it himself, he offered it to Mo Jiuye.","\"How can you have such delicious dried meat without wine? You drink first.\"","In the army, Mo Jiuye often ate meat and drank wine in large mouthfuls with the officers and soldiers.","Recalling that feeling, he didn't refuse but accepted the wine gourd, just about to take a swig when He Zhiran stopped him.","\"You're still injured. No alcohol.\"","At her words, Mo Jiuye’s hand froze in mid air still holding up the wine gourd.","But soon he returned the wine gourd to Peng Wang.","\"My wife is right, I'm injured and shouldn't drink.\"","Peng Wang looked at them with some amusement, and meaningfully teased:","\"I didn't expect our prestigious Duke to be so afraid of his wife.\"","Of course Mo Jiuye knew Peng Wang was joking, but he still said seriously: \"Be careful with your words, sir. I'm just an exiled convict now, no longer any Duke.\"","Peng Wang also realized his words were inconsiderate.","\"In that case, I won't call you Duke, and you needn't call me Sir either. If you don't mind, just call me Brother Peng.\"","Mo Jiuye wasn't fussy. And he quite approved of Peng Wang's character.","\"Brother Peng.\"","Peng Wang took a big gulp of wine and guffawed. \"Ha ha ha... Good. From now on you're my brother Mo, and Lady He is my sister-in-law.\"","Having a closer relationship with the captain of the guards was something He Zhiran had been hoping for.","She roasted the dried meat even more enthusiastically.","Following the alluring aroma, the sisters-in-law and Mo Hengyue soon arrived too. He Zhiran busily invited them to try the dried meat.","They simply couldn't stop eating after one taste.","It was so delicious, not just on the road in exile, even back in the capital they had never eaten anything so flavorful.","The sisters-in-law felt bad that He Zhiran was working so hard. After carefully learning her dried meat roasting technique, they took over for her.","He Zhiran stretched lazily, then brought some roasted dried meat for everyone else to try.","Whoever tasted the delicious dried meat sang its praises.","In her delight, He Zhiran simply declared unlimited rations of dried meat for today.","By nightfall, due to limited tools, only a third of the meat had been dried.","Mrs. Zhao was worried the wolf meat would spoil if left too long, and volunteered her women to work through the night.","Mistress Xie also said the Fang family would rest tomorrow morning and they would continue work.","At this rate all the dried meat could be done by tomorrow nightfall.","The weather was muggy this season. To prevent spoilage of the curing wolf meat, He Zhiran led people to move it riverside.","The temperature there was relatively lower, better for preservation.","After a busy day, they could finally rest.","After washing up, He Zhiran returned to the tent.","Mo Jiuye said caringly, \"Rest early. You worked the hardest today.\"","He Zhiran thought Mo Jiuye would say something more, but he didn't.","Since he didn't bring it up, she would.","\"The Lis will probably reach the capital tomorrow.\"","\"Mm. When they reach the capital, news of the person who died in the hut will quickly reach my enemies.\" Mo Jiuye's tone was extremely indifferent, as if the matter had nothing to do with him.","He Zhiran didn't understand his attitude.","\"Aren't you worried they'll send someone after us again?\"","\"It's not something we can prevent.\" If he hadn't been busy with He Zhiran all day, Mo Jiuye would have likely spent the whole day pondering this issue.","But he didn't want her bothered over it too, which was why he deliberately acted so indifferent.","Given their current situation, with things like this all they could do was passively take the beating and counter when possible.","Taking the initiative to attack would not be so easy.","They couldn't even catch the ringleader.","With Li Rou’er dead, peace had returned for all of two days before having to worry about enemies striking again.","But He Zhiran was never afraid of such things.","Just some invisible troubles? Let them come!"]},{"number":68,"title":"Chapter 68: The Rich Woman with Four Million","paragraphs":["Moreover, what Mo Jiuye said also made sense. The enemy was hiding while they were exposed, so it was indeed difficult to prevent attacks. All they could do was stay vigilant at all times and adapt to changes.","To give Mo Jiuye more tools for self-defense, He Zhiran did not take back the mini sleeve arrows used to kill the wolf pack. Instead, she bought another set of arrows for him.","\"This is for you. It may come in handy at critical moments.\"","Ever since getting the sleeve arrows, Mo Jiuye had grown deeply fond of this exquisite little weapon.","He looked deeply at He Zhiran. \"Thank you.\"","This thing was simply a life-saver for Mo Jiuye now.","No one knew what troubles might lie ahead. Having a weapon in hand would at least allow him to cope for a while.","He Zhiran was worried Mo Jiuye would ask about the origins of her mini sleeve arrows. To avoid the topic, she simply rolled over with her back facing him.","\"I'm tired. Let's rest early.\"","Mo Jiuye did have such questions in mind, but he did not have the urge to get to the bottom of it. After all, this was not the first time he had seen He Zhiran use such advanced weapons...","He Zhiran really was tired. She had originally planned to check the sales in the online store, but she could no longer resist the sudden drowsiness and had to listen to her body's desire to visit the god of dreams.","...","Sure enough, as expected, before nightfall the next day, with the hard work of the women, all the wolf jerky was roasted.","Peng Wang immediately decided to leave some for everyone to eat and take the rest into the nearby town to exchange for money tomorrow morning.","He Zhiran was thinking that later she would discuss with Peng Wang and ask for permission to go into town with him tomorrow as well, in order to purchase more supplies.","But before she could even open her mouth, Peng Wang took the initiative to come over.","\"Sister, if you and Brother Mo are willing tomorrow when going into town, you can come along.\"","He knew He Zhiran's family had given her quite a bit of silver when sending her off.","With silver in hand, purchasing more supplies was understandable.","\"Sure, I'll go with you tomorrow and buy some supplies to bring back,\" He Zhiran responded with a smile. She had been hoping for this, and now it just fell right into her lap without even needing to ask.","Mo Jiuye also wanted to go into town with He Zhiran, but he worried that assassins from Beijing might choose this moment to attack, and the defenseless women back home would be in danger.","\"I still have injuries, so I won't go along.\"","Peng Wang didn't think too much of it and assumed Mo Jiuye was telling the truth.","\"Then it's decided. The town is quite far. We'll set off before dawn tomorrow.\"","After seeing Peng Wang off, lying in the tent, He Zhiran entered her space with her consciousness.","She wanted to check the sales figures of the store. It had been two days already. There should be some profit now, right?","With this thought, He Zhiran tapped open her phone screen. She saw that all the merchandise in the store had been sold out, and her account had been credited 4.25 million Yuan.","The pleasant surprise came so suddenly that she was somewhat overwhelmed.","To verify that this wasn't a dream, He Zhiran subconsciously pinched her own leg.","The pain reminded her that this was all real.","She had assumed that with such expensive antiques, selling a few items in a year would be good, but she did not expect that in just two days, all 19 items were sold out.","He Zhiran curiously clicked into the records, intending to check the sale times of the merchandise.","As it turned out, all the items in the store had been purchased by someone named \"Little Collector\", including that first silver hairpin sold on the opening day...","This explained one thing: on the first day Little Collector bought that lowest priced silver hairpin to first verify the authenticity of the merchandise.","After confirming that the silver hairpin was indeed an antique, Little Collector decided to invest heavily in purchasing the rest.","Not only that, Little Collector left reviews for all sold merchandise. The content was mostly that the prices were low and the items were definitely genuine, even asking the seller to add more new inventory.","This made He Zhiran very grateful. Her shop had just opened, and such reviews were helpful references for potential new customers.","Over 4 million was by no means a small amount for He Zhiran.","Although she did not yet know how to spend this money, who would complain about having too much money?","Moreover, her space contained many items taken from the imperial treasury. Although they looked valuable, to He Zhiran they were just taking up space.","Ordinary items were still okay - she could casually take them to a pawn shop to exchange for silver and have tangible cash in hand.","However, all these items came from the imperial treasury. Just showing them would surely reveal clues for people to investigate her and Mo Jiuye; that would end up being a pyrrhic victory.","Now things were perfect: she could leisurely list these antiques for sale on Taobao Mall without any risk. Not only would this free up some space in her medical room, she would also gain considerable income.","Although she didn't currently need this money, the road ahead was still long and who knew when she might have such needs.","If she really ended up not needing the money, she could also find a way to donate it to charity to help those in need.","In short, the successful merchandise sales were an enormously good thing for He Zhiran, no matter how she looked at it.","He Zhiran still understood the principle of striking while the iron was hot. She used her mind to select dozens more items from her space, took pictures, priced them, and uploaded them to the mall.","The fledgling female tycoon who now possessed over 4 million Yuan finally fell asleep contentedly after three days.","The next day, before dawn even broke, He Zhiran got up as promised and set off for the town with Peng Wang and another official.","After being made into jerky, the wolf meat did not take up much space. All that could be seen piled high like a small mountain on the wooden cart were wolf hides.","The wolf hides were piled so high that the official pushing the cart could not even see the road. Peng Wang had no choice but to walk in front to lead the way.","For ease of travel, Peng Wang and the official had found some ordinary peasant clothes from somewhere and put them on.","Seen from afar, the three of them looked just like ordinary country hunters going into town to sell their game.","Finally, a little after morning on the hour of Chen, they arrived at Pingyuan County.","Perhaps due to its large population, it looked slightly livelier than Yunlai County.","The important purpose of this trip was to sell the wolf hides and jerky. Peng Wang directly led them to the only fur shop here.","After examining the wolf hides, the shopkeeper did indeed offer one tael of silver per hide as Peng Wang had said.","Just as Peng Wang was about to readily agree, He Zhiran stepped forward.","\"Shopkeeper, these hides have been processed and dried. How can you offer the same price as for whole wolves brought in?\"","The shopkeeper saw that the speaker was a young woman and simply dismissed her words outright.","\"Little lady doesn't understand the business. Hides are worth the least this season. I'm offering one tael of silver per hide because they've been processed.\"","Upon hearing this, He Zhiran calmly asked, \"So by the shopkeeper's words, when are hides worth more money?\""]},{"number":69,"title":"Chapter 69: Sold out","paragraphs":["He Zhiran looked at Peng Wang.","\"Brother Peng, anyway these skins won't spoil until winter comes, so we might as well sell them when winter arrives.\"","Peng Wang was very cooperative in his reply: \"Alright, whatever my younger sister says.\"","As he spoke, he gestured at the clerks to leave with him.","Seeing that the deal was about to slip away, the shopkeeper immediately put on a smiling face to block their way.","\"Gentlemen, don't rush to leave. Let's discuss this further.\"","\"There's nothing more to discuss. We worked hard to get so many wolf skins, of course we'll wait to sell them when prices are highest.\"","As Peng Wang saw the shopkeeper come to obstruct them, he was gleeful inside but still pretended that he wanted to leave.","The anxious shopkeeper directly shouted: \"How about this - I'll pay an extra 100 wen per skin. That's very high already!\"","He Zhiran turned her head and held out a palm to the shopkeeper.","\"Pay an extra 500 wen and you have a deal.\"","\"500 wen is too much. Even in winter, wolf fur isn't worth that much,\" the shopkeeper was nearly in tears. With an extra 500 wen, his profits would be halved.","\"Then forget it. We're going to the capital in a few days anyway, and can definitely get a good price for them there,\" He Zhiran said, and prepared to leave.","Now the shopkeeper was truly anxious.","\"Fine, one and a half taels of silver per skin. I'll buy all the wolf fur.\"","Although his profit margin had decreased, it was still better than making no profit.","Peng Wang was impressed that He Zhiran had negotiated an extra 25 taels worth of silver with just a few sentences.","He secretly gave her a thumbs up.","The wolf skins were quickly unloaded from the wooden cart, revealing dried wolf meat packed in several large iron pots.","Curious, the shopkeeper asked: \"Brothers, what is this?\"","Having earned extra money, Peng Wang was in a good mood and generously handed him a piece of dried meat.","\"Boss, have a taste. This is dried wolf meat.\"","\"Dried wolf meat?\" The shopkeeper had been in business for many years, but this was the first time he had heard of such a thing.","He took the dried meat from Peng Wang and cautiously bit off a piece.","And he simply could not stop eating after that first bite.","\"Delicious, chewy, and more fragrant the more you chew...\"","On the way here, He Zhiran had suggested that with so much dried meat, it would be impossible for them to retail it bit by bit at the marketplace. It would be best to find a teahouse or restaurant and negotiate for them to purchase the whole batch.","Therefore, even as the shopkeeper of the fur shop continuously praised how tasty it was, they had no intention of selling him some. Seeing how much he liked it, Peng Wang generously gave him a few more pieces.","After receiving the silver, Peng Wang was about to leave with his men, but as soon as he turned around, the shopkeeper chased him out.","\"Gentlemen, please wait!\"","Peng Wang looked back: \"Something else?\"","The shopkeeper came up to them, grinning from ear to ear.","\"Brothers, might this dried wolf meat be for sale?\"","\"Of course it's for sale, but we won't be selling it in small amounts,\" Peng Wang replied.","He had just finished speaking when a man looking about thirty years old, wearing silk brocade robes, walked out of the shop.","The man was waving a fan, believing himself to have elegant demeanor as he approached them.","\"Cui is my unworthy name. In three days I will be hosting a poetry gathering, where scholarly gentlemen from the surrounding counties will be in attendance. I noticed this dried wolf meat and thought it would make for a fine snack. If possible, I would like to purchase some.\"","Peng Wang instinctively looked to He Zhiran upon this prospect of business.","He Zhiran already knew dried wolf meat would be in demand.","\"Master Cui, we don't sell our meat in small amounts. If you would purchase the whole batch, then we can discuss pricing,\" she said.","Master Cui first glanced at the amount of dried meat on the cart before replying, \"No problem.\"","Hearing this, He Zhiran did not hesitate either and directly named her price: \"For all of this dried meat, 300 wen per jin.\"","\"300 wen per jin? Young lady, you're practically robbing us!\" The shopkeeper felt the price was unbelievable.","Not just the shopkeeper, even Peng Wang was somewhat shocked upon hearing this quote.","If not for the meat being so tasty, even if they had properly prepared this wolf meat and brought it to market, they probably couldn't have gotten much money for it.","This girl had directly opened with 300 wen.","He Zhiran's price did contain some room for negotiation - naturally this would not be a fixed price sale, and the other party would certainly bargain.","But she absolutely would not take the initiative to make concessions.","\"It takes five jin of wolf meat to make one jin of dried meat. These wolves were hunted by my family risking their lives, and go through many processing steps. I feel this price is very reasonable,\" she said.","\"Even if it's five jin of wolf meat for one jin of dried meat, it's still not worth 300 wen per jin!\" the shopkeeper retorted.","Master Cui echoed in agreement: \"Indeed, 300 wen per jin is too expensive.\"","Seeing both of them think the price was too high, Peng Wang guessed this deal was likely going south.","In a moment of anxiety, he secretly nudged He Zhiran, hinting with his eyes for her to lower the price.","But He Zhiran ignored Peng Wang and instead addressed the shopkeeper and Master Cui:","\"I presume both of you tried the meat and found the flavor satisfactory, which is why you want to buy some.\"","Seeing as neither party rebutted, He Zhiran continued,","\"The method of making dried meat is secret recipe passed down in our family. I believe you simply cannot buy meat this delicious anywhere else.","Master Cui, since you are hosting a poetry gathering, I'm certain the attendees will be prominent and influential people.","When you serve them this unique dried meat at the event, I assure you it will have an unanticipated effect.\"","He Zhiran's words had indeed struck Master Cui's heart.","After hesitating a number of times, he finally said, \"200 wen per jin. I'll take the whole batch.\"","In He Zhiran's estimation, the lowest acceptable price for the meat was 150 wen per jin. Hearing the offer of 200 wen, she was already elated internally.","However, so as not to betray her delight, He Zhiran hesitated briefly, seemingly conflicted.","Seeing her uncertainty, Master Cui spoke again,","\"I'll add another 20 wen per jin, but I can't go higher.\"","He Zhiran put on a look of indecision, turning to face Peng Wang as if unable to make up her mind.","\"Big brother Peng, can we agree to this price?\"","Peng Wang played along very cooperatively, making a pained expression as he said, \"220 wen per jin it is then! If this sells our dried meat, we can return home that much sooner.\"","Only then did He Zhiran reluctantly look to Master Cui.","\"Since my elder brother has agreed, I've got no say. It's a deal for 220 wen per jin.\"","The shopkeeper called over helpers to weigh the meat.","There was a total of 168 jin of dried wolf meat, priced at 36 taels and 980 wen.","Master Cui directly gave He Zhiran 40 taels of silver.","To Peng Wang, being able to sell these unwanted wolf parts for 40 taels was like finding free money on the ground."]},{"number":70,"title":"Chapter 70: The enemy of my enemy is my Friend.","paragraphs":["After leaving the fur shop, Peng Wang gave He Zhiran another thumbs up.","\"Sister, I'm really convinced today. If it weren't for you, I could only have sold these fifty wolves for 50 taels. But now, thanks to you, I got more than double the price.\"","In fact, He Zhiran was not very knowledgeable about doing business. She was merely benefiting from Duo Huo Yi Shi's expertise and understanding some basics about haggling.","Being praised like an idol by Peng Wang, she felt a little embarrassed.","\"Big Brother Peng, please don't flatter me too much. I was just lucky.\"","\"Sister, don't be modest. I don't give compliments lightly.\"","As he spoke, Peng Wang looked at the sky.","\"We've been on the road for so long and must be hungry by now. Let's find a place to fill our stomachs first, then I'll accompany you to purchase supplies.\"","The three strolled along, looking for a place to eat.","Suddenly, a man came flying out of a book store ahead of them, his body slamming heavily onto the ground.","Then, several young men dressed as scholars walked out of the bookstore.","\"Fei Nanyu, you poor devil, how dare you call yourself a scholar?\"","\"If I see you come to the bookstore again, I'll beat you every time.\"","Fei Nanyu?","Hearing this name, He Zhiran immediately thought of someone.","Historical records stated that after Nan Qi died, Fei Nanyu held court for six years before plotting to usurp the throne.","The Fei surname was rare, and for someone to dare use the royal surname in their name, even if the characters were different, ordinary people wouldn't normally dare to do so.","Therefore, she could determine that the man before her was the famous founding emperor of the Daxing dynasty – Fei Nanyu.","He Zhiran did not know much about Fei Nanyu's past, so she was unclear about what happened before he became emperor.","Seeing the future founding emperor in such a miserable state, He Zhiran's first reaction was that for Fei Nanyu, even if they could not be friends, they must not become enemies.","If the historical records were correct, Mo Jiuye died on the third day after being exiled. The exact cause of death had always been a mystery.","Now that she had come here, on the very first day, she had already changed Mo Jiuye's fate of being severely caned 100 times by Emperor Shunwu. And now, more than three days had passed since Mo Jiuye was exiled from the capital, yet he remained alive and kicking.","This showed that she had already changed Mo Jiuye's fate twice.","The Mo family's enemies were the imperial family. To take revenge, they would inevitably stand in opposition to the imperial family.","In the future, Fei Nanyu would become Da Shun dynasty's greatest enemy.","There was a saying, the enemy of my enemy is my friend.","Therefore, He Zhiran greatly valued this opportunity to befriend Fei Nanyu.","At this moment, Fei Nanyu looked very miserable. Blood kept flowing from his broken nose. The shabby clothes he wore were also stained with traces of blood.","He raised his arm and casually wiped his face, struggling to sit up.","Just then, the two scholars had already walked over disdainfully, about to continue beating him.","At the same time, He Zhiran felt a gaze staring at them from above behind her.","She instinctively turned her head back. Behind her was a two-story tea house.","If she was not mistaken, that gaze had come from the second floor.","So He Zhiran looked towards the second floor. She saw the window there was open, but no one was inside her line of sight.","With no time to think further, seeing that Fei Nanyu was about to suffer another beating, He Zhiran dashed forward and stood in front of him.","\"I advise you two gentlemen, stop while you still can.\"","After saying just one sentence, with He Zhiran’s keen senses, she felt that gaze again.","But now was not the time for her to investigate. He Zhiran stared evenly at the scholars.","The two scholars looked at the woman blocking their way. Her clothes were covered in patches and her face was full of dirt.","The taller scholar said contemptuously, \"What beggar is this, mind your own business and scram!\"","He Zhiran still stood motionless in place, arms crossed over her chest.","\"What if I insist on interfering?\"","\"You're asking for death.\" The shorter scholar said, raising his hand to slap He Zhiran.","Since He Zhiran had already chosen to intervene, she was prepared to fight back.","Just as she was about to retaliate, Peng Wang charged forward and kicked the short scholar in the stomach.","At the same time, the guard also punched the tall scholar.","Peng Wang didn’t know why He Zhiran wanted to intervene. However, from his understanding of her, she was no rash person and must have her own reasons for doing this.","Therefore, Peng Wang chose to support her unconditionally.","Seeing his boss take action, the guard naturally could not hold back either.","The two scholars were beaten. Clutching their painful spots, they glared furiously at their opponents.","The other scholars also surrounded them, glaring at the group. But no one dared make another move.","\"You beggars have guts beating people openly on the street?\"","He Zhiran was not angry, but laughed instead. She pointed to Fei Nanyu behind her and said,","\"Weren't you guys also openly beating someone on the street? This is called getting a taste of your own medicine. Understand?\"","From the scholars' attire, they were probably sons of wealthy families who were used to being arrogant.","Even if He Zhiran was speaking the truth, they would not admit it.","\"Who saw us beating anyone? It was you who openly beat scholars before the public, yet you're slamming accusations instead!\"","Peng Wang had a fiery temper. Worried that He Zhiran would be taken advantage of by so many scholars, he strode forward and said,","\"The three of us personally witnessed you scholars beating someone on the street. If you don't believe us, let's go to the authorities right now for the county magistrate to decide!\"","He had already thought this through. After all, he himself held an eighth-rank official post. At worst, he could reveal his identity at the county office, how could he still be afraid of some unlearned scholars?","Hearing about seeing the authorities, the scholars instantly cowered.","What if the county magistrate really upheld justice for Fei Nanyu? Their hard-earned positions as tongsheng might be revoked.","\"We didn't beat anyone, why should we go to the authorities with you?\"","\"Then don't go to the authorities, but you still have to compensate his medical fees, that's a fact.\" This was He Zhiran's main goal at the moment.","From Fei Nanyu's attire, it could be inferred that he was currently destitute. What he needed most now should be money.","She could give the money herself, but it had to be done aboveboard, otherwise with Fei Nanyu's astute mind he would surely think she had ulterior motives.","Hearing that the matter could be resolved with money, and to avoid escalating the situation, the scholars could only reluctantly compromise.","\"How much compensation do you want?\"","\"There are five of you total. I think twenty taels per person should be just right.\" He Zhiran said calmly.","\"What? Twenty taels each? Fei Nanyu is not even worth it.\" The short scholar retorted first.","\"In that case, let's go to the authorities and ask the county magistrate to decide if he's worth it or not!\""]},{"number":71,"title":"Chapter 71: Emperor Shunwu Paid the Bill","paragraphs":["He Zhiran pretended to go help Fei Nanyu up, and asked, \"Are you going to come with us to the county government office on our cart?\"","Fei Nanyu glared at the students, then nodded, \"Fine, I'll trouble the young lady.\"","Seeing they were serious, one of the students quickly softened.","\"It's just twenty taels of silver per person. We agree to pay. It's a small matter, no need to disturb His Honor the county magistrate.\"","Seeing this, He Zhiran held out her hand to them.","\"Since you don't want to go to the yamen, hand over the silver!\"","The students looked at each other, then turned their backs to pool their money.","Soon, one hundred taels of silver was in front of He Zhiran and the others.","Peng Wang waved his hand dismissively at them.","The five students hurriedly scrambled away.","He Zhiran gave Fei Nanyu the hundred taels of silver.","\"Take this!\"","Although injured, the unruly pride in Fei Nanyu's eyes still could not be blocked.","\"Why did you help me? Aren't you afraid of offending them?\"","He Zhiran shrugged, seeming casual as she answered, \"I can't ignore injustice.\"","So Fei Nanyu wouldn't be suspicious, she looked away instead of meeting his eyes.","\"Can you walk?\"","\"I can.\"","Saying so, Fei Nanyu painfully got to his feet and bowed deeply to them.","\"Many thanks for assisting me. If we meet again in the future, I will certainly repay you all fully.\"","Having said this, he turned and limped away.","Only after Fei Nanyu's figure disappeared did He Zhiran gather Peng Wang and the attendant to go find food.","He Zhiran couldn't determine if her actions today saving Fei Nanyu would bring reward in the future.","But she believed that even if they didn't become friends later, having today's events as a foundation, they at least wouldn't become enemies.","While He Zhiran thought this over, Peng Wang couldn't help but asking,","\"Sister, from my understanding of you, you aren't the sort to meddle. Why save him?\"","Since she had her own selfish reasons, He Zhiran naturally wouldn't tell the truth.","\"I really hate unfair odds. I couldn't help getting involved.\"","Of course Peng Wang didn't believe her, but since she didn't want to say, he couldn't keep questioning either.","After walking about ten minutes, Peng Wang pointed to an inconspicuous stand and said,","\"Their wontons here are delicious, and their signature braised meat too. Want to try them?\"","He Zhiran was starving now. As long as it could fill her stomach, she wasn't picky about what to eat.","And from Peng Wang's tone, places he had eaten at before and still wanted to eat again probably wouldn't be bad.","\"I have no objections. Big brother Peng's arrangements stand.\"","The attendant echoed, \"Wherever boss wants to eat, we'll eat there.\"","Seeing they both didn't object, Peng Wang headed toward the wonton stand first.","They ordered three bowls of wontons and a large plate of braised meat.","After a taste, He Zhiran found the wontons and braised meat flavor actually pretty good.","Compared to the delicacies she'd eaten in her previous life though, there was still something missing.","But for the ancient era with scarce resources, making food taste this good was already quite good.","The weather itself was hot. After a steaming bowl of wontons, all three had beads of sweat on their foreheads.","Seeing the blazing sun outside, the attendant was reluctant.","\"Boss, the sun is too harsh. Should we find a place to rest first before going on?\"","Peng Wang agreed. Usually when escorting prisoners and rushing on the road, if they met the high noon sun, they would choose somewhere shaded to take a break and continue traveling in the afternoon.","\"There's a teahouse over there. We can go drink some chilled tea and rest our feet.\"","He Zhiran also wanted to drink iced tea, but she knew clearly this was the only chance she had to act alone, and couldn't miss it.","\"Big brother Peng, I'm not afraid of heat. I still want to buy some things, so why don't you two go rest while I shop, and find you at the teahouse after I'm done?\"","From the recent happenings, Peng Wang no longer saw He Zhiran as an exiled prisoner, and believed she was moral.","For such a small request, Peng Wang naturally wouldn't object, moreover since he didn't want to accompany He Zhiran shopping in the sweltering heat.","\"That works too. We'll go rest our feet while little sister goes shopping.\"","And so He Zhiran split off from the other two. She searched out another fabric shop.","Considering her family had no spare clothes to change into, smelling in this heat, when possible this issue had to be resolved.","So before going out she had planned to buy some cloth for sister-in-laws to make a few outfits over these days with no traveling.","Not far away, she saw another fabric shop.","He Zhiran didn't forget her current identity, unwilling to be too ostentatious.","She chose some thinner, more refined hemp cloth and bought a good amount.","Seeing her buy so much fabric, the owner attentively threw in some scraps.","He Zhiran wasn't skilled with feminine handicrafts and didn't know what use the scraps were, but seeing the shopkeeper present them like a treasure, they were sure to come in handy under skilled hands.","After thanking the shopkeeper, He Zhiran kept pushing the cart forward.","She planned to find a deserted place to take out some of the remaining flour and rice from her space, and check if there was any suitable food in Taobao Treasure to take back too.","Turning a corner, He Zhiran wheeled the cart into a quiet alley. After checking no one was around, her consciousness entered her space. She took out two bags each of rice and flour.","She also purchased twenty roast chicken and twenty roast duck from Taobao Treasure, changing all packaging to oil paper neatly rewrapped and loaded on the cart.","Besides these, she wanted to buy some pork and vegetables too.","Considering the sweltering weather today, He Zhiran was too lazy to keep wandering the market. She simply handled everything in Taobao Treasure instead.","Looking at the heaping cart, she felt no pressure at all in her heart.","After all, it was Emperor Shunwu footing the bill...","And that was indeed so. The four million plus that He Zhiran earned was all exchanged using Emperor Shunwu's imperial treasury, so it was him paying alright!","Seeing it had only been half an hour since parting with Peng Wang, if she went to find them at the teahouse now after buying so much stuff so quickly, it was uncertain whether they would be suspicious.","So He Zhiran was in no rush to leave either. She pushed the cart to a shaded area and sat atop an empty space.","Incidentally she bought herself an iced drink in Taobao Treasure to quench her thirst too.","Ever since crossing over, He Zhiran hadn't felt so content.","She sat atop the wooden cart, leisurely sipping icy cold drink, rocking her legs to and fro...","Just as she was a bit too complacent, she suddenly sensed footsteps coming from the alley entrance direction.","He Zhiran quickly put the remaining half glass of iced drink into her space, and looked towards the sound."]},{"number":72,"title":"Chapter 72: Once upon a Time","paragraphs":["It was Fei Nanyu!","He was limping in front holding a coffin carried by four men behind him.","When Fei Nanyu saw He Zhiran, his brows immediately furrowed as he looked her up and down carefully, as if trying to see through something.","Facing such a gaze, He Zhiran's expression remained calm.","\"What are you doing here?\"","\"I saw it was quiet here, so I took a rest and cooled off at the same time.\"","As she saw the four men carrying the coffin over, He Zhiran instinctively pushed her wheeled wooden cart to the side against the wall to make way for them.","Seeing the cart full of goods, Fei Nanyu did not doubt her.","He saluted He Zhiran with cupped fists, \"There is a funeral at home to take care of. I shall take my leave first.\"","After saying that, he left without looking back.","Seeing Fei Nanyu lead the group into the innermost courtyard, He Zhiran also got up and pushed the wheeled wooden cart away.","On the road, He Zhiran saw a large pile of straw hats displayed on a roadside stall.","For the exiled, especially these women, being roasted under the scorching sun all day long, they desperately needed hats like these.","So she bought all 28 straw hats from the stall without hesitation.","When Peng Wang saw He Zhiran return so quickly at the teahouse, he was indeed very shocked.","\"It's rare for you to go out once. Why didn't you walk around more, young lady?\"","He Zhiran looked up at the sky, \"It was too hot. There were many things on the cart and I couldn't walk any further, so I came back.\"","Peng Wang took a look at the things on the wooden cart and couldn't help but click his tongue.","It seemed that Lord He must not have stinted on giving his daughter silver. Otherwise, with her level of consumption, she would probably run out halfway through the journey.","\"Since you've bought everything, let's hurry back now.\"","With the help of the clerks pushing the wheeled wooden cart, they quickly left Pingyuan County.","Peng Wang and the clerks were used to traveling on the road, so they moved faster.","Although He Zhiran herself was tough, but the body of the original owner was too weak to keep up with the pace of the two men.","Peng Wang turned back and saw He Zhiran walking with some difficulty. He let her sit in the corner of the wheeled wooden cart to rest.","Being stuck with a weak body, He Zhiran had no choice but to admit defeat. It would probably improve after traveling on the road for a long time.","After saying thanks, she squeezed in next to the grain and sat down.","Thinking of Fei Nanyu in Pingyuan County she saw today, and the elusive gaze in the teahouse, He Zhiran felt it necessary to quickly learn about the history of this period.","So she pretended to fall asleep, leaning on the grain with a straw hat covering her head. But her consciousness had actually entered the space.","In Taobao Mall, He Zhiran bought several books about this period of history in order to understand the information more comprehensively. She even looked through \"Unofficial History\".","Her consciousness quickly browsed the table of contents of the history books, and finally found the chapter titled \"Fei Nanyu\" in the later part.","He Zhiran read it carefully—","Fei Nanyu's father was a scholar who taught him to read and write from a young age.","Fei Nanyu was extremely talented in studying. At the age of twelve, he was the top scholar. When he brought this news back home to celebrate, his mother fell seriously ill.","In order to treat his mother, the Fei family had spent almost all their money, but still couldn't save her life. Not long after, Fei's father also fell ill.","In order to support the family, Fei Nanyu gave up the path of further studying for the imperial civil service examinations. He silently took on the responsibility of making money and taking care of his father.","With his scholar status, he could have easily taught in a private school. But that way, he wouldn't have been able to take care of his disabled father.","Left with no choice, Fei Nanyu could only take on some copying work, sitting at home copying books to make money while taking care of his father at the same time.","This kind of life lasted for eight years.","When Fei Nanyu turned twenty-one, his father finally lost the battle against illness and passed away.","In order to bury his father properly, Fei Nanyu went to the bookstore where he often copied books, wanting to borrow some silver from the boss in advance.","But instead he ran into several bullies who had been jealous of Fei Nanyu's superior intelligence since childhood. Looking down on his current down and out state, they beat him violently without saying anything.","Luckily, he was saved by Third Prince Nan Qi who happened to pass by, and also lent him money to properly bury his father.","Since then, Fei Nanyu became a staff member of Nan Qi. It can be said that without Fei Nanyu's contributions, Nan Qi wouldn't have become the next emperor of the Da Shun Dynasty.","After Nan Qi ascended the throne, the person he trusted most was Fei Nanyu. He bestowed him as Prime Minister, second only to the emperor in power.","The first memorial Fei Nanyu submitted after becoming Prime Minister was to petition for the innocence of Mo Jiuye. With Nan Qi's absolute trust in him, he naturally did not object.","In the third month after Nan Qi's ascension, an imperial edict announced to the whole kingdom that Mo Jiuye was never guilty of surrendering to the enemy and betraying the country back then, but was wrongfully exiled.","For this, Nan Qi even personally built a tomb with ceremonial attire for Mo Jiuye.","It can be said that Fei Nanyu rose meteorically. However, his ambition was not satisfied with just being Prime Minister.","Before Nan Qi's death, he had already secretly started building his own power. Until it grew to a certain scale after some years, he raised troops in revolt and took over the Da Shun Dynasty by force.","Although Fei Nanyu seized power through a coup, he was a diligent ruler beloved by the people.","During Fei Nanyu's 28 year reign, the people went from starving to well-fed, border unrests from endless to dare not stir up trouble. All these fully demonstrated that he was an exceptionally capable ruler.","He was even posthumously honored by later generations as \"The Only Emperor in History\".","Upon reading this, He Zhiran seemed to understand many things.","If her guess was right, the gaze she felt in the teahouse should be that of Third Prince Nan Qi.","That is to say, her appearance disrupted a chance encounter between Nan Qi and Fei Nanyu.","She had unintentionally changed history again. She didn't know if Fei Nanyu would still have the opportunity to meet Nan Qi in the future with this deviation.","With things going differently, the direction of future events would also change accordingly.","That meant she could no longer accurately predict what would happen to Nan Qi and Fei Nanyu. She could only adapt to changes.","Unable to grasp the general direction of the future, He Zhiran was not frustrated either. During her free time, she started reading that \"Unofficial History\".","To He Zhiran's surprise, it also contained records of Nan Qi and Fei Nanyu's affairs. Although more explicit than the official history books, the content did not differ much.","After reading about Fei Nanyu in \"Unofficial History\", He Zhiran continued flipping through and surprisingly found descriptions about Mo Jiuye...","With a gossipy mentality, He Zhiran read it carefully.","Unexpectedly, the first sentence said—Mo Jiuye's origins remain a mystery to this day.","A mystery?","He Zhiran was as excited as discovering a new continent. Her interest in this part skyrocketed instantly.","Some said that Mo Jiuye was not the Mo Family's own son, but the third prince born to Concubine Yuan, Emperor Shunwu's favored consort.","When Concubine Yuan was pregnant, she invited Master Wuchen from Enye Temple to determine the fetus’ gender."]},{"number":73,"title":"Chapter 73: Distributing the Silver","paragraphs":["Master Wuchen immediately told Concubine Yuan that she was pregnant with a little princess.","In order to maintain her position in the palace, Concubine Yuan planned to secretly switch her child if she gave birth to a daughter.","She secretly sent countless underlings to find and locate some women who were pregnant at the same time as her. As soon as someone's due date was close to hers, she would take that family's son and pass him off as her own.","On the day Concubine Yuan gave birth, she bribed the midwife and instructed her not to make any announcement after a successful delivery, but to wrap up the baby and hand it directly to her personal attendant.","Coincidentally, Concubine Yuan and the wife of the Duke of Guo from that year happened to give birth on the same day. Moreover, the wife of the Duke of Guo gave birth to precisely the boy she wanted.","Through Concubine Yuan's covert maneuvering, the newborn son of the Duke of Mo's house became the Third Prince, Nan Qi.","In fact, Concubine Yuan herself had also given birth to a boy. But because she believed too strongly in Master Wuchen's predictions, she had instructed the midwife not to announce anything when the child was born. Naturally, the midwife, who was bribed with silver, kept a tight lip and didn't say a word. She simply wrapped up the child and handed him over to the attendant.","As a result, aside from the midwife, everyone else was unaware at the time that Concubine Yuan had given birth to a little prince...","Only after the children had been switched did Concubine Yuan send someone to notify the Emperor.","When the Emperor heard that he had another prince, he was elated. He personally selected gifts and sent them to Concubine Yuan's palace.","The next day, when the personal attendant was about to silence the midwife, she learned that the concubine had actually given birth to a little prince as well, but had foolishly switched him with the Mo family's child...","When Concubine Yuan learned of this, she was heartbroken and inconsolable for quite some days.","But alas, the Emperor had already seen the Mo family's child, so even if she wanted to switch her own child back, it was completely impossible now. She could only let the mistake stand.","When Nan Qi turned five, it was time for him to start studying. Concubine Yuan made a request of the Emperor, saying that Mo Jiuye, the ninth son of the Mo family, was born on the same day as Nan Qi, and that was also a kind of fate. She hoped Mo Jiuye could become Nan Qi’s study companion.","This way, she could see her own son regularly.","Emperor Shunwu had no objections. He immediately issued an decree summoning Mo Jiuye into the palace.","After reading this passage, He Zhiran sucked in a breath of cold air.","Although this book was unofficial history, the content recorded in unofficial histories was not necessarily all fabricated.","Much of the unofficial histories contained records of secrets unknown to the public - things those in power did not want passed down.","That was why they tried to obstruct the existence of unofficial histories.","However, many such unknown secrets were still passed down to this day.","If this record really existed, it would not be hard to understand why Nan Qi would suddenly make a move against Mo Jiuye.","He must have obtained some information and learned of the switched-at-birth incident between them. He was worried the truth would come out, so he took action against Mo Jiuye.","This was no trivial matter. She had to think about how to subtly ask Mo Jiuye some questions.","At this moment, He Zhiran was sitting up straight, lightly tapping her chest with her small hand. To outsiders, she looked as if she had just had a nightmare.","He Zhiran was still quite disturbed by this.","If this unofficial history was true, then didn't it mean Emperor Shunwu had killed his own son with his own hands?","It was a real embodiment of Cao Zhi's Seven Steps Verse...","The wooden cart rattled and shook as it carried He Zhiran’s endless thoughts back to camp.","By now, the sun had set in the west, and the Mo family were all sitting by the roadside, craning their necks expectantly in their direction.","Seeing He Zhiran sitting atop the wooden cart from afar, Mo Hanxuan waved his little hand and shouted, \"Sister-in-Law Nine is back!\"","He Zhiran jumped down from the cart and walked toward her family.","Her sister-in-law considerately handed her a damp towel. \"Ninth sister, you must be tired out from the trip. Quick, wipe off your sweat.\"","He Zhiran felt very comforted by her family's concern.","In her past life, she had lived 24 years without parental love or affection. She had never experienced the taste of so-called family bonds.","She didn't expect that after accidentally traveling to another world, she would gain the family affection she could only yearn for but never obtain.","Although the road of exile was arduous and dangerous, He Zhiran firmly believed that they would definitely get through this ordeal safely and live happily together in the future.","After thanking her sister-in-law, she took the towel and wiped her face.","Peng Wang also handed all 115 taels of silver they earned today to He Zhiran. He had agreed to let her distribute it, and would not go back on his word.","He Zhiran called over the Fang and Xie families when she received the silver, and showed all the silver to everyone present.","\"Our wolf skins sold for 75 taels, and the dried meat sold for 40 taels. Our total income is 115 taels.\"","Hearing He Zhiran recite these figures, the Fang and Xie family members looked at each other in surprise.","They were happy in their hearts, but also silently wondering to themselves.","These silvers had nothing to do with them. Why was the He family announcing the accounts in front of everyone?","Soon their confusion was resolved.","He Zhiran took out 20 taels of silver and handed it to Xie Tianhai. \"Uncle Xie, this is your share.\"","Xie Tianhai was utterly confused. For the current Xie family, 20 taels of silver could be considered a huge sum.","If used thriftily, it would be enough for their family to live for several months.","Looking at the silver He Zhiran held out to him, Xie Tianhai didn't know whether to take it or not.","His eyes couldn't help but drift towards Peng Wang.","Peng Wang shrugged indifferently.","\"If the He family wants to give it to you, then take it. The Xie family did contribute when fighting off the wolf pack, skinning them, and making dried meat. This is what you deserve.\"","In Peng Wang's heart, giving the Xie family 20 taels really was a bit much.","Although he had just said they participated in those things, if he thought carefully about it, at least 45 out of those 50 wolves were killed by Mo Jiuye and his wife alone.","Although the Xie family did contribute significant effort in skinning the wolves and drying the meat, it still wasn't worth giving them that high of a cut.","Although He Zhiran also understood this reasoning in her heart, her decision to do this was after careful deliberation.","Putting aside the fact that the Xie family was her sister-in-law's maternal family, ever since that misunderstanding with Mo Jiuye had been cleared up, He Zhiran knew that the Fang and Xie families were exceptionally reasonable people.","They still had a long way to go together in exile. It would be better for the families to look after each other rather than fight and scheme.","Moreover, the Fang and Xie families were currently eating and drinking what her Mo family provided. That probably didn't feel good.","Now a rare opportunity to earn some silver had appeared. If He Zhiran shortchanged them and only symbolically gave them a tiny amount like wages, then her family would have to continue providing disaster relief for them in the future.","This was also He Zhiran's way of discreetly preserving their dignity.","Seeing Peng Wang's words, Xie Tianhai assumed this idea had come from him. He excitedly took the twenty taels of silver.","Seeing this, Peng Wang reminded, \"I wouldn't be so kind-hearted as to give you silver. If not for He Zhiran speaking up, I reckon your family wouldn't even see the shadow of any silver.\"","After this explanation, Xie Tianhai suddenly understood. He now knew the Mo family got along well with Peng Wang, but even so, he could never imagine Peng Wang actually listening to He Zhiran and agreeing to give them a share of the silver.","Thinking of this, Xie Tianhai sincerely cupped a fist towards He Zhiran. \"Niece, I will always remember this act of grace.\""]},{"number":74,"title":"Chapter 74: Younger Brothers and Sisters are Sensible","paragraphs":["He Zhiran quickly returned the courtesy.","\"Uncle Xie, don't be so polite. We will be living together for a long time to come and should help each other out.\"","After speaking, He Zhiran turned to look at the Fang family members who had envious looks on their faces. She also took out twenty taels of silver and handed it to Fang Chuanzhou.","\"Uncle Fang, this is for you. Take it.\"","Fang Chuanzhou already understood the general situation and did not say too much like Xie Tianhai. After giving his thanks, the Fang family members all had satisfied smiles on their faces.","There were 75 taels left. He Zhiran was not lacking silver in the first place. She only symbolically kept 25 taels and gave the remaining fifty taels all to Peng Wang.","Peng Wang had originally thought that getting thirty or forty taels would be good enough. He absolutely did not expect that He Zhiran would be so generous as to give him fifty taels.","This was equivalent to all the money that could be earned by selling those wolves to the fur shops by himself and the other officers.","\"Sister, isn't this a bit too much?\" Peng Wang did not even know when he had started to view money as dirt, to the point that he felt there was too much silver that had come to his hands.","He Zhiran laughed and said, \"Brother Peng is a good person who does not see us as criminals. We are all clear in our hearts that without your agreement, we would not have gotten a penny from those wolves. It is precisely because I know you are a good person that I tried to figure out a way to maximize the profits made from those fifty wolves. This way, it not only does not hinder your ability to earn extra income, but we prisoners also get a share. It's a win-win.\"","There was no denying that He Zhiran's words completely delighted Peng Wang.","Peng Wang laughed while holding the silver: \"Hahaha... Little sister is so sensible. Rest assured that as long as I am around, I guarantee that you all will not suffer hardships on the road to exile.\"","With Peng Wang's public promise, He Zhiran's efforts were not in vain. What could be more important than traveling comfortably on the road to exile?","Just as old Lady Mo felt gratified to have such a sensible daughter-in-law, He Zhiran had already come before her.","\"Mother, this is the first sum of money our Mo family has earned. Please keep it safe.\"","Seeing the silver that He Zhiran handed over, old Lady Mo felt warmth in her heart, but still refused it,","\"You should keep the silver. Today mother will act as the head of the household and from now on, the Mo family will be headed by the Hes.\"","Old Lady Mo was worried the other daughters-in-law would be unhappy, so she looked them over as she spoke.","The sisters-in-law were already convinced by He Zhiran's wisdom and integrity, so how could they be unhappy?","The Eldest Sister-in-law quickly represented the other sisters-in-law,","\"Mother is right. Little Sister-in-law is capable and wise. Although our Mo family has fallen, we still need someone sensible to be the head of household.\"","Then she looked at He Zhiran and sincerely said, \"Eldest Sister-in-law will listen to all your arrangements from now on, Little Sister-in-law.\"","\"I also agree for Little Sister-in-law to be the head of household.\"","\"Little Sister-in-law, Third Sister-in-law also agrees.\"","\"Little Sister-in-law, from now on Fifth Sister-in-law will listen to everything you say.\"","The Mo women, who had not held out much hope for the future earlier, were now reignited with fighting spirit and expressed their attitudes one after another.","Even the tough guy Mo Jiuye was moved by He Zhiran's wisdom and integrity at this moment. He was even feeling grateful that he did not know what virtues and abilities he possessed that allowed him to marry such a virtuous wife.","Seeing that everyone unanimously agreed with mother-in-law's words, He Zhiran did not pretend to decline and slipped that twenty-five taels of silver into her space.","\"Alright, since everyone trusts me, I'll temporarily be the head of this household.\"","Peng Wang's fifty taels of silver could not be enjoyed by him alone. He still had to distribute some to his subordinates so they could also live it up.","Peng Wang first called away the officers.","With the officers leaving, the space they previously occupied could directly see in the direction of the He family.","The He family members were furious as they glared at He Zhiran.","They had also heard parts of the earlier conversation about dividing up the silver, but there was no share for the He family. If they did not fear those officers, they would have gone over long ago to reason things out with He Zhiran.","How could the Fang and Xie families get to divide up silver while he had also used rocks to defend against the wolf pack. It was just that he had been at the very back and did not dare charge to the front...","He Zhiran glanced at the He family members. She had long been immune to their unkind looks.","She beckoned her mother-in-law, sisters-in-law, aunt, as well as the women from the Xie and Fang families to come over to the cart.","When He Zhiran had returned, the women had seen the coarse cloth on the cart and had looked upon them enviously.","Although these fabrics were inferior to what even the servants of their former households had worn, they were still better than nothing in such special times.","Moreover, although the coarse cloth did not look good, making them into clothes would still be much better than their current patched outfits.","When Mo Hanyue saw that Ninth Sister-in-law had brought back so many things from her trip into the city, she immediately smiled happily.","\"Ninth Sister-in-law, you're so nice to have purchased so many good things back.\"","He Zhiran lovingly stroked Mo Hanyue's head.","\"The weather is hot. We haven't had a change of clothes since leaving the Capital city. I just randomly bought some cloth to make a new set of clothing for each of us over the next few days while we don't need to travel.\"","Hearing they could make new clothes, which woman would not be delighted?","Moreover, their current outfits with patches were already extremely dirty. With the hot weather, the smell of sweat mixed with mud was revolting even to themselves.","Although the Fang and Xie families knew He Zhiran was kind, they did not think her purchase of cloth would include portions for them.","Zhao Shi thought for a bit before stepping forward to say, \"Sister He, Auntie sees you've bought quite a lot of cloth. Could you sell some to our Fang family? Don't worry, Auntie has silver now. We will buy them from you. We can even help make clothes for your family members.\"","Seeing Mrs. Zhao bring it up, the Xie family members also nodded in agreement.","He Zhiran could see that the two families had misunderstood her intentions.","The reason she had bought so much cloth was precisely so that everyone could have a share.","It was just that she did not take the initiative to give some to the Fangs and Xies because she could not endlessly provide for them unconditionally.","She wanted the two families to clearly recognize that there were no such things as unlimited free lunches in this world, much less the Mo family being able to support them for their entire lives.","She did intend to ask them for help making the clothes and planned to use the cloth as payment for their labor. This would be a mutually beneficial transaction.","\"Auntie, I did buy back a lot of cloth. You can help make the clothes. I won't pay you anything else and the cloth will serve to offset the costs. How about that?\"","Zhao Shi knew that although He Zhiran had phrased it this way, she was still helping them in a roundabout fashion.","The Fang family accepted this sentiment.","\"Alright, mine and my daughters-in-law's sewing skills are decent enough. We'll take on this job.\"","The Xie family members also expressed that they could help. And they sincerely thanked He Zhiran.","Seeing that Ninth Sister-in-law had already assigned out the clothing making tasks, the sisters-in-law became somewhat anxious.","The impatient Second Sister-in-law was just about to say that they could also make clothes when she was stopped by old Lady Mo, who had been observing things.","Old Lady Mo had long seen He Zhiran's intentions and fully approved of her approach. Naturally, she could not let her own family members mess things up.","Although confused after being stopped by mother-in-law, Second Sister-in-law still obediently shut her mouth.","He Zhiran publicly handed out all of the cloth. Zhao Shi patted her chest and guaranteed that they would start helping measure and tailor clothing for everyone after dinner. They would even work through the night these few days when they did not need to travel to quickly make all the clothes.","After all of the cloth for clothes had been allocated, He Zhiran left the twelve straw hats for her own family's use and gave the rest to the Fang and Xie family members. There was a limited quantity so they could only take turns using them.","The Fang and Xie families happily took their things and left. He Zhiran then took out the bag of fabric scraps the cloth shop owner had gifted her.","Seeing those fabric scraps, the sisters-in-law subconsciously looked at their own embroidered shoes, which already revealed their toes.","Not only were the toes revealed, but the soles would probably be worn through after another two days of traveling.","Ninth Sister-in-law really was thoughtful to have bought so many fabric scraps back for them to make shoes."]},{"number":75,"title":"Chapter 75: Aren't you curious how I know this","paragraphs":["The sisters-in-law's praises for He Zhiran in their hearts were soon shattered by her words.","\"Mother, sisters-in-law, the shop owner of the fabric store gave me these fabric scraps for free. I thought it would be good to bring them back to patch up some clothes, so I didn't refuse.\"","\"Sister-in-law, aren't these fabric scraps for making shoes?\" The second sister-in-law yelled out loudly.","\"Shoes?\" He Zhiran was completely confused. How could shoes be made from such small fabric scraps?","It was not surprising that she did not know, as the original owner hated women's chores and did not let the servants around her do them either. As a result, she knew nothing about the materials used to make shoes.","He Zhiran, a soul from thousands of years in the future, wore shoes that were either uniformly distributed in the army or bought by herself outside. How could she understand these things?","The second sister-in-law circled around He Zhiran as if she had discovered a new continent.","\"Sister-in-law, don't tell me you have never even seen shoes being made?\"","He Zhiran spread her hands helplessly and casually found an excuse.","\"When I was at home, I would hold medical books and study medical skills all day, so I didn't have time to look at these things.\"","Thinking of the sister-in-law's extraordinary medical skills, the sisters-in-law deeply believed in her excuse.","It was not surprising that the sister-in-law did not know women's red works, as she must not have spared much effort to learn such good medical skills.","After days of displacement, the sisters-in-law had gradually accepted this kind of life.","Carrying a full bag of fabric scraps off the carriage, they planned to add soles to the shoes after dinner.","The food was left on the carriage. He Zhiran left enough roast chicken and duck for her family to eat, and the rest was divided between the officials and the Xie and Fang families.","The Xie and Fang family members naturally thanked them profusely, and took the initiative to offer silver.","Seeing their eager looks to give her money, He Zhiran wanted to say:","Go ahead and eat! Don't worry, this is all paid for by the dog emperor.","However, she only dared to think this to herself and did not dare to say it out loud.","After some polite refusals, He Zhiran forcibly sent away the people trying to push silver at her, and finally had some peace and quiet.","Although the sisters-in-law liked the taste of the dishes cooked by the sister-in-law, thinking of her hard work today, they urged her to rest in the tent and took some meat and vegetables from the carriage on their own initiative to make dinner.","Returning to the tent, Mo Jiuye was seen holding a blade of grass in his mouth, sitting there not knowing what he was thinking.","She simply sat down next to him, with the section in the unofficial history describing Mo Jiuye’s background going through her mind.","At the same time, she was also thinking about how to subtly let Mo Jiuye know about what she understood.","Seeing the silent He Zhiran, Mo Jiuye took the initiative to speak.","\"You've had a hard time today. If you're uncomfortable, I can give you a massage.\"","He Zhiran quite approved of Mo Jiuye's massage skills. Upon hearing him take the initiative to offer her a massage, she felt a reflexive soreness in her back.","\"I really am a little uncomfortable.\"","Without another word, Mo Jiuye went behind her and started massaging from her shoulders.","He Zhiran looked around and saw that her family was busy and no one was paying attention here, so she spoke up, \"I met a person you wouldn't expect today in Pingyuan County.\"","\"Who?\" Mo Jiuye's tone was still somewhat cold as usual. He Zhiran was already used to it.","\"Nan Qi!\"","\"Nan Qi?\" Mo Jiuye was clearly somewhat incredulous. \"What is he doing here?\"","This was also a question in He Zhiran's mind.","Fortunately, this section was recorded in the unofficial history.","She was thinking about how to tell Mo Jiuye in a way that wouldn't arouse his suspicions.","After racking her brains, He Zhiran was still defeated by herself in the end.","She couldn't think of a reasonable excuse no matter how hard she tried, but she still felt it necessary to inform Mo Jiuye about such a big matter.","Since she wanted to tell Mo Jiuye about this, He Zhiran decided to go all out and first try out the waters by mentioning this matter.","\"What if I said I know the purpose of Nan Qi coming to Pingyuan County? Would you find it very strange, or even suspect that I might be a spy sent by Nan Qi?\"","Mo Jiuye answered without even thinking: \"If you were Nan Qi's person, I would have died long ago. Why would he still go through so much trouble to send someone to assassinate me?\"","\"Aren't you curious why I would know these things?\"","Mo Jiuye did not hide his true thoughts on this.","\"I am indeed very curious. You said before that everyone has their own secrets. I'll say it again, as long as you don't do anything detrimental to the Mohists, I won't take the initiative to probe into your secrets.\"","This was the second time He Zhiran had heard him say this.","Moreover, he really meant what he said and never asked anything he shouldn't.","After testing the waters, He Zhiran slowly spoke, \"A few years ago, a master helped Nan Qi divine that a noble person would appear in Pingyuan County this August.\"","Mo Jiuye felt it was somewhat absurd to look for a noble person based on a master's divination, but it was not surprising for this to happen to Nan Qi.","No one knew when Nan Qi started to increasingly believe in these divination techniques, to the point that at one time he went everywhere looking for divination masters to tell his fortune.","Therefore, he did not doubt at all what He Zhiran said.","Although he could not ask He Zhiran how she knew these things, Mo Jiuye felt that he could ask some other questions.","\"Do you think he can find that so-called noble person?\"","He Zhiran did not intend to conceal this question either.","\"If I hadn't shown up in Pingyuan County today, I'm afraid he would have already met that noble person.\"","\"What do you mean by that?\" Mo Jiuye was a little confused. He could not figure out for the life of him what this matter had to do with He Zhiran.","\"That noble person of his is called Fei Nanyu. He passed the county exam at the age of 12 and is an extremely talented person ...\"","He Zhiran selectively told some of Fei Nanyu's experiences, as well as how he got to know Nan Qi and helped him ascend the throne.","Of course, she chose to reserve Fei Nanyu's overthrow of the dynasty for now.","After all, such things were too incredulous. She was worried that Mo Jiuye would not believe it on one hand, and on the other hand, she did not want him to know too much about these things too soon.","After all, her arrival had already changed many things, and bigger changes might happen in the future.","With so much incredible information flooding Mo Jiuye's brain all at once, he fell into contemplation.","The name Fei Nanyu sounded vaguely familiar to him, as if he had heard it somewhere before but couldn't recall where for the moment.","Seeing that Mo Jiuye did not respond for a long time, He Zhiran thought he did not believe what she said.","Glancing at him, Mo Jiuye was frowning in thought.","\"What's wrong? Do you find my words illogical somewhere?\"","Mo Jiuye shook his head. \"I was thinking, who is Fei Nanyu? His name sounds familiar for some reason.\"","He Zhiran did not hurry him, only quietly enjoying Mo Jiuye's massage service.","After thinking for a long time, Mo Jiuye said, \"I remember now.\"","He Zhiran asked, \"Where did you hear about this person?\""]},{"number":76,"title":"Chapter 76: Imprint of the Family","paragraphs":["When I was young, I often went in and out of Concubine Yuan's palace as Nan Qi's study companion.","Concubine Yuan had a trusted personal maid named Fe Mama. Concubine Yuan looked at me and Nan Qi chatting casually with Fe Mama.","Concubine Yuan asked Fe Mama if she happened to have a nephew around our age. If so, she wondered if he could also be brought into the palace to play together.","At that time, Fe Mama rejected the idea, claiming that Fei Nanyu's status was too lowly and that she feared he would be rude to the noble lady if he came over.","Thinking of the records in the history books about Fei Nanyu's age, he was indeed similar to Mo Jiuye.","Therefore, He Zhiran felt that Fe Mama's nephew was undoubtedly Fei Nanyu.","According to what Mo Jiuye said, Fe Mama was Concubine Yuan's trusted aide, so she should not lack money. Why didn't she lend a helping hand when her own nephew's family was so destitute?","Such a question flashed through He Zhiran's mind and then disappeared in an instant. After all, how one deals with relatives has nothing to do with the big picture.","Her purpose in letting Mo Jiuye know about Fei Nanyu's existence was exactly what they had been chatting about for so long.","Thinking that Mo Jiuye had taken the initiative to mention that he often went in and out of Concubine Yuan's palace when he was young, He Zhiran tentatively asked him, \"What was Concubine Yuan's attitude towards you when you often went to her palace?\"","Speaking of this, Mo Jiuye had a very deep impression.","\"I don't know why, but the Noble Concubine treated me even better than she treated Nan Qi.\"","He Zhiran: This is right. It matches almost completely with the wild history records. Concubine Yuan must have known that Mo Jiuye was her own son, that's why she was like this.","Mo Jiuye was quite sensitive. He instantly felt that He Zhiran's question was a bit strange.","\"Why do you ask like this?\"","Seeing Mo Jiuye's serious look, He Zhiran couldn't help but want to tease him a little.","\"Have you ever thought that you might be Concubine Yuan's child?\"","\"That's impossible!\" Mo Jiuye categorically denied it, and his expression became even more serious.","\"Are you that sure?\" He Zhiran persisted in asking unrelentingly.","\"Of course I'm sure. When I, a Mo Family Man, was born, I had the unique family mark of the Mo Family.\" Mo Jiuye had no doubt about his own origins.","\"Family mark?\" This was the first time He Zhiran had heard that a family would have some kind of mark. This couldn't be explained scientifically unless it was done deliberately by people.","\"When I and my eight elder brothers were born, we all had a crescent-shaped birthmark on our left shoulders.","My father said this was an ancient inheritance passed down in the Mo Family Clan, and it was the same with him and many more of my ancestors.\"","Seeing Mo Jiuye speak categorically, He Zhiran was confused.","There are endless wonders in the world, and something as bizarre as transmigration could happen, so a family mark was not that strange.","What He Zhiran first thought of when she saw this section about Mo Jiuye's origins in the wild history was that this was very likely the real reason why Nan Qi had attacked him.","This speculation was soon negated by the Mo Family's family mark. The reason why Nan Qi targeted Mo Jiuye became a mystery again.","At the same time, a series of question marks also appeared in Mo Jiuye's mind.","Why did Nan Qi want him dead?","Why did He Zhiran ask such a question?","Both harbored their own thoughts and neither spoke again.","Because they had things on their minds, they only ate some casual food for dinner.","Lying back in the tent again, He Zhiran was wide awake.","Her consciousness entered the shop space and she first checked the sales of the shop. Only one item was sold today, adding 250,000 yuan to the account.","There were still many items in stock left and no need to replenish, so He Zhiran simply continued to read that wild history book, hoping for some other gains.","At the same time, upstairs in the inn in Pingyuan County.","Nan Qi sat at the table, rhythmically tapping the table with his fingers.","\"Master, I just received a carrier pigeon letter from Li Lu.\"","While speaking, He Feng had already respectfully delivered a small paper roll about 5 centimeters long to Nan Qi.","Nan Qi calmly unrolled the paper, and after reading the contents, slammed the table hard.","\"A bunch of useless trash! Killing the wrong person when trying to kill someone, what use do I have keeping such incompetents around?\"","He Feng did not know what was written in Li Lu's letter, but seeing the Master so angry, something big must have happened.","\"Master, what happened?\" He Feng cautiously asked.","Nan Qi unpleasantly threw the note to him.","\"See for yourself.\"","After reading the contents of the note, He Feng analyzed, \"The Li Family people were escorted back to the capital. Master Li Lu's news should not be false.\"","\"Humph! Now that Mo Jiuye is awake, and given his vigilance, he must have guessed that He Liang was just his scapegoat. If I want to take his life again in the future, I'm afraid it won't be so easy.\"","Calmed down now, Nan Qi carefully considered what to do next.","Although He Feng didn't know why his Master was so determined to kill Mo Jiuye, he knew clearly in his heart that this matter was a must-win for the Master.","\"Master, why don't your subordinate send a few people out to find out where Mo Jiuye and the others' exiled team has reached, understand the situation there, and also plan the next step?\"","Nan Qi waved his hand: \"No need. With the Li family escorted back to the capital, the exiled team must be waiting in place for the officials to return and continue on together.","Pingyuan County is a necessary stop for exile to the northwest. We'll just wait here. I want to meet Mo Jiuye myself.\"","With the Master having made up his mind, He Feng simply brought up something else.","\"Master, tomorrow will be the last day according to what Master Wuchen said. If you still haven't met that noble person, what should we do?\"","\"Master Wuchen's calculations have never been wrong before. I must find that person.\" Nan Qi's tone carried an unquestionable assertiveness.","Moreover, he had already planned to stay here and wait for Mo Jiuye, so it was not unreasonable to look for that noble person for a few more days...","Unknowingly, He Zhiran had read through that entire Wild History book again, especially the section describing Mo Jiuye's origins.","From every perspective, there were no flaws in this description.","Moreover, Mo Jiuye also said that the Concubine treated him even better than Nan Qi. Why was that?","He Zhiran racked her brains to speculate on various possibilities. Finally, she thought of Nan Qi in a flash of inspiration.","Having found a new breakthrough, He Zhiran was a little excited. She turned over with a bigger movement than normal, accidentally pressing Mo Jiuye's arm.","Feeling something wrong, He Zhiran moved her body away at the fastest speed.","She didn't know if it was her movement that woke Mo Jiuye up, or if he hadn't fallen asleep like her either.","Unexpectedly, Mo Jiuye sat up with his tone still revealing no warmth at all.","\"Can't you sleep either?\"","\"Yeah, thinking about things in my head, so a bit insomnia.\" He Zhiran did not hide it.","Mo Jiuye asked again: \"Still thinking about my origins?\"","Being asked right on target, He Zhiran hesitated for a moment and asked:","\"Can you and Nan Qi bathe together?\"","As an intelligent person, Mo Jiuye grasped the true meaning behind this question at once.","\"I can confirm he doesn't have a birthmark on him.\""]},{"number":77,"title":"Chapter 77: The moment he laid a hand on me, we were no longer brothers.","paragraphs":["At this point, He Zhiran was completely disappointed.","Originally, she still thought that the birthmark on Mo Jiuye might have been tattooed on later by the Mo family.","But Nan Qi did not have the unique birthmark that the Mo family members had at all, which completely showed that they had not been switched at birth after all.","In other words, the unofficial historical records on this were completely implausible after closer examination.","After getting the last answer from Mo Jiuye about his birth, He Zhiran completely gave up her doubts about his identity.","At the same time, she was even more puzzled by Nan Qi's behavior towards him.","The one who bells the cat must take the bell off. It seemed now that only Nan Qi himself knew the answer.","Seeing that He Zhiran was still deep in thought, Mo Jiuye really wanted to ask her where she had heard such a preposterous thing.","But thinking of the promise he had made to her, Mo Jiuye still tried his best to restrain his curiosity.","In order to prevent this woman from indulging in wild fantasies, Mo Jiuye chose to share his guesses.","\"I grew up with Nan Qi since childhood, and we were the closest of friends. He has always been truly good to me.","I remember when I was fighting on the border and we were running out of food supplies, I sent a letter to the court but got no solution for a long time. My soldiers were about to run out of food at the critical moment when Nan Qi took money out of his own pocket to hire people to collect food supplies from various places to deliver to the border. That time he really gave me timely help.","The first time I went into battle, I accidentally got hit by the enemy's poisoned arrow. To help me detoxify, Nan Qi raced to Medicine Valley to get me antidotes.","There have been many more such things that can fully prove Nan Qi's true feelings for me.","It wasn't until I returned to the capital from the borders earlier this year that I sensed something wrong with him. Although he still welcomed me back from the city outskirts as usual based on our many years of friendship, relying on my understanding of him over the years, my intuition told me that he wasn't happy to see me come back.","Moreover, his eyes were always dodgy, and when I asked him curiously if something had happened to him, he chose not to answer me directly but beat around the bush instead.","After I had settled down in the capital, the first thing I did was rush over to Wang's mansion to see him.","But he asked me a question – if I were not the emperor's son, would we still be good brothers.","At that time, I didn't take his words to heart and casually reassured him.","Thinking about it now, based on the question Nan Qi asked, it is very likely that he had heard something, or that he was really not of royal blood himself, but the one who was swapped with him would definitely not be me.\"","After listening to Mo Jiuye's account, He Zhiran thought of another possibility.","\"From what you said, Nan Qi's brotherly affection for you was definitely real before, and his sudden change in attitude later on. I guess he should not really be of royal blood himself, and had indeed been swapped at birth.","However, the news he obtained was that the one he was swapped with was you. Worried that the truth would be revealed after a long time, that was why he tried to kill you?\"","Mo Jiuye said solemnly, \"These are just my guesses after all. His true identity still remains unknown.\"","\"If that's really the case, don't you want to clear up the misunderstanding with him?\" He Zhiran wanted to understand Mo Jiuye's true thoughts.","Mo Jiuye shook his head with a wry smile.","\"Whether it was a misunderstanding or not, the moment he made a move against me, we can no longer be brothers.\"","Seeing Mo Jiuye becoming increasingly dejected, they had analyzed everything they could think of regarding the matter. He Zhiran decided to end this topic.","The two of them fell silent at the same time, not knowing what to say for a moment.","Finally, it was Mo Jiuye who broke the quiet in the tent.","\"I'll go sit by the river for a while, it's cooler there.\"","It was indeed a little stuffy inside the tent. The first thing He Zhiran thought of was that it would be great if she could enter her space and take a bath.","Seeing Mo Jiuye about to leave, this might be a good opportunity.","\"Uh... can you come back after half an hour?\"","Mo Jiuye looked at her deeply and murmured in agreement.","He Zhiran knew he had agreed. Seeing his figure disappear, she immediately slipped into her space.","Time was precious. He Zhiran took the quickest cold shower, then blow dried her hair and changed into a set of clean undergarments.","Looking at the clock on the wall, it had just been 40 minutes since she entered.","After leaving her space, Mo Jiuye had not yet returned. He Zhiran lay down on her side and gradually fell asleep.","She clearly felt the familiar scent appearing next to her after some unknown period of time.","Knowing Mo Jiuye had returned, He Zhiran's body subconsciously shifted aside to give him more space.","Mo Jiuye had just entered the tent when he smelled the long-absent fragrance.","He didn't know why, but he felt strangely obsessed with this smell.","He even felt some kind of primitive impulse churning inside him.","Mo Jiuye shook his head hard a few times in effort to keep himself sober. Then he gently lay down on the other side...","In the next two days, they still had to wait for the Eighth Old Zhou and others to return.","He Zhiran couldn't lend the ladies a hand in what they were working on, but she wasn't idle either. Besides being responsible for three meals a day, she spent all her remaining time making medicine.","The silver ring snake had been kept in her space for several days now. He Zhiran planned to make use of the free time to make the toxins she wanted from it.","Hidden in her tent, she used some modern medical tools to extract snake venom from the silver ring snake.","According to some formula notes, adding different medicinal ingredients could make toxins with different effects.","This was also not difficult for He Zhiran. All kinds of medicinal materials could be purchased from Taobao Treasure.","After two days of effort, He Zhiran finally successfully produced two toxins and an anesthetic incense.","One kind could paralyze a person's consciousness for a short time. He Zhiran named this toxin 'Loss of Consciousness'.","The other was more straightforward. Once someone ingested it, they would die immediately, saving He Zhiran the trouble of making an antidote.","She named this toxin 'Death Descends'.","The anesthetic incense was self-explanatory. Once lit, any person that smelled it would quickly lose consciousness, with drug efficacy lasting about two hours.","Of course, for her own safety, He Zhiran also simultaneously made the antidote to the incense.","She treasured and carefully kept these things for future need.","On He Zhiran's side, she had successfully produced anesthetic incense and toxins. On the other side, the ladies had finished making all the clothes and shoes.","It so happened that the Eighth Old Zhou had also returned from the capital with several officials.","Looking at the sky, it was already the early Geng Hour. Peng Wang decided to stop over here for one more night and set off early the next morning.","After resting for another night, everyone took the opportunity to change into new clothes and shoes, putting those old dirty ones in packages for later use.","At the first light of dawn the next day, after breakfast as commanded by Peng Wang, the troop set forth again in full strength.","Pingyuan County was a requisite stop on the way going northwest. In the afternoon, the mighty parade entered Pingyuan County.","Had it not been for the few officials following in the parade, nobody would have guessed that this group of neatly and properly dressed people were exiled convicts.","As they entered the city, the group aroused many inquisitive gazes. Following tacit understanding, the Mo family members lowered their wide-rimmed hats a bit so that people could not see their faces."]},{"number":78,"title":"Chapter 78: Meet Fei Nanyu Again","paragraphs":["Peng Wang County was not small in area. They needed to traverse the entire county city.","Entering from the east city gate and leaving from the west city gate, the whole process would take about two hours.","On the way, the officers had to replenish some supplies, so when they arrived at the west city gate, it would at least be around dusk.","Staying overnight in Peng Wang County was inevitable, so after entering Peng Wang County, Peng Wang did not urge everyone to hurry.","They went shopping for some necessities while walking and stopping along the way.","The Fang and Xie families each had twenty taels of silver. Under the officers turning a blind eye, they also bought some daily necessities.","However, they did not dare to be too extravagant. After all, there was still a long way to go in the future. It would be difficult to spend all the hard-earned silver too quickly. It had to be used at more critical moments.","The Mo family people were much more generous. Let alone He Zhiran having countless silver, the amount of silver sent by Third Sister-in-law and Fourth Sister-in-law's natal families was not small either.","Seeing their silver finally having a use, the two sister-in-laws were very enthusiastic.","They would buy things they saw fit all the way. By the time the carts were full and could not hold any more items, they reluctantly stopped.","The He family members all had long faces, watching others buying things while the feeling was indescribable.","With the two sister-in-laws' contributions, He Zhiran did not participate this time.","It was only when they passed a woodware store that she became a little interested.","She discussed with Peng Wang, \"Big Brother Peng, can I buy two more carts?\"","Peng Wang knew He Zhiran's intention. They had more and more items and it was indeed a little inconvenient to carry them.","However, he still rejected it.","\"Sister, I'm afraid you don't know that in a few days, we will encounter a lot of mountain roads, and there is even a section we have to climb over the mountain to get through. At that time, even the two carts you have now will not be able to keep up.","I advise you that if you want to buy carts, wait until after we have crossed that mountain.\"","He Zhiran did not know that they would have to cross mountains and ridges along the way.","\"Since this is the case, I'll listen to Big Brother Peng.\"","Although she did not care about the money for buying a few carts, and it would not hurt to throw them away after using them for a few days, they still had special identities after all, and it was better not to be too high-profile.","At the same time, she also considered one thing, that is, food supplies could not be replenished too much for the next period of time, so as not to be too heavy burden when climbing the mountain.","Just as He Zhiran was thinking about specifically how to do it, when she looked up, she saw Master Cui, who had purchased dried wolf meat from them, was warmly greeting guests to enter in front of the nearby restaurant.","He Zhiran had long heard about Master Cui's purpose of buying so much dried wolf meat, which was nothing more than to host some poetry meeting.","Today must be the day the poetry meeting was held.","She was not interested in this. She lowered her straw hat again, not wanting to have any more intersection with the other party.","At this moment, a discordant voice suddenly came from ahead.","\"Fei Nanyu, you poor worthless fool. You took advantage when someone helped you last time to deceive us of 100 taels of silver. You still dare to show up in front of us?\"","\"Fei Nanyu, take a look at yourself in the mirror to see what kind of virtue you have. This is a poetry meeting hosted by Master Cui. It is not something that every Tom, Dick and Harry has the qualifications to attend.\"","\"Get lost quickly. If you're slow, be careful brothers will not be polite to you.\"","He Zhiran looked in the direction where the voice came from, still the few students she saw in front of the bookstore last time.","A few people trapped Fei Nanyu in a corner and verbally attacked him.","Fei Nanyu stood with his back straight, not the slightest bit afraid.","\"As fellow scholars, why can I not attend the poetry meeting?\"","As Fei Nanyu spoke, those students gradually closed in on him.","\"You extorted money from us and still dare to unabashedly call yourself a scholar?\"","At the same time, the students had already made gestures to attack.","Master Cui heard the voices here and ran over to see what was going on.","More and more onlookers were also attracted over.","The small alley was soon crowded with people and impassable.","Master Cui looked at the few young men dressed as students in front of him.","\"Why are you making trouble when I'm hosting a poetry meeting?\"","In front of Master Cui, the students naturally did not dare to attack Fei Nanyu again. They soon put on flattering faces.","\"Master Cui, you don't know. This person defrauded us of 100 taels of silver a few days ago. Yet today he came to the poetry meeting to make trouble with our money. Naturally, we can't let such a person enter.\"","At this time, Fei Nanyu's face was already showing anger. He saluted Master Cui with clasped hands.","\"Student Fei Nanyu has the honor of being a scholar. I ask, am I qualified to attend the poetry meeting you host?\"","Master Cui answered without hesitation: \"Of course you are qualified.\"","He paused and then said, \"However, having just heard what they said about your improper behavior, if no one recommends you, I absolutely wouldn't allow you to enter the venue.\"","Just as Fei Nanyu was about to say something to defend himself, a figure in white holding a fan suddenly jumped down from the second floor and landed lightly between Master Cui and Fei Nanyu.","Nan Qi did not hide his identity.","\"If this prince personally recommends this gentleman to attend the poetry meeting, does Master Cui think it’s feasible?\"","When Master Cui saw Nan Qi, he quickly kneeled before him and saluted.","\"Prince Qi really makes me feel inferior. You don't need any recommendation to bring people to the poetry meeting.\"","Nan Qi revealed a satisfied smile. He looked kindly at Fei Nanyu, \"Let's go. Come with me to the elegant room upstairs.\"","In the instant Nan Qi appeared, Fei Nanyu's expression changed slightly, but soon returned to normal.","However, this small movement of his did not escape the eyes of He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye who were not far away.","Like He Zhiran, when Mo Jiuye heard the name Fei Nanyu, he paid full attention to everything here until the moment Nan Qi appeared, then he fully believed He Zhiran's words.","He saw Fei Nanyu salute Nan Qi neither humble nor pushy, \"Thank you, Prince, for your favor.\"","After speaking, Fei Nanyu followed Nan Qi into the restaurant.","Seeing this scene, the students were instantly dumbfounded.","They never imagined that Fei Nanyu would actually gain the favor of Prince Qi.","If Fei Nanyu told on them in front of Prince Qi, not only would they be finished, but their families would also be implicated.","At this time, everyone watched as Fei Nanyu followed Prince Qi into the restaurant, and had lost interest in watching those students acting pitiful.","Seeing the onlooking crowd gradually dispersing, Peng Wang called to the prisoners to continue moving forward.","Coming out of this busy commercial district, Peng Wang came to He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye.","\"Sister, the one you saved is clearly not an ordinary person to have caught Prince Qi's eyes.\"","He Zhiran could hear the probing tone in Peng Wang's voice.","\"Big Brother Peng jests. How could I possibly know he's acquainted with Prince Qi? I just happened to see a group bullying an individual at that time and found it unbearable.\""]},{"number":79,"title":"Chapter 79: A Visit from Nan Qi","paragraphs":["At this moment, Mo Jiuye also had a bellyful of words that he wanted to say to He Zhiran. Seeing Peng Wang lingering here and showing no signs of leaving, he deliberately pretended to look uncomfortable.","\"My wife, my chest feels a little uncomfortable. Can you support me for a bit?\"","With one glance, He Zhiran could tell that Mo Jiuye was pretending to be sick. She very cooperatively supported one of his arms.","\"My husband, your wounds definitely haven't healed completely yet. Today's journey must have tired you out. Let me support you slowly as we walk. When we get to the inn, I'll take another good look at your injuries.\"","Mo Jiuye's body leaned against He Zhiran's, looking extremely weak in the eyes of outsiders.","Peng Wang thought Mo Jiuye was really uncomfortable. He hurriedly ordered the team to walk slower, and he personally ran to the front to press down the pace.","Seeing Peng Wang walking away, Mo Jiuye looked around again. Only his own people were looking at him with concern.","He blinked at Old Lady Mo and the others, signaling that he was fine. Only then did he whisper to He Zhiran:","\"Your appearance has only changed the time they met.\"","What Mo Jiuye meant was that the two still had an intersection.","He Zhiran was not particularly surprised by this. Besides, she was also happy for Nan Qi and Fei Nanyu to get to know each other. As long as Fei Nanyu became Nan Qi's staff officer, she could infer some things based on the records in the history books and know both herself and her enemy.","\"This is not necessarily a bad thing.\"","\"Why?\" Mo Jiuye did not understand.","He Zhiran did not know how to explain this to Mo Jiuye.","\"I can't explain too much. I can only say it's my intuition.\"","When she said this, Mo Jiuye became even more confused.","But he knew very well that he could not get any more useful information from He Zhiran. So he could only silently speculate in his heart.","The husband and wife leaned against each other, each lost in their own thoughts as they arrived at the westernmost edge of Pingyuan County.","There was still a familiar inn there that Peng Wang was acquainted with. He directly led everyone inside.","The Eighth Old Zhou went in and said something to the boss. Soon an attendant came out with him to show everyone the guest rooms on the first floor.","The guest rooms were still divided into rooms for ten people and rooms for couples.","This time, the officials did not intend to claw back the money for the rooms. Instead, the attendant from the inn directly reported the prices.","The prices were the same for both the ten person rooms and the couple rooms, 100 wen each.","Now that He Zhiran was the head of the Mo family, the Fourth Sister-in-Law was holding the silver and came to pay her.","\"Sister-in-Law, the Fourth Sister-in-Law will pay for the rooms today. What kind of rooms do you think would be suitable for us?\"","Although He Zhiran was currently the head of the household, there were some things she still wanted to consult everyone's opinion on more. She brought the Fourth Sister-in-Law to Old Lady Mo and the other women.","\"Mother, how should we allocate the rooms today?\"","Old Lady Mo looked around and said, \"I think it's still the same as last time. You and Jiuye can take a room for two, and the rest will stay with me in a ten person room.\"","He Zhiran got Old Lady Mo's opinion and turned to the Fourth Sister-in-Law, \"Sister-in-Law, let's do as Mother said!\"","\"Okay,\" the Fourth Sister-in-Law replied and went to pay the attendant.","The Xie family and Fang family did not have much silver on them, so they tacitly chose the ten person rooms even though they each had over ten people and were reluctant to open another room.","Only the He family looked bitterly at Peng Wang, hoping he would take pity on them and not make them sleep outside again.","Having been an escort officer for many years, Peng Wang was not the kind of person who would go soft when he saw others' misery.","\"What are you looking at? If you don't have silver, then sleep in the woodshed in the backyard.\"","The He family looked at each other helplessly before finally resigning themselves to their fate.","The woodshed still had \"room\" in its name. It was at least better than sleeping in a dirty and smelly grass shed.","After everyone was settled with their lodging arrangements, each family began looking for an open space to start their stoves and cook dinner.","After traveling all day, everyone was tired. Although the sky was not yet dark, they returned to their rooms early to rest.","He Zhiran was afraid Mo Jiuye would continue to ask about Fei Nanyu, so despite not being sleepy at all, she still faced the wall pretending to be asleep.","Mo Jiuye was also tactful and did not say anything more even though he noticed she was not actually sleeping.","They thought the night would pass peacefully. But in the late hours of the night, someone actually knocked on their door.","Mo Jiuye sat up cautiously and asked in a deep voice, \"Who is it?\"","\"Jiuye, it's this prince.\"","He Zhiran also sat up and exchanged glances with Mo Jiuye.","Neither of them had expected that Nan Qi would take the initiative to show himself.","After hesitating for a moment, Mo Jiuye slowly opened the door.","By this time, He Zhiran had also tidied up her clothes and lit the oil lamp on the table.","The moment the door opened, not only Nan Qi but also Fei Nanyu appeared before them.","In the dim light of the oil lamp, He Zhiran clearly captured the slightly complicated look in Fei Nanyu's eyes when he first saw Mo Jiuye.","But he soon concealed his abnormality and stood properly by Nan Qi's side.","\"Jiuye, won't you invite me in to sit for a bit?\"","Mo Jiuye's expression was calm, as if he did not know about Nan Qi's recent actions against him. He shifted slightly to the side to clear the doorway.","Nan Qi strode in and headed straight to sit at the round table. He then gestured for Mo Jiuye to do the same.","Unhurriedly, Mo Jiuye sat down and did not forget to pull He Zhiran along to sit by his side.","Only then did Nan Qi notice He Zhiran's presence.","His eyes suddenly lit up. At the same time, he suddenly remembered the scene of Fei Nanyu being bullied by several students in the street.","Despite recognizing He Zhiran, Nan Qi was too proud to expose it on the spot. Instead, he looked at Mo Jiuye and said, \"Jiuye, won't you introduce me to your wife?\"","Although they used to interact in this way before, when Nan Qi spoke like this now, Mo Jiuye felt a mocking sense to his words that he did not perceive previously.","Especially Nan Qi's eyes when he looked at He Zhiran just now made him inexplicably uncomfortable.","\"The only woman who could be sharing a room with me this late is my wife. Who else could it be?\"","Nan Qi did not change his attitude because of Mo Jiuye. He continued unhurriedly, \"Sister-in-Law is truly a worthy wife of the Mo family. When Nanyu encountered difficulties, she did not fear the mob but rushed to help him draw her sword.\"","Since Nan Qi had made it clear, He Zhiran felt that she no longer needed to keep a low profile.","\"Although this common woman does not have much ability, I cannot stand those who bully others by taking advantage of their power. Please forgive me for the trouble, Your Highness.\"","At this point, Fei Nanyu also courteously cupped his fist towards He Zhiran. \"Thank you, Lady Mo, for your righteous help.\"","He Zhiran looked closely at Fei Nanyu's expression. Seeing that he remained as calm and undisturbed as before, she lightly replied, \"Sir, there is no need to stand on ceremony. I believe if it were anyone else, they would not turn a blind eye in such a situation either.\"","As she spoke, He Zhiran looked meaningfully at Nan Qi again and said, \"Isn't that right, Prince Nan?\""]},{"number":80,"title":"Chapter 80: I thank the Prince for the Mohism's concern","paragraphs":["Nan Qi did not know if he was somewhat sensitive, but after hearing He Zhiran's words that were a little yin and yang, he suddenly remembered the scene he saw upstairs that day when Fei Nanyu was being bullied.","At that time, he had observed for a long time and saw that although Fei Nanyu was bullied by those people and had no power to fight back, the pride of a scholar still remained.","Master Wu Chen said that his noble person was by no means an ordinary person.","And his first feeling when he saw Fei Nanyu had a little meaning of being by no means an ordinary person.","Just because he hesitated for that moment, wanting to confirm again, the matter of saving people was seized by He Zhiran.","So Nan Qi and Fei Nanyu's first affinity was lost.","Thinking of these things, Nan Qi looked sharply at He Zhiran.","\"Sister-in-law is right. To draw the sword to help the unfair, I think anyone in the world who has some blood would do the same.\"","In fact, Nan Qi did not know that when He Zhiran asked the question with meaning, ostensibly she was asking Nan Qi, but she was actually speaking for Fei Nanyu to hear.","With her depth of wisdom recorded in the history books, she could not have failed to understand.","When she said those words, He Zhiran's side vision kept staring at Fei Nanyu's expression from time to time.","Sure enough, after Fei Nanyu heard her words, he was stunned for a moment, and soon returned to normal.","He wondered in his heart, could this woman know something?","After thinking about it carefully, he soon let it go. With such a big secret, this woman could not possibly know.","Although Fei Nanyu had doubts in his heart, He Zhiran had just spoken to Nan Qi. If he said more, it would appear suspicious.","He Zhiran achieved her goal and did not speak again.","Nan Qi looked around the inn environment and sighed.","\"Jiu Ye, I am really ashamed about the banishment of the Duke of Protector’s residence. Recently my imperial concubine mother has been in poor health, and I have been busy looking for a good doctor, so I did not pay much attention to court news during this period.","When I learned about this, you were already on the road to exile in Pingyuan County, so I hurried here, thinking of helping the Mo Family settle down.\"","Mo Jiuye tapped the table habitually with his fingers, trying hard to restrain the anger in his heart, and continued to act out the play of deep brotherhood with him here.","\"I thank Duke Nan for his concern on behalf of the Mo Family. There is no need to settle us down. We are all criminals exiled by the court. We will live whatever kind of life we should in the future and dare not have any extravagant hopes.\"","Hearing Mo Jiuye's tone of speech, Nan Qi suddenly felt that the man who grew up with him since childhood seemed to have become a stranger.","Could Mo Jiuye have discovered something?","But soon he let it go again. He did want Mo Jiuye dead, but facing the latter, he did not have the courage to make it clear.","He was very clear about Mo Jiuye’s martial arts prowess. It was no exaggeration to say that he could fight a hundred men alone. Nan Qi was not stupid enough to confront him directly.","If the assassination failed, the best way was to outsmart him. Nan Qi came today partly to test Mo Jiuye’s injuries, and also to look for a chance to poison him.","With this thought, Nan Qi eased his mood a little and said, \"We are brothers. Since the Duke of Protector’s residence was searched and exiled when I was not there, you should at least give me a chance to see you off.\"","After Nan Qi finished speaking, he was already at the door of the room, and finally said, \"Don't worry about the officials. I will personally let them know to stay here for one more day.\"","Mo Jiuye did not get up to see them off, still sitting in his original position.","Fei Nanyu followed behind Nan Qi, with one hand behind his back, swaying back and forth towards them a few times.","Both Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran saw his small gesture.","\"His meaning should be that he does not recommend you to attend the banquet.\" This was how He Zhiran interpreted Fei Nanyu's actions.","Mo Jiuye still maintained his original sitting posture.","\"I must go. In any case, the grievances between Nan Qi and I must end.\"","He Zhiran did not quite understand what he meant.","\"Do you plan to kill Nan Qi?\"","Mo Jiuye shook his head, \"No, if I did that, I could have a moment of satisfaction, but where would I put my family then?\"","He Zhiran was even more confused.","\"Since you can't kill him, what grievances need to be resolved?\"","\"I want to tell him the fact that I am from the Mo family, so that he knows I am not the person who was swapped.","If I can successfully resolve the misunderstanding, I will break off relations with him on the spot, and our brotherhood will end there.","Although this is not very meaningful, at least there will be one less person calculating against us on the road to exile in the future.\"","For someone like Nan Qi, He Zhiran indeed felt a sense of satisfaction from killing him, but what Mo Jiuye said made sense.","In addition to himself, the Mo family had so many women and children. His sisters-in-law and their natal families were all in the capital city. Once Nan Qi died, the emperor's wrath would surely implicate those relatives.","\"In that case, may I accompany you to the banquet tomorrow?\"","Mo Jiuye rejected without even thinking about it, in an unquestionable tone.","\"No, I cannot let you take the risk with me.\"","He Zhiran’s proposal to accompany him to the banquet naturally had some consideration.","Not to mention the various high-tech weapons in her space, the most important thing was that if Nan Qi poisoned the food and wine, with her by his side, Mo Jiuye would have an extra layer of protection.","In order to persuade Mo Jiuye, He Zhiran really went all out.","Taking advantage of her sleeve to conceal her actions, she took out a mini pistol from her space.","She placed the gun in front of Mo Jiuye.","\"Do you believe that even with your skills, you cannot escape my weapon?\"","Mo Jiuye looked at the piece of iron in front of him not even as big as his palm, and picked it up with great interest to play with it.","Seeing that his hand touched the trigger, He Zhiran hurriedly reminded him verbally.","\"That's the switch, don't mess with it.\"","Mo Jiuye was very obedient, and his fingers immediately left the trigger position.","He looked up at He Zhiran, \"I didn't see that such a small piece of iron could have such great power?\"","In the current environment, He Zhiran could not demonstrate the power of the mini pistol to Mo Jiuye either, so she could only explain patiently.","\"Cao Ren's death was caused by a similar weapon.\"","He Zhiran had already implicitly admitted that Cao Ren's death was her doing.","Speaking of Cao Ren's death, Mo Jiuye had witnessed the entire assassination process with his own eyes."]},{"number":81,"title":"Chapter 81: Yuanyang Wine Pot","paragraphs":["However, the weapon He Zhiran had used to kill someone at that time was much bigger than this mini handgun. Moreover, the might of that weapon was still vivid in his mind. Even he couldn't figure out how that hidden weapon was shot out, which showed how fast it was.","Seeing Mo Jiuye was already attracted by this mini handgun, He Zhiran intended to press the advantage.","\"You've seen my weapon. With me following you, not only will I not become a burden, but I can also assist you.\"","Mo Jiuye was still hesitating.","He Zhiran continued persuading: \"Think about my medical skills. In case Nan Qi stealthily puts something nasty in the food and drinks, I would be able to detect it the first time, right?\"","Hearing her speak plausibly, Mo Jiuye finally compromised.","\"You can come with me. But if we encounter any danger, saving your own life is the most important thing. Don't mind me, got it?\"","He Zhiran nodded quickly: \"Got it, got it. Don't worry, I will definitely not put myself in any danger.\"","After settling the matter, the two returned to bed again. Despite neither of them having any shred of drowsiness, they still tried hard to maintain a posture, for fear of any accidental physical contact...","Early next morning, Peng Wang indeed didn't arrange to continue rushing on the journey.","For this reason, everyone was a little puzzled.","However, no one took the initiative to ask the reason. Of course they were happy to have an extra day of rest at the inn.","It wasn't until close to noon when a carriage arrived outside the inn.","The coachman came in to invite Mo Jiuye, and the officers didn't show any intention of stopping him. Then everyone suddenly realized why they didn't continue the journey today, and it turned out to be related to Mo Jiuye!","They just didn't know who would have such great power to not only make them halt the journey temporarily, but also to send a carriage to pick up the convicted felon.","Mo's old lady worriedly held Mo Jiuye's arm.","\"Jiuye?\"","Mo Jiuye patted Mo's old lady's arm lightly: \"Mother, don't worry. An acquaintance has prepared a farewell dinner for your son. I'll go and come back soon.\"","Although Mo's old lady felt worried in her heart, after all she was someone who had seen the world.","She deeply knew she couldn't stop her son's footsteps.","Therefore she earnestly exhorted: \"You're no longer the prestigious Duke Who Protects the Country. Don't stick your neck out for things.\"","\"Mother, don't worry. I'm going with my husband, nothing will happen.\"","In order to let her mother-in-law feel at ease, He Zhiran took the initiative to help Mo Jiuye explain.","Hearing He Zhiran would accompany her son together, Mo's old lady felt a little more assured.","\"Alright, you two watch out for each other when you're outside.\"","After appeasing Mo's old lady, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye got on the carriage together.","The coachman took a deep look at He Zhiran, seeming wanting to say something but hesitated.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran tacitly chose to ignore him.","The carriage all the way faced no obstacles and soon arrived at Tianfu Restaurant.","Nan Qi personally welcomed them at the door.","To his surprise, He Zhiran had come along as well.","Stunned for a moment, Nan Qi soon put on an innocent smile.","\"Sister-in-law coming works out just great. I specially ordered nourishing soup suitable for women to supplement the body.\"","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran also put on a good show, nodded gratefully to Nan Qi, then followed him upstairs to the private room.","The two guards in front of the private room door quickly gave way when they saw their master come.","Nan Qi ordered the guards: \"Without this king's order, no one is allowed to come in and disturb.\"","\"Yes.\"","Upon entering the private room, the only things on the table were eight dishes with one soup, and an exquisite wine jug.","The dishes contained both meat and vegetable, looking quite good, showing Nan Qi had really spent great efforts.","However, He Zhiran actually didn't care about the dishes. Her full attention was placed on that wine jug.","For ordinary people this wine jug merely looked a bit valuable. But with just a glance, He Zhiran was able to detect its intricacy.","If she didn't recognize wrongly, this was the Mandarin Duck wine jug that frequently appeared in period TV dramas in her previous life.","There were two layers inside the jug. At the handle place there was an extremely small mechanism button. Those who knew about it could control whether poisoned wine or non-poisoned wine would pour out from the jug.","He Zhiran sneered to herself inwardly. In order to take Mo Jiuyi's life, no scheme was too much for Nan Qi!","Today Nan Qi's confidence could be said to be brimming. He smilingly asked them to sit down.","He Zhiran deliberately chose the seat closest to the Mandarin Duck wine jug.","Nan Qi said some polite remarks, then promptly got up to take the wine jug, but was overtaken by He Zhiran first.","\"Duke being able to invite my husband and I to dine disregarding criticism is the greatest honor to us as a couple. How could we let you personally pour the wine?\"","As He Zhiran spoke, she went directly to his side without even glancing at Nan Qi's about-to-be-constipated face. First she filled the wine cups.","Nan Qi stared fixedly at He Zhiran's hand holding the wine jug. Seeing she didn't press that button, he felt slightly relieved.","He Zhiran pretended not to notice Nan Qi's fleeting constipated expression and soon refilled Mo Jiuye's cup.","In order to verify whether the wine cup had poison, she deliberately said loudly: \"This wine smells so fragrant. What a pity I don't drink. I'll just take the liberty of smelling it.\"","As she talked, she swiftly picked up Mo Jiuye's cup and held it under her nose to sniff, then put it back after making sure there was no problem.","\"Excuse me for my bad lifelong habit since young to like smelling good wine despite not drinking.\"","The corner of Nan Qi's mouth twitched.","\"It doesn't matter. There's no outsider here. Sister-in-law please feel at ease.\"","Mo Jiuye could naturally understand He Zhiran's series of actions telling him the wine was fine.","Thus, Mo Jiuye took the initiative to lift the wine cup.","\"Thank Duke Nan for not despising me for my convicted status and seeing me off. Jiuye will drink first to you.\"","Seeing Mo Jiuye drink all of the wine in one gulp, Nan Qi didn't equivocate and finished it in one go too.","Seeing Nan Qi about to take the wine jug again, He Zhiran promptly stood up and grasped the wine jug in her hand.","\"I'll pour.\"","Seeing He Zhiran still didn't press that mechanism button, Nan Qi guessed she shouldn't have discovered anything odd about the wine jug.","Only problem was, with her hugging the wine jug refusing to let go, how could he pour the poisoned wine into Mo Jiuye's cup?","Thinking of this, Nan Qi felt vexed in his heart.","However, no matter how he indicated he wanted to personally pour wine for this brother, He Zhiran always managed to snatch the wine jug first somehow.","At the same time, He Zhiran inspected every dish on the table and gave Mo Jiuye a signal after confirming no issue with the food for him to eat to his heart's content without worries.","Soon, the non-poisoned portion of wine in the jug got completely poured out by He Zhiran.","Seeing there was no change in Mo Jiuye's complexion, she could ascertain he had decent capacity for liquor.","As for Nan Qi, although he still sat upright, his face had turned red.","If these two competed in drinking, Nan Qi would definitely be the first to pass out."]},{"number":82,"title":"Chapter 82: I Mo Jiuye is the direct blood of the Mo family","paragraphs":["He Zhiran deliberately shook the wine pot in her hand: \"Your Highness, the wine is gone.\"","At this moment, Nan Qi hated that he couldn't kick He Zhiran out of the window, however, his purpose had not yet been achieved, he had to continue to endure.","\"Come, bring another pot of wine.\"","Unfortunately, another pot of wine would not be a mandarin duck-shaped wine pot anymore.","Nan Qi thought that when the new wine pot was delivered, He Zhiran would no longer have to hold on to the mandarin duck wine pot, and he would always find a chance to pour the poisoned wine into Mo Jiuye's cup.","Who knew that He Zhiran didn't play by the rules at all, and didn't even help them pour the wine...","Not only that, she also put the wine pot by her side.","\"I've been busy for half a day, and I'm really a little hungry.\"","With that said, she began to eat the dishes on the table with gusto.","Nan Qi almost died of anger by He Zhiran.","For the sake of the overall situation, he tried his best to suppress the anger in his heart and continued to drink with Mo Jiuye.","Mo Jiuye felt that the time was almost right, so he took the initiative to say:","\"Do you still remember the crescent-shaped birthmark on my left shoulder?\"","Nan Qi, who was slightly drunk, nodded: \"Of course I remember, when we were young we often secretly ran to Father Emperor's hot spring pool to bathe, and I said that your birthmark looks very special.\"","Mo Jiuye carefully observed the changes in Nan Qi's expression and continued:","\"Do you know what legend says about this birthmark?\"","Nan Qi raised his eyebrows: \"It's just a birthmark, what else can it say?\"","Mo Jiuye said in a deep voice: \"That is the unique mark that only Mo Family men have. For generations of Mo Family men, as long as they are males, they will have this crescent-shaped birthmark on their left shoulder after birth.\"","Nan Qi was stunned.","\"Are you saying this is a birthmark that only Mo Family men have?\"","\"That's right, the crescent-shaped birthmark is the unique mark of Mo Family men.\" Mo Jiuye affirmed.","Nan Qi had fallen into thought. He didn't know why Mo Jiuye would mention the birthmark to him. Could it be that he knew something?","Soon, Nan Qi completely changed his face.","\"What exactly do you know?\"","Mo Jiuye still maintained his calm appearance.","\"Although you and I can no longer continue to be intimate friends who talk about everything like before, I, Mo Jiuye, have always been frank and upright, especially between you and me, I don't want any misunderstandings.","I believe my words are very clear. I also hope that the target of my grudge does not exist for you.\"","After a pause, Mo Jiuye got up: \"I have said everything, I believe you are a smart person who will understand these things.\"","Seeing that Mo Jiuye was about to leave, Nan Qi immediately stopped him.","\"Wait, make it clear before you go.\"","Mo Jiuye had already pulled He Zhiran to the door. Hearing Nan Qi's voice, they both stopped.","Mo Jiuye turned his head: \"Haven't I made it clear enough?\"","Nan Qi still did not give up.","\"Tell me, what do you know?\"","Mo Jiuye could now confirm that what He Zhiran had told him about the possibility of Nan Qi being switched at birth did exist, and Nan Qi wanted to kill him because of this.","Although he had eliminated the misunderstanding of being switched, he had exposed the fact that he knew the other's secrets, going around in circles, there would always be reasons for the other to kill him.","Left with no other choice, Mo Jiuye had to go back to his seat.","\"What I can tell you now is that I've known about this since I was very young. I treated you as a brother, whether true or false, I never mentioned it to outsiders.","If it wasn't for you sending someone to kill me, even if I was facing you in person, I wouldn't have mentioned it.\"","Nan Qi hugged his head with both hands, his eyes had already turned crimson.","In order to prevent him from making reckless moves out of desperation, He Zhiran casually picked up the mandarin duck wine pot on the table.","Right in front of Nan Qi, she pressed the mechanism button and poured out a cup of poisoned wine.","\"Prince Nan, this wine pot of yours is indeed good, it must be invaluable, right?\"","Nan Qi stared wide-eyed at He Zhiran in disbelief.","\"You......\"","He Zhiran smiled, but the smile did not reach her eyes.","\"Prince Nan went through a lot of trouble to get my husband's life. This mandarin duck wine pot must have been very difficult to obtain, right?\"","Nan Qi almost spit out a mouthful of old blood. If it wasn't for his fear of Mo Jiuye, he would have killed this hateful woman without hesitation.","He Zhiran ignored Nan Qi's murderous gaze and calmly took out a small paper bag from her sleeve.","She opened the small paper bag to reveal a white powder inside.","\"Has Prince Nan ever heard of a poison called Seven Days Overturn?\"","Nan Qi pointed at the bag of medicine powder in disbelief and asked, \"Is this Seven Days Overturn?\"","The highly toxic Seven Days Overturn was very precious in Da Shun. This was absolutely the best choice for a silent kill.","As the name suggests, those who are poisoned by it will not have any discomfort. They will die on the seventh day without any signs or symptoms.","Even doctors can't figure out the cause of death.","Thinking of this, Nan Qi was frightened and thought that if he had really been poisoned, death would have been inevitable...","He Zhiran did not answer directly, but asked rhetorically: \"If I had put this medicinal powder in your wine glass just now, who would have known that you died at my hands?\"","After a pause, He Zhiran continued: \"If it wasn't for my husband's kindness towards your brotherly affection, do you think you could have lived to see the eighth day?\"","In fact, the bag of powder in He Zhiran’s hand was just ordinary flour. She had indeed heard of Seven Days Overturn, but she didn’t have the formula for making it. Moreover, she heard that this kind of poison was extremely precious, and had even become unavailable regardless of price.","She did this only to let Nan Qi know that they did not intend to kill him, let alone spread his secrets.","Although Mo Jiuye didn't know where He Zhiran got the Seven Days Overturn from, he took the opportunity to say:","\"With my abilities, it would not be difficult for me to let you take this Seven Days Overturn silently.","Out of our past affection, I'll let you off today, and I also hope you'll do the same.\"","After listening to their words, Nan Qi had no choice but to reconsider the credibility between him and Mo Jiuye.","No matter from which perspective the analysis was made, what Mo Jiuye said was the truth.","First of all, he understood Mo Jiuye's character very well. Mo Jiuye was an upright gentleman.","He had known his secret for a long time, and had not revealed the slightest bit to outsiders.","This not only showed that Mo Jiuye had been protecting him in the past, but also proved that the person who was switched with him was indeed not Mo Jiuye."]},{"number":83,"title":"Chapter 83: I still owe you a wedding night.","paragraphs":["As for where exactly things had gone wrong, Nan Qi had no way of knowing and could only continue to investigate later.","Now that Mo Jiuye had gotten hold of the Seven Days Fall that was so advantageous to him, even though he'd had such a good opportunity earlier, he hadn't made a move against Nan Qi.","All of this pointed to one issue - Mo Jiuye cherished dearly the brotherly affection they had once shared.","After quite some time, Nan Qi slowly stood up and opened the door with his own hand.","\"Let's go. I hope you can forget about today's matters.\"","Although Nan Qi's words were simple, they both understood that he would not go after Mo Jiuye again in the future.","Having accomplished their purpose in coming, He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye left the private room without any reluctance.","The two had just walked downstairs to the first floor when they saw Fei Nanyu sitting there alone, drinking.","Fei Nanyu was facing the direction of the staircase. Catching sight of them immediately, he visibly relaxed.","Then he nodded slightly at the two in greeting, without saying much else.","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye likewise nodded back at Fei Nanyu before leaving the restaurant.","The driver had only received orders to bring them here earlier and had no idea these two would still be alive to leave. So the carriage had long since been brought 'round back.","In any case, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran hadn't intended to let Nan Qi's people drive them back. So the two strolled leisurely through the streets of Pingyuan County.","Mo Jiuye still couldn't resist his curiosity and asked,","\"Do you really have the Seven Days Fall?\"","He Zhiran smiled wryly. Feeling they were no longer being tailed by Nan Qi's men, she took out that little paper package again.","Opening the package, she lightly blew on its contents. The white powder instantly dispersed, kicking up a cloud of white dust...","\"This is just a smokescreen - plain flour.\"","Mo Jiuye was truly convinced. He didn't know what else this woman had stored up in her brain to even think up a solution like this.","For the first time before He Zhiran, a smile spread across his face, his tone unconsciously gentle and doting,","\"You really are quite something.\"","He Zhiran was rather smug. \"Of course! I have tricks aplenty up my sleeve.\"","Just then, as He Zhiran was getting a bit complacent, a carriage came careening down the busy street.","Mo Jiuye reflexively pulled He Zhiran into his embrace, lifting her up as he swiftly dodged to the side.","They managed to avoid the oncoming carriage, but because of the force of Mo Jiuye's movement, He Zhiran lost her balance, her face ending up right against his.","The sudden warmth made Mo Jiuye's heart start racing uncontrollably.","Moreover, he was being completely honest with himself that he really liked this feeling.","Even when the two had steadily gotten to their feet, he still didn't let go of He Zhiran, and instead hoped they could stay frozen in this position forever.","He Zhiran felt it too - her body seemed to have been suddenly jolted with electricity, numb and tingling all over.","When she raised her eyes, all she saw was Mo Jiuye's handsome visage magnified before her.","He Zhiran could feel her face starting to burn. Wanting to avoid an embarrassing situation, she hurriedly pushed against the man still holding her.","Mo Jiuye snapped back to his senses then. Flushing, he hastily removed his arms from her waist.","The two simultaneously turned their heads aside, not daring to look at one another.","After a long awkward silence, Mo Jiuye was the first to speak. \"Let's go. We should head back.\"","\"Oh!\" He Zhiran stuck close by Mo Jiuye's side as they walked. She couldn't have dreamed that even she would have a shy side.","The two maintained their silence all along the way back. After who knew how long, they finally returned to the inn.","Seeing them come back safe and sound, the Mo family attendants finally felt the huge rock in their hearts drop.","Wanting to avoid any more awkward contact with Mo Jiuye, He Zhiran hurried off to chat with her sisters-in-law.","Not until nightfall when they returned to their room were the two forced to face one another again.","The room was so quiet all they could hear was the thumping of each other's hearts.","In the end, it was still Mo Jiuye who broke the silence.","\"Um... You should rest early!\"","\"Mm!\" He Zhiran promptly buried herself under the quilt on her side of the bed, sticking close to the wall.","Likewise, Mo Jiuye lay at the edge of the bed, as long as he didn't fall off it was fine.","Perhaps because of the alcohol he'd had at lunch, Mo Jiuye slept more heavily than usual tonight.","Not wanting her insomnia to affect their journey tomorrow, He Zhiran had purposefully taken a sleeping pill before bed.","As a result, it was the first night the two managed to sleep so soundly at the same time.","Although she'd had the sleeping pill, He Zhiran's biological clock was still perfectly accurate.","At the usual hour she typically rose, she already felt awake.","But today was different than normal. She felt as if she were enveloped in a giant furnace.","With eyes still shut, she carefully sensed that her face seemed to be pressed against something hard while her body felt weighted down by something on top.","She suddenly opened her eyes. What filled her vision was surprisingly a man's chest.","Her face was plastered right against it. The thing weighing down her body turned out to be Mo Jiuye's arm and one leg.","Glancing down at her own somewhat numb arm, she saw it was wrapped around Mo Jiuye's waist.","Good heavens! She'd actually spent the entire night snuggling with this man.","Wanting to avoid an embarrassing situation, He Zhiran gingerly freed her arm from Mo Jiuye's waist and slowly shifted her body backward.","In truth, Mo Jiuye had already woken up.","Despite being full grown men, this was still his first time being so intimately close to a woman. Although he didn't dislike the feeling, he feared He Zhiran would be repulsed.","Rather than face what would surely be an awkward situation or bring an end to this delightful sensation, Mo Jiuye chose to pretend he was still sleeping.","But to He Zhiran, the more careful she tried to be, the more nervous she became. As she moved, her knee happened to bump into something it shouldn't have.","Having lived twenty-four celibate years in her past life, she was still fairly knowledgeable about such matters.","He Zhiran couldn't help crying out in surprise.","At the same time, Mo Jiuye couldn't restrain a muffled grunt.","Their eyes met. The two simultaneously shifted backwards.","Fortunately for He Zhiran, there was a wall right behind her so moving with large motions posed no problem.","Mo Jiuye, on the other hand, had terrible luck. Putting strength into shifting back, his whole body tumbled straight onto the floor.","Luckily his martial arts skills came in handy. With a swift flip, he landed steadily, sparing himself embarrassment before He Zhiran.","Seeing Mo Jiuye frozen there like an ignorant youth, He Zhiran kind of wanted to laugh.","But she still forcibly controlled herself.","To diffuse the awkwardness, the words slipped from her mouth,","\"There's nothing strange about a married couple cuddling. Don't get so tense.\"","For a man's man like Mo Jiuye, this remark was somewhat grating to his ears.","Shouldn't he be the one saying this instead of having his words snatched away by this woman?","\"I know I still owe you a perfect wedding night full of nuptial bliss. Once things settle down in the Northwest, I will definitely make it up to you.\"","As Mo Jiuye spoke, it was as if a tiny voice inside him cried out:","If you're willing, I could make up that wedding night right now..."]},{"number":84,"title":"Chapter 84: It's My Fault You got the wrong Idea.","paragraphs":["He Zhiran was stunned.","She vigorously cleaned out her ears, feeling that she must have misheard.","Her impression of Mo Jiuye had always been that he was aloof, profound, taciturn and even shy at times.","If she hadn't heard it with her own ears just now, she really wouldn't have believed that Mo Jiuye was capable of saying something like this.","Besides, when did I ever ask you to make up for our wedding night?","Did I say something wrong that made you misunderstand? It's my fault if I gave you the wrong idea...","But when she thought about it carefully, she didn't actually mind physical contact with Mo Jiuye.","Could it be that she was starting to like him?","That wasn't possible - they had only known each other for a few days!","There was no way she could start to like someone so quickly.","Although in her past life she had idolized Mo Jiuye, the definition of an idol was completely different from that of a lover.","For a moment, He Zhiran felt her thoughts descend into chaos.","However, she had never considered avoiding the issue.","As a modern woman, she had always dared to love and hate openly. It was just that right now, she still wasn't sure exactly what her feelings were.","He Zhiran vigorously shook her head, desperately trying to keep a clear mind.","No matter how things developed between her and Mo Jiuye, everything would follow its own course...","\"I'm going to go out and see when we'll be setting off.\" In order to alleviate the awkwardness, He Zhiran hastily changed the subject.","Seeing her flee as though she were flying, the tense mood that Mo Jiuye was in finally eased up a bit.","After a simple breakfast and getting everything packed up neatly, Peng Wang gave an order and everyone continued on their journey.","Unexpectedly, when they arrived at the city gate, they encountered Fei Nanyu again.","Upon seeing the exiled entourage, Fei Nanyu walked over to meet them. It was obvious that he had been intentionally waiting here.","Fei Nanyu also recognized Peng Wang as the man who had been with He Zhiran when she helped get him out of trouble that day.","Fei Nanyu clasped his hands towards Peng Wang and exchanged some pleasantries, before immediately heading towards the group of Mozi followers. His target was very clearly the couple's direction.","Mo Jiuye immediately became vigilant, thinking first that Fei Nanyu had likely been sent by the King of Qi.","When Fei Nanyu reached them, he stopped in front of the two.","\"Madam Mo, I know that your journey into exile is long and arduous.\" As he spoke, he took out a stack of silver notes from his robe.","\"This is a token of my regard, and I hope it can help you out a little.\"","He Zhiran could see that the silver notes Fei Nanyu held were all 100 taels each, with about ten notes total. That meant Fei Nanyu was gifting them about 1,000 taels of silver.","For ordinary exiled prisoners, 1,000 taels of silver was definitely a huge sum.","But for He Zhiran, who controlled the assets of the entire state treasury, it truly was nothing.","The fact that Fei Nanyu could take out so much silver at once meant that it must have been a reward from Nan Qi.","No matter how highly Nan Qi thought of Fei Nanyu, he would not have given him too much silver after just getting to know him briefly.","For Fei Nanyu to be able to take out this much silver to give to her at one time, he had probably emptied out all he had.","He Zhiran was grateful for this point - it showed that Fei Nanyu was someone who knew how to be thankful.","However, she could not accept Fei Nanyu's silver notes.","The only reason Fei Nanyu was gifting her with so much silver was to repay her for helping him out that day.","If he was just an ordinary person it would be fine, but Fei Nanyu was no ordinary person - he would become the future emperor.","He Zhiran would not be stupid enough to write off her debt of gratitude to Fei Nanyu with 1,000 taels of silver.","Although she didn't know whether there would be any more interactions between them in the future, she wanted to gamble on Fei Nanyu's humanity.","After all, Mo Jiuye's fate in this life had already changed. Being exonerated after death was very different from being cleared of injustice while still alive.","And the person most likely to help clear Mo Jiuye's name while he was still living was none other than Fei Nanyu.","Since He Zhiran did not reach out to take the silver, she firmly declined: \"Mr. Fei, I cannot accept this silver. You should take it back!\"","Yet Fei Nanyu persisted.","\"Madam Mo, you may not know this, but if it weren't for your help that day, I'm afraid I wouldn't even have had the ability to buy my late father a coffin.","I will forever remember your great kindness, and I only hope that you will accept this token of thanks to set my mind at ease.\"","Set your mind at ease?","How could that be possible? I want you to remember this debt of gratitude for the rest of your life...","As He Zhiran muttered inwardly, she resolutely pushed the silver notes back towards him.","Seeing this, Mo Jiuye stepped forward and said, \"Sir, my wife has always been stubborn. Since she said she won't accept it, she definitely won't. Please don't make things difficult for her.\"","Seeing how the couple was rejecting the proffered silver, everyone felt it was a pity on their behalf.","Having 1,000 taels of silver by their side during their exile would solve any problems they might face, likely lasting them all the way until they reached the northwest.","They really didn't understand why the couple didn't want so much silver.","The other wives watched anxiously, but they all knew He Zhiran always had her own reasons for things. So without saying anything, they could only stare longingly as the silver notes were refused.","Fei Nanyu realized his silver would not be making its way into their hands today. He smiled helplessly and put the notes back into his robe.","\"Since that's the case, I won't force you.\"","As he spoke, Fei Nanyu leaned forward and whispered into Mo Jiuye's ear, \"If I gain the power, I will definitely help exonerate you.\"","Although his voice was soft, He Zhiran managed to catch part of what he said.","This was the assurance she wanted from Fei Nanyu - it was far more valuable than 1,000 taels of silver.","Mo Jiuye solemnly nodded once and likewise whispered softly, \"Then thank you in advance, Mr. Fei.\"","Fei Nanyu lightly patted Mo Jiuye's shoulder and strode away with large steps.","The group continued on, hurrying along for three straight days until the afternoon of the fourth day. The weather had become exceptionally muggy.","Old Man Heaven picked this moment to change his temper. The previously clear skies gradually became filled with dark clouds after a fierce gust of wind.","Zhou Laoba hurried to catch up with Peng Wang at the rear of the group.","\"Boss, it's going to rain.\"","Peng Wang looked up at the sky full of clouds and said, \"This rain doesn't look like it'll be small. Go on for another ten li and there's a village. Let's quicken our pace and take shelter from the rain at one of the villagers' homes.\"","\"Alright.\" Zhou Laoba acknowledged him then turned and shouted at the crowd: \"Hurry it up, or the whip will be waiting for anyone who falls behind!\"","Anxious as well, no one wanted to get caught in the rain. Urged on by Zhou Laoba's yell, they obediently picked up the pace.","It seemed Heaven was not on their side, for just after they had gone a short distance, large raindrops began pelting down.","To make matters worse, they were surrounded by open country without any place to take shelter.","Left with no other choice, Peng Wang could only order them to keep moving forward.","The rain grew heavier and heavier, pouring down relentlessly.","The officers were alright - when they had set out from the capital, each of them had prepared an oiled-paper umbrella. But they, the exiled prisoners, were not so fortunate and had no rain gear at all."]},{"number":85,"title":"Chapter 85: The Best Thing to do in a flood is to go high.","paragraphs":["The grass hats on the heads of the Mohist people were soon soaked through, and the only function they could still serve was to prevent the rain from falling directly on their faces.","He Zhiran came up with an expedient plan for everyone to open up the tents a little wider to serve as temporary shelter from the rain.","The dirt road beneath their feet was also becoming increasingly slippery.","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye both ran to Old Lady Mo, afraid that she might accidentally slip and fall.","Indeed, walking was difficult for Old Lady Mo. Only with the support of her son and daughter-in-law did she feel balanced.","The sisters-in-law and Mo Hanyue also helped each other walk, tightly holding on to one another. Not only that, but everyone tried their best to quicken their pace.","The other families also followed the example of the Mohist people, keeping up with their footsteps.","At this moment, things were most difficult for the He family.","Not only were they usually unable to eat their fill or sleep soundly, they also had no tools to fend off the rain. Now they still had to push that heavy wooden cart forward with great difficulty.","Their current plight was a perfect embodiment of the common saying: when it rains, it pours.","What was even more annoying was that at this moment, the wooden cart got stuck in the mud.","With He Zhiyuan being the only adult man in the He family, and the others being elderly, weak, women, and children, even with several people coming to help, they were unable to pull the cart out.","The officers were already in a hurry to get going. Seeing the He family falling behind, they went up without hesitation and whipped them a few times.","It made the He family members cry out in pain.","Considering that there were also the Mohist family’s food, vegetables and some daily necessities on the wooden cart,","Mo Jiuye walked with large strides towards the cart.","Seeing Mo Jiuye come over, the He family immediately stopped screaming.","Mo Jiuye didn’t even glance at them. He grasped the cart handle tightly with both hands. With a force, he single-handedly pulled the cart out.","Seeing that Mo Jiuye had already pulled the cart away, He Zhiyuan wiped the rain from his face and hurried to catch up, very proactively helping to push the cart.","Thanks to Mo Jiuye’s actions, the He family was finally able to keep up.","He Zhiyuan looked at the lonely, proud figure ahead.","“Thank you for helping.”","Mo Jiuye hadn’t pulled the cart to help the He family.","Hearing He Zhiyuan’s thanks, he said coldly, “I did it for my own family's supplies. Don't think too much.”","He Zhiyuan’s thanks came from the bottom of his heart. No matter what Mo Jiuye's attitude was in pulling the cart, after all he had helped resolve a crisis for the He family.","\"In any case, I have to thank you this time.\"","Mo Jiuye didn't speak again, but lowered his head to keep pulling the cart...","The heavy rain showed no signs of stopping at all.","The water on the road soon rose above everyone's ankles.","He Zhiran inexplicably felt a sense of crisis rising in her heart.","In ancient times, roads had no drainage facilities. If the heavy rain continued, it was hard to prevent some unpredictable disasters from happening.","At this time, Peng Wang pointed to the front and said, \"Everyone hurry up. The village ahead is not far away.\"","He Zhiran looked in the direction Peng Wang was pointing.","Faintly visible through the rain was a village.","As if seeing hope, everyone quickened their pace.","Soon, following Peng Wang, they arrived at the entrance to the village.","Fortunately, the accumulated water here was not as deep as on the road.","Peng Wang didn't seem unfamiliar with this village. He directly led everyone along the road towards the inside. Soon he stopped in front of a rather large courtyard and went up to knock on the door.","\"Is Village Chief Liu in?\"","Perhaps due to the heavy rain, Peng Wang shouted several times but no one responded.","With no other choice, he opened the door and entered himself.","Not long after Peng Wang entered, the door opened again. Coming out with him was an old man who looked fifty or sixty years old.","Peng Wang pointed to the crowd at the door and said: “Village Chief Liu, you just arrange a place for us to take shelter from the rain.”","Village Chief Liu looked at so many people standing outside, instantly speechless.","“Your Honor, I’m afraid my house doesn’t have room for so many people!”","“Village Chief Liu, as long as it shelters from the rain, they can squeeze together, and it will be no problem.” Not wanting to give Village Chief Liu a chance to refuse, Peng Wang finished speaking and waved for everyone to enter the yard.","Village Chief Liu was helpless, and could only open the doors to his family’s two side rooms.","“These are the only two empty rooms. I'll leave it to you to handle, Your Honor!”","Peng Wang chose a room for himself and the officers, and the rest of the people all entered the other wing room.","Seeing a place to shelter from the rain, the people swarmed inside. Fortunately, the size of the wing room was not small. After all the prisoners entered, although they could only stand shoulder to shoulder, at least they no longer had to stand in the rain.","The heavy rain still showed no signs of stopping or weakening. The accumulated water in Village Chief Liu's yard had already started to deepen, and there were even signs of it seeping into the house.","Standing at the door, the Fang family shouted, “Oh no, rainwater is flowing into the house!”","He Zhiran inexplicably felt a wave of panic stirring in her heart.","She tugged at Mo Jiuye’s sleeve at her side and said in a low voice, “I feel we can’t stay here to take shelter from the rain.”","At this moment, Mo Jiuye also frowned.","“Yeah, I’m worried that if the heavy rain continues, flooding is very likely to occur here.”","He Zhiran continued, “I just saw a mountain south of the village. We’d still be safer going there.”","Mo Jiuye pondered for a moment, then nodded, \"I’ll go discuss with Eldest Brother Peng right away to see if he agrees.\"","Peng Wang sat on the only chair in the wing room, looking bitterly at the still overcast sky.","Seeing Mo Jiuye come, he took the initiative to ask: “Brother, it’s too cramped over there. Why not squeeze over here with us for now?”","Mo Jiuye didn’t have the heart to squeeze together here at all. He got straight to the point.","“Eldest Brother Peng, if this rain keeps up, I'm afraid the whole village will be submerged in just a few hours.”","Upon hearing Mo Jiuye’s words, Peng Wang unconsciously glanced at the accumulated water in the yard. Indeed, it was much deeper than when they first arrived here. Mo Jiuye’s words were not alarmist.","“So, what do you suggest we do?”","Mo Jiuye pointed to the nearby mountain top,","“When there’s flooding, the best thing to do is go to high ground.”","Although Peng Wang knew Mo Jiuye was reasonable, he still hesitated.","Apart from not knowing if what Mo Jiuye said would actually happen, even if there really was flooding, with so many people going up the mountain, what if they couldn’t find a place to take shelter from the rain? They’d only get soaked to death.","Peng Wang directly expressed his doubts,","“Brother, if we can’t find a place to shelter from the rain on the mountain, what should we do?”","Originally thinking Peng Wang was a wise man, who knew he would make such a foolish decision at this critical moment?","“Eldest Brother Peng, there are two choices: one is we might get soaked by rain on the mountain; the other is to stay at the foot of the mountain and be washed away by the flood.”","At this point, Mo Jiuye felt it necessary to portray the situation more gravely.","Peng Wang also knew it was reasonable, but he still held a trace of wishful thinking. What if the rain stopped? Wouldn’t they have gone through the trouble for nothing?"]},{"number":86,"title":"Chapter 86: Just Listen to your brother.","paragraphs":["\"Brother, should we observe a little longer?\" Mo Jiuye saw that Peng Wang was determined, so he could only remind helplessly.","\"I hope Brother Peng can make a decision before it gets dark, otherwise, it will be even harder for us to go up the mountain.\"","Peng Wang nodded: \"Well, in half a hour, if it is still raining, then I'll listen to you and we'll go up the mountain.\"","Mo Jiuye went back and told He Zhiran about Peng Wang's decision, then returned to the wing room where the yamen runners were.","Not only was it convenient here to observe the rain, but most importantly, he could continue to persuade Peng Wang to lead everyone up the mountain.","The half hour Peng Wang mentioned passed quickly, and not only did the rain show no signs of weakening, but it was falling even harder.","The rainwater had completely flooded into the wing room.","Mo Jiuye took the opportunity to say, \"Brother Peng, for everyone's safety, we must go up the mountain immediately.\"","Peng Wang gritted his teeth: \"Fine, I'll listen to you, brother.\"","After saying that, he ordered the yamen runners to tell the people in the other wing room to pack up and set off immediately.","He Zhiran had already deeply realized the seriousness of the problem. She ran to Peng Wang and said,","\"Brother Peng, you'd better advise Li Zheng to notify all the villagers to go up the mountain, or find other high ground, they must not continue to stay here.\"","He Zhiran's words still carried some weight to Peng Wang. As everyone was packing up in puzzlement, he knocked on Liu Li Zheng's door again.","He Zhiran didn't know exactly how Peng Wang persuaded them, but when he came out of Li Zheng's house, his face showed some helplessness.","He had done what he should, Peng Wang didn't feel guilty. He ordered the prisoners who had bewildered looks on their faces to go up the mountain again.","Seeing the sisters-in-law coming out of the wing rooms, still hugging their luggage tightly.","He Zhiran advised: \"Sisters, these have all been soaked by the rain, it's better not to bring them along.\"","\"Sister-in-law He, these beddings were hard to obtain, they can still be used after drying, Second Sister-in-law is not afraid of hardship and can bring them along.\"","\"Yes, Sister-in-law He, Fifth Sister-in-law can too, she's not afraid of hardship either.\"","\"Seventh Sister-in-law also can.\"","\"... \"","He Zhiran knew that the sisters-in-law could be said to have almost all been nobles in the capital city before. Their awareness of natural disasters was not very high.","Helplessly, she could only patiently reason with them.","\"Sisters, you felt it just now when rushing here, how difficult it was to move forward carrying weight on this muddy road. The mountain road is even more so. With one careless step, your whole person could slide down.","It is really not wise to bring such heavy baggage that is useless now.\"","Although the sisters-in-law knew He Zhiran was right, they were still reluctant to leave their belongings behind.","Seeing their tangled expressions, Old Lady Mo said heavily, \"You should all listen to the He family girl.\"","Since the mother-in-law had spoken, the sisters-in-law could only resentfully put their luggage in the wing rooms.","The Fang and Xie families were sensible. Although they didn't know why He Zhiran asked everyone to abandon their luggage, they just habitually imitated her actions.","Everyone put their luggage in the wing rooms completely. Listening to He Zhiran, they only brought out the tents.","Seeing everyone was ready, Peng Wang gave the order and they set off in the rain.","They walked with difficulty on the muddy village road. No one could understand Peng Wang's approach, but they didn't dare to complain and could only follow resentfully behind him with stomachs full of grievances.","When no one was paying attention to her, He Zhiran purchased two bags of charcoal from Taobao mall, wrapped them tightly in oilcloth, and took them out of her space.","Of the entire team, apart from He Zhiran carrying an oilcloth package on her back, the rest only held up a tent to shelter from the rain.","Mo Jiuye was attentive. With one glance, he noticed He Zhiran's big package. He hurriedly took it over and put it on his own back.","Soon, everyone arrived at the foot of the mountain and found a small path up the mountain. Mo Jiuye took the lead in front to open up the path for everyone.","The others supported each other as they followed behind.","It was most difficult for the He family, who had to take the paralyzed He Ming with them up the mountain. The difficulty was too great.","In order not to let the He family affect the pace, He Zhiran took the initiative to give them a suggestion.","That was to remove the boards from the wooden cart and tie He Ming to it, then pull it along with ropes.","Even the yamen runners couldn't ignore the greater good now and took the initiative to provide hemp ropes.","Even so, the He family still fell far behind the team.","Fortunately, when everyone reached halfway up the mountain, they discovered there was a mountain depression not far ahead.","In He Zhiran's understanding of danger, that place was most suitable for everyone to take temporary shelter.","Although there was no place for shelter from the wind and rain, the advantage was that there were no trees there. Even if there was lightning, there would not be accidents.","In addition, she also considered the possibility of landslides in this kind of weather.","So sheltering from the floodwaters in the mountain depression was the best position.","So she took the initiative to suggest going there to Peng Wang.","Peng Wang was unwilling at first. He intended to find a cave that could at least shelter them from the rainwater.","He Zhiran could only explain her reasoning to him.","Although Peng Wang felt He Zhiran was being alarmist, in the end he compromised, thinking of her capabilities.","Beyond their expectations, after everyone arrived at the mountain depression, they discovered joyfully that there were actually three caves of varying sizes there.","Peng Wang was overjoyed. After checking them, he allocated the caves for temporary shelter according to the number of people.","He still favored the Mo family somewhat, letting them have the smallest one to themselves.","Although the cave was smaller, the Mo family was very satisfied since it was only their own family together.","He allocated the largest cave to the people of the other three families.","The yamen chose the medium-sized one.","Everyone now had a place to shelter from the rain, but thorny problems followed.","Their clothes were soaked through. If they couldn't change or dry them in time, it would easily lead to illnesses like colds.","Also, now they had no food or water sources. Going hungry for a night would surely be another torment for them.","He Zhiran had prepared in advance for these issues.","She publicly unwrapped the oilcloth package, revealing the charcoal inside.","The moment the Mo women saw the charcoal, their eyes widened.","\"Sister-in-law He, what's this?\"","He Zhiran had already thought up an explanation.","\"Seeing the charcoal at the Liu family's place, I considered we might need it on the mountain. So I kept aside a couple silvers to bring these along.\"","Mo Hanyue looked at her admiringly. \"Sister-in-law He, you are truly amazing. Even things like this you can think of.\"","\"That's right, Sister-in-law He. Second Sister-in-law now most admires you.\"","He Zhiran smiled at everyone. She took out an oilcloth wrapped match from her clothes and lit the charcoal together with Mo Jiuye.","At the same time, Mo Jiuye also gave He Zhiran a thumbs up for her thoughtfulness.","The firewood on the mountain was soaked by the rainwater. Even if they found some, it would probably be unable to ignite. But it was different with this charcoal. Not only was it easy to ignite, but it burned for a long time.","He Zhiran had bought fast burning charcoal. With little effort, she lit it easily."]},{"number":87,"title":"Chapter 87: Dinner problem Solved","paragraphs":["As the temperature in the cave gradually rose, the women gathered around the fire to dry their clothes.","Unfortunately, it was not easy to dry the clothes while wearing them.","Seeing this, Mo Jiuye decided to go out for a while to take shelter.","When He Zhiran saw him leaving, she quickly went up and handed him two small packages of charcoal.","\"Take these with you and deliver some to Elder Brother Peng and the others.\"","Mo Jiuye looked at the two small packages of charcoal, reluctant to part with them.","He had carried the charcoal up the mountain himself, so he knew best how much there was. Even if he didn't give it away, he was afraid it wouldn't burn for very long.","There was barely enough for his own family, yet he was supposed to share it with others.","He Zhiran saw his dilemma.","\"Don't worry, I still have some over there.\"","Mo Jiuye immediately thought back to the scene of massive loss of goods from the state treasury, and he instantly felt more confident.","\"Alright, I'll bring them over right away.\"","After Mo Jiuye left, He Zhiran took the initiative to stand guard at the mouth of the cave, allowing the women to take off their clothes and quickly dry them.","Gradually, the sky had darkened, and there was still no sign of the heavy rain letting up.","Fortunately, the terrain here was high, and all the rainwater flowed down the hillside without any accumulation.","Sitting in front of the embers, Peng Wang had to admire the Mo Jiuye couple.","\"Brother, you and your wife really had foresight. The area below the mountain must be flooded by now.\"","Mo Jiuye was clearly somewhat worried.","\"It looks like Village Chief Liu didn't listen to your advice.\"","Peng Wang also sighed.","\"I've said all I could. Village Chief Liu is stubborn by nature, he always feels that I'm fearmongering.\"","Mo Jiuye shook his head helplessly, also at a loss for what to do.","Seeing the two chatting, Zhang Qing squeezed over to join in the fun.","\"Boss, although we may have escaped a flood disaster by coming up the mountain, we can't stay here for a day or two without starving to death, can we?\"","This issue was not something Peng Wang hadn't considered. At first, he only thought they would stay up the mountain to avoid the rain for one night and could leave the next morning.","But looking at the still pouring rain, he was also unsure.","At this moment, Mo Jiuye suddenly stood up and strode to the mouth of the cave.","Mo Jiuye's actions were not difficult to guess. Something must have happened.","The two tacitly followed him to the mouth of the cave.","\"Brother, what's going on?\"","Mo Jiuye gestured to Peng Wang to keep quiet, then said softly, \"Elder Brother Peng, lend me your saber. I seem to have heard the sound of a wild boar.\"","Hearing there was a wild boar, Peng Wang inexplicably became somewhat excited.","If it was just him and the few government clerks, he might feel nervous. However, standing in front of him was the youngest war god of the previous Da Shun dynasty. He immediately felt relieved.","Peng Wang took Zhang Qing's saber and handed it to Mo Jiuye, \"Be careful, brother.\"","Seeing that Mo Jiuye had already gone out of the cave, Peng Wang raised his saber and followed along.","\"Brother, let me help you.\"","At the same time, He Zhiran also heard the movement outside.","A smile appeared on her face as she thought to herself: dinner is settled.","She had just walked out of the cave when she saw Mo Jiuye's shadow flash as he sprinted towards the bushes up ahead. Peng Wang ran wildly behind, unable to keep up with Mo Jiuye.","Knowing that Mo Jiuye had made his move, He Zhiran simply returned to the mouth of the cave.","With such heavy rain, if not for Mo Jiuye's keen sense of danger, they might not have discovered the wild boar so early.","Hearing the wild boar cry out in the distance, it was soon drowned out by the storm.","Not long after, Mo Jiuye and Peng Wang came back dragging a pitch-black wild boar.","Peng Wang immediately called over several men from the other three families and ordered them to clean the wild boar properly.","Only then did everyone notice that Mo Jiuye had actually braved the rain to hunt a wild boar.","Now this was good - at least they wouldn't go hungry tonight.","At the same time, they were also deeply aware of Peng Wang's reason for bringing them up the mountain. Such heavy rain had been falling for so long, the area below the mountain must have already been flooded.","Everyone now felt somewhat fortunate that although they had lost a lot of belongings, their lives were safe.","Figuring the women's clothes should be just about dry after all this time, Mo Jiuye returned to the cave where his family was staying.","Hearing there was wild boar meat for dinner brought smiles that could not be contained to everyone's faces.","He Zhiran was more attentive. Seeing Mo Jiuye's clothes soaked again, she pulled him to sit by the embers so he could dry off properly.","At the same time, Mo Jiuye also noticed that the pile of charcoal in the corner seemed to have increased compared to before.","He looked deeply at He Zhiran but the probing look in his eyes was much less than in the past.","He had probably seen too many strange things like this and was gradually becoming numb to them...","He Zhiran propped up the tent and went out to gather some branches.","There was no other way - all the cooking utensils had been left behind at Village Chief Liu's house. They could only roast the wild boar meat over the fire.","In any case, it was good that they could fill their stomachs.","The government clerks were also not idle. In order to eat the wild boar meat sooner, everyone took out their daggers or sabers and cut the meat into evenly sized chunks according to He Zhiran's requirements.","The women were responsible for skewering all the wild boar meat.","With so many people to cook dinner for, He Zhiran alone would surely be overwhelmed. Thus, fires were lit in all three caves and everyone worked on their own provisions.","The government clerks and people from the other three families had no seasoning and could only eat the bland wild boar meat. But it was different for the Mo family.","He Zhiran's pockets held a little bit of everything...","There was salt, and she could take out a small bottle of vegetable oil.","That's not all. While roasting the meat, He Zhiran would also secretly sprinkle on some spices that were not too intense in flavor.","It had to be said, the Mo family's dinner tonight was simply too delicious.","The He family also benefited from the heavy rain today, for the first time enjoying the same treatment as everyone else.","The government clerks didn't have their usual black steamed buns to give them, so they certainly couldn't watch them go hungry, especially since there was so much meat from one wild boar that with so many people it was just enough.","Therefore, Peng Wang closed one eye and let them eat the wild boar meat to their content.","Just as everyone had just finished their meal and was preparing to rest, they faintly heard a commotion in the distance, accompanied by women's crying and children's wailing.","Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran exchanged a glance.","\"It should be those villagers.\" Mo Jiuye said with certainty.","\"Yes, the situation below the mountain is probably worse than we imagined.\" He Zhiran said, voicing her guess.","The crying and footsteps grew closer and closer.","While no one was paying attention, He Zhiran used Taobao Treasure to buy a wooden torch with an ancient style design and handed it lit to Mo Jiuye.","Holding up the torch, Mo Jiuye went to the mouth of the cave.","In the faint firelight he could see a group of people walking up the mountain path towards them.","Hearing that Mo Jiuye had also noticed the sound outside, Peng Wang hurriedly jogged over.","\"Brother, I'm afraid the village has already been flooded.\"","\"Fortunately they went up the mountain, casualties shouldn't be too severe.\" Mo Jiuye said heavily in response."]},{"number":88,"title":"Chapter 88: We Rise and Fall Together","paragraphs":["As Village Chief Liu and the villagers were speaking, the sounds of footsteps and crying grew closer and closer.","Those villagers had seen the firelight on this side of the valley, and they all walked towards Village Chief Liu's direction.","Before long, in the blurred vision obscured by the dark night and heavy rain, a group of figures appeared. Looking closely, the one leading them was none other than Village Chief Liu.","Peng Wang shouted loudly, \"Village Chief Liu, how are things at the foot of the mountain?\"","Hearing the familiar voice, Village Chief Liu quickened his pace in an instant. Without even standing firmly, he said in a crying tone:","\"It's all because I didn't listen to your advice. Now the village has been completely submerged by the flood waters. Less than 30 percent of the people escaped.\"","Speaking to here, Village Chief Liu unexpectedly burst into tears, looking extremely miserable.","The villagers behind him also cried louder and louder.","All the villagers gathered in front of the cave, estimated to be about forty to fifty people.","Moreover, most of them were young people, with the elderly, weak, women and children only accounting for an extremely small portion.","Without even thinking, it was certain that those who had not been able to climb the mountain together must have perished.","Thinking of so many people dying in the flood waters, Peng Wang and Mo Jiuying felt a wave of grief.","It really fulfilled that saying - flood waters are merciless!","Now was not the time to feel regret. Peng Wang swept his eyes around and immediately made a decision.","All the women would go to the Mo family’s mountain cave. He would stay in the biggest mountain cave with the yamen runners and those male convicted criminals. They would give up their current mountain cave shelter to those villagers.","Although it would be more crowded this way, they couldn’t just watch those villagers have nowhere to stay.","After arranging everything, Mo Jiuying and He Zhiran brought some charcoal to the villagers for them to dry their clothes first.","As for food, they had not yet thought of a solution.","Mo Jiuying and He Zhiran had just handed the charcoal to Village Chief Liu when they suddenly heard someone cry out from among the villagers.","\"Village Chief Liu, my family’s Li Tiezhu has fainted. What should I do? Our village’s medical practitioner was washed away by the flood waters. Who can treat my Tiezhu...?\"","Upon hearing this, He Zhiran rushed forward without hesitation.","\"I know some medical skills. Why don't you let me take a look?\"","Seeing that the one volunteering so enthusiastically was a woman who looked very young, Village Chief Liu felt somewhat suspicious in his heart.","He did not believe at all that such a young girl would understand medical skills.","Peng Wang could discern his hesitation with one glance.","\"Village Chief Liu, the young Madam Mo is no ordinary doctor. It would not be an exaggeration to call her a divine doctor.\"","Hearing Peng Wang crown her with the title of divine doctor, He Zhiran had no time to be modest.","She urged Village Chief Liu, \"The situation is urgent. Do not delay any further.\" Now still not knowing the patient's specific condition, if the treatment time was delayed, it could cost a life.","Village Chief Liu still believed Peng Wang's words very much. He quickly cleared a space to facilitate He Zhiran in examining Li Tiezhu's condition.","Under the firelight, He Zhiran observed the patient. Before long, she sucked in a breath of cold air.","Unilateral submandibular lymphadenopathy with swelling had appeared on Li Tiezhu.","The first thing that came to her mind was bubonic plague.","He Zhiran looked towards the villagers and asked, \"Is his family here?\"","\"I'm Li Tiezhu's wife.\" The one speaking was precisely the woman who had discovered Li Tiezhu fainting and cried for help earlier.","Seeing the woman was a little nervous, He Zhiran said solemnly, \"Don't panic. Answer my questions carefully.\"","\"Alright.\"","\"Before he lost consciousness, did he have symptoms like chills, high fever, severe headache, intermittent vomiting coupled with breathing difficulties?\"","Listening to the symptoms listed out by He Zhiran, Li Tiezhu's wife kept nodding.","\"What you said is all correct. My Tiezhu did indeed show such symptoms these last two days.\"","As she spoke, Li Tiezhu's wife had already grabbed He Zhiran's sleeve tightly, anxiously asking, \"Doctor, is my Tiezhu suffering from some serious illness?\"","Based on Li Tiezhu's symptoms, it matched the manifestations of bubonic plague almost perfectly.","To further confirm her diagnosis, He Zhiran turned to find Village Chief Liu. She called him to the side.","\"Village Chief Liu, have there been a lot of rats in your village recently?\"","Hearing her mention rats, Village Chief Liu heaved a deep sigh.","\"Don't even mention it. In previous years there were rats in the village, but the numbers were not very high. I don't know why, but recently the number of rats has increased tremendously, and their sizes have become much bigger. Just yesterday, I discovered several dead rats in my storeroom at home.\"","Listening to Village Chief Liu's reply, He Zhiran's expression became even more grave.","\"Village Chief Liu, what Li Tiezhu has should be bubonic plague.\"","\"Bubonic plague?\" Village Chief Liu was instantly stunned.","He was not unfamiliar with this term.","Twenty some years ago, he had heard of such an illness occurring in a county town several hundred li from here.","Initially, the imperial court dispatched many imperial doctors to provide treatment, but in the end even the imperial doctors could not escape being infected by the bubonic plague. Afterwards, in order to prevent the further spread of the plague, the imperial court could only order for that county town to be sealed off.","Those poor commoners in that city either died painfully from illness or starved to death. In short, not a single one survived.","Just thinking about this, Village Chief Liu's legs turned soft.","\"Doctor, no, Divine Doctor, I beg you to save us!\"","As he spoke, Village Chief Liu had already knelt on the ground before He Zhiran, kneeling repeatedly.","Standing at the cave entrance, Mo Jiuying realized something was wrong and rushed over.","At this time, He Zhiran had just helped Village Chief Liu stand up.","Mo Jiuying asked solemnly, \"What has happened?\"","In order not to cause panic among the villagers, He Zhiran mouthed two words silently to Mo Jiuying: \"Bubonic plague.\"","Even someone like Mo Jiuying who frequently saw life and death could not help his face from turning pale dramatically upon hearing these two words.","\"How could this be?\" His lips moved as he spoke softly at the same time as he drew closer towards He Zhiran's direction.","He Zhiran quickly stopped him, \"Don't come over.\"","Naturally, Mo Jiuying understood her intentions. She was worried that if he got too close to those villagers, he would be infected with the plague.","As a stalwart man, how could he allow He Zhiran to face life and death alone as a woman?","Although he knew that there was no escaping being infected, he still rushed forward without hesitation.","In fact, He Zhiran was not actually afraid of the bubonic plague.","In her previous life, she had formulated Chinese medicine that had a special effect against the bubonic plague. As long as the condition of infected persons had not yet progressed to late stage organ damage, she could achieve eradication of the pathogen.","Unfortunately she had transmigrated before she could make this good news public.","What was unexpected was that soon after transmigrating here, the special effect treatment for bubonic plague had a use.","Although she did not have medicinal materials for treating the plague stored in her space, everything could be bought on Taobao Treasure Mall. The only issue was how these medicinal materials could see the light under this mountain cave.","Next, she saw Mo Jiuying had already come to her side, silently holding her small hand.","The expression in Mo Jiuying's eyes was very sincere.","\"We advance and retreat together.\"","Seeing that she could not stop Mo Jiuying's participation with her words, He Zhiran readily accepted his company.","At the same time, she also subconsciously squeezed Mo Jiuying's hand in return, signalling him to be at ease."]},{"number":89,"title":"Chapter 89: Why don't we run now","paragraphs":["Village Chief Liu pleaded again.","\"Doctor He, I beg you!\"","As he spoke, he turned to look at the villagers who still did not know what had happened.","He Zhiran reminded again: \"I suggest you temporarily keep the plague a secret for now to avoid panic, which will only make things worse.","Also, you all have the potential to become infected now, so to avoid harming more people, no one can leave the cave without my permission from now on.","If you can do as I say, I will try to treat you all.\"","Hearing that He Zhiran would try to treat them, Village Chief Liu saw a ray of hope.","He nodded repeatedly and promised: \"Doctor He, please rest assured, I will definitely not spread this matter.\"","With Village Chief Liu's promise, He Zhiran took out a package of silver needles from her sleeve while hiding it from view.","She was currently unable to prepare medicines to treat the plague, so she could only use acupuncture to temporarily stabilize Li Tiezhu's condition and prevent it from deteriorating further.","Sure enough, she skillfully inserted silver needles at several acupoints on Li Tiezhu's body.","Mo Jiuye silently accompanied her at her side.","After about a quarter of an hour, Li Tiezhu's breathing became much smoother, though he still had not regained consciousness.","He Zhiran put away the silver needles and told Li Family Madam, \"He should wake up within half an hour.\"","Li Family Madam thanked her profusely, thinking Li Tiezhu was fine now.","\"Thank you so much for saving his life, doctor.\"","He Zhiran had wanted to tell her that Li Tiezhu had only temporarily stabilized and was still not completely out of danger.","But seeing Li Family Madam's relief, she held herself back from saying it.","Moreover, He Zhiran felt that there was no need to isolate everyone at this point. Those who would have contracted it have already been exposed, so to put it bluntly, everyone present had the potential to become infected with the plague if they did not take preventive medicine in time.","He Zhiran got up, and solemnly pulled Mo Jiuye to the mouth of the cave.","\"I need your help.\"","Mo Jiuye knew the situation was urgent. All he could do was fully cooperate.","\"Just tell me what you need me to do.\"","He Zhiran roughly explained her plan to Mo Jiuye in a volume only the two of them could hear.","Mo Jiuye nodded without hesitation: \"Alright, I'll go talk to Brother Peng right away.\"","Peng Wang had returned to the cave of the officials. Seeing Mo Jiuye come over, he quickly asked, \"Brother, how are things over there?\"","Likewise not wanting the plague matter to startle too many people, Mo Jiuye pulled Peng Wang to a secluded spot.","\"Brother Peng, my wife diagnosed the patient with plague.\"","Hearing the two words \"plague\", Peng Wang felt a tingling sensation on his scalp, even thinking about the possibility that they too could become infected.","Peng Wang's usual composure was gone, and he stared intently at Mo Jiuye, seemingly making some big decision.","\"Brother, shouldn't we run now?\"","Peng Wang understood how the imperial court dealt with the plague — not a single infected person would be spared, all were sentenced to death.","And it was because he understood this that Peng Wang panicked into losing his reason.","He certainly did not want to be trapped somewhere waiting to die. If they ran now, at least they still had a chance to live.","Mo Jiuye hadn't come to ask Peng Wang for escape ideas, but to convey He Zhiran's request.","\"Brother Peng, we can't leave.\"","Peng Wang did not understand: \"You're not leaving? You want to stay here and wait to die?\"","In fact, Mo Jiuye was tense too, with so many of his relatives here.","If infected with the plague, no one stood a chance of surviving.","But still, he was willing to trust in He Zhiran.","\"Brother Peng, my wife said that when she was coming up the mountain earlier, she saw some herbs that might be able to prevent and treat the plague.\"","While not denying He Zhiran's medical skills, Peng Wang still did not think it would work for the plague, which was different from other diseases. Not only did it spread rapidly, but most fatally, no drug could cure it.","\"Brother, I know you're a tough guy, but think about your family too — what if there's no cure? Won't we all die here?\"","Mo Jiuye chose to believe He Zhiran, and regardless of what Peng Wang said, he did not change his mind.","\"Brother Peng, just give us some more time. I'll accompany my wife to collect herbs. With the flooding below the mountain now, even if we wanted to escape from here, it would be impossible. Why not let my wife give it a try?\"","Thinking about the flooding below the mountain, Peng Wang finally realized that they really could not leave this place.","Then to survive, their final ray of hope could only lie with He Zhiran.","\"Alright, hurry up and be safe. Pay attention to safety.\" As he spoke, Peng Wang grabbed two bamboo hats for Mo Jiuye.","Mo Jiuye gave Peng Wang a reassuring look, took the bamboo hats, and left.","When He Zhiran went to ask Mo Jiuye for help just now, she had already anticipated that she would have to reveal her secrets to him again.","Nevermind whether or not she believed Mo Jiuye's moral character, facing the problem now of so many lives potentially endangered by the plague, she had to place her own secrets as secondary priority.","Going down the same path as before, the two set off briskly while wearing bamboo hats.","It was dark, the roads were slippery, and for He Zhiran's safety, Mo Jiuye did not let go of her hand at all times.","He Zhiran thought, my secrets are going to be revealed a little bit more anyway, so I might as well give people some additional room for curiosity.","So, she directly retrieved a national treasury-grade night pearl from her space.","As soon as the night pearl appeared, the surroundings immediately became clear.","Mo Jiuye took a look at the night pearl, barely stopping himself from asking where on earth she took that thing out from.","But then again, her suddenly producing a night pearl wasn't much different from her taking out so much charcoal and some other items.","He figured she must have something like a magic bag of holding. Otherwise, Mo Jiuye really couldn't think of any other reasonable explanation at the moment.","It was He Zhiran's first time openly using her space in front of Mo Jiuye, already going way beyond cheekily hiding little things.","Though she felt strangely apprehensive, she immediately pointed to a flat area not far away to prevent Mo Jiuye from getting a chance to inquire further.","\"Let's go over there.\"","Mo Jiuye nodded and walked on ahead to guide the way.","The two came to the spot He Zhiran had indicated, and a military tent suddenly appeared out of thin air.","This was a top-tier military tent, housed in He Zhiran's medical office space. The exterior and practicality were both superb.","While Mo Jiuye stared blankly, He Zhiran had already pulled him into the tent.","Without the rain striking them, it immediately became much more comfortable.","To prevent anyone from again passing by and noticing something abnormal, after entering the tent, He Zhiran stowed away the night pearl back into her space.","\"The place where I store my treasury items has medicinal ingredients. To avoid suspicion, let's stay here for an hour before returning.\"","Mo Jiuye nodded: \"Okay.\"","Seeing Mo Jiuye tactfully complying, He Zhiran again took two chairs out from her space."]},{"number":90,"title":"Chapter 90: Brother and sister, I'm afraid this is not right","paragraphs":["In the last two days, three more items were sold from the shop, bringing in 980,000 yuan after deducting expenses.","After checking, He Zhiran hurried to search for medicinal herbs.","She now needed to purchase freshly picked herbs, only then would those people believe the herbs were just picked from the mountain.","Fortunately, everything imaginable could be found on Taobao.","He Zhiran was now considered quite wealthy, so she had no financial pressures when it came to spending.","Before long, she had purchased all the medicinal herbs she needed.","It was pitch black inside the tent. Mo Jiuye only felt something suddenly covering his feet.","Reaching out, it was all grass...","At this time, He Zhiran's somewhat guilty voice rang out.","\"We'll take these herbs back with us in a bit.\"","\"Can these herbs of yours cure the plague?\"","It wasn't that Mo Jiuye didn't believe in her medical skills, but rather that the plague was too evil. If it could be cured so easily by these herbs, wouldn't that be too simple?","\"If it's not late stage or critical, taking the medicine a few times will cure it. But if it's like Li Tiezhu, my silver needles must be used together with the medicine.\" He Zhiran said firmly.","Mo Jiuye heaved a deep sigh.","\"Tell me what I need to do, I'll do whatever you say.\"","He Zhiran spread her hands. \"Now that we have the medicine, you just need to help me conceal things a bit.\"","\"No problem, I'll do my best.\"","The two fell silent again until an hour later, when He Zhiran packed up the tent and returned with Mo Jiuye, carrying the herbs.","Since they left, Peng Wang had been standing at the mouth of the cave, craning his neck in anticipation, hoping they would come back with good news.","Seeing two figures in the distance, he rushed out into the pouring rain to meet them.","\"Brother, did you get the herbs?\"","This was the only hope for everyone to survive.","\"We got them.\" Mo Jiuye replied in a low voice.","When he got to them, Peng Wang took the herbs He Zhiran was holding without hesitation, pointing to the cave where the villagers were taking shelter.","\"I saw them bring an iron pot when they went up the mountain, let's make medicine there.\"","Peng Wang didn't want to wait a second longer, only hoping the medicine could cure the sick.","When the three entered the cave with the villagers carrying the herbs, Village Chief Liu anxiously told He Zhiran that several more people had fallen ill since they left.","The current symptoms were still at the fever and vomiting stage.","Without a doubt, He Zhiran immediately asked Village Chief Liu to set up a large iron pot over the coals to prepare medicine.","However, a new problem arose.","No water...","Village Chief Liu was after all a native here, relatively familiar with the local environment.","\"There is a mountain spring in the high ground, water can be fetched from there.\"","However, with how dark it was outside in this pouring rain, fetching water posed a big problem.","At this point, the most critical thing on Peng Wang's mind was living.","\"I'll take people to fetch water right now.\"","He Zhiran was originally planning to use the trick from before again - pop out for a bit then take water from her storage space.","Now that Peng Wang had stepped up, she was spared some trouble.","Those in the know understood the severity of the situation, so there was no dragging of feet as actions were swiftly carried out.","Peng Wang borrowed several water containers from Village Chief Liu and called some guards to fetch water in the rain.","In less than an hour, just as Mo Jiuye was starting to worry and wanted to go take a look, Peng Wang and company finally came back with water.","Village Chief Liu arranged for people to decoct the medicine, while at the same time, He Zhiran also checked on and asked about the current condition of the villagers.","The first batch of medicine was decocted, He Zhiran let the villagers drink it first, leaving the rest for the guards.","The second batch was for the exiles.","The current situation was - treat the sick, prevent the healthy from falling ill.","After everyone drank the medicine, it was already light out.","Fortunately, the heavy rain had stopped by this time.","Peng Wang immediately sent people down the mountain to check on the situation.","The news the guards brought back was even more serious than imagined.","The village had been completely submerged in floodwaters, all houses had collapsed, and countless corpses were floating on the surface.","Hearing this, everyone sighed in dismay.","In the face of such an incident, Peng Wang was at a total loss on what more could be done. He even treated Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran as his main support and refuge.","\"Brother, sister, do you have any good solutions?\"","Faced with this, even Mo Jiuye felt somewhat helpless for a time.","\"Given the current situation, I'm afraid all we can do is wait for the government to handle things.\"","But He Zhiran didn't think so.","\"Great floods often lead to great plagues. There are already villagers who have contracted the plague. If those corpses aren't dealt with promptly, I'm afraid this plague will spiral out of control.\"","\"What should we do then?\" The same words spilled simultaneously from Mo Jiuye and Peng Wang.","\"The best approach is to salvage and cremate those corpses as soon as possible. That's the most effective way to curb the spread of the epidemic.\"","In He Zhiran's understanding, this was the most viable solution.","Peng Wang and Mo Jiuye's eyes widened in unison. They found the notion of cremating corpses somewhat hard to accept.","In the eyes of these ancient people, respecting the dead was of utmost importance - only proper burials could put the living at ease.","Cremating corpses was the ultimate disrespect to the dead. Moreover, their family members surely would not agree.","\"Sister, I'm afraid that wouldn't be appropriate?\"","He Zhiran understood his feelings. Trying to change a person's deep-rooted beliefs was no easy feat.","But for the greater good, or rather, considering the lives of more survivors, she could only continue persuading.","\"Elder Brother Peng, I understand everyone's wish for their loved ones to rest in peace with proper burials.","But consider this - those plagued corpses, left unattended, would not only give off extremely foul stench, but also contaminate our air and water supply, potentially triggering even more outbreaks.","Don't you think that poses immense danger to the living as well?\"","After hearing He Zhiran's words, Mo Jiuye's original position immediately wavered.","\"She's right, the survivors are most important now. If the plague spreads far and wide, the consequences would be unimaginable.\"","Peng Wang wasn't a stubborn old fossil incapable of seeing reason. When it came down to balancing interests and making difficult choices, he would be decisive.","\"With floods this major, it surely wasn't just this village that was hit. There are too many bodies for us alone to handle.\"","This quandary truly had no easy solution. Even He Zhiran couldn't think of a better approach.","She merely made a general suggestion for the direction to take. As for detailed execution, she didn't have a clue.","In the end, it was Mo Jiuye who proposed a rather viable plan.","\"It would be best to communicate this with officials, get their men to carry it out. But of course, that's contingent upon convincing the magistrates first.\"","Peng Wang mulled over it briefly. \"Why don't I try, I'm relatively familiar with the county prefect here. Hopefully he isn't too traditionalist.\"","Things had come to this. He Zhiran felt she had done all she could.","It seemed reaching out to the county prefect was their only recourse now. As for whether the outcome would be ideal, that relied solely on luck."]},{"number":91,"title":"Chapter 91: Stop right there","paragraphs":["Although there was a reasonable plan, the floodwaters below the mountain had not yet receded, and Peng Wang was unable to go down the mountain to look for the county magistrate.","Faced with this situation, he could only wait patiently and hope that the flood would recede sooner.","He Zhiran had purchased enough herbal medicine last night, so things were settled on this side. She planned to arrange for the villagers to continue boiling medicine.","She didn't know if Village Chief Liu had let something slip, but those villagers already knew of their plague infection.","At this time, the villagers were somewhat agitated emotionally, and didn't even want to stay in the cave and wait to die. They desperately wanted to escape from here.","Although Village Chief Liu's mind was still relatively clear, he also believed He Zhiran’s words and did not allow those people to come out without her consent.","However, those villagers had been so frightened that they had lost all reason. With Village Chief Liu's strength alone, how could he stop them?","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye came to the mouth of the cave. What met their eyes was the scene of the villagers pushing Village Chief Liu aside and rushing out.","Mo Jiuye shouted, \"Everyone stand still!\"","The leading villager was startled, then raised the axe in his hand and waved it at Mo Jiuye a couple of times.","\"If you want to die then stay here, don't stop us.\"","How could Mo Jiuye possibly let these villagers leave? He rushed ahead to block the entrance of the cave.","He Zhiran also came up to stand beside him. The couple blocked the cave entrance.","The leading villager had only wanted to scare Mo Jiuye away with the axe. Now with them blocking the entrance, he didn't dare let his raised axe fall.","So the two sides stood still for about thirty seconds.","Peng Wang also heard the commotion here. He led the yamen runners to block the entrance, flashing out their sabers at the same time.","Seeing that the other side had weapons, the villagers instantly lost their previous momentum.","\"Sir, please let us leave! We don't want to die yet.\"","He Zhiran stepped forward, standing in front of the speaker.","\"Who said we’re letting you die?\"","A villager said bitterly, \"Some of us have already been infected with the plague. If we don't leave here and the government finds out, they will definitely lock us up and burn us alive.\"","Upon hearing this, He Zhiran patiently asked, \"Didn't you all drink the medicine last night?\"","Not understanding why she was asking, the villagers nodded in unison.","He Zhiran pointed to Li Tiezhu, who was being supported by his wife, \"Tell everyone the truth, isn't your physical condition much better now compared to yesterday?\"","Li Tiezhu instinctively touched the position under his jaw.","\"The swelling here has indeed gone down.\"","He Zhiran then looked towards the other villagers who had previously shown symptoms.","\"What about you all? Have the symptoms of fever and vomiting yesterday alleviated?\"","A few people nodded woodenly, \"I haven't vomited again since drinking the medicine.\"","\"Apart from feeling a little dizzy, my other symptoms are gone.\"","He Zhiran nodded and scanned the crowd again.","\"Did you hear that? After those who have been infected eat my medicine, their symptoms have improved.","Judging by this situation, as long as you keep taking the medicine, I guarantee you will recover completely within three days.","You must have heard of the severity of the plague. Anyone who catches it basically has no chance of survival.","If you don't want to die, stay here obediently and keep taking the medicine.","Of course, if you insist on leaving I won't stop you, as long as you don't regret it.\"","After listening to He Zhiran's words, the villagers hesitated.","What she said did make sense. Even if they escaped from here, with no one to provide medical treatment, let alone a place to stay, it would still be death.","Soon, some people understood this logic.","\"I won't leave. I'd rather die here, at least it's still in my hometown.\"","\"I won't leave either. I can't spread the disease to more people.\"","Village Chief Liu took the opportunity to persuade them for a bit more before the villagers finally regained their senses and returned to the cave.","He Zhiran handed the herbs to Village Chief Liu and asked him to arrange for people to continue decocting the medicine.","The commotion here was not small, so even the exiled criminals and yamen runners found out about the plague.","At first, like those villagers, they were extremely horrified.","Gradually, under the persuasion of Peng Wang and Mo Jiuye, they slowly gave up the idea of fleeing this place.","In the Mo family’s eyes, they had reached a crucial moment of life and death.","At this time, the family must unite and support Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran even more.","The sisters-in-law and Mo Hengyue surrounded He Zhiran.","\"Sister-in-law, being able to be with family even in death, I'm not afraid. If there's anything you need help with, just order me to do it!\"","\"That’s right, sister-in-law, we Mo family members are not afraid. If you need help just speak up.\"","\"......\"","He Zhiran was once again touched by her family's support. She smiled and reassured everyone.","\"Sisters-in-law, Hengyue, you don't need to worry. My medicine not only treats the plague but also prevents infection.","You have all taken it already. I believe the possibility of infection is very small.\"","With He Zhiran’s words, everyone heaved a sigh of relief. At the same time, they felt extremely fortunate that Ninth Brother had married such a capable wife before his exile.","The family was enthusiastic and truly wanted to help, but He Zhiran really had nothing for them to do right now.","She gently persuaded everyone to leave before turning around to discover Mo Jiuye missing.","He Zhiran only thought he had gone to relieve himself somewhere and didn't think much of it.","It wasn’t until half an hour later when the medicine had been decocted and distributed that Mo Jiuye returned carrying several pheasants and rabbits.","He Zhiran suddenly understood that this guy had gone hunting.","Having skills made a difference. In just half an hour he was able to hunt this much game.","Unfortunately, with so many people taking refuge here, what Mo Jiuye brought back could only be described as a drop in the bucket.","In times like these, they had to be a little selfish and let their family fill their stomachs first before considering others.","Mo Jiuye thought this way too, which was why he directly gave the game he brought back to his sisters-in-law to roast and share with the family.","Peng Wang and Village Chief Liu came up to Mo Jiuye almost at the same time.","At this moment, both men had pleading expressions on their faces...","\"Brother, I know you’re capable. Can you go out again to hunt...\"","His words trailed off as he spoke, but he had to say them.","In order not to starve, they could only ask Mo Jiuye for help.","Village Chief Liu looked at Mo Jiuye just as pleadingly, hoping he would agree to Peng Wang's request, so he could also share the spoils.","Without expecting to eat meat, at least they could drink some chicken broth at a time like this.","Under normal circumstances with Mo Jiuye’s capabilities, casually hunting some game in the mountains would be no problem at all. However, the situation today was special.","Not to mention the slippery paths, he didn’t know whether it was due to the heavy rains, but when he tried using his lightness skill to go further out, he could only find these few pheasants and rabbits."]},{"number":92,"title":"Chapter 92: When you meet someone you like, Your Heart Beats Faster.","paragraphs":["Although He Zhiran did not personally witness the difficulties Mo Jiuye faced while hunting for prey, she could deduce from the current environment that it was not easy to hunt for game after the heavy rain.","Seeing that Mo Jiuye was about to refuse, she quickly interjected, \"Husband, the medicinal herbs are running out. If you go hunting, you can also gather some on the way back.\"","Based on Mo Jiuye's understanding of her, he knew that her words were definitely not just about collecting herbs.","Therefore, the refusal he was about to blurt out was instantly swallowed back.","\"Alright, let's go now.\"","Seeing that Mo Jiuye did not refuse, Peng Wang instinctively assumed that he had agreed to her request.","After all, he completely trusted these two people now and was not worried that they would run away.","Mo Jiuye led her up the mountain, walking on the slippery mountain path, which was a great challenge for He Zhiran, who had no lightness skills.","Fortunately, with Mo Jiuye holding her hand all the way, He Zhiran did not slip.","He Zhiran, as a modern soul, did not pay much attention to the physical contact between the two, but Mo Jiuye was different.","He walked ahead, and his face would occasionally flush with heat, and his heartbeat would even accelerate beyond his control.","This was not the first time Mo Jiuye had felt this way after physical contact with He Zhiran, and he had to take it seriously.","When he was in the military camp, he had heard his married colleagues say that their heart rate would increase when they met someone they liked.","Could it be that he liked He Zhiran?","Mo Jiuye did not reject this feeling; on the contrary, he quite liked it.","With this in mind, he unconsciously tightened his grip on He Zhiran's hand.","Unable to see Mo Jiuye's face, He Zhiran thought that his actions were simply to better protect her.","With a slightly nervous yet pleasant mood, Mo Jiuye led He Zhiran to a spacious place.","He knew that He Zhiran's main purpose for coming out with him was not really to gather herbs.","Seeing that she showed no intention of stopping, Mo Jiuye asked softly, \"Where do you want to go?\"","Where to go?","He Zhiran didn't have a specific destination in mind. The main reason she followed Mo Jiuye was to buy some items in Taobao.","Looking around at the surroundings, it felt quite pleasant.","If it weren't for the heavy rain last night or the fact that they were both exiled criminals, she really wanted to stay here and enjoy the beauty of nature.","However, for now, she needed to be practical.","Although she no longer kept many things from Mo Jiuye, she couldn't simply take items out of space in broad daylight like magic tricks in front of him.","\"How about you go for a stroll and look for some prey? I'll stay here and prepare, and then I'll call you back, how about that?\"","Having Mo Jiuye search for prey was just an excuse. They hadn't seen a trace of prey along the way; He Zhiran simply used it as a casual excuse to keep him away.","Mo Jiuye naturally understood her thoughts.","\"Alright, I'll go farther away. If you encounter any danger, just shout.\"","\"Well, don't worry! If there's any danger, I'll definitely call you back to save me.\"","Mo Jiuye continued walking uphill, turning his head three times, hoping that He Zhiran would ask him to stay.","However, He Zhiran did not say anything to make him stay...","It wasn't until Mo Jiuye's figure disappeared that He Zhiran arrived under a dense grove of trees and quickly entered a trance-like state.","Taking out her phone, she purchased herbs for those people to take a day's worth.","Additionally, to accompany Mo Jiuye on the hunt, she bought ten live rabbits for meat.","Wild chickens had become a protected species in the future, so they were not sold on Taobao. However, wild chicken eggs were available.","Although wild chicken eggs were more expensive than regular chicken eggs, at least they were obtainable.","With everything prepared, He Zhiran shouted in the direction Mo Jiuye had left.","\"Mo Jiuye, I'm ready.\"","She shouted twice in a row but received no response.","He Zhiran grew anxious and walked up the hill to search for him.","Just as she had walked less than a hundred meters, she saw a familiar figure.","Mo Jiuye was coming towards her, carrying a wild mountain goat on his shoulder.","He had heard He Zhiran's call, but he was in the middle of catching the mountain goat, afraid that making a sound would scare it away, so he didn't answer immediately.","With the goat captured, Mo Jiuye didn't dare to linger. He hoisted the goat onto his shoulder and walked quickly in He Zhiran's direction.","Seeing the mountain goat on Mo Jiuye's shoulder, He Zhiran felt a bit regretful.","If she had known he could catch a mountain goat, she would have bought one from Taobao as well.","Mo Jiuye had already approached her and, after a moment of hesitation, he pretended to be calm and held her hand.","\"Let's go!\"","Seeing the live rabbits, Mo Jiuye was somewhat shocked.","He couldn't even find this many wild rabbits with his skills, so how did He Zhiran manage it?","Could it be that these rabbits also came from her magical treasure chest?","But soon, he used his previous reasoning to convince himself that these were secrets that couldn't be explored.","Sorting out his thoughts, Mo Jiuye found some branches and tied them together with vines to make a raft.","The two of them pulled the fully loaded raft back to the cave.","Peng Wang's eyes lit up when he saw these things.","\"Brother, sister-in-law, you've worked hard. In this special period, being able to keep everyone from going hungry is all thanks to you.\"","Both Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran didn't mind the credit. Their greatest hope now was for the whole family to safely reach the northwest.","\"Peng Big Brother, you're too polite. It was just a small effort on our part.\"","Mo Jiuye exchanged a few polite words and then left with the wild mountain goat, two rabbits, and some wild chicken eggs, while also pulling He Zhiran along.","As for the remaining game, Peng Wang would take care of it.","The sisters-in-law took the initiative to handle the game, although they were still a bit hesitant, they persevered.","The ninth brother and ninth sister-in-law had already done so much for everyone, and they had to do their best to share the burden.","Peng Wang was responsible for distributing food to the other families and villagers. Although it wasn't as abundant as what the Mo family had, no one complained. At a time like this, without Mo Jiuye and his wife, they would either starve to death or die from illness. They were too grateful to even express it properly.","Even the He family, who harbored resentment towards Mo Jiuye, had softened their animosity to a great extent. He Zhiyuan even personally approached Mo Jiuye to express his gratitude.","Both He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye could tell that He Zhiyuan now had friendly intentions towards them. However, trust is not built overnight, and they couldn't befriend just anyone.","Mo Jiuye simply nodded in acknowledgment, indicating his acceptance of He Zhiyuan's gratitude, and ceased any further interaction with him.","After an hour of busyness, Madam Mo, accompanied by the other women of the household, finally managed to prepare the wild game brought back by Mo Jiuye.","Mo Jiuye had already set up a bonfire in an open space. In such an environment, roasting the wild game was the most convenient cooking method.","Of course, if they wanted it to taste good, they still needed He Zhiran's culinary skills."]},{"number":93,"title":"Chapter 93: Meng Huining","paragraphs":["The Mohists happily ate a \"wild barbecue\". He Zhiran also took the time to give Li Tiezhu another acupuncture treatment.","The people who originally had the idea of escaping now gave up on that idea after seeing Li Tiezhu's obvious improvement.","Seeing that the accumulated water on the nearby ground was becoming less and less, Peng Wang sent Zhang Qing with two people down the mountain to take a look. If the flood had receded, they would continue on their way early tomorrow morning.","This trip had delayed too much of their travel time. If they didn't speed up, they were afraid they wouldn't be able to deliver the prisoners to the northwest within the prescribed time.","About an hour after Zhang Qing left with the people, he ran back, panting.","\"Boss, the water under the mountain has receded almost completely. I tried it, the deepest place just barely went past my knees.","Also, the magistrate of Dongfeng County personally brought people here for disaster relief. They have already salvaged some of the corpses in the water.\"","When he heard that the magistrate of Dongfeng County had personally come for disaster relief, Peng Wang thought of He Zhiran's suggestion.","That was that if these corpses could not be cremated in time, it would easily lead to a plague breaking out.","Thinking of this, Peng Wang felt that he had to go and talk to the magistrate himself about this matter.","After all, he had heard this from He Zhiran, so Peng Wang decided to take her and Mo Jiuye with him to go there.","After making some simple arrangements for things here, the three of them hurried down the mountain.","At the foot of the mountain, what met their eyes was a mess.","The houses in the village had been completely washed away by the big flood. In the murky water lay more than a dozen corpses.","In addition to that, there were also some items from the commoners' homes that had been washed everywhere by the flood.","In the distance, a young man in magistrate's official clothes was directing a group of subordinates to move those corpses to higher ground.","While He Zhiran and the others were observing that magistrate, the magistrate's gaze also turned towards them.","If Peng Wang hadn't been wearing official clothes, he might have thought these few were surviving commoners from nearby.","The magistrate gave orders to his subordinates, then sloshed through the water towards them.","Peng Wang's side also went to meet him in turn.","When the two sides were not far apart, the magistrate and Peng Wang recognized each other at the same time.","Meeting an acquaintance, Peng Wang was very enthusiastic.","\"Is that my young brother Meng?\"","Meng Huaining clasped his fist towards Peng Wang: \"Brother Peng, long time no see.\"","Seeing that there was still a dozen or so meters between them and Meng Huaining, Peng Wang walked while quietly introducing Meng Huaining to Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran.","\"This one is Elder State Minister Meng's own grandson, named Meng Huaining.\"","Mo Jiuye was not familiar with Meng Huaining, but he was no stranger to Elder State Minister Meng, whom Peng Wang had mentioned.","Elder State Minister Meng was Emperor Shunwu's left and right hand man, and could be said to be a pillar minister of the Da Shun Dynasty.","It wasn't until Emperor Shunwu ascended to the throne that, in order to monopolize power, he used Elder State Minister Meng's old age and frailness as an excuse to order him to return home and retire.","Not long after, there was news that Elder State Minister Meng had died on the road back home.","He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye had opposite knowledge. She didn't know much about Elder State Minister Meng's affairs, but she was not unfamiliar with his grandson Meng Huaining.","Fei Nanyu was able to build the strongest country during his reign, and Meng Huaining had an indispensable role.","This person had unconventional thinking and was good at accepting new things. He often made bold suggestions to Fei Nanyu.","Knowing that Meng Huaining had talent, Fei Nanyu gave him ample room to exert himself.","He Zhiran quickly went over in her mind what she knew about Meng Huaining, then looked at Mo Jiuye and said in a voice that only the two of them could hear: \"Meng Huaining is worth befriending.\"","Mo Jiuye didn't know what He Zhiran's reminder was based on, but based on those past events, he could be certain that almost everything she said was correct.","Therefore, Mo Jiuye nodded deeply to indicate that he understood.","As they walked closer, after exchanging brief pleasantries with Meng Huaining, Peng Wang introduced Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran to him.","Meng Huaining was no stranger to Mo Jiuye.","Who in the Da Shun Dynasty didn't know the famous God of War?","As for the crime Mo Jiuye was accused of, no one was clearer in their heart than Meng Huaining that he had been wronged.","Emperor Shunwu's reason for convicting the Mohists was nothing more than that Mo Jiuye's great accomplishments overshadowed him, making him uncomfortable.","It was because his own grandfather's great accomplishments had overshadowed and aroused jealousy that he met a violent death on the road home...","Although the Meng family knew the real cause of the Senior Minister's death, in order to preserve the lives of their whole family, they could only claim to outsiders that the Senior Minister had died of illness.","Mo Jiuye had driven away foreign enemies countless times and kept the Da Shun dynasty safe. He was someone Meng Huaining sincerely respected from the bottom of his heart.","What's more, the Mohists' fate was almost the same misfortune as his own family's.","Without any pretense, Meng Huaining took the initiative to cup his fist towards Mo Jiuye.","\"General Mo, this humble official pays his respects.\"","Mo Jiuye hurriedly returned the courtesy: \"I am no longer a general now, but a prisoner reviled by all. Meng Excellency calling me that is not appropriate.\"","In fact, Meng Huaining also weighed it over and over before choosing to address Mo Jiuye this way.","The Mohists had been loyal and upright for generations, and were all great heroes standing tall and unwavering in his eyes. Now they were exiled under false accusations, so it wasn't good to call him Duke anymore.","Out of respect for the Mohists, Meng Huaining addressed Mo Jiuye as General.","Meng Huaining waved his hand: \"No, the Mohists have protected the country for generations. You deserve to be called General.\"","Seeing the two of them going back and forth over forms of address here, Peng Wang spoke up: \"At first glance, Brother Meng is a sentimental person, and Brother Mo is straightforward. In my opinion, why don't you two address each other as brothers? That would be more intimate.\"","Hearing this, Mo Jiuye quickly reported his age: \"This humble one is now twenty-one. I wonder, how old is Meng Excellency?\"","\"I'm one year older than you. If Brother Mo doesn't mind, just call me Big Brother Meng.\"","\"Big Brother Meng.\"","After exchanging some idle chatter, Peng Wang did not forget the purpose of this trip.","He took the initiative to tell Meng Huaining about He Zhiran's suggestion.","Meng Huaining's reaction did not disappoint He Zhiran.","He was indeed as recorded in history - unconventional in his thinking, bold, and astute.","Although Meng Huaining did not immediately oppose Peng Wang's proposal, he also did not make a decision right away.","In order to further confirm the pros and cons, he asked some detailed questions about the reasons and circumstances.","Peng Wang could make suggestions, but when it came to explaining details, he couldn't do it.","So he directly pushed He Zhiran forward.","Meng Huaining did not slight her because she was a woman.","\"Sister, you mean these commoners' corpses must be cremated?\"","He Zhiran said solemnly: \"Yes, the sooner the better. This is the only way to effectively prevent the outbreak of an epidemic.","Moreover, I must tell Brother Meng that among the villagers taking refuge with us, some have already been infected with plague.\"","\"What? Did you say the villagers taking refuge have contracted plague?\" Meng Huaining sucked in a breath of cold air. This news was too sudden. For him as the parent official, it was like a bolt from the blue on a sunny day."]},{"number":94,"title":"Chapter 94: Deliver the Medicine","paragraphs":["Seeing this, He Zhiran quickly explained: “Elder Brother Meng need not worry. The master who taught me medicine once gave me a prescription for treating plague. Those people have now been given the medicine and are no longer in mortal danger.","What I want to remind you is that those villagers were already infected with the plague before going up the mountain. The origin of the plague is still unclear now, and we cannot rule out the possibility that people from surrounding villages are also infected.","Therefore, I hope you will keep this matter in mind and send more people to investigate the situation. If anything is found to be wrong, measures must be taken immediately.”","Regarding He Zhiran’s claim that she had a prescription for treating the plague, Meng Huaining did not completely believe it.","After all, the plague was different from other diseases. He had heard from his elders that during the plague in the Da Shun Dynasty era, many doctors lost their lives without being able to come up with a cure.","He sincerely believed in Mo Jiuye’s character and was willing to believe that his wife was a good person.","But for such a major event as treating the plague, Meng Huaining did not dare to be careless at all.","If it was not handled properly, thousands or even tens of thousands could end up dead...","“Sister, is your medicine really as effective as you say?”","Peng Wang could testify to this.","“Brother Meng, I saw with my own eyes people on the verge of death being saved. There is no doubt about this.”","With Peng Wang's testimony, Meng Huaining did gain some more confidence.","At the same time, he also felt that immediately cremating the corpses made a lot of sense.","In order not to exacerbate the situation, Meng Huaining immediately gathered manpower to cremate the corpses of the commoners that had been salvaged.","Last night, upon hearing about the flooding here, Meng Huaining had written a memorial overnight to report to the imperial court, hoping that the court would send an imperial envoy as soon as possible to resolve the crisis.","In less than a day, he wrote another memorial report about the outbreak of the plague.","As for how Emperor Shunwu’s side would arrange things, there was currently no way for him to interfere with the emperor's own decisions.","If it had been those with less courage, even if they deeply understood the importance of cremating the corpses, they probably would not have dared to implement it without an order from the imperial court.","This showed Meng Huaining’s wisdom and courage.","Seeing Meng Huaining handling things in an orderly manner, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran simultaneously developed admiration for him.","By the time all the corpses of the commoners that had been salvaged were cremated, the sky was almost dark.","For the first time in front of He Zhiran and the others, Meng Huaining revealed a hesitant look.","After thinking it over, Meng Huaining reluctantly spoke up.","“Sister, I know this may be asking too much, but as a local official responsible for the people, I have no choice but to think about treating the commoners under me.”","He Zhiran immediately saw through what was on his mind. He was preoccupied with the prescription for treating the plague.","Even if it was Emperor Shunwu himself who came to ask her for it, she would not have given out the prescription.","However, the person before her now was different. Setting aside Meng Huaining’s future achievements for the time being, just looking at the present, he was responsible and had a sense of responsibility.","Moreover, this was someone she intended to get acquainted with Mo Jiuye.","With so many reasons, He Zhiran would naturally not be miserly.","Although she had spent a lot of effort in her previous life researching this prescription.","Her goal in working hard to study it was precisely to be able to treat more people. Now that there was an opportunity to treat even more people, and she could also owe Meng Huaining a huge favor, He Zhiran did not feel any pressure to provide the prescription.","Seeing that He Zhiran had not responded for a long time, Meng Huaining thought that she was unwilling.","“Sister, I guarantee that no one other than myself will know of this prescription. I will also not let anyone know that it came from you. Also, I will have many people purchase the types of medicinal ingredients, so as not to draw suspicion. Once the crisis passes, I will personally destroy the prescription. Does this sound feasible?”","He Zhiran had never intended to reject Meng Huaining’s request in the first place. Now that the other party had already said so much, she would naturally not be pretentious.","“Alright, I trust that Elder Brother Meng will definitely keep his word.”","Soon, Meng Huaining sent someone to fetch paper and writing brush.","He Zhiran was already extremely familiar with the prescription she had formulated. The only thing that troubled her was whether she could write the complex characters of this era properly.","Especially when using a writing brush, she had not taken any calligraphy classes in her previous life.","For this, she could only place her hopes on the memories of the original owner.","He Zhiran hesitated for a moment before picking up the brush, then made two strokes on the paper. Immediately afterwards, she lowered the brush tip.","Whether it was due to the habits of this body or something else, when He Zhiran used the writing brush to write the complex characters of this era, she was actually very skilled.","Not only that, the words she wrote were all neat and well-structured. It was evident that the original owner had put in a lot of effort in this area.","Once the ink on the prescription had dried, He Zhiran handed it to Meng Huaining.","“Here is the prescription. If anyone asks about it in the future, I hope Elder Brother Meng will help conceal some parts for me.”","It was still unknown what would become of Mo Jiuye in the future. As his wife, she must not gain fame for herself externally, so as to avoid unnecessary trouble.","Meng Huaining took the prescription and put it away carefully. He earnestly cupped his fist towards He Zhiran.","“Sister, rest assured. I will never reveal this matter. Similarly, I will definitely fulfill my promise.”","“Then I can rest easy.” He Zhiran replied with a smile.","Seeing that it was getting late, Peng Wang made arrangements to return to the mountain and decided to rest for the night before setting off the next morning.","As for the villagers on the mountain, Meng Huaining would also send people to settle them the next morning.","The few bid farewell to each other and by the time they returned to the cave, the sky was completely dark.","The sisters-in-law had long roasted the remaining game and were waiting for He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye to return so everyone could eat together.","Nothing else of note happened that night.","The next morning, Peng Wang urged everyone to continue on their journey.","The villagers sincerely kowtowed to thank their lifesaver He Zhiran. He Zhiran also exhorted them that if they were grateful for her lifesaving grace, they must not say that it was her who saved them.","Although the villagers did not know why the goddess doctor who saved them was unwilling to leave her name, they still promised under her request not to speak of it.","The sudden flooding had not only submerged Village Chief Liu’s village. After walking a section towards the west, devastation could be seen everywhere.","It was clear how many innocent commoners had been harmed by this great flood.","Alas, natural disasters did not differentiate between ancient and present times. When facing such things, humans were the most vulnerable group, and no one could resist the heavens...","Including the yamen runners, everyone no longer had much in the way of living supplies on them. Although this made it a lot easier to travel, it also brought many more inconveniences at the same time.","Take their three daily meals for example. Not only was there no grain, but it was also very difficult to find clean water sources.","Fortunately, they found some pots and other items washed away by the flood. This solved some of their burning problems.","Despite having cookware, the surrounding areas were severely stricken by disaster, and there was simply nowhere to purchase food ingredients.","Left with no other choice, He Zhiran could only lead everyone to forage for wild vegetables from the mountains they passed to get through the days.","They lived this way for four consecutive days. Finally, on the fifth day at noon, everyone arrived at Anning Prefecture."]},{"number":95,"title":"Chapter 95: Anningshire","paragraphs":["If it were in the past, Peng Wang would never have brought prisoners with him to a large prefecture to purchase supplies.","There were many wealthy people in the prefectures, and prices were much higher than those in some small counties.","For officers, it was more appropriate to purchase the same items in cheaper places.","However, things were different now. They had been eating wild vegetable soup for four or five days. If this continued, they would probably run out of strength to keep traveling.","The group entered Anning Commandery under Peng Wang's lead.","Perhaps because they rarely came here, Peng Wang was not as familiar with this place as he was with other counties.","Asking all the way, they arrived at what was said to be the cheapest inn in Anning Commandery.","It had to be said that the prefecture was much more prosperous than the counties. Even the cheapest inn here looked higher-grade than those they had stayed at before.","The front door of the inn was wide open to the street. A waiter stood at the door specially to attract customers.","Seeing people coming, the waiter sized them up first. Seeing Peng Wang and others dressed as officers, he warmly welcomed them in.","They had wanted to casually get a few ten-people rooms to accommodate the prisoners, as they did before. But the inn simply didn't have such rooms.","The cheapest five-people room cost 500 wen per night.","At this point, Peng Wang didn't care too much. If it was expensive, then so be it. After all, they could still afford it.","The Mo family had money on hand and would arrange it themselves. As for the other families, those who were willing to spend money would stay in the guest rooms, while those without money would sleep outside the inn. As long as no one ran away, other things were secondary.","The Fang and Xie families did feel somewhat reluctant to spend so much money to stay in the hotel, especially since the five-person rooms could only accommodate five people.","But after so many days of dining in the wind and sleeping in the dew, they were somewhat uncomfortable physically. Finally, they gritted their teeth and decided to rent a room anyway so the whole family could squeeze together, which was still better than sleeping outside.","He Zhiran didn't feel anything about this. She directly booked two five-people rooms and a double room.","The He family was most miserable, only being able to rest in the corridor behind the inn.","After everyone settled down, Peng Wang took the initiative to ask He Zhiran if she wanted to go out and purchase supplies.","Of course He Zhiran would not refuse. She expressed her gratitude and prepared to go out.","Seeing this, the Fang and Xie families also pleaded with Peng Wang, hoping he could give them some time to purchase supplies.","It had to be said that these two families were really taking advantage of the Mo family. Not only did Peng Wang give them some money, but the officers did not take advantage of them either.","To the Fang and Xie families, this was already the greatest blessing bestowed upon them by heaven.","Although Peng Wang did not object to the two families going out shopping, he could not let them go out alone with the extremely trusting attitude he had towards He Zhiran.","Therefore, just to be safe, Peng Wang sent two officers to follow them.","Seeing that He Zhiran had already stepped out of the door, Mo Jiuye bid Peng Wang farewell and hurried to catch up with her.","\"I'll go with you.\"","Seeing Mo Jiuye's firm attitude, He Zhiran did not object.","The two tacitly accelerated their pace to keep their distance from the Xie and Fang families behind them as much as possible. This would make their actions more convenient.","With Mo Jiuye following her, it was not so convenient for her to take things out of her space.","Fortunately, there were abundant goods in Anning Commandery. As long as they had money, they could buy whatever they needed.","While shopping, the two also discovered that almost everyone in Anning Commandery was talking about one thing—the flood in Dongfeng County.","What most people discussed was not how serious the disaster was, but how bold County Prefect Meng Huaining was to dare burn the bodies of the dead.","It was said that this matter had already shocked the imperial court. His Majesty had sent Prince Qi as the imperial censor to handle this matter.","As soon as Prince Qi arrived, Meng Huaining would probably be severely punished.","It was understandable. The common people could not accept the fact that their family members’ corpses were cremated. Meng Huaining must have thought of the possible consequences when he decided to do it.","What was unexpected was that His Majesty had actually sent Nan Qi as the imperial censor to handle this matter.","From He Zhiran's understanding of history, Nan Qi was in desperate need of talent at this moment.","Once he expressed support for Meng Huaining's approach, Meng Huaining would certainly be grateful to Nan Qi for appreciating his talents and join his camp.","This was probably one of the opportunities for Meng Huaining to get acquainted with Fei Nanyu.","Of course, these things were just guesses made by He Zhiran in her heart. She was not very concerned about the details.","Although Fei Nanyu and Meng Huaining were key figures in the future court, they currently had no impact on the Mo family.","He Zhiran only hoped that once Meng Huaining joined Nan Qi's camp, he would keep his promise and not reveal that she had provided him with prescriptions.","Mo Jiuye listened casually as well. After all, court affairs no longer had anything to do with him...","Mo Jiuye was almost silent on the road. Whenever He Zhiran bought something, he would take the initiative to carry it for her, so that she wouldn't have to work hard at all.","Seeing that Mo Jiuye was already full of the items she had purchased, He Zhiran took the initiative to help.","But Mo Jiuye stubbornly refused to let her lend a hand, insisting on advancing steadily under the weight by himself.","He Zhiran had no choice. Seeing that Mo Jiuye was already full of supplies, the two returned to the inn together.","Old Lady Mo brought the women over to help organize things. The Third and Fourth Sister-in-Laws took He Zhiran aside.","The two took out a purse from their bosoms at the same time and gave them to her.","\"Ninth Sister-in-Law, you’ve been spending your own money all the way since we left the capital. Now mother-in-law has asked you to be in charge, so we’re handing all our money over for you to manage.\"","He Zhiran was stunned for a moment, and quickly returned the purses.","\"Sisters-in-Law, take the money back. I’ll come to you when I run out.\"","What He Zhiran was thinking was that one never knew whether the journey ahead would be peaceful. If she got separated from her family or something else happened, at least they would have money on hand and their lives wouldn't be too difficult.","The two sister-in-laws didn't know He Zhiran's real thoughts. They insisted on giving her the money.","After being rejected by He Zhiran again, they had to give up the idea for the time being and went to help handle the supplies.","After days of dining in the wind and sleeping in the dew, everyone finally enjoyed a normal meal and felt very satisfied.","Only the He family, who had no money, could only eat the dark steamed buns given by the officers.","After resting for a night in the inn, everyone felt revived, as if with full health.","Under Peng Wang's order, everyone set off again.","After continuous marching for three days, they were blocked by a mountain.","The Eighth Old Zhou stepped forward and pointed to the mountain ahead, \"Boss, it's already afternoon. Why don't we rest here tonight and cross the mountain tomorrow?\"","\"Okay, let's rest at the foot of the mountain tonight and climb it tomorrow.\"","The Eighth Old Zhou turned his head and shouted at the team behind: \"Go to the foot of the mountain. Find your place to rest. Continue traveling tomorrow!\""]},{"number":96,"title":"Chapter 96: Ox Horn Mountain","paragraphs":["After listening to Old Zhou's words, He Zhiran had already guessed that this place was probably the mountain that Peng Wang had said they were going to climb over.","Peng Wang took the initiative to come to Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran's front to clarify things for them.","\"This mountain is called Niu Jiao Mountain. The top of the mountain is somewhat similar in shape to cattle horns, so it got that name.","If we hadn't wasted so much time on the road earlier, we could have chosen to walk around the foot of the mountain. If that was the case, it would have taken seven or eight more days.","We have climbed over this mountain before and did not find any large beasts, but there were more wild chickens and rabbits and the like. We can also hunt game to satisfy our cravings.\"","He Zhiran looked up, and as Peng Wang said, there were two mountain tops at the highest point of the mountain that looked like cattle horns. The name was quite appropriate.","In addition, the mountains were connected endlessly, giving people a sense of majesty even when standing at the foot of the mountain.","It goes without saying that crossing over from here would also be very tiring.","At this time, most people had already found suitable places to stop and were resting in the tents.","Mo Jiuye came to He Zhiran and pointed to the tent that had just been set up, \"After walking all day, go in and rest!\"","He Zhiran was indeed a little tired, so she responded and followed Mo Jiuye back into the tent.","After resting for a while, He Zhiran called Mo Jiuye to go up the mountain with her to take a look.","She said to take a look, but she was mainly considering that there were only women at home. She wanted to find some branches to make simple trekking poles for them.","That way, if they encountered difficult parts of the mountain road, they would have some help.","The two worked together to make ten simple trekking poles and took them back.","Seeing the new gadgets in their hands again, the Xie family and Fang family asked about the use and then followed suit.","After safely spending the night, everyone had a simple breakfast the next day, packed up the luggage and some items, carried them on their backs, and followed the officials up Niu Jiao Mountain.","At first it was fine. Everyone had rested for the night so their energy was full. After walking for an hour, people began to fall behind frequently.","Especially the He family, they had to have a few people looking after He Ming no matter if they were carrying things on their backs or lifting them. Therefore, they were often the last in line.","Even though the officials swung their whips to threaten them to speed up, they simply couldn't quicken their pace.","Left with no choice, Peng Wang could only lead the troops to walk and stop repeatedly.","This speed of marching happened to benefit Mo Jiuye.","From time to time he would hunt prey in the bushes or other places on the side of the road.","He Zhiran also took the women of the family to pick herbs along the way.","Seeing that the marching speed was slowed down but there was still such a harvest, Peng Wang's dissatisfaction with the He family also faded a lot.","Just like this, walking and stopping all the way, in the afternoon the troops had entered the deep mountains.","It must be said that this was definitely a natural oxygen bar bestowed by nature.","Looking down the mountain, it felt like standing on top of the world.","From here you could see in all directions, clouds and mist stretched endlessly, peaks floated, nine winding turns, making people's minds broaden and forget to return.","Facing such a beautiful scenery, He Zhiran temporarily forgot everything and sincerely felt the comfort brought by nature.","Just as she was immersed in oblivion, suddenly a woman's scream was heard from below.","Everyone's eyes were all looking towards the source of the sound.","I saw Mrs. Zhao sitting on the ground, her expression very painful.","He Zhiran hurried over.","\"He’s family, my mother-in-law just stepped on a rock and probably sprained her foot,\" said the daughter-in-law of the Fang family as she grabbed He Zhiran and told her about her mother-in-law's situation.","Without doubting, He Zhiran rolled up Mrs. Zhao's trousers to check.","Seeing her ankle protruding obviously, this was no simple sprain!","\"Auntie, your bone is fractured.\"","As He Zhiran spoke, her eyes had already started searching around.","Hearing that her bone was broken, Mrs. Zhao's tears flowed down instantly.","\"It's because I'm useless, I can't even walk well.\"","As she spoke, she unconsciously looked in the direction of the He family.","At this moment, He Ming was being carried by several women walking hard towards them.","Mrs. Zhao didn't want to be a burden on her family like He Ming, so while her daughter-in-law's attention wasn't on her, she closed her eyes and rolled down the slope next to her.","She only hoped that King Yama would appear quickly to take her away, absolutely not dragging her family down...","No one had expected Mrs. Zhao to be so desperate.","When everyone realized something was wrong with Mrs. Zhao, her whole body had already rolled several meters down the hillside.","\"Mother!\"","\"Mrs. Zhao, what are you doing?\"","\"Mother, stop quickly...\"","The Fang family rushed towards Mrs. Zhao's direction at once.","But the terrain there was steep. If they fell accidentally while chasing, they would end up in the same situation as Mrs. Zhao.","Because of this, although the Fang family chased after her, they couldn't catch up to Mrs. Zhao who was rolling down faster and faster.","Seeing Mrs. Zhao's body rolling farther and farther away, the Fang family was no longer hopeful.","At this moment, they clearly saw that Mrs. Zhao's tumbling body suddenly stopped, and Mo Jiuye stood steadily in front of a big tree, blocking Mrs. Zhao's body from rolling down.","The Fang family breathed a sigh of relief at the same time and carefully went towards them.","With everyone's efforts, Mrs. Zhao was finally brought back to the original place.","Fortunately, Mrs. Zhao only had some abrasions on her exposed skin, otherwise she was fine.","When Mrs. Zhao saw the anxious eyes of her loved ones, tears poured out uncontrollably once more.","\"Why are you doing this? Our Fang family is unlucky enough, why keep me to drag you down... woo woo...\"","Seeing this, Fang Chuanzhou's eyes brimmed with tears too.","He knew clearly in his heart that his old wife had done this so that they could march unencumbered. But he couldn't accept her doing something like this.","\"We have three sons, and even if nothing else at least there’s still me this bag of old bones. The four of us big men can carry you while marching. How can that be considered a burden? You must not think so desperately!\"","\"That's right, mother, we brothers have plenty of strength to take turns carrying you on our backs, it won't be a burden at all.\"","\"Mother, your daughter-in-law can also take care of your daily needs. You must not have such thoughts.\"","Seeing her family care so much about herself, Mrs. Zhao couldn't hold back her tears even more.","At this time, Peng Wang had also rushed over. Hearing that Mrs. Zhao had broken her leg and then tried to commit suicide, he was both angry and had a headache.","Therefore, his attitude was extremely unfriendly.","\"Mrs. Zhao, if you dare to commit suicide and break my rules here, I will send someone to whip your family every day after you die, and make sure they suffer a fate worse than death.\"","For Mrs. Zhao, this was much more effective than the Fang family's persuasion.","Mrs. Zhao was stunned for a moment, and immediately assured him.","\"Master Official, please don't beat my sons. I promise I won't think about it anymore.\"","She was even a little scared afterwards, afraid that if she really died, her family would be implicated."]},{"number":97,"title":"Chapter 97: These People are After Me.","paragraphs":["Seeing that Peng Wang's words had the desired effect, the Fang family finally breathed a sigh of relief.","Fang Chuanzhou took the initiative to find He Zhiran and asked her to help set Zhao's dislocated bones.","At the same time, the rest of the Fang family had already arrived in front of Mo Jiuye and knelt down to kowtow one after another, sincerely thanking him for saving Zhao's life.","He Zhiran skillfully pushed Zhao's protruding bones back into place and then used several small wooden sticks she had just found to immobilize the injury.","The Fang family thanked He Zhiran profusely once again.","Fang Chuanzhou even boasted that it was Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran who had saved Zhao’s life, and from now on the Fang family would work like oxen and horses to repay them.","After staying for a while, everyone continued on their way until they found a mountain gorge to rest in before nightfall.","With Mo Jiuye around, He Zhiran didn’t need to worry about whether the surroundings were safe or not, she only needed to focus on resting.","The sisters-in-law were also scrambling to prepare dinner, so He Zhiran suddenly had free time.","The mountain winds were strong. After dinner, everyone crowded back into the tents.","Although Mo Jiuye was there, He Zhiran still did not rest easy in such an environment.","Her consciousness entered her space dimension and looked at the clock on the wall, it was past three in the morning now.","There was still some time before wake up, He Zhiran closed her eyes, intending to sleep a little longer.","Just as her consciousness was hazy, she felt Mo Jiuye next to her suddenly sit up.","At the same time, she also vaguely sensed rustling sounds nearby.","He Zhiran instinctively sat up and her eyes met Mo Jiuye’s. They almost simultaneously sensed the smell of danger.","The couple tidied up quickly and walked out of the tent together.","The moment they appeared outside the tent, they saw the two guarding officers had almost simultaneously been shot in the chest with arrows and instantly collapsed to the ground.","Mo Jiuye instinctively pulled He Zhiran to his side and spoke urgently at a rapid speed.","\"These people are after me, stay here and don't move. I'll lure them away.\"","No sooner had he finished speaking than his body was already leaping into the air. After a few ups and downs, he raced towards a nearby clump of trees.","Dozens of figures in black appeared one after another, pushing their speed to the limit as they closely followed Mo Jiuye's footsteps, occasionally firing an arrow in his direction.","At the same time, Peng Wang and the other officers also heard the commotion outside and came out one by one, bleary-eyed, to see what was going on.","Seeing their two colleagues lying in pools of blood, Peng Wang immediately rushed over with his men.","He Zhiran watched Mo Jiuye's figure quickly disappear. There was only one thought in her mind.","She wanted to fight alongside Mo Jiuye.","With this thought, He Zhiran also sprang into action. She shouted at Peng Wang,","\"Peng Ge, there are assassins. I'm going to help my husband.\"","Peng Wang wanted to stop her, but seeing that He Zhiran was already running farther and farther away, he could only acquiesce to her actions and continued to deal with his companions.","By now, Mo Jiuye had led the group of attackers farther and farther away.","He Zhiran simply couldn’t keep up.","Fortunately, her hearing was quite good. By listening carefully, she could discern the direction of the sounds.","As He Zhiran gave chase, her consciousness entered her space dimension.","At this critical juncture, she couldn't care less and decisively took out the most powerful machine gun from the weapons inside her space.","At the same time, the urgency of the situation did not make her lose her head.","Using such an advanced weapon in ancient times, it would be fine if all these attackers died, but if someone escaped and reported this incident, it would surely alarm Emperor Shunwu.","She was worried it would endanger her family.","Therefore, He Zhiran decisively bought a head wrap to wrap her head up tightly.","Clutching the machine gun, she followed the trail of corpses from the attackers to accurately locate Mo Jiuye’s position.","He Zhiran finally saw the stalemate between the attackers in black and Mo Jiuye at a cliff’s edge up ahead.","At this point, the arrows in Mo Jiuye’s double-armed crossbow had already been spent. He was preparing to engage the opponents with his bare hands.","Taking advantage of when all the attackers' attention was focused on Mo Jiuye, He Zhiran selected an excellent sniping spot.","A series of deafening explosions rang out in the silent and empty valley.","He Zhiran successfully took down four or five of the attackers in black.","At the same time, she also successfully attracted everyone's attention. All the attackers in black turned to look in her direction.","Mo Jiuye also discovered her figure. No matter what, he never imagined that this woman had actually dared to chase all the way here.","Before Mo Jiuye could say anything to order her away, He Zhiran pulled the machine gun’s trigger again.","These attackers were all highly skilled in martial arts. Having learned their lesson, they were now much more vigilant.","They evaded the bullets flying at them in an orderly fashion.","Although a few more people failed to dodge successfully, most were still alive.","The few men in black tacitly glanced at each other before immediately becoming more orderly.","He Zhiran’s actions did not stop as she continued firing at the men in black.","Her barrage did relieve a lot of pressure on Mo Jiuye.","Mo Jiuye also took the opportunity to come to her side.","Seeing the men in black getting closer and closer to He Zhiran, Mo Jiuye didn’t waste a single word. He swept her into his arms and used his lightness skill to retreat.","He Zhiran also took the opportunity to shoot at the men in black again.","The number of men in black visibly decreased rapidly. Thinking all had been killed and this assassination attempt was over, an unexpected situation arose.","To their surprise, a few persistent men in black were still chasing them relentlessly from behind, while more trouble appeared up ahead.","Without a doubt, He Zhiran took out a Swiss army knife from her space and gave it to Mo Jiuye. She continued aiming her gun at the remaining men in black.","By now, the two were cooperating seamlessly with their backs turned to each other.","He Zhiran shot the last few men in black with her machine gun, while Mo Jiuye brandished the Swiss army knife to fend off arrows flying in from the opposite direction.","Luckily, He Zhiran soon disposed of the men in black on her side. As soon as she turned around, she was yanked behind Mo Jiuye by him.","“Stay behind me and don't come out.\"","He Zhiran was here to help, how could she possibly obediently cower behind him?","Her consciousness entered her space again as she bought two large shields and held them in front of herself and Mo Jiuye.","At the same time, the two retreated in sync, aiming to lure those attackers out.","Having a target, both Mo Jiuye’s close combat and her long range shooting became more focused.","Sure enough, those men in black all revealed themselves after the two had retreated less than ten meters.","He Zhiran’s hands once again held a machine gun full of bullets, firing at the men in black’s direction.","Although Mo Jiuye did not know what weapon He Zhiran was using, he could determine that her weapon was suitable for long range attacks. Its power would weaken if those men in black drew close enough to pose a threat to He Zhiran.","To prevent those men in black from getting near and endangering He Zhiran, Mo Jiuye left her the shield and went up to engage them directly with his lightness skill."]},{"number":98,"title":"Chapter 98: Don't move. Just listen to me.","paragraphs":["The black-clothed people behind were now somewhat disarrayed. However, they still took advantage of their greater numbers and had no intention of retreating.","As Mo Jiuye killed the enemies, he also took great care to protect He Zhiran, afraid those black-clothed people would get past him and harm her. The two cooperated seamlessly.","Unexpectedly, just as He Zhiran was about to take out a machine gun from her space, three black-clothed people suddenly appeared from somewhere behind her.","The black-clothed people instantly surrounded He Zhiran. Faced with this situation, if He Zhiran continued using the machine gun, it would be equal to seeking her own destruction.","In order to change tactics, He Zhiran decisively swapped her machine gun for the same Swiss army knife Mo Jiuye had.","Facing three black-clothed experts, all He Zhiran could do was evade.","Just when she saw Mo Jiuye, having dealt with the black-clothed people in front of him, running over to save her, He Zhiran was forced by the three black-clothed people in front of her to the edge of the cliff.","If she retreated another step, she would immediately be crushed to pieces.","The black-clothed people naturally wouldn’t let such an opportunity pass. Their attacks on He Zhiran became even more vicious.","He Zhiran estimated the distance to Mo Jiuye. Even with his superb qinggong, he probably wouldn’t make it in time to save her.","Rather than be stabbed by the black-clothed people, she might as well jump off the cliff. With her space, she would have a good chance of surviving.","In order to have something to cushion her fall, He Zhiran went all out. Just before plunging over the cliff, seeing the black-clothed person rushing at her face on, she didn’t dodge. Her army knife stabbed deep into her opponent's chest. Then her body also quickly tilted backward...","Seeing this, Mo Jiuye’s eyes turned blood red.","\"No...\"","As he spoke, Mo Jiuye’s figure also flew past the black-clothed people and jumped off after her.","Mo Jiuye tilted his head downward, constantly keeping his right hand stretched out towards He Zhiran, while also circulating his inner energy to the extreme. He hoped to grab her before she plummeted off the cliff.","The moment He Zhiran jumped off the cliff, she had already decided that once she dropped some distance and confirmed the black-clothed people's line of sight couldn’t see her, she would enter her space at the fastest speed.","Then she would quickly go in and out until the distance to the ground was safe for her to choose to jump down.","Unexpectedly, just as she was about to enter her space, when she glanced up, she saw Mo Jiuye who had jumped down after her.","He Zhiran knew clearly that even with Mo Jiuye’s qinggong, recklessly jumping from such a height would probably give him little chance of survival.","Was he trying to get himself killed?","Leaving no room for doubt about him, in order for Mo Jiuye to live, the moment she touched his outstretched hand, He Zhiran moved her thoughts and brought both of them into her space.","The scene changed abruptly. Mo Jiuye instantly became vigilant, even adopting a posture ready to attack.","However, when he saw He Zhiran was in front of him, he instantly withdrew his actions.","Seeing the space filled with national treasury items and the unfamiliar everything before him, Mo Jiuye didn’t even know what to ask.","Since He Zhiran had chosen to bring him in with her, she clearly knew that her space would no longer remain a secret from Mo Jiuye.","Just as she was thinking about how to explain things to Mo Jiuye, he suddenly clutched his lower abdomen while spurting out a mouthful of blood.","Mo Jiuye’s body tipped straight backward.","He Zhiran quickly reached out to support him.","With a doctor's experience, she knew his injury must be serious.","There was no time for too much thought. He Zhiran rubbed her somewhat bloodshot eyes and started preparing to perform surgery on Mo Jiuye’s wounds.","She removed all of Mo Jiuye’s outer clothes. The white underclothes had already been dyed red. He Zhiran unhesitatingly stripped Mo Jiuye completely naked. Even having seen countless injured people in her past life, she was still shocked speechless by Mo Jiuye’s wounds.","His body seemed fine, with only some external injuries that didn’t seem to have damaged any internal organs.","But it was different with his abdomen. Not only was the skin and flesh split open, but his internal organs could also vaguely be seen.","He Zhiran inexplicably felt a surge of heartache.","Bearing such heavy injuries, how did he still manage to persevere?","And to willingly jump off a cliff in order to save her... wasn’t that just seeking death?","There was no time for too much feeling. He Zhiran rubbed her somewhat bloodshot eyes and started preparing to suture Mo Jiuye’s wounds.","Three hours later, He Zhiran finally dealt with the most serious injury to Mo Jiuye’s abdomen. She then took advantage of him still being under anesthesia and sutured the rest of his wounds before hooking him up to an IV.","Seeing the blood staining Mo Jiuye’s body, He Zhiran also helped clean him off completely.","In her past life, she had seen countless male patients so she felt nothing in particular, simply seeing everyone as the same.","However, facing Mo Jiuye, she didn’t know why, but she would inexplicably blush and her heart would race. Her eyes would even intentionally avoid certain areas.","After a period of busyness, five hours had unknowingly passed.","Mo Jiuye also gradually regained consciousness.","Just after opening his eyes, the first thing that met his sight was the dazzlingly bright ceiling light and the few transparent bottles on the shelf.","He Zhiran had just gone to the bathroom to take a quick shower. Feeling that Mo Jiuye should be about to wake up, she came over to check on him.","Mo Jiuye was still somewhat weak. He opened his mouth with difficulty, but his eyes tightly stared at her.","He Zhiran knew what he was thinking in his heart. It was nothing more than wanting to know where this place was.","Since she had chosen to bring Mo Jiuye in, she was already prepared to frankly reveal some of the truth.","\"Your injuries are serious. Don't move. Just listen to me.\"","Mo Jiuye blinked to indicate for her to continue.","\"This is a space I coincidentally obtained when I was little. At first, I was also very scared, but after gradually getting familiar with it, I discovered this place was extremely against heaven...\"","He Zhiran started off with lies and proceeded to explain to Mo Jiuye some of the uses and benefits of her space.","\"My medical skills were also learned in here. And when I stole things from the national treasury, I would send them into my space.","In addition, there is also something called a cell phone in this space that can be used to buy many things not available outside...\"","He Zhiran chattered on ceaselessly. In short, other than concealing her identity as a transmigrator, she basically didn’t hold anything back from Mo Jiuye regarding the secrets of her space.","Mo Jiuye was shocked at first. After all, the things she spoke of were too fantastical.","However, recalling the national treasury items he saw after first entering, he also quickly accepted it.","If she didn’t have such heaven-defying capabilities, how could she have emptied the national treasury?","One could only say, in this wide world, nothing is impossible.","After listening to all of He Zhiran’s explanation, Mo Jiuye arduously opened his mouth, “Your space is too against heaven. In order to better protect yourself in the future, you absolutely can’t let anyone else know about it.”","He Zhiran naturally understood the idiom ‘possessing a treasure leads to destruction.’ There were two reasons she brought Mo Jiuye inside. One was to save his life.","The other was that from the moment Mo Jiuye jumped off the cliff after her, she saw his true feelings and also clearly saw Mo Jiuye’s attitude towards her."]},{"number":99,"title":"Chapter 99: You Are Responsible for Me","paragraphs":["Being willing to go all out for her sake, no matter whether Mo Jiuye's feelings towards her were familial love, friendship or romantic love, He Zhiran could conclude that Mo Jiuye cared for her.","This was enough to show that Mo Jiuye was trustworthy.","Therefore, after confiding all her secrets to Mo Jiuye, He Zhiran did not feel pressured at all, on the contrary, she felt very relaxed.","At the very least, if she wanted to take some supplies out of the space in the future, there would be someone in the know to help cover for her.","Mo Jiuye calmed his thoughts before noticing his own body.","His body was covered by a snow-white blanket, and he could feel that he was completely naked at the moment.","Sensing all this, Mo Jiuye's body stiffened.","His first reaction was that he had been completely seen through by He Zhiran.","Recalling the scene of He Zhiran changing his bandages on their wedding night, it was simply incomparable to this “full view” today...","He Zhiran was unaware of Mo Jiuye's inner thoughts at the moment, as she was preparing to change his IV drip with a medicine bottle in her hand.","Unexpectedly, a sudden sentence from Mo Jiuye nearly made her drop the bottle in her hand.","\"You've seen all of my body, so you have to take responsibility for me.\"","He Zhiran's eyes widened as she pointed at herself.","\"I have to take responsibility?\"","Although Mo Jiuye looked a little embarrassed, he still hardened his scalp and said:","\"Yes, you need to take responsibility.\"","At the moment He Zhiran jumped off the cliff, he had already deeply realized his feelings.","He had already fallen for this woman. Knowing that the chances of surviving the jump were slim, he still followed her without any hesitation.","At that time, there was only one thought in his mind - he could not live without her in this life.","Given his personality, he should have said \"I will take responsibility for you\" as before.","However, Mo Jiuye deliberately reversed it this time, with the intention of relying on this woman for the rest of his life.","From He Zhiran's understanding of Mo Jiuye, he was not the kind of person who would make casual jokes.","It could be seen that he was serious about what he said.","But in her ears, it sounded a little awkward.","Shouldn't he be saying \"I will take responsibility for you\"?","Why was it reversed?","When her gaze fell on Mo Jiuye's body, she suddenly realized.","It turned out that he was asking her to take responsibility because she had seen all of him.","Thinking of this, He Zhiran wanted to laugh.","And she did laugh out loud.","\"Hahaha, okay, I will take responsibility for you.\"","Seeing that she was not serious, Mo Jiuye was unsure of the authenticity of her words.","\"Are you really promising?\"","He Zhiran had already confirmed her feelings when she jumped off the cliff, so she would naturally not pretend to be aloof like the ancient women.","\"It's true. As long as you are willing to treat me well, I will also take responsibility for you for the rest of my life.\"","As soon as she finished speaking, she saw Mo Jiuye smile for the first time.","Although he was still weak, that smile could definitely captivate thousands of young girls.","He Zhiran was in a good mood. This eye candy of a man was now hers.","After Mo Jiuye’s IV drip was changed, He Zhiran looked at the clock on the wall and saw that it was already eight o'clock in the evening.","Without realizing it, the two of them had been in the space for almost a whole day.","In a hurry to perform surgery on Mo Jiuye earlier, He Zhiran had not yet carried out her plan to use the space to slow down her descent.","At this time of day, the sky outside was already dark. Without being able to see the environment clearly outside, she could not rashly implement her plan.","Although Mo Jiuye could not read the time on the clock, he could feel that they had been staying in this space for a very long time.","\"We've been out for so long, Mother and my sisters-in-law must be very worried.\"","He Zhiran had considered this point, but given Mo Jiuye's current condition, he was clearly not suitable to be moved around.","\"There's no way. Your wound is very serious and you can't move around casually. Also, it's already late now, we can't safely land at the bottom of the cliff, so we can only think of another way tomorrow.\"","Mo Jiuye also knew that this was the truth, but thinking that his family would worry for him, he felt a little restless lying there...","Going back to that morning when Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran disappeared one after another, Peng Wang led the officials to check on the condition of the two companions.","At that time, they were already breathless, extremely similar to the state of the Eighth Old Zhou when he was pulled out of the water after falling in previously.","Peng Wang was reminded of the breath recovery method used by He Zhiran to treat the Eighth Old Zhou.","He called over a few officials and performed CPR on the two companions according to He Zhiran's method. They were busy for a while, but there was still no sign of them waking up, so Peng Wang had no choice but to give up.","On the same day, the bodies of the two companions were buried in a nearby hill.","The exiled people also woke up after hearing the commotion.","The Mo family women learned from Peng Wang that Mo Jiuye had been chased away by a group of people in black and He Zhiran went after him. They were almost frantic with anxiety.","Unfortunately, when faced with such an incident, they could do nothing and could only pray to heaven to keep them safe and bring them back.","The Fang and Xie families came to persuade and comfort the Mo family women, hoping that they could relax their hearts, believing that Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran would definitely come back.","Peng Wang also ordered his troops to stay put at their original location and wait.","And so they waited for a whole day.","During this whole day, the Mo family women's faces were washed with tears.","Up until this moment, they still had not seen Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran return. Even though everyone kept silent about it, they all knew in their hearts that the two had most likely perished.","Only Old Lady Mo still firmly believed that her son and daughter-in-law would definitely come back.","Seeing her daughters-in-law and daughter crying, she had to pull herself together.","\"Jiuye and He’shi are not dead. What are you all crying for?\"","Hearing this, all the sisters-in-law looked towards Old Lady Mo.","The eldest sister-in-law raised her head, trying her best not to let the tears fall.","\"Mother, they have been away for a whole day. If they could come back, they would have already.\"","However, Old Lady Mo did not want to believe this.","\"Have you forgotten?","When my Mo family men went to battlefields to kill enemies, didn't they also often go out for several days before coming back?","Back then there was also no news at all ...\"","After listening to Old Lady Mo's words, everyone seemed to see hope again and immediately cheered up.","\"Mother is right. Ninth brother and ninth sister-in-law are so powerful, they must be fine.\"","\"That’s right, they must have been caught up with something. As long as we keep waiting, they will definitely come back.\"","Old Lady Mo looked around and saw that her words had achieved the desired effect. She continued instructing:","\"It’s getting late, everyone go back and rest. In case Jiuye and He’shi come back late at night, don’t let yourselves be too tired tomorrow to travel.\"","Hearing this, the sisters-in-law wiped their tears and returned to their tents to rest.","On Peng Wang's side, the deaths of the two brothers that morning had also left them dejected. At the same time, they were worried about Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran's safety, leaving Peng Wang completely sleepless right now."]},{"number":100,"title":"Chapter 100: Witness the Power of Thermal Weapons.","paragraphs":["Peng Wang sat in the middle of everyone and lit a bonfire, sitting there in a daze.","The Eighth Old Zhou and Zhang Qing saw this and walked over to accompany him.","Zhang Qing was always frank, saying whatever came to his mind.","\"Boss, I see those people in black are all here for Mo Jiuye. It's a pity for our two brothers to suffer this injustice.\"","Peng Wang glanced at Zhang Qing, his tone a little harsh.","\"Do I still need to say that when everyone knows clearly?\"","Zhang Qing did not shut up because of Peng Wang's attitude.","\"Boss, Mo Jiuye and his wife haven't come back yet, I'm afraid things don't bode well for them.\"","When he heard these words, tears had already welled up in The Eighth Old Zhou's eyes.","He didn't know why, but when he heard that He Zhiran's situation was dangerous, his heart felt as painful as being pricked by a needle.","Such a good woman, how could she be in danger?","Fortunately, it was dark and neither Peng Wang nor Zhang Qing saw the tears in the corners of his eyes, otherwise Peng Wang would definitely scold him severely again.","Peng Wang sighed, \"It's been a whole day, if they were coming back they should have been back by now.\"","These unspoken words meant that he judged that He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye were already dead.","Zhang Qing continued, \"Boss, if so, do we have to continue on our way tomorrow?\"","Peng Wang nodded, \"We've already delayed this mission for too long, we must set off early tomorrow morning.\"","The silent The Eighth Old Zhou listened. When he heard they would set off tomorrow, the pain in his heart became more intense.","\"Boss, can we wait one more day? I plan to go out and look for people.\"","Peng Wang looked at him inquisitively.","In the firelight, traces of tears could vaguely be seen on The Eighth Old Zhou's face.","There was no need to think about it, this guy was stubbornly obsessed with Miss He.","Peng Wang sighed deeply, \"That's good too. I'll give you three days. Whether you find them or not, you must catch up with us.\"","\"Don't worry boss, I will catch up with you guys within three days.\"","The Eighth Old Zhou knew he could understand the implication in Peng Wang's words.","But he just wouldn't give up. No matter how he felt, it was He Zhiran who had saved his life at first. Now that He Zhiran and Mo Jiuye were of unknown fate, if he continued on like this he would feel guilty for the rest of his life.","\"Boss, you guys continue on tomorrow, I will stay to look for traces of them.\"","Peng Wang knew The Eighth Old Zhou's temperament. He looked stubborn on the outside, but once he made up his mind even ten oxen couldn't pull him back.","He sighed deeply, \"That's good too. I'll give you three days. Whether you find them or not, you must rejoin the team.\"","\"Don't worry boss, I will catch up with you guys within three days.\"","The Eighth Old Zhou felt that three days was enough. He refused to believe two living people could just disappear into thin air.","At least he had to see the person alive, or see their corpse if dead.","On the Mo family's side, although the women had all returned to their own tents, not one of them could fall asleep.","Especially Old Lady Mo. In front of others she didn't dare show her grief, because once she collapsed these people wouldn't have a backbone anymore.","Now in the deep of night, she sat in her tent, looking out from time to time, hoping a miracle would happen and her son and daughter-in-law would return safely.","Mo Hanyue got up and snuggled into Old Lady Mo's arms.","\"Mother, ninth brother and ninth sister-in-law won't abandon us.\"","Old Lady Mo lovingly stroked her daughter's head, \"Um, they will definitely come back.\"","......","In the space, Mo Jiuye and He Zhiran were also wide awake.","Thinking of today's assassination attempt, if Mo Jiuye also had a machine gun like hers, and they both fired from afar at the same time, perhaps Mo Jiuye wouldn't have been severely injured and she wouldn't have been forced to jump off the cliff.","Therefore, He Zhiran felt it necessary to teach Mo Jiuye how to use those firearms.","In case they encountered similar dangers in the future, he would have one more lifesaving method.","Seeing He Zhiran bring over a large pile of strange metal gadgets, Mo Jiuye was immediately invigorated.","Among them there were some he had seen He Zhiran use before, so they weren't unfamiliar.","\"Are these all your weapons?\"","He Zhiran first took out the machine gun she had used today.","\"This is called a machine gun. It can fire continuously, suitable for when there are many enemies.\"","As she spoke, she demonstrated to Mo Jiuye how to use the machine gun and how to load bullets step by step.","For someone who was a veteran of the battlefield, seeing such a weapon was like seeing a great treasure, very exciting.","Mo Jiuye wanted to get up and mimic He Zhiran, holding the machine gun and comparing it, but with so many wounds on his body even the slightest movement hurt like hell.","Seeing Mo Jiuye's painful expression, He Zhiran quickly stopped his movements.","\"You can't move now. There are plenty of these machine guns. After you recover, feel free to take one to play with or even use for hunting. I won't be distressed.\"","He Zhiran really wouldn't feel distressed. Facing those men in black today, when her machine gun ran out of bullets she didn't want to waste time reloading, so she would take out a new one from her space. As a result there were now more than ten identical machine guns in her space.","Mo Jiuye felt a little disappointed at not being able to personally feel what it was like to hold a machine gun.","But he also knew his wounds were too severe and he shouldn't exercise too early.","\"We agreed, after I recover you must give me one of these machine guns.\"","He Zhiran didn't expect this man to love the weapons in her space so much that his tone became somewhat childish.","Amused but also touched, she took out the sniper rifle again.","\"This is called a sniper rifle. The characteristics are high accuracy and long range, suitable for long-range assassinations.\"","Then she took out the exquisite little mini pistol.","\"This is suitable to carry around for self defense.\"","\"And this is a tranquilizer gun that can make people temporarily lose consciousness. If you want to capture someone alive then use this.\"","Mo Jiuye became more and more interested the more he listened. If these weapons had been on past battlefields there wouldn't have been so many dead and injured brothers.","However, he knew clearly in his heart that He Zhiran's weapons were too extraordinary and shouldn't see too much daylight.","Especially since he was no longer the Duke of Protection. Future battlefields had nothing to do with him anymore.","But with these weapons in He Zhiran's hands, her safety would have greater assurance.","After seeing all this, He Zhiran joyfully discovered a large cardboard box in the medical room with ten hand grenades inside.","She didn't know who had put them in the medical room. If she had known earlier she wouldn't have had so much trouble dealing with those men in black. Fortunately both her and Mo Jiuye got away unharmed.","No matter what, it was a good thing to have another highly lethal weapon in her space, which would definitely come in handy sooner or later when facing unexpected situations in the future.","She took out a grenade to show Mo Jiuye.","\"This is called a hand grenade. It contains four thousand steel balls that burst out like falling flowers everywhere in an explosion, and can instantly kill enemies.\"","Without even thinking about it Mo Jiuye knew this was an area attack weapon.","He hated that his wounds didn't immediately heal so he could witness the power of these weapons.","Thinking of his injuries, Mo Jiuye was truly grateful to have He Zhiran. Otherwise he didn't know if he would still be alive now.","Just as he was silently grateful to He Zhiran, he suddenly felt his lower abdomen tighten.","He saw He Zhiran take a box of grenades out and struggled to get up."]}]);
